#: src/macros-by-example.md:530
msgid "From another crate, you can refer to the macro by path:"
msgstr "在另一个 crate 中，可以通过路径引用该宏："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:535 src/macros-by-example.md:562
msgid "\"example warning\""
msgstr "\"example warning\""

#: src/macros-by-example.md:539
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.decl.scope.macro_export.macro_use\\] `macro_export` allows the use "
"of \\[`macro_use`\\]\\[macro.decl.scope.macro_use\\] on an `extern crate` to "
"import the macro into the [`macro_use` prelude](names/preludes.md#macro_use-"
"prelude)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.decl.scope.macro_export.macro_use\\] `macro_export` 允许在 `extern "
"crate` 上使用 \\[`macro_use`\\]\\[macro.decl.scope.macro_use\\]，以将该宏导"
"入 [`macro_use` prelude](names/preludes.md#macro_use-prelude)。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:552
msgid ""
"Using `macro_use` in a dependent crate allows you to use the macro from the "
"prelude:"
msgstr "在依赖 crate 中使用 `macro_use`，可以让你从 prelude 使用该宏："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:561
msgid "// Resolved via macro prelude.\n"
msgstr "// 通过宏 prelude 解析。\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:567
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.decl.scope.macro_export.local_inner_macros\\] Adding "
"`local_inner_macros` to the `macro_export` attribute causes all single-"
"segment macro invocations in the macro definition to have an implicit "
"`$crate::` prefix."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.decl.scope.macro_export.local_inner_macros\\] 向 `macro_export` 属"
"性添加 `local_inner_macros`，会使宏定义中的所有单段宏调用都带有隐式的 "
"`$crate::` 前缀。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:570
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] This is intended primarily as a tool to migrate code written "
"before [`$crate`](macro.decl.hygiene.crate) was added to the language to "
"work with Rust 2018's path-based imports of macros. Its use is discouraged "
"in new code."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 这主要是作为一种迁移工具，用于迁移在 [`$crate`]"
"(macro.decl.hygiene.crate) 加入语言之前编写的代码，使其能够与 Rust 2018 的基"
"于路径的宏导入配合工作。不鼓励在新代码中使用它。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:577
msgid "// Automatically converted to $crate::helper!().\n"
msgstr "// 自动转换为 $crate::helper!()。\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:586
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.hygiene\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.hygiene\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:587
msgid "Hygiene"
msgstr "卫生性"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:589
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.decl.hygiene.intro\\] Macros by example have _mixed-site hygiene_. "
"This means that [loop labels](expressions/loop-expr.md#loop-labels), [block "
"labels](expr.loop.block-labels), and local variables are looked up at the "
"macro definition site while other symbols are looked up at the macro "
"invocation site. For example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.decl.hygiene.intro\\] 示例宏具有*混合位置卫生性*。这意味着[循环标"
"签](expressions/loop-expr.md#loop-labels)、[块标签](expr.loop.block-labels)和"
"局部变量会在宏定义位置查找，而其他符号会在宏调用位置查找。例如："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:595
msgid "\"this is never called\""
msgstr "\"this is never called\""

#: src/macros-by-example.md:600
msgid "// Uses `x` from the definition site.\n"
msgstr "// 使用定义位置的 `x`。\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:601
msgid "// Uses `func` from the invocation site.\n"
msgstr "// 使用调用位置的 `func`。\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:607
msgid "/* does not panic */"
msgstr "/* does not panic */"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:612
msgid ""
"Labels and local variables defined in macro expansion are not shared between "
"invocations, so this code doesn’t compile:"
msgstr ""
"宏展开中定义的标签和局部变量不会在各次调用之间共享，因此这段代码无法编译："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:628
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.decl.hygiene.crate\\] A special case is the `$crate` metavariable. "
"It refers to the crate defining the macro, and can be used at the start of "
"the path to look up items or macros which are not in scope at the invocation "
"site."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.decl.hygiene.crate\\] 一个特殊情况是 `$crate` 元变量。它指代定义该"
"宏的 crate，并且可以用在路径开头，用于查找在调用位置不在作用域内的条目或宏。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:633
msgid "//// Definitions in the `helper_macro` crate.\n"
msgstr "//// `helper_macro` crate 中的定义。\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:636
msgid ""
"// () => { helper!() } // This might lead to an error due to 'helper' not "
"being in scope.\n"
msgstr "// () => { helper!() } // 这可能因 'helper' 不在作用域内而导致错误。\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:644
msgid ""
"//// Usage in another crate.\n"
"// Note that `helper_macro::helper` is not imported!\n"
msgstr ""
"//// 在另一个 crate 中的用法。\n"
"// 注意，未导入 `helper_macro::helper`！\n"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:654
msgid ""
"Note that, because `$crate` refers to the current crate, it must be used "
"with a fully qualified module path when referring to non-macro items:"
msgstr ""
"注意，因为 `$crate` 指代当前 crate，所以引用非宏条目时必须将它与完全限定模块"
"路径一起使用："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:667
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.decl.hygiene.vis\\] Additionally, even though `$crate` allows a "
"macro to refer to items within its own crate when expanding, its use has no "
"effect on visibility. An item or macro referred to must still be visible "
"from the invocation site. In the following example, any attempt to invoke "
"`call_foo!()` from outside its crate will fail because `foo()` is not public."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.decl.hygiene.vis\\] 此外，即使 `$crate` 允许宏在展开时引用其自身 "
"crate 内的条目，它的使用也不会影响可见性。被引用的条目或宏仍然必须从调用位置"
"可见。在下面的示例中，任何从其 crate 外部调用 `call_foo!()` 的尝试都会失败，"
"因为 `foo()` 不是公开的。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:679
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Prior to Rust 1.30, `$crate` and \\[`local_inner_macros`\\]\\"
"[macro.decl.scope.macro_export.local_inner_macros\\] were unsupported. They "
"were added alongside \\[path-based imports of macros\\]\\"
"[macro.decl.scope.macro_export\\], to ensure that helper macros did not need "
"to be manually imported by users of a macro-exporting crate. Crates written "
"for earlier versions of Rust that use helper macros need to be modified to "
"use `$crate` or `local_inner_macros` to work well with path-based imports."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 在 Rust 1.30 之前，`$crate` 和 \\[`local_inner_macros`\\]\\"
"[macro.decl.scope.macro_export.local_inner_macros\\] 尚不受支持。它们是与\\"
"[宏的基于路径的导入\\]\\[macro.decl.scope.macro_export\\]一同加入的，以确保导"
"出宏的 crate 的用户不需要手动导入辅助宏。为较早 Rust 版本编写且使用辅助宏的 "
"crate，需要修改为使用 `$crate` 或 `local_inner_macros`，才能与基于路径的导入"
"良好配合。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:682
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:683
msgid "Follow-set ambiguity restrictions"
msgstr "Follow 集歧义限制"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:685
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.intro\\] The parser used by the macro system is "
"reasonably powerful, but it is limited in order to prevent ambiguity in "
"current or future versions of the language."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.intro\\] 宏系统使用的解析器相当强大，但为了防止当前"
"或未来语言版本中的歧义，它也受到限制。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:688
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-restriction\\] In particular, in addition to "
"the rule about ambiguous expansions, a nonterminal matched by a metavariable "
"must be followed by a token which has been decided can be safely used after "
"that kind of match."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-restriction\\] 特别是，除了关于歧义展开的规则"
"外，由元变量匹配的非终结符后面必须跟随一个已被判定可安全用于该类匹配之后的 "
"token。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:691
msgid ""
"As an example, a macro matcher like `$i:expr [ , ]` could in theory be "
"accepted in Rust today, since `[,]` cannot be part of a legal expression and "
"therefore the parse would always be unambiguous. However, because `[` can "
"start trailing expressions, `[` is not a character which can safely be ruled "
"out as coming after an expression. If `[,]` were accepted in a later version "
"of Rust, this matcher would become ambiguous or would misparse, breaking "
"working code. Matchers like `$i:expr,` or `$i:expr;` would be legal, "
"however, because `,` and `;` are legal expression separators. The specific "
"rules are:"
msgstr ""
"举例来说，像 `$i:expr [ , ]` 这样的宏匹配器在今天的 Rust 中理论上可以被接受，"
"因为 `[,]` 不能成为合法表达式的一部分，因此解析总是无歧义的。不过，因为 `[` "
"可以开始尾随表达式，不能安全地排除 `[` 出现在表达式之后的可能性。如果在较后"
"的 Rust 版本中接受了 `[,]`，这个匹配器就会变得有歧义，或被错误解析，从而破坏"
"可工作的代码。不过，像 `$i:expr,` 或 `$i:expr;` 这样的匹配器是合法的，因为 "
"`,` 和 `;` 是合法的表达式分隔符。具体规则如下："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:693
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-expr-stmt\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-expr-stmt\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:694
msgid "`expr` and `stmt` may only be followed by one of: `=>`, `,`, or `;`."
msgstr "`expr` 和 `stmt` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`=>`、`,` 或 `;`。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:696
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-pat_param\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-pat_param\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:697
msgid ""
"`pat_param` may only be followed by one of: `=>`, `,`, `=`, `|`, `if`, or "
"`in`."
msgstr "`pat_param` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`=>`、`,`、`=`、`|`、`if` 或 `in`。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:699
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-pat\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-pat\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:700
msgid "`pat` may only be followed by one of: `=>`, `,`, `=`, `if`, or `in`."
msgstr "`pat` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`=>`、`,`、`=`、`if` 或 `in`。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:702
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-path-ty\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-path-ty\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:703
msgid ""
"`path` and `ty` may only be followed by one of: `=>`, `,`, `=`, `|`, `;`, "
"`:`, `>`, `>>`, `[`, `{`, `as`, `where`, or a macro variable of `block` "
"fragment specifier."
msgstr ""
"`path` 和 `ty` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`=>`、`,`、`=`、`|`、`;`、`:`、`>`、"
"`>>`、`[`、`{`、`as`、`where`，或片段说明符为 `block` 的宏变量。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:705
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-vis\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-vis\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:706
msgid ""
"`vis` may only be followed by one of: `,`, an identifier other than a non-"
"raw `priv`, any token that can begin a type, or a metavariable with a "
"`ident`, `ty`, or `path` fragment specifier."
msgstr ""
"`vis` 后面只能跟随以下之一：`,`、除一个非 raw 的 `priv` 之外的标识符、任何可"
"以开始类型的 token，或带有 `ident`、`ty` 或 `path` 片段说明符的元变量。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:708
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-other\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.token-other\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:709
msgid "All other fragment specifiers have no restrictions."
msgstr "所有其他片段说明符没有限制。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:711
msgid "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.edition2021\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.edition2021\\]"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:712
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2021\\] Before the 2021 edition, `pat` may also be followed by `|"
"`."
msgstr "\\[!EDITION-2021\\] 在 2021 edition 之前，`pat` 后面也可以跟随 `|`。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:715
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.repetition\\] When repetitions are involved, then "
"the rules apply to every possible number of expansions, taking separators "
"into account. This means:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.decl.follow-set.repetition\\] 涉及重复时，这些规则会在考虑分隔符的"
"情况下应用于每一种可能的展开次数。这意味着："

#: src/macros-by-example.md:718
msgid ""
"If the repetition includes a separator, that separator must be able to "
"follow the contents of the repetition."
msgstr "如果重复包含分隔符，则该分隔符必须能够跟随在重复内容之后。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:719
msgid ""
"If the repetition can repeat multiple times (`*` or `+`), then the contents "
"must be able to follow themselves."
msgstr "如果重复可以重复多次（`*` 或 `+`），则其内容必须能够跟随其自身。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:720
msgid ""
"The contents of the repetition must be able to follow whatever comes before, "
"and whatever comes after must be able to follow the contents of the "
"repetition."
msgstr ""
"重复的内容必须能够跟随在其前面的任何内容之后，而其后面的任何内容也必须能够跟"
"随在重复内容之后。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:721
msgid ""
"If the repetition can match zero times (`*` or `?`), then whatever comes "
"after must be able to follow whatever comes before."
msgstr ""
"如果重复可以匹配零次（`*` 或 `?`），则其后面的任何内容必须能够跟随在其前面的"
"任何内容之后。"

#: src/macros-by-example.md:723
msgid "For more detail, see the [formal specification](macro-ambiguity.md)."
msgstr "更多细节见[形式化规约](macro-ambiguity.md)。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:1
msgid "r\\[macro.proc\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.proc\\]"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.proc.intro\\] _Procedural macros_ allow creating syntax extensions "
"as execution of a function. Procedural macros come in one of three flavors:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.proc.intro\\] *过程宏* 允许通过执行函数来创建语法扩展。过程宏有三种"
"形式："

#: src/procedural-macros.md:7
msgid "[Function-like macros](#the-proc_macro-attribute) - `custom!(...)`"
msgstr "[类函数宏](#the-proc_macro-attribute) - `custom!(...)`"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:8
msgid "[Derive macros](macro.proc.derive) - `#[derive(CustomDerive)]`"
msgstr "[derive 宏](macro.proc.derive) - `#[derive(CustomDerive)]`"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:9
msgid ""
"[Attribute macros](#the-proc_macro_attribute-attribute) - "
"`#[CustomAttribute]`"
msgstr "[属性宏](#the-proc_macro_attribute-attribute) - `#[CustomAttribute]`"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:11
msgid ""
"Procedural macros allow you to run code at compile time that operates over "
"Rust syntax, both consuming and producing Rust syntax. You can sort of think "
"of procedural macros as functions from an AST to another AST."
msgstr ""
"过程宏允许你在编译时运行操作 Rust 语法的代码，既消费 Rust 语法，也产生 Rust "
"语法。可以大致将过程宏看作从一个 AST 到另一个 AST 的函数。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.proc.def\\] Procedural macros must be defined in the root of a "
"crate with the [crate type](linkage.md) of `proc-macro`. The macros may not "
"be used from the crate where they are defined, and can only be used when "
"imported in another crate."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.proc.def\\] 过程宏必须定义在 [crate 类型](linkage.md)为 `proc-"
"macro` 的 crate 根中。这些宏不得从定义它们的 crate 中使用，只能在另一个 "
"crate 中导入后使用。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:16
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] When using Cargo, Procedural macro crates are defined with the "
"`proc-macro` key in your manifest:"
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 使用 Cargo 时，过程宏 crate 通过清单中的 `proc-macro` 键定义："

#: src/procedural-macros.md:24
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.proc.result\\] As functions, they must either return syntax, "
"panic, or loop endlessly. Returned syntax either replaces or adds the syntax "
"depending on the kind of procedural macro. Panics are caught by the compiler "
"and are turned into a compiler error. Endless loops are not caught by the "
"compiler which hangs the compiler."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.proc.result\\] 作为函数，它们必须返回语法、panic 或无限循环三者之"
"一。返回的语法会根据过程宏的种类替换或添加语法。panic 会被编译器捕获并转换为"
"编译器错误。无限循环不会被编译器捕获，而会使编译器挂起。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:27
msgid ""
"Procedural macros run during compilation, and thus have the same resources "
"that the compiler has. For example, standard input, error, and output are "
"the same that the compiler has access to. Similarly, file access is the "
"same. Because of this, procedural macros have the same security concerns "
"that [Cargo's build scripts](../cargo/reference/build-scripts.html) have."
msgstr ""
"过程宏在编译期间运行，因此拥有与编译器相同的资源。例如，标准输入、标准错误和"
"标准输出与编译器可访问的是同一组资源。类似地，文件访问也是相同的。因此，过程"
"宏具有与 [Cargo 的构建脚本](../cargo/reference/build-scripts.html)相同的安全"
"隐患。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:29
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.proc.error\\] Procedural macros have two ways of reporting errors. "
"The first is to panic. The second is to emit a \\[`compile_error`\\] macro "
"invocation."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.proc.error\\] 过程宏有两种报告错误的方式。第一种是 panic。第二种是"
"发出 \\[`compile_error`\\] 宏调用。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:32
msgid "r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro-crate\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro-crate\\]"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:33
msgid "The `proc_macro` crate"
msgstr "`proc_macro` crate"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:35
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro-crate.intro\\] Procedural macro crates almost "
"always will link to the compiler-provided [`proc_macro` crate](proc_macro). "
"The `proc_macro` crate provides types required for writing procedural macros "
"and facilities to make it easier."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro-crate.intro\\] 过程宏 crate 几乎总是会链接到编译器"
"提供的 [`proc_macro` crate](proc_macro)。`proc_macro` crate 提供编写过程宏所"
"需的类型，以及使编写过程宏更容易的设施。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:38
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro-crate.token-stream\\] This crate primarily "
"contains a [`TokenStream`](proc_macro::TokenStream) type. Procedural macros "
"operate over _token streams_ instead of AST nodes, which is a far more "
"stable interface over time for both the compiler and for procedural macros "
"to target. A _token stream_ is roughly equivalent to `Vec<TokenTree>` where "
"a `TokenTree` can roughly be thought of as lexical token. For example `foo` "
"is an `Ident` token, `.` is a `Punct` token, and `1.2` is a `Literal` token. "
"The `TokenStream` type, unlike `Vec<TokenTree>`, is cheap to clone."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro-crate.token-stream\\] 这个 crate 主要包含 "
"[`TokenStream`](proc_macro::TokenStream) 类型。过程宏操作的是 *token 流* 而不"
"是 AST 节点；随着时间推移，对编译器和过程宏而言，token 流都是稳定得多的目标接"
"口。*token 流* 大致等价于 `Vec<TokenTree>`，其中 `TokenTree` 大致可以看作词"
"法 token。例如，`foo` 是 `Ident` token，`.` 是 `Punct` token，`1.2` 是 "
"`Literal` token。与 `Vec<TokenTree>` 不同，`TokenStream` 类型的克隆成本很低。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:41
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro-crate.span\\] All tokens have an associated "
"`Span`. A `Span` is an opaque value that cannot be modified but can be "
"manufactured. `Span`s represent an extent of source code within a program "
"and are primarily used for error reporting. While you cannot modify a `Span` "
"itself, you can always change the `Span` _associated_ with any token, such "
"as through getting a `Span` from another token."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro-crate.span\\] 所有 token 都有关联的 `Span`。`Span` "
"是一个不能被修改但可以被构造的不透明值。`Span` 表示程序中一段源代码的范围，主"
"要用于错误报告。虽然你不能修改 `Span` 本身，但始终可以更改与任何 token *关联"
"* 的 `Span`，例如通过从另一个 token 获取 `Span` 来更改。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:44
msgid "r\\[macro.proc.hygiene\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.proc.hygiene\\]"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:45
msgid "Procedural macro hygiene"
msgstr "过程宏卫生性"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:47
msgid ""
"Procedural macros are _unhygienic_. This means they behave as if the output "
"token stream was simply written inline to the code it's next to. This means "
"that it's affected by external items and also affects external imports."
msgstr ""
"过程宏是 *非卫生的*。这意味着它们的行为就像输出 token 流被直接内联写入其旁边"
"的代码一样。这意味着它会受到外部项的影响，也会影响外部导入。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:49
msgid ""
"Macro authors need to be careful to ensure their macros work in as many "
"contexts as possible given this limitation. This often includes using "
"absolute paths to items in libraries (for example, `::std::option::Option` "
"instead of `Option`) or by ensuring that generated functions have names that "
"are unlikely to clash with other functions (like `__internal_foo` instead of "
"`foo`)."
msgstr ""
"在这种限制下，宏作者需要谨慎地确保他们的宏能在尽可能多的上下文中工作。这通常"
"包括对库中的项使用绝对路径（例如使用 `::std::option::Option` 而不是 "
"`Option`），或者确保生成的函数具有不太可能与其他函数冲突的名称（例如使用 "
"`__internal_foo` 而不是 `foo`）。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:53
msgid "r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro\\]"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:54
msgid "The `proc_macro` attribute"
msgstr "`proc_macro` 属性"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:56
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro.intro\\] The _`proc_macro` [attribute]"
"(attributes.md)_ defines a \\[function-like\\]\\[macro.invocation\\] "
"procedural macro."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.proc.proc_macro.intro\\] *`proc_macro` [属性](attributes.md)* 定义"
"一个 \\[类函数\\]\\[macro.invocation\\] 过程宏。"

#: src/procedural-macros.md:59
msgid ""
"\\[!EXAMPLE\\] This macro definition ignores its input and emits a function "
"`answer` into its scope."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EXAMPLE\\] 这个宏定义会忽略其输入，并在其作用域中发出一个函数 `answer`。"

