"inline module blocks, the relative location of the file path depends on the "
"kind of source file the `path` attribute is located in. \"mod-rs\" source "
"files are root modules (such as `lib.rs` or `main.rs`) and modules with "
"files named `mod.rs`. \"non-mod-rs\" source files are all other module "
"files. Paths for `path` attributes inside inline module blocks in a mod-rs "
"file are relative to the directory of the mod-rs file including the inline "
"module components as directories. For non-mod-rs files, it is the same "
"except the path starts with a directory with the name of the non-mod-rs "
"module. For example, the following code snippet would use the paths shown "
"based on where it is located:"
msgstr ""
