#: src/items/enumerations.md:112
msgid "Discriminants"
msgstr "判别值"

#: src/items/enumerations.md:114
msgid ""
"r\\[items.enum.discriminant.intro\\] Each enum instance has a "
"_discriminant_: an integer logically associated to it that is used to "
"determine which variant it holds."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.enum.discriminant.intro\\] 每个枚举实例都有一个*判别值*：它是在逻辑"
"上与该实例关联的整数，用于确定该实例持有哪个变体。"

#: src/items/enumerations.md:117
msgid ""
"r\\[items.enum.discriminant.repr-rust\\] Under the [`Rust` representation]"
"(../type-layout.md#the-rust-representation), the discriminant is interpreted "
"as an `isize` value. However, the compiler is allowed to use a smaller type "
"(or another means of distinguishing variants) in its actual memory layout."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.enum.discriminant.repr-rust\\] 在 [`Rust` 表示](../type-"
"layout.md#the-rust-representation)下，判别值被解释为 `isize` 值。不过，编译器"
"允许在实际内存布局中使用更小的类型（或用另一种方式区分变体）。"

#: src/items/enumerations.md:120
msgid "Assigning discriminant values"
msgstr "赋予判别值"

