msgstr "// 这是允许的，因为它在验证前会被移除。\n"

#: src/items/unions.md:1
msgid "r\\[items.union\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:4
msgid "r\\[items.union.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.syntax\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.intro\\] A union declaration uses the same syntax as a "
"struct declaration, except with `union` in place of `struct`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.intro\\] 联合体声明使用与结构体声明相同的语法，只是用 "
"`union` 代替 `struct`。"

#: src/items/unions.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.namespace\\] A union declaration defines the given name in "
"the [type namespace](../names/namespaces.md) of the module or block where it "
"is located."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.namespace\\] 联合体声明会在其所在模块或块的[类型命名空间](../"
"names/namespaces.md)中定义给定名称。"

#: src/items/unions.md:24
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.common-storage\\] The key property of unions is that all "
"fields of a union share common storage. As a result, writes to one field of "
"a union can overwrite its other fields, and size of a union is determined by "
"the size of its largest field."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.common-storage\\] 联合体的关键性质是，联合体的所有字段共享同"
"一份存储。因此，写入联合体的一个字段可能覆盖其其他字段，并且联合体的大小由其"
"最大字段的大小决定。"

#: src/items/unions.md:27
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.field-restrictions\\] Union field types are restricted to "
"the following subset of types:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.field-restrictions\\] 联合体字段类型被限制为以下类型子集："

#: src/items/unions.md:30
msgid "r\\[items.union.field-copy\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.field-copy\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:31
msgid "`Copy` types"
msgstr "`Copy` 类型"

#: src/items/unions.md:33
msgid "r\\[items.union.field-references\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.field-references\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:34
msgid "References (`&T` and `&mut T` for arbitrary `T`)"
msgstr "引用（任意 `T` 的 `&T` 和 `&mut T`）"

#: src/items/unions.md:36
msgid "r\\[items.union.field-manually-drop\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.field-manually-drop\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:37
msgid "`ManuallyDrop<T>` (for arbitrary `T`)"
msgstr "`ManuallyDrop<T>`（任意 `T`）"

#: src/items/unions.md:39
msgid "r\\[items.union.field-tuple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.field-tuple\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:40
msgid "Tuples and arrays containing only allowed union field types"
msgstr "仅包含允许的联合体字段类型的元组和数组"

#: src/items/unions.md:42
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.drop\\] This restriction ensures, in particular, that union "
"fields never need to be dropped. Like for structs and enums, it is possible "
"to `impl Drop` for a union to manually define what happens when it gets "
"dropped."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.drop\\] 这项限制尤其确保联合体字段永远不需要被丢弃。与结构体"
"和枚举一样，可以为联合体 `impl Drop`，以手动定义它被丢弃时发生什么。"

#: src/items/unions.md:45
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.fieldless\\] Unions without any fields are not accepted by "
"the compiler, but can be accepted by macros."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.fieldless\\] 没有任何字段的联合体不会被编译器接受，但可以被宏"
"接受。"

#: src/items/unions.md:48
msgid "r\\[items.union.init\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.init\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:49
msgid "Initialization of a union"
msgstr "联合体的初始化"

#: src/items/unions.md:51
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.init.intro\\] A value of a union type can be created using "
"the same syntax that is used for struct types, except that it must specify "
"exactly one field:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.init.intro\\] 可以使用与结构体类型相同的语法创建联合体类型的"
"值，只是必须恰好指定一个字段："

#: src/items/unions.md:60
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.init.result\\] The expression above creates a value of type "
"`MyUnion` and initializes the storage using field `f1`. The union can be "
"accessed using the same syntax as struct fields:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.init.result\\] 上面的表达式创建一个 `MyUnion` 类型的值，并使"
"用字段 `f1` 初始化存储。可以使用与结构体字段相同的语法访问该联合体："

#: src/items/unions.md:70
msgid "r\\[items.union.fields\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.fields\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:71
msgid "Reading and writing union fields"
msgstr "读取和写入联合体字段"

#: src/items/unions.md:73
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.intro\\] Unions have no notion of an \"active "
"field\". Instead, every union access just interprets the storage as the type "
"of the field used for the access."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.intro\\] 联合体没有“活动字段”的概念。相反，每次联合体"
"访问都只是将该存储解释为用于此次访问的字段的类型。"

#: src/items/unions.md:76
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.read\\] Reading a union field reads the bits of the "
"union at the field's type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.read\\] 读取联合体字段会按该字段的类型读取联合体的位。"

#: src/items/unions.md:79
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.offset\\] Fields might have a non-zero offset (except "
"when [the C representation](../type-layout.md#reprc-unions) is used); in "
"that case the bits starting at the offset of the fields are read"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.offset\\] 字段可能具有非零偏移量（使用 [C 表示](../"
"type-layout.md#reprc-unions)时除外）；在这种情况下，会读取从这些字段偏移量开"
"始的位。"

#: src/items/unions.md:82
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.validity\\] It is the programmer's responsibility to "
"make sure that the data is valid at the field's type. Failing to do so "
"results in [undefined behavior](../behavior-considered-undefined.md). For "
"example, reading the value `3` from a field of the [boolean type](../types/"
"boolean.md) is undefined behavior. Effectively, writing to and then reading "
"from a union with [the C representation](../type-layout.md#reprc-unions) is "
"analogous to a [`transmute`](std::mem::transmute) from the type used for "
"writing to the type used for reading."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.validity\\] 程序员有责任确保数据对于该字段的类型是有效"
"的。未能做到这一点会导致[未定义行为](../behavior-considered-undefined.md)。例"
"如，从[布尔类型](../types/boolean.md)的字段读取值 `3` 是未定义行为。实际上，"
"对于具有 [C 表示](../type-layout.md#reprc-unions)的联合体，先写入再读取类似于"
"从写入所用类型到读取所用类型的 [`transmute`](std::mem::transmute)。"

#: src/items/unions.md:85
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.read-safety\\] Consequently, all reads of union "
"fields have to be placed in `unsafe` blocks:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.read-safety\\] 因此，所有对联合体字段的读取都必须放在 "
"`unsafe` 块中："

#: src/items/unions.md:97
msgid ""
"Commonly, code using unions will provide safe wrappers around unsafe union "
"field accesses."
msgstr "通常，使用联合体的代码会围绕不安全的联合体字段访问提供安全封装。"

#: src/items/unions.md:99
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.write-safety\\] In contrast, writes to union fields "
"are safe, since they just overwrite arbitrary data, but cannot cause "
"undefined behavior. (Note that union field types can never have drop glue, "
"so a union field write will never implicitly drop anything.)"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.fields.write-safety\\] 相比之下，写入联合体字段是安全的，因为"
"它们只是覆盖任意数据，而不能导致未定义行为。（注意，联合体字段类型永远不会有 "
"drop glue，因此写入联合体字段永远不会隐式丢弃任何东西。）"

#: src/items/unions.md:102
msgid "r\\[items.union.pattern\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.pattern\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:103
msgid "Pattern matching on unions"
msgstr "对联合体进行模式匹配"

#: src/items/unions.md:105
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.pattern.intro\\] Another way to access union fields is to "
"use pattern matching."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.pattern.intro\\] 访问联合体字段的另一种方式是使用模式匹配。"

#: src/items/unions.md:108
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.pattern.one-field\\] Pattern matching on union fields uses "
"the same syntax as struct patterns, except that the pattern must specify "
"exactly one field."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.pattern.one-field\\] 对联合体字段进行模式匹配使用与结构体模式"
"相同的语法，只是该模式必须恰好指定一个字段。"

#: src/items/unions.md:111
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.pattern.safety\\] Since pattern matching is like reading the "
"union with a particular field, it has to be placed in `unsafe` blocks as "
"well."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.pattern.safety\\] 由于模式匹配就像用特定字段读取联合体，因此"
"它也必须放在 `unsafe` 块中。"

#: src/items/unions.md:120 src/patterns.md:886 src/patterns.md:890
msgid "\"ten\""
msgstr "\"ten\""

#: src/items/unions.md:127
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.pattern.subpattern\\] Pattern matching may match a union as "
"a field of a larger structure. In particular, when using a Rust union to "
"implement a C tagged union via FFI, this allows matching on the tag and the "
"corresponding field simultaneously:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.pattern.subpattern\\] 模式匹配可以将联合体作为更大结构的一个"
"字段来匹配。特别是，当通过 FFI 使用 Rust 联合体实现 C 的 tagged union 时，这"
"允许同时匹配标签和相应字段："

#: src/items/unions.md:157
msgid "r\\[items.union.ref\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.union.ref\\]"

#: src/items/unions.md:158
msgid "References to union fields"
msgstr "对联合体字段的引用"

#: src/items/unions.md:160
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.ref.intro\\] Since union fields share common storage, "
"gaining write access to one field of a union can give write access to all "
"its remaining fields."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.ref.intro\\] 由于联合体字段共享同一份存储，获得对联合体某个字"
"段的写访问可能会获得对其所有剩余字段的写访问。"

#: src/items/unions.md:163
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.ref.borrow\\] Borrow checking rules have to be adjusted to "
"account for this fact. As a result, if one field of a union is borrowed, all "
"its remaining fields are borrowed as well for the same lifetime."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.ref.borrow\\] 借用检查规则必须调整以考虑这一事实。因此，如果"
"联合体的一个字段被借用，其所有剩余字段也会在相同生命周期内被借用。"

#: src/items/unions.md:167
msgid ""
"// ERROR: cannot borrow `u` (via `u.f2`) as mutable more than once at a "
"time\n"
msgstr "// ERROR: 不能同时多次将 `u`（通过 `u.f2`）可变借用\n"

#: src/items/unions.md:172
msgid ""
"//                    ---- first mutable borrow occurs here (via `u.f1`)\n"
msgstr "//                    ---- 第一次可变借用在此处发生（通过 `u.f1`）\n"

#: src/items/unions.md:174
msgid ""
"//                    ^^^^ second mutable borrow occurs here (via `u.f2`)\n"
msgstr "//                    ^^^^ 第二次可变借用在此处发生（通过 `u.f2`）\n"

#: src/items/unions.md:177
msgid "//  - first borrow ends here\n"
msgstr "//  - 第一次借用在此处结束\n"

#: src/items/unions.md:183
msgid ""
"r\\[items.union.ref.use\\] As you could see, in many aspects (except for "
"layouts, safety, and ownership) unions behave exactly like structs, largely "
"as a consequence of inheriting their syntactic shape from structs. This is "
"also true for many unmentioned aspects of Rust language (such as privacy, "
"name resolution, type inference, generics, trait implementations, inherent "
"implementations, coherence, pattern checking, etc etc etc)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.union.ref.use\\] 可以看到，在许多方面（除布局、安全性和所有权之"
"外），联合体的行为与结构体完全相同，这很大程度上是因为它们继承了结构体的语法"
"形态。对于 Rust 语言中许多未提及的方面（如私有性、名称解析、类型推断、泛型、"
"trait 实现、固有实现、一致性、模式检查等等）也是如此。"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:1
msgid "r\\[items.const\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.const\\]"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:4
msgid "r\\[items.const.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.const.syntax\\]"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[items.const.intro\\] A _constant item_ is an optionally named _[constant "
"value](../const_eval.md#constant-expressions)_ which is not associated with "
"a specific memory location in the program."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.const.intro\\] *常量项*是一个可以有名称也可以没有名称的 *[常量值]"
"(../const_eval.md#constant-expressions)*，它不与程序中的特定内存位置关联。"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[items.const.behavior\\] Constants are essentially inlined wherever they "
"are used, meaning that they are copied directly into the relevant context "
"when used. This includes use of constants from external crates, and non-"
"[`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy) types. References to the same "
"constant are not necessarily guaranteed to refer to the same memory address."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.const.behavior\\] 常量本质上会在使用处内联，也就是说，使用常量时会"
"将它们直接复制到相关上下文中。这包括来自外部 crate 的常量以及非 [`Copy`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#copy) 类型。对同一常量的引用不一定保证指向同一内"
"存地址。"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[items.const.namespace\\] The constant declaration defines the constant "
"value in the [value namespace](../names/namespaces.md) of the module or "
"block where it is located."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.const.namespace\\] 常量声明会在其所在模块或块的[值命名空间](../"
"names/namespaces.md)中定义该常量值。"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:19
msgid ""
"r\\[items.const.static\\] Constants must be explicitly typed. The type must "
"have a `'static` lifetime: any references in the initializer must have "
"`'static` lifetimes. References in the type of a constant default to "
"`'static` lifetime; see [static lifetime elision](../lifetime-"
"elision.md#const-and-static-elision)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.const.static\\] 常量必须显式标注类型。其类型必须具有 `'static` 生命"
"周期：初始化式中的任何引用都必须具有 `'static` 生命周期。常量类型中的引用默认"
"采用 `'static` 生命周期；参见[static 生命周期省略](../lifetime-"
"elision.md#const-and-static-elision)。"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:22
msgid ""
"r\\[items.const.static-temporary\\] A reference to a constant will have "
"`'static` lifetime if the constant value is eligible for [promotion]"
"(destructors.scope.const-promotion); otherwise, a temporary will be created."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.const.static-temporary\\] 如果常量值符合[提升]"
"(destructors.scope.const-promotion)条件，对该常量的引用将具有 `'static` 生命"
"周期；否则，将创建一个临时值。"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:30 src/lifetime-elision.md:176
msgid "\"bitstring\""
msgstr "\"bitstring\""

#: src/items/constant-items.md:43
msgid ""
"r\\[items.const.expr-omission\\] The constant expression may only be omitted "
"in a [trait definition](traits.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.const.expr-omission\\] 只有在 [trait 定义](traits.md) 中才可以省略"
"常量表达式。"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:46
msgid "r\\[items.const.destructor\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.const.destructor\\]"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:47
msgid "Constants with destructors"
msgstr "带析构器的常量"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:49
msgid ""
"Constants can contain destructors. Destructors are run when the value goes "
"out of scope."
msgstr "常量可以包含析构器。当值离开作用域时会运行析构器。"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:56
msgid "\"Dropped. Held {}.\""
msgstr "\"Dropped. Held {}.\""

#: src/items/constant-items.md:64
msgid ""
"// x gets dropped at end of function, calling drop.\n"
"    // prints \"Dropped. Held 0.\".\n"
msgstr ""
"// x 在函数结束时被丢弃，调用 drop。\n"
"    // 打印 \"Dropped. Held 0.\"。\n"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:69
msgid "r\\[items.const.unnamed\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.const.unnamed\\]"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:70
msgid "Unnamed constant"
msgstr "未命名常量"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:72
msgid ""
"r\\[items.const.unnamed.intro\\] Unlike an [associated constant](../items/"
"associated-items.md#associated-constants), a [free](../glossary.md#free-"
"item) constant may be unnamed by using an underscore instead of the name. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.const.unnamed.intro\\] 与[关联常量](../items/associated-"
"items.md#associated-constants)不同，[自由](../glossary.md#free-item)常量可以"
"通过使用下划线代替名称而成为未命名常量。例如："

#: src/items/constant-items.md:77
msgid "// OK although it is the same name as above:\n"
msgstr "// OK，虽然它与上面的名称相同：\n"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:82
msgid ""
"r\\[items.const.unnamed.repetition\\] As with [underscore imports](use-"
"declarations.md#underscore-imports), macros may safely emit the same unnamed "
"constant in the same scope more than once. For example, the following should "
"not produce an error:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.const.unnamed.repetition\\] 与[下划线导入](use-"
"declarations.md#underscore-imports)一样，宏可以在同一作用域中安全地多次发出相"
"同的未命名常量。例如，以下代码不应产生错误："

#: src/items/constant-items.md:90
msgid ""
"// This expands to:\n"
"// const _: () = ();\n"
"// const _: () = ();\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会展开为：\n"
"// const _: () = ();\n"
"// const _: () = ();\n"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:96
msgid "r\\[items.const.eval\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.const.eval\\]"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:97
msgid "Evaluation"
msgstr "求值"

#: src/items/constant-items.md:99
msgid ""
"[Free](../glossary.md#free-item) constants are always [evaluated](../"
"const_eval.md) at compile-time to surface panics. This happens even within "
"an unused function:"
msgstr ""
"[自由](../glossary.md#free-item)常量总是在编译时[求值](../const_eval.md)以暴"
"露 panic。即使位于未使用的函数中也是如此："

#: src/items/constant-items.md:102
