msgstr "// 错误：未使用的参数\n"

#: src/items/generics.md:210
msgid ""
"r\\[items.generics.const.exhaustiveness\\] When resolving a trait bound "
"obligation, the exhaustiveness of all implementations of const parameters is "
"not considered when determining if the bound is satisfied. For example, in "
"the following, even though all possible const values for the `bool` type are "
"implemented, it is still an error that the trait bound is not satisfied:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.generics.const.exhaustiveness\\] 解析 trait 约束义务时，在判断约束"
"是否满足时，不会考虑 const 参数的所有实现是否穷尽。例如，在下面示例中，即使 "
"`bool` 类型的所有可能 const 值都已实现，trait 约束不满足仍然是错误："

#: src/items/generics.md:222
msgid "// ERROR: trait bound `Foo<B>: Bar` is not satisfied\n"
msgstr "// 错误：trait 约束 `Foo<B>: Bar` 不满足\n"

#: src/items/generics.md:226
msgid "r\\[items.generics.where\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.generics.where\\]"

#: src/items/generics.md:227
msgid "Where clauses"
msgstr "where 子句"

#: src/items/generics.md:229
msgid "r\\[items.generics.where.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.generics.where.syntax\\]"

#: src/items/generics.md:242
msgid ""
"r\\[items.generics.where.intro\\] _Where clauses_ provide another way to "
"specify bounds on type and lifetime parameters as well as a way to specify "
"bounds on types that aren't type parameters."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.generics.where.intro\\] *where 子句*提供了另一种为类型和生命周期参"
"数指定约束的方式，也提供了一种为不是类型参数的类型指定约束的方式。"

#: src/items/generics.md:245
msgid ""
"r\\[items.generics.where.higher-ranked-lifetimes\\] The `for` keyword can be "
"used to introduce [higher-ranked lifetimes](../trait-bounds.md#higher-ranked-"
"trait-bounds). It only allows \\[LifetimeParam\\] parameters."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.generics.where.higher-ranked-lifetimes\\] `for` 关键字可用于引入[高"
"阶生命周期](../trait-bounds.md#r-bound.higher-ranked)。它只允许 \\"
"[LifetimeParam\\] 参数。"

#: src/items/generics.md:251
msgid "// Could use A<T: Iterator> instead\n"
msgstr "// 也可以改用 A<T: Iterator>\n"

#: src/items/generics.md:252
msgid "// Bound on an associated type\n"
msgstr "// 关联类型上的约束\n"

#: src/items/generics.md:253
msgid "// Bound on `String`, using the type parameter\n"
msgstr "// `String` 上的约束，使用类型参数\n"

#: src/items/generics.md:254 src/trait-bounds.md:85
msgid "// Allowed, but not useful\n"
msgstr "// 允许，但没有用处\n"

#: src/items/generics.md:260
msgid "r\\[items.generics.attributes\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.generics.attributes\\]"

#: src/items/generics.md:263
msgid ""
"Generic lifetime and type parameters allow [attributes](../attributes.md) on "
"them. There are no built-in attributes that do anything in this position, "
"although custom derive attributes may give meaning to it."
msgstr ""
"泛型生命周期参数和类型参数允许带有[属性](../attributes.md)。没有内建属性会在"
"此位置产生任何作用，不过自定义 derive 属性可以为其赋予意义。"

#: src/items/generics.md:265
msgid ""
"This example shows using a custom derive attribute to modify the meaning of "
"a generic parameter."
msgstr "此示例展示如何使用自定义 derive 属性修改泛型参数的含义。"

#: src/items/generics.md:269
msgid ""
"// Assume that the derive for MyFlexibleClone declared `my_flexible_clone` "
"as\n"
"// an attribute it understands.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 假设 MyFlexibleClone 的 derive 将 `my_flexible_clone` 声明为\n"
"// 它所理解的属性。\n"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:1
msgid "r\\[items.associated\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.associated\\]"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:4
msgid "r\\[items.associated.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.associated.syntax\\]"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.intro\\] _Associated Items_ are the items declared in "
"[traits](traits.md) or defined in [implementations](implementations.md). "
"They are called this because they are defined on an associate type — the "
"type in the implementation."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.intro\\] *关联项* 是在 [trait](traits.md) 中声明或在[实"
"现](implementations.md)中定义的项。之所以这样称呼，是因为它们定义在一个所关联"
"的类型上，即该实现中的类型。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.kinds\\] They are a subset of the kinds of items you "
"can declare in a module. Specifically, there are [associated functions]"
"(#associated-functions-and-methods) (including methods), [associated types]"
"(#associated-types), and [associated constants](#associated-constants)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.kinds\\] 它们是可以在模块中声明的项种类的一个子集。具体"
"来说，有[关联函数](#associated-functions-and-methods)（包括方法）、[关联类型]"
"(#associated-types)和[关联常量](#associated-constants)。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:23
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.related\\] Associated items are useful when the "
"associated item is logically related to the associating item. For example, "
"the `is_some` method on `Option` is intrinsically related to Options, so "
"should be associated."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.related\\] 当关联项在逻辑上与其所关联的项相关时，关联项"
"很有用。例如，`Option` 上的 `is_some` 方法与 Option 有内在关联，因此应该作为"
"关联项。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:26
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.decl-def\\] Every associated item kind comes in two "
"varieties: definitions that contain the actual implementation and "
"declarations that declare signatures for definitions."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.decl-def\\] 每种关联项都有两种形式：包含实际实现的定义，"
"以及为定义声明签名的声明。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:29
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.trait-items\\] It is the declarations that make up the "
"contract of traits and what is available on generic types."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.trait-items\\] 这些声明构成了 trait 的契约，以及泛型类型"
"上可用的内容。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:32
msgid "r\\[items.associated.fn\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.associated.fn\\]"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:33
msgid "Associated functions and methods"
msgstr "关联函数和方法"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:35
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.intro\\] _Associated functions_ are [functions]"
"(functions.md) associated with a type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.intro\\] *关联函数* 是与某个类型关联的[函数]"
"(functions.md)。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:38
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.decl\\] An _associated function declaration_ "
"declares a signature for an associated function definition. It is written as "
"a function item, except the function body is replaced with a `;`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.decl\\] *关联函数声明* 为关联函数定义声明签名。它的写"
"法与函数项相同，只是函数体替换为 `;`。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:41
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.name\\] The identifier is the name of the function."
msgstr "r\\[items.associated.name\\] 该标识符是函数的名称。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:44
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.same-signature\\] The generics, parameter list, return "
"type, and where clause of the associated function must be the same as the "
"associated function declarations's."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.same-signature\\] 关联函数的泛型、参数列表、返回类型和 "
"where 子句必须与关联函数声明中的对应部分相同。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:47
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.def\\] An _associated function definition_ defines a "
"function associated with another type. It is written the same as a [function "
"item](../types/function-item.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.def\\] *关联函数定义* 定义一个与另一类型关联的函数。"
"它的写法与[函数项](../types/function-item.md)相同。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:50
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] A common example is an associated function named `new` that "
"returns a value of the type with which it is associated."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 一个常见示例是名为 `new` 的关联函数，它返回与其关联的类型的值。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:71
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.qualified-self\\] When the associated function is "
"declared on a trait, the function can also be called with a [path](../"
"paths.md) that is a path to the trait appended by the name of the trait. "
"When this happens, it is substituted for `<_ as Trait>::function_name`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.qualified-self\\] 当关联函数在 trait 上声明时，也可以"
"用一个[路径](../paths.md)来调用该函数，该路径是在指向该 trait 的路径后附加该 "
"trait 的名称。发生这种情况时，它会被替换为 `<_ as Trait>::function_name`。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:82
msgid "// These 4 are all equivalent in this case.\n"
msgstr "// 在这个情况下，这 4 种写法都是等价的。\n"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:90
msgid "r\\[items.associated.fn.method\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.associated.fn.method\\]"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:91
msgid "Methods"
msgstr "方法"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:93
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.method.intro\\] Associated functions whose first "
"parameter is named `self` are called _methods_ and may be invoked using the "
"[method call operator](../expressions/method-call-expr.md), for example, "
"`x.foo()`, as well as the usual function call notation."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.method.intro\\] 第一个参数名为 `self` 的关联函数称为 "
"*方法*，可以使用[方法调用运算符](../expressions/method-call-expr.md)来调用，"
"例如 `x.foo()`；也可以使用通常的函数调用记法。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:96
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.method.self-ty\\] If the type of the `self` "
"parameter is specified, it is limited to types resolving to one generated by "
"the following grammar (where `'lt` denotes some arbitrary lifetime):"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.fn.method.self-ty\\] 如果指定了 `self` 参数的类型，则该"
"类型限于能解析为由以下语法生成的某种类型（其中 `'lt` 表示某个任意生命周期）："

#: src/items/associated-items.md:104
msgid ""
"The `Self` terminal in this grammar denotes a type resolving to the "
"implementing type. This can also include the contextual type alias `Self`, "
"other type aliases, or associated type projections resolving to the "
"implementing type."
msgstr ""
"此语法中的 `Self` 终结符表示解析为实现类型的类型。这也可以包括上下文类型别名 "
"`Self`、其他类型别名，或解析为实现类型的关联类型投影。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:109
msgid "// Examples of methods implemented on struct `Example`.\n"
msgstr "// 在结构体 `Example` 上实现的方法示例。\n"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:130
msgid ""
"r\\[associated.fn.method.self-pat-shorthands\\] Shorthand syntax can be used "
"without specifying a type, which have the following equivalents:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[associated.fn.method.self-pat-shorthands\\] 可以使用不指定类型的简写语"
"法，其等价形式如下："

#: src/items/associated-items.md:133
msgid "Shorthand"
msgstr "简写"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:133
msgid "Equivalent"
msgstr "等价形式"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:135
msgid "`self: Self`"
msgstr "`self: Self`"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:136
msgid "`&'lifetime self`"
msgstr "`&'lifetime self`"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:136
msgid "`self: &'lifetime Self`"
msgstr "`self: &'lifetime Self`"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:137
msgid "`&'lifetime mut self`"
msgstr "`&'lifetime mut self`"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:137
msgid "`self: &'lifetime mut Self`"
msgstr "`self: &'lifetime mut Self`"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:139
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Lifetimes can be, and usually are, elided with this shorthand."
msgstr "\\[!NOTE\\] 使用这种简写时，生命周期可以省略，而且通常会省略。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:142
msgid ""
"r\\[associated.fn.method.self-pat-mut\\] If the `self` parameter is prefixed "
"with `mut`, it becomes a mutable variable, similar to regular parameters "
"using a `mut` [identifier pattern](../patterns.md#identifier-patterns). For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[associated.fn.method.self-pat-mut\\] 如果 `self` 参数带有 `mut` 前缀，它"
"就会成为可变变量，类似于使用 `mut` [标识符模式](../patterns.md#identifier-"
"patterns)的常规参数。例如："

#: src/items/associated-items.md:152
msgid "As an example of methods on a trait, consider the following:"
msgstr "作为 trait 上方法的示例，请考虑以下代码："

#: src/items/associated-items.md:163
msgid ""
"This defines a trait with two methods. All values that have [implementations]"
"(implementations.md) of this trait while the trait is in scope can have "
"their `draw` and `bounding_box` methods called."
msgstr ""
"这定义了一个带有两个方法的 trait。当该 trait 在作用域内时，所有具有此 trait "
"[实现](implementations.md)的值都可以调用其 `draw` 和 `bounding_box` 方法。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:191
msgid "r\\[items.associated.fn.params.edition2018\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.associated.fn.params.edition2018\\]"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:192
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] In the 2015 edition, it is possible to declare trait "
"methods with anonymous parameters (e.g. `fn foo(u8)`). This is deprecated "
"and an error as of the 2018 edition. All parameters must have an argument "
"name."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] 在 2015 edition 中，可以使用匿名参数声明 trait 方法（例"
"如 `fn foo(u8)`）。这已被弃用，并且从 2018 edition 起是错误。所有参数都必须具"
"有参数名。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:195
msgid "r\\[items.associated.fn.param-attributes\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.associated.fn.param-attributes\\]"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:196
msgid "Attributes on method parameters"
msgstr "方法参数上的属性"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:198
msgid ""
"Attributes on method parameters follow the same rules and restrictions as "
"[regular function parameters](functions.md#attributes-on-function-"
"parameters)."
msgstr ""
"方法参数上的属性遵循与[常规函数参数](functions.md#attributes-on-function-"
"parameters)相同的规则和限制。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:200
msgid "r\\[items.associated.type\\]"
msgstr "r\\[items.associated.type\\]"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:201
msgid "Associated types"
msgstr "关联类型"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:203
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.intro\\] _Associated types_ are [type aliases]"
"(type-aliases.md) associated with another type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.intro\\] *关联类型* 是与另一类型关联的[类型别名]"
"(type-aliases.md)。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:206
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.restrictions\\] Associated types cannot be defined "
"in [inherent implementations](implementations.md#inherent-implementations) "
"nor can they be given a default implementation in traits."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.restrictions\\] 关联类型不能在[固有实现]"
"(implementations.md#inherent-implementations)中定义，也不能在 trait 中给出默"
"认实现。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:209
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.decl\\] An _associated type declaration_ declares "
"a signature for associated type definitions. It is written in one of the "
"following forms, where `Assoc` is the name of the associated type, `Params` "
"is a comma-separated list of type, lifetime or const parameters, `Bounds` is "
"a plus-separated list of trait bounds that the associated type must meet, "
"and `WhereBounds` is a comma-separated list of bounds that the parameters "
"must meet:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.decl\\] *关联类型声明* 为关联类型定义声明签名。它写"
"成以下形式之一，其中 `Assoc` 是关联类型的名称，`Params` 是以逗号分隔的类型、"
"生命周期或 const 参数列表，`Bounds` 是以加号分隔的、关联类型必须满足的 trait "
"约束列表，`WhereBounds` 是以逗号分隔的、参数必须满足的约束列表："

#: src/items/associated-items.md:222
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.name\\] The identifier is the name of the declared "
"type alias."
msgstr "r\\[items.associated.type.name\\] 该标识符是所声明类型别名的名称。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:225
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.impl-fulfillment\\] The optional trait bounds must "
"be fulfilled by the implementations of the type alias."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.impl-fulfillment\\] 可选的 trait 约束必须由该类型别"
"名的实现满足。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:228
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.sized\\] There is an implicit [`Sized`](../special-"
"types-and-traits.md#sized) bound on associated types that can be relaxed "
"using the special `?Sized` bound."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.sized\\] 关联类型上有一个隐式的 [`Sized`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#sized) 约束，可以使用特殊的 `?Sized` 约束放宽它。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:231
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.def\\] An _associated type definition_ defines a "
"type alias for the implementation of a trait on a type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.def\\] *关联类型定义* 为某个类型上的 trait 实现定义"
"类型别名。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:234
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.def.restriction\\] They are written similarly to "
"an _associated type declaration_, but cannot contain `Bounds`, but instead "
"must contain a `Type`:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.def.restriction\\] 它们的写法类似于 *关联类型声明"
"*，但不能包含 `Bounds`，而是必须包含 `Type`："

#: src/items/associated-items.md:240
msgid "// the type `Type` here may reference `Params`\n"
msgstr "// 这里的类型 `Type` 可以引用 `Params`\n"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:242
msgid "// deprecated, prefer the form above\n"
msgstr "// 已弃用，优先使用上面的形式\n"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:245
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.alias\\] If a type `Item` has an associated type "
"`Assoc` from a trait `Trait`, then `<Item as Trait>::Assoc` is a type that "
"is an alias of the type specified in the associated type definition."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.alias\\] 如果类型 `Item` 拥有来自 trait `Trait` 的"
"关联类型 `Assoc`，那么 `<Item as Trait>::Assoc` 就是一个类型，它是关联类型定"
"义中指定类型的别名。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:248
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.param\\] Furthermore, if `Item` is a type "
"parameter, then `Item::Assoc` can be used in type parameters."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.param\\] 此外，如果 `Item` 是类型参数，那么 "
"`Item::Assoc` 可以用于类型参数中。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:251
msgid ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.generic\\] Associated types may include [generic "
"parameters](generics.md) and [where clauses](generics.md#where-clauses); "
"these are often referred to as _generic associated types_, or _GATs_. If the "
"type `Thing` has an associated type `Item` from a trait `Trait` with the "
"generics `<'a>` , the type can be named like `<Thing as Trait>::Item<'x>`, "
"where `'x` is some lifetime in scope. In this case, `'x` will be used "
"wherever `'a` appears in the associated type definitions on impls."
msgstr ""
"r\\[items.associated.type.generic\\] 关联类型可以包含[泛型参数](generics.md)"
"和 [where 子句](generics.md#where-clauses)；这些通常称为 *泛型关联类型*，或 "
"_GAT_。如果类型 `Thing` 拥有来自 trait `Trait`、带有泛型 `<'a>` 的关联类型 "
"`Item`，则该类型可以命名为类似 `<Thing as Trait>::Item<'x>` 的形式，其中 "
"`'x` 是作用域内的某个生命周期。在这种情况下，impl 上的关联类型定义中凡是出现 "
"`'a` 的位置都会使用 `'x`。"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:256
msgid "// Associated type declaration\n"
msgstr "// 关联类型声明\n"

#: src/items/associated-items.md:265
msgid "// Associated type definition\n"
msgstr "// 关联类型定义\n"

