msgstr "`link(name = \"CoreFoundation\", kind = \"framework\")`"

#: src/attributes.md:173
msgid "r\\[attributes.activity\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.activity\\]"

#: src/attributes.md:174
msgid "Active and inert attributes"
msgstr "活跃属性和惰性属性"

#: src/attributes.md:176
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.activity.intro\\] An attribute is either active or inert. "
"During attribute processing, _active attributes_ remove themselves from the "
"form they are on while _inert attributes_ stay on."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.activity.intro\\] 属性要么是活跃的，要么是惰性的。在属性处理过"
"程中，*活跃属性*会从其所在的形式上移除自身，而 *惰性属性*会保留下来。"

#: src/attributes.md:179
msgid ""
"The [`cfg`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg-attribute) and [`cfg_attr`]"
"(conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg_attr-attribute) attributes are active. "
"[Attribute macros](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro_attribute-attribute) "
"are active. All other attributes are inert."
msgstr ""
"[`cfg`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg-attribute) 和 [`cfg_attr`]"
"(conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg_attr-attribute) 属性是活跃的。[属性宏]"
"(procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro_attribute-attribute)是活跃的。所有其他属"
"性都是惰性的。"

#: src/attributes.md:181
msgid "r\\[attributes.tool\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.tool\\]"

#: src/attributes.md:182
msgid "Tool attributes"
msgstr "工具属性"

#: src/attributes.md:184
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.tool.intro\\] The compiler may allow attributes for external "
"tools where each tool resides in its own module in the [tool prelude](names/"
"preludes.md#tool-prelude). The first segment of the attribute path is the "
"name of the tool, with one or more additional segments whose interpretation "
"is up to the tool."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.tool.intro\\] 编译器可以允许外部工具使用属性，其中每个工具都位"
"于 [tool prelude](names/preludes.md#tool-prelude) 中自己的模块内。属性路径的"
"第一个段是工具名称，后面可以有一个或多个附加段，其解释由工具决定。"

#: src/attributes.md:187
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.tool.ignored\\] When a tool is not in use, the tool's "
"attributes are accepted without a warning. When the tool is in use, the tool "
"is responsible for processing and interpretation of its attributes."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.tool.ignored\\] 未使用某个工具时，该工具的属性会被接受且不发出"
"警告。使用该工具时，该工具负责处理和解释它的属性。"

#: src/attributes.md:190
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.tool.prelude\\] Tool attributes are not available if the "
"[`no_implicit_prelude`](names/preludes.md#the-no_implicit_prelude-attribute) "
"attribute is used."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.tool.prelude\\] 如果使用了 [`no_implicit_prelude`](names/"
"preludes.md#the-no_implicit_prelude-attribute) 属性，则工具属性不可用。"

#: src/attributes.md:194
msgid "// Tells the rustfmt tool to not format the following element.\n"
msgstr "// 告诉 rustfmt 工具不要格式化以下元素。\n"

#: src/attributes.md:198
msgid ""
"// Controls the \"cyclomatic complexity\" threshold for the clippy tool.\n"
msgstr "// 控制 clippy 工具的“圈复杂度”阈值。\n"

#: src/attributes.md:200
msgid "\"100\""
msgstr "\"100\""

#: src/attributes.md:204
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` currently recognizes the tools \"clippy\", \"rustfmt\", "
"\"diagnostic\", \"miri\", and \"rust_analyzer\"."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 目前识别工具 \"clippy\"、\"rustfmt\"、\"diagnostic\"、"
"\"miri\" 和 \"rust_analyzer\"。"

#: src/attributes.md:207
msgid "r\\[attributes.builtin\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.builtin\\]"

#: src/attributes.md:208
msgid "Built-in attributes index"
msgstr "内置属性索引"

#: src/attributes.md:210
msgid "The following is an index of all built-in attributes."
msgstr "以下是所有内置属性的索引。"

#: src/attributes.md:213
msgid ""
"[`cfg`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg-attribute) --- Controls "
"conditional compilation."
msgstr ""
"[`cfg`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg-attribute) --- 控制条件编译。"

#: src/attributes.md:214
msgid ""
"[`cfg_attr`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg_attr-attribute) --- "
"Conditionally includes attributes."
msgstr ""
"[`cfg_attr`](conditional-compilation.md#the-cfg_attr-attribute) --- 有条件地"
"包含属性。"

#: src/attributes.md:217
msgid ""
"[`test`](attributes/testing.md#the-test-attribute) --- Marks a function as a "
"test."
msgstr ""
"[`test`](attributes/testing.md#the-test-attribute) --- 将函数标记为测试。"

#: src/attributes.md:218
msgid ""
"[`ignore`](attributes/testing.md#the-ignore-attribute) --- Disables a test "
"function."
msgstr ""
"[`ignore`](attributes/testing.md#the-ignore-attribute) --- 禁用测试函数。"

#: src/attributes.md:219
msgid ""
"[`should_panic`](attributes/testing.md#the-should_panic-attribute) --- "
"Indicates a test should generate a panic."
msgstr ""
"[`should_panic`](attributes/testing.md#the-should_panic-attribute) --- 指示测"
"试应产生 panic。"

#: src/attributes.md:222
msgid "[`derive`](attributes/derive.md) --- Automatic trait implementations."
msgstr "[`derive`](attributes/derive.md) --- 自动实现 trait。"

#: src/attributes.md:223
msgid ""
"[`automatically_derived`](attributes/derive.md#the-automatically_derived-"
"attribute) --- Marker for implementations created by `derive`."
msgstr ""
"[`automatically_derived`](attributes/derive.md#the-automatically_derived-"
"attribute) --- 由 `derive` 创建的实现的标记。"

#: src/attributes.md:226
msgid ""
"[`macro_export`](macros-by-example.md#the-macro_export-attribute) --- "
"Exports a `macro_rules` macro for cross-crate use."
msgstr ""
"[`macro_export`](macros-by-example.md#the-macro_export-attribute) --- 导出 "
"`macro_rules` 宏，以供跨 crate 使用。"

#: src/attributes.md:227
msgid ""
"[`macro_use`](macros-by-example.md#the-macro_use-attribute) --- Expands "
"macro visibility, or imports macros from other crates."
msgstr ""
"[`macro_use`](macros-by-example.md#the-macro_use-attribute) --- 扩展宏可见"
"性，或从其他 crate 导入宏。"

#: src/attributes.md:228
msgid ""
"[`proc_macro`](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro-attribute) --- Defines a "
"function-like macro."
msgstr ""
"[`proc_macro`](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro-attribute) --- 定义类函数"
"宏。"

#: src/attributes.md:229
msgid "[`proc_macro_derive`](macro.proc.derive) --- Defines a derive macro."
msgstr "[`proc_macro_derive`](macro.proc.derive) --- 定义派生宏。"

#: src/attributes.md:230
msgid ""
"[`proc_macro_attribute`](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro_attribute-"
"attribute) --- Defines an attribute macro."
msgstr ""
"[`proc_macro_attribute`](procedural-macros.md#the-proc_macro_attribute-"
"attribute) --- 定义属性宏。"

#: src/attributes.md:233
msgid ""
"[`allow`](attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`expect`]"
"(attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`warn`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`deny`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`forbid`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes) --- Alters the default lint level."
msgstr ""
"[`allow`](attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`expect`]"
"(attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`warn`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`deny`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes), [`forbid`](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes) --- 更改默认 lint 级别。"

#: src/attributes.md:234
msgid ""
"[`deprecated`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-deprecated-attribute) --- "
"Generates deprecation notices."
msgstr ""
"[`deprecated`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-deprecated-attribute) --- 生成弃"
"用通知。"

#: src/attributes.md:235
msgid ""
"[`must_use`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-must_use-attribute) --- Generates "
"a lint for unused values."
msgstr ""
"[`must_use`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-must_use-attribute) --- 为未使用的"
"值生成 lint。"

#: src/attributes.md:236
msgid ""
"[`diagnostic::on_unimplemented`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-"
"diagnosticon_unimplemented-attribute) --- Hints the compiler to emit a "
"certain error message if a trait is not implemented."
msgstr ""
"[`diagnostic::on_unimplemented`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-"
"diagnosticon_unimplemented-attribute) --- 如果某个 trait 未实现，则提示编译器"
"发出特定错误消息。"

#: src/attributes.md:237
msgid ""
"[`diagnostic::do_not_recommend`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-"
"diagnosticdo_not_recommend-attribute) --- Hints the compiler to not show a "
"certain trait impl in error messages."
msgstr ""
"[`diagnostic::do_not_recommend`](attributes/diagnostics.md#the-"
"diagnosticdo_not_recommend-attribute) --- 提示编译器不要在错误消息中显示某个 "
"trait impl。"

#: src/attributes.md:239
msgid "ABI, linking, symbols, and FFI"
msgstr "ABI、链接、符号和 FFI"

#: src/attributes.md:240
msgid ""
"[`link`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link-attribute) --- Specifies a native "
"library to link with an `extern` block."
msgstr ""
"[`link`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link-attribute) --- 指定要与 `extern` "
"块链接的原生库。"

#: src/attributes.md:241
msgid ""
"[`link_name`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link_name-attribute) --- "
"Specifies the name of the symbol for functions or statics in an `extern` "
"block."
msgstr ""
"[`link_name`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link_name-attribute) --- 指定 "
"`extern` 块中函数或静态项的符号名称。"

#: src/attributes.md:242
msgid ""
"[`link_ordinal`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link_ordinal-attribute) --- "
"Specifies the ordinal of the symbol for functions or statics in an `extern` "
"block."
msgstr ""
"[`link_ordinal`](items/external-blocks.md#the-link_ordinal-attribute) --- 指"
"定 `extern` 块中函数或静态项的符号序号。"

#: src/attributes.md:243
msgid ""
"[`no_link`](items/extern-crates.md#the-no_link-attribute) --- Prevents "
"linking an extern crate."
msgstr ""
"[`no_link`](items/extern-crates.md#the-no_link-attribute) --- 阻止链接 "
"extern crate。"

#: src/attributes.md:244
msgid "[`repr`](type-layout.md#representations) --- Controls type layout."
msgstr "[`repr`](type-layout.md#representations) --- 控制类型布局。"

#: src/attributes.md:245
msgid ""
"[`crate_type`](linkage.md) --- Specifies the type of crate (library, "
"executable, etc.)."
msgstr "[`crate_type`](linkage.md) --- 指定 crate 的类型（库、可执行文件等）。"

#: src/attributes.md:246
msgid ""
"[`no_main`](crates-and-source-files.md#the-no_main-attribute) --- Disables "
"emitting the `main` symbol."
msgstr ""
"[`no_main`](crates-and-source-files.md#the-no_main-attribute) --- 禁用发出 "
"`main` 符号。"

#: src/attributes.md:247
msgid ""
"[`export_name`](abi.md#the-export_name-attribute) --- Specifies the exported "
"symbol name for a function or static."
msgstr ""
"[`export_name`](abi.md#the-export_name-attribute) --- 指定函数或静态项的导出"
"符号名称。"

#: src/attributes.md:248
msgid ""
"[`link_section`](abi.md#the-link_section-attribute) --- Specifies the "
"section of an object file to use for a function or static."
msgstr ""
"[`link_section`](abi.md#the-link_section-attribute) --- 指定函数或静态项要使"
"用的目标文件节。"

#: src/attributes.md:249
msgid ""
"[`no_mangle`](abi.md#the-no_mangle-attribute) --- Disables symbol name "
"encoding."
msgstr "[`no_mangle`](abi.md#the-no_mangle-attribute) --- 禁用符号名称编码。"

#: src/attributes.md:250
msgid ""
"[`used`](abi.md#the-used-attribute) --- Forces the compiler to keep a static "
"item in the output object file."
msgstr ""
"[`used`](abi.md#the-used-attribute) --- 强制编译器在输出目标文件中保留静态"
"项。"

#: src/attributes.md:251
msgid ""
"[`crate_name`](crates-and-source-files.md#the-crate_name-attribute) --- "
"Specifies the crate name."
msgstr ""
"[`crate_name`](crates-and-source-files.md#the-crate_name-attribute) --- 指定 "
"crate 名称。"

#: src/attributes.md:254
msgid ""
"[`inline`](attributes/codegen.md#the-inline-attribute) --- Hint to inline "
"code."
msgstr ""
"[`inline`](attributes/codegen.md#the-inline-attribute) --- 提示内联代码。"

#: src/attributes.md:255
msgid ""
"[`cold`](attributes/codegen.md#the-cold-attribute) --- Hint that a function "
"is unlikely to be called."
msgstr ""
"[`cold`](attributes/codegen.md#the-cold-attribute) --- 提示某函数不太可能被调"
"用。"

#: src/attributes.md:256
msgid ""
"[`naked`](attributes/codegen.md#the-naked-attribute) --- Prevent the "
"compiler from emitting a function prologue and epilogue."
msgstr ""
"[`naked`](attributes/codegen.md#the-naked-attribute) --- 防止编译器发出函数序"
"言和尾声。"

#: src/attributes.md:257
msgid ""
"[`no_builtins`](attributes/codegen.md#the-no_builtins-attribute) --- "
"Disables use of certain built-in functions."
msgstr ""
"[`no_builtins`](attributes/codegen.md#the-no_builtins-attribute) --- 禁用某些"
"内置函数的使用。"

#: src/attributes.md:258
msgid ""
"[`target_feature`](attributes/codegen.md#the-target_feature-attribute) --- "
"Configure platform-specific code generation."
msgstr ""
"[`target_feature`](attributes/codegen.md#the-target_feature-attribute) --- 配"
"置平台特定的代码生成。"

#: src/attributes.md:259
msgid ""
"[`track_caller`](attributes/codegen.md#the-track_caller-attribute) --- Pass "
"the parent call location to `std::panic::Location::caller()`."
msgstr ""
"[`track_caller`](attributes/codegen.md#the-track_caller-attribute) --- 将父级"
"调用位置传递给 `std::panic::Location::caller()`。"

#: src/attributes.md:260
msgid ""
"[`instruction_set`](attributes/codegen.md#the-instruction_set-attribute) --- "
"Specify the instruction set used to generate a function's code."
msgstr ""
"[`instruction_set`](attributes/codegen.md#the-instruction_set-attribute) --- "
"指定用于生成函数代码的指令集。"

#: src/attributes.md:262
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "文档"

#: src/attributes.md:263
msgid ""
"`doc` --- Specifies documentation. See [The Rustdoc Book](../rustdoc/the-doc-"
"attribute.html) for more information. [Doc comments](comments.md#doc-"
"comments) are transformed into `doc` attributes."
msgstr ""
"`doc` --- 指定文档。更多信息见 [The Rustdoc Book](../rustdoc/the-doc-"
"attribute.html)。[文档注释](comments.md#doc-comments)会转换为 `doc` 属性。"

#: src/attributes.md:266
msgid ""
"[`no_std`](names/preludes.md#the-no_std-attribute) --- Removes std from the "
"prelude."
msgstr ""
"[`no_std`](names/preludes.md#the-no_std-attribute) --- 从 prelude 中移除 "
"std。"

#: src/attributes.md:267
msgid ""
"[`no_implicit_prelude`](names/preludes.md#the-no_implicit_prelude-attribute) "
"--- Disables prelude lookups within a module."
msgstr ""
"[`no_implicit_prelude`](names/preludes.md#the-no_implicit_prelude-attribute) "
"--- 禁用模块内的 prelude 查找。"

#: src/attributes.md:270
msgid ""
"[`path`](items/modules.md#the-path-attribute) --- Specifies the filename for "
"a module."
msgstr "[`path`](items/modules.md#the-path-attribute) --- 指定模块的文件名。"

#: src/attributes.md:273
msgid ""
"[`recursion_limit`](attributes/limits.md#the-recursion_limit-attribute) --- "
"Sets the maximum recursion limit for certain compile-time operations."
msgstr ""
"[`recursion_limit`](attributes/limits.md#the-recursion_limit-attribute) --- "
"设置某些编译期操作的最大递归限制。"

#: src/attributes.md:274
msgid ""
"[`type_length_limit`](attributes/limits.md#the-type_length_limit-attribute) "
"--- Sets the maximum size of a polymorphic type."
msgstr ""
"[`type_length_limit`](attributes/limits.md#the-type_length_limit-attribute) "
"--- 设置多态类型的最大大小。"

#: src/attributes.md:276
msgid "Runtime"
msgstr "运行时"

#: src/attributes.md:277
msgid ""
"[`panic_handler`](panic.md#the-panic_handler-attribute) --- Sets the "
"function to handle panics."
msgstr ""
"[`panic_handler`](panic.md#the-panic_handler-attribute) --- 设置用于处理 "
"panic 的函数。"

#: src/attributes.md:278
msgid ""
"[`global_allocator`](runtime.md#the-global_allocator-attribute) --- Sets the "
"global memory allocator."
msgstr ""
"[`global_allocator`](runtime.md#the-global_allocator-attribute) --- 设置全局"
"内存分配器。"

#: src/attributes.md:279
msgid ""
"[`windows_subsystem`](runtime.md#the-windows_subsystem-attribute) --- "
"Specifies the windows subsystem to link with."
msgstr ""
"[`windows_subsystem`](runtime.md#the-windows_subsystem-attribute) --- 指定要"
"链接的 Windows 子系统。"

#: src/attributes.md:281
msgid "Features"
msgstr "特性"

#: src/attributes.md:282
msgid ""
"`feature` --- Used to enable unstable or experimental compiler features. See "
"[The Unstable Book](../unstable-book/index.html) for features implemented in "
"`rustc`."
msgstr ""
"`feature` --- 用于启用不稳定或实验性编译器特性。有关 `rustc` 中实现的特性，"
"见 [The Unstable Book](../unstable-book/index.html)。"

#: src/attributes.md:284
msgid "Type System"
msgstr "类型系统"

#: src/attributes.md:285
msgid ""
"[`non_exhaustive`](attributes/type_system.md#the-non_exhaustive-attribute) "
"--- Indicate that a type will have more fields/variants added in future."
msgstr ""
"[`non_exhaustive`](attributes/type_system.md#the-non_exhaustive-attribute) "
"--- 指示未来会为类型添加更多字段/变体。"

#: src/attributes.md:288
msgid ""
"[`debugger_visualizer`](attributes/debugger.md#the-debugger_visualizer-"
"attribute) --- Embeds a file that specifies debugger output for a type."
msgstr ""
"[`debugger_visualizer`](attributes/debugger.md#the-debugger_visualizer-"
"attribute) --- 嵌入一个指定某个类型的调试器输出的文件。"

#: src/attributes.md:289
msgid ""
"[`collapse_debuginfo`](attributes/debugger.md#the-collapse_debuginfo-"
"attribute) --- Controls how macro invocations are encoded in debuginfo."
msgstr ""
"[`collapse_debuginfo`](attributes/debugger.md#the-collapse_debuginfo-"
"attribute) --- 控制宏调用如何编码到 debuginfo 中。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:1
msgid "r\\[attributes.testing\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.testing\\]"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:2
msgid "Testing attributes"
msgstr "测试属性"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:4
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) are used for specifying "
"functions for performing tests. Compiling a crate in \"test\" mode enables "
"building the test functions along with a test harness for executing the "
"tests. Enabling the test mode also enables the [`test` conditional "
"compilation option](../conditional-compilation.md#test)."
msgstr ""
"以下[属性](../attributes.md)用于指定执行测试的函数。以 \"test\" 模式编译 "
"crate 会启用测试函数的构建，并同时构建用于执行测试的测试框架。启用测试模式也"
"会启用 [`test` 条件编译选项](../conditional-compilation.md#test)。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:10
msgid "r\\[attributes.testing.test\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.testing.test\\]"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:11
msgid "The `test` attribute"
msgstr "`test` 属性"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.intro\\] The _`test` [attribute](../"
"attributes.md)_ marks a function to be executed as a test."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.intro\\] *`test` [属性](../attributes.md)* 将函数"
"标记为要作为测试执行。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:26
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.syntax\\] The `test` attribute uses the \\"
"[MetaWord\\] syntax."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.syntax\\] `test` 属性使用 \\[MetaWord\\] 语法。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:29
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.allowed-positions\\] The `test` attribute may "
"only be applied to [free functions](../glossary.md#free-item) that are "
"monomorphic, that take no arguments, and where the return type implements "
"the [`Termination`](std::process::Termination) trait."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.allowed-positions\\] `test` 属性只能应用于单态、"
"不接受参数且返回类型实现了 [`Termination`](std::process::Termination) trait "
"的[自由函数](../glossary.md#free-item)。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:32
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Some of types that implement the [`Termination`]"
"(std::process::Termination) trait include:"
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 实现 [`Termination`](std::process::Termination) trait 的一些类型"
"包括："

#: src/attributes/testing.md:37
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.duplicates\\] Only the first use of `test` on a "
"function has effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.duplicates\\] 在一个函数上，只有第一次使用 "
"`test` 会生效。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:45
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.stdlib\\] The `test` attribute is exported from "
"the standard library prelude as \\[`std::prelude::v1::test`\\]."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.stdlib\\] `test` 属性由标准库 prelude 以 \\"
"[`std::prelude::v1::test`\\] 导出。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:48
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.enabled\\] These functions are only compiled "
"when in test mode."
msgstr "r\\[attributes.testing.test.enabled\\] 这些函数只在测试模式下编译。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:51
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The test mode is enabled by passing the `--test` argument to "
"`rustc` or using `cargo test`."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 通过向 `rustc` 传递 `--test` 参数或使用 `cargo test` 可以启用测试"
"模式。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:54
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.success\\] The test harness calls the returned "
"value's [`report`](std::process::Termination::report) method, and classifies "
"the test as passed or failed depending on whether the resulting [`ExitCode`]"
"(std::process::ExitCode) represents successful termination. In particular:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.test.success\\] 测试框架会调用返回值的 [`report`]"
"(std::process::Termination::report) 方法，并根据产生的 [`ExitCode`]"
"(std::process::ExitCode) 是否表示成功终止，将测试归类为通过或失败。具体来说："

#: src/attributes/testing.md:57
msgid "Tests that return `()` pass as long as they terminate and do not panic."
msgstr "返回 `()` 的测试只要会终止且不 panic，就会通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:58
msgid ""
"Tests that return a `Result<(), E>` pass as long as they return `Ok(())`."
msgstr "返回 `Result<(), E>` 的测试只要返回 `Ok(())`，就会通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:59
msgid ""
"Tests that return `ExitCode::SUCCESS` pass, and tests that return "
"`ExitCode::FAILURE` fail."
msgstr ""
"返回 `ExitCode::SUCCESS` 的测试会通过，而返回 `ExitCode::FAILURE` 的测试会失"
"败。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:60
msgid "Tests that do not terminate neither pass nor fail."
msgstr "不会终止的测试既不通过也不失败。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:69 src/attributes/testing.md:70
msgid "// expected to succeed\n"
msgstr "// 预期会成功\n"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:76
msgid "r\\[attributes.testing.ignore\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.testing.ignore\\]"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:77
msgid "The `ignore` attribute"
msgstr "`ignore` 属性"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:79
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.intro\\] The _`ignore` [attribute](../"
"attributes.md)_ can be used with the \\[`test` attribute\\]\\"
"[attributes.testing.test\\] to tell the test harness to not execute that "
"function as a test."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.intro\\] *`ignore` [属性](../attributes.md)* 可"
"以与 \\[`test` 属性\\]\\[attributes.testing.test\\] 一起使用，用来告知测试框"
"架不要将该函数作为测试执行。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:91
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The `rustc` test harness supports the `--include-ignored` flag "
"to force ignored tests to be run."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 测试框架支持 `--include-ignored` 标志，用于强制运行被忽略"
"的测试。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:94
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.syntax\\] The `ignore` attribute uses the \\"
"[MetaWord\\] and \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntaxes."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.syntax\\] `ignore` 属性使用 \\[MetaWord\\] 和 "
"\\[MetaNameValueStr\\] 语法。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:97
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.reason\\] The \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] form of "
"the `ignore` attribute provides a way to specify a reason why the test is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.reason\\] `ignore` 属性的 \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] 形式提供了一种指定测试被忽略原因的方式。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:103
msgid "\"not yet implemented\""
msgstr "\"not yet implemented\""

#: src/attributes/testing.md:109
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.allowed-positions\\] The `ignore` attribute "
"may only be applied to functions annotated with the `test` attribute."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.allowed-positions\\] `ignore` 属性只能应用于以 "
"`test` 属性标注的函数。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:115
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.duplicates\\] Only the first use of `ignore` "
"on a function has effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.duplicates\\] 在一个函数上，只有第一次使用 "
"`ignore` 会生效。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:121
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.behavior\\] Ignored tests are still compiled "
"when in test mode, but they are not executed."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.ignore.behavior\\] 在测试模式下，被忽略的测试仍会被编"
"译，但不会被执行。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:125
msgid "r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic\\]"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:126
msgid "The `should_panic` attribute"
msgstr "`should_panic` 属性"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:128
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.intro\\] The _`should_panic` [attribute]"
"(../attributes.md)_ causes a test to pass only if the \\[test function\\]\\"
"[attributes.testing.test\\] to which the attribute is applied panics."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.intro\\] *`should_panic` [属性](../"
"attributes.md)* 使测试仅在应用该属性的\\[测试函数\\]\\"
"[attributes.testing.test\\] panic 时通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:134 src/attributes/testing.md:136
msgid "\"values don't match\""
msgstr "\"values don't match\""

#: src/attributes/testing.md:140
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.syntax\\] The `should_panic` attribute "
"has these forms:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.syntax\\] `should_panic` 属性有以下形式："

#: src/attributes/testing.md:148 src/attributes/testing.md:156
#: src/attributes/testing.md:164
msgid "\"error: some message, and more\""
msgstr "\"error: some message, and more\""

#: src/attributes/testing.md:151
msgid ""
"\\[MetaNameValueStr\\] --- The given string must appear within the panic "
"message for the test to pass."
msgstr ""
"\\[MetaNameValueStr\\] --- 给定字符串必须出现在 panic 消息中，测试才会通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:155 src/attributes/testing.md:163
msgid "\"some message\""
msgstr "\"some message\""

#: src/attributes/testing.md:159
msgid ""
"\\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] --- As with the \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntax, "
"the given string must appear within the panic message."
msgstr ""
"\\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] --- 与 \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] 语法一样，给定字符串"
"必须出现在 panic 消息中。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:167
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.allowed-positions\\] The `should_panic` "
"attribute may only be applied to functions annotated with the `test` "
"attribute."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.allowed-positions\\] `should_panic` 属性"
"只能应用于以 `test` 属性标注的函数。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:173
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.duplicates\\] Only the first use of "
"`should_panic` on a function has effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.duplicates\\] 在一个函数上，只有第一次使"
"用 `should_panic` 会生效。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:179
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.expected\\] When the \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] form or the \\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] form with the "
"`expected` key is used, the given string must appear somewhere within the "
"panic message for the test to pass."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.expected\\] 使用 \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] "
"形式，或使用带有 `expected` 键的 \\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] 形式时，给定字符"
"串必须出现在 panic 消息中的某处，测试才会通过。"

#: src/attributes/testing.md:182
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.return\\] The return type of the test "
"function must be `()`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.testing.should_panic.return\\] 测试函数的返回类型必须是 `()`。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:2
msgid "r\\[attributes.derive\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.derive\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:5
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.intro\\] The _`derive` \\[attribute\\]\\"
"[attributes\\]_ invokes one or more [derive macros](macro.proc.derive), "
"allowing new [items](../items.md) to be automatically generated for data "
"structures. You can create `derive` macros with [procedural macros]"
"(macro.proc.derive)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.intro\\] *`derive` \\[属性\\]\\[attributes\\]* 会调用一"
"个或多个[派生宏](macro.proc.derive)，允许为数据结构自动生成新的[项](../"
"items.md)。可以使用[过程宏](macro.proc.derive)创建 `derive` 宏。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:8
msgid ""
"\\[!EXAMPLE\\] The \\[`PartialEq`\\]\\[macro@PartialEq\\] derive macro emits "
"an [implementation](../items/implementations.md) of \\[`PartialEq`\\] for "
"`Foo<T> where T: PartialEq`. The \\[`Clone`\\]\\[macro@Clone\\] derive macro "
"does likewise for \\[`Clone`\\]."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EXAMPLE\\] \\[`PartialEq`\\]\\[macro@PartialEq\\] 派生宏会为 `Foo<T> "
"where T: PartialEq` 生成 \\[`PartialEq`\\] 的[实现](../items/"
"implementations.md)。\\[`Clone`\\]\\[macro@Clone\\] 派生宏同样会为 \\"
"[`Clone`\\] 生成相应实现。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:19
msgid "The generated `impl` items are equivalent to:"
msgstr "生成的 `impl` 项等价于："

#: src/attributes/derive.md:36
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.syntax\\] The `derive` attribute uses the \\"
"[MetaListPaths\\] syntax to specify a list of paths to [derive macros]"
"(macro.proc.derive) to invoke."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.syntax\\] `derive` 属性使用 \\[MetaListPaths\\] 语法来"
"指定要调用的[派生宏](macro.proc.derive)路径列表。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:39
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.allowed-positions\\] The `derive` attribute may only "
"be applied to \\[structs\\]\\[items.struct\\], \\[enums\\]\\[items.enum\\], "
"and \\[unions\\]\\[items.union\\]."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.allowed-positions\\] `derive` 属性只能应用于 \\"
"[structs\\]\\[items.struct\\]、\\[enums\\]\\[items.enum\\] 和 \\[unions\\]\\"
"[items.union\\]。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:42
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.duplicates\\] The `derive` attribute may be used any "
"number of times on an item. All derive macros listed in all attributes are "
"invoked."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.duplicates\\] `derive` 属性可以在一个项上使用任意次数。"
"所有属性中列出的全部派生宏都会被调用。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:45
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.stdlib\\] The `derive` attribute is exported in the "
"standard library as:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.stdlib\\] `derive` 属性在标准库中以下列名称导出："

#: src/attributes/derive.md:48
msgid "\\[`core::derive`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`core::derive`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:49
msgid "\\[`std::derive`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`std::derive`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:50
msgid "\\[`core::prelude::v1::derive`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`core::prelude::v1::derive`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:51
msgid "\\[`std::prelude::v1::derive`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`std::prelude::v1::derive`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:53
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.built-in\\] Built-in derives are defined in the \\"
"[language prelude\\]\\[names.preludes.lang\\]. The list of built-in derives "
"are:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.built-in\\] 内置派生定义在\\[语言 prelude\\]\\"
"[names.preludes.lang\\] 中。内置派生的列表如下："

#: src/attributes/derive.md:56
msgid "\\[`Clone`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`Clone`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:57
msgid "\\[`Copy`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`Copy`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:58
msgid "\\[`Debug`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`Debug`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:59
msgid "\\[`Default`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`Default`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:60
msgid "\\[`Eq`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`Eq`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:61
msgid "\\[`Hash`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`Hash`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:62
msgid "\\[`Ord`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`Ord`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:63
msgid "\\[`PartialEq`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`PartialEq`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:64
msgid "\\[`PartialOrd`\\]"
msgstr "\\[`PartialOrd`\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:66
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.built-in-automatically_derived\\] The built-in derives "
"include the \\[`automatically_derived` attribute\\]\\"
"[attributes.derive.automatically_derived\\] on the implementations they "
"generate."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.built-in-automatically_derived\\] 内置派生会在它们生成"
"的实现上包含 \\[`automatically_derived` 属性\\]\\"
"[attributes.derive.automatically_derived\\]。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:69
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.behavior\\] During macro expansion, for each element "
"in the list of derives, the corresponding derive macro expands to zero or "
"more [items](../items.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.behavior\\] 在宏展开期间，对于派生列表中的每个元素，相"
"应的派生宏会展开为零个或多个[项](../items.md)。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:73
msgid "r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived\\]"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:74
msgid "The `automatically_derived` attribute"
msgstr "`automatically_derived` 属性"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:76
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.intro\\] The "
"_`automatically_derived` \\[attribute\\]\\[attributes\\]_ is used to "
"annotate an [implementation](../items/implementations.md) to indicate that "
"it was automatically created by a [derive macro](macro.proc.derive). It has "
"no direct effect, but it may be used by tools and diagnostic lints to detect "
"these automatically generated implementations."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.intro\\] "
"*`automatically_derived` \\[属性\\]\\[attributes\\]* 用于标注[实现](../items/"
"implementations.md)，以表明该实现是由[派生宏](macro.proc.derive)自动创建的。"
"它没有直接效果，但工具和诊断 lint 可以使用它来检测这些自动生成的实现。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:79
msgid ""
"\\[!EXAMPLE\\] Given \\[`#[derive(Clone)]`\\]\\[macro@Clone\\] on `struct "
"Example`, the [derive macro](macro.proc.derive) may produce:"
msgstr ""
"\\[!EXAMPLE\\] 给定 `struct Example` 上的 \\[`#[derive(Clone)]`\\]\\"
"[macro@Clone\\]，[派生宏](macro.proc.derive)可以生成："

#: src/attributes/derive.md:93
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.syntax\\] The "
"`automatically_derived` attribute uses the \\[MetaWord\\] syntax."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.syntax\\] "
"`automatically_derived` 属性使用 \\[MetaWord\\] 语法。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:96
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.allowed-positions\\] The "
"`automatically_derived` attribute may only be applied to an [implementation]"
"(../items/implementations.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.allowed-positions\\] "
"`automatically_derived` 属性只能应用于[实现](../items/implementations.md)。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:102
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.duplicates\\] Using "
"`automatically_derived` more than once on an implementation has the same "
"effect as using it once."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.duplicates\\] 在一个实现上多次使"
"用 `automatically_derived` 与使用一次具有相同效果。"

#: src/attributes/derive.md:108
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.behavior\\] The "
"`automatically_derived` attribute has no behavior."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.derive.automatically_derived.behavior\\] "
"`automatically_derived` 属性没有任何行为。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:1
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:2
msgid "Diagnostic attributes"
msgstr "诊断属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:4
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) are used for controlling or "
"generating diagnostic messages during compilation."
msgstr "以下[属性](../attributes.md)用于在编译期间控制或生成诊断消息。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:7
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:8
msgid "Lint check attributes"
msgstr "Lint 检查属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:10
msgid ""
"A lint check names a potentially undesirable coding pattern, such as "
"unreachable code or omitted documentation."
msgstr "lint 检查命名一种可能不合需要的编码模式，例如不可达代码或缺失文档。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.level\\] The lint attributes `allow`, "
"`expect`, `warn`, `deny`, and `forbid` use the \\[MetaListPaths\\] syntax to "
"specify a list of lint names to change the lint level for the entity to "
"which the attribute applies."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.level\\] `allow`、`expect`、`warn`、`deny` "
"和 `forbid` 这些 lint 属性使用 \\[MetaListPaths\\] 语法来指定 lint 名称列表，"
"以更改该属性所适用实体的 lint 级别。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:19
msgid "For any lint check `C`:"
msgstr "对于任意 lint 检查 `C`："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:21
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.allow\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.allow\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:22
msgid ""
"`#[allow(C)]` overrides the check for `C` so that violations will go "
"unreported."
msgstr "`#[allow(C)]` 会覆盖对 `C` 的检查，使违规不会被报告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:25
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.expect\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.expect\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:26
msgid ""
"`#[expect(C)]` indicates that lint `C` is expected to be emitted. The "
"attribute will suppress the emission of `C` or issue a warning, if the "
"expectation is unfulfilled."
msgstr ""
"`#[expect(C)]` 表示预期会发出 lint `C`。该属性会抑制 `C` 的发出；如果期望未满"
"足，则会发出警告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:30
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.warn\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.warn\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:31
msgid "`#[warn(C)]` warns about violations of `C` but continues compilation."
msgstr "`#[warn(C)]` 会对 `C` 的违规发出警告，但继续编译。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:33
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.deny\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.deny\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:34
msgid "`#[deny(C)]` signals an error after encountering a violation of `C`,"
msgstr "`#[deny(C)]` 在遇到 `C` 的违规后发出错误，"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:36
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.forbid\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.forbid\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:37
msgid ""
"`#[forbid(C)]` is the same as `deny(C)`, but also forbids changing the lint "
"level afterwards,"
msgstr "`#[forbid(C)]` 与 `deny(C)` 相同，但还禁止之后更改 lint 级别，"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:40
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The lint checks supported by `rustc` can be found via `rustc -W "
"help`, along with their default settings and are documented in the [rustc "
"book](../../rustc/lints/index.html)."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 支持的 lint 检查及其默认设置可通过 `rustc -W help` 查看，"
"并记录在 [rustc book](../../rustc/lints/index.html) 中。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:45 src/attributes/diagnostics.md:74
msgid "// Missing documentation is ignored here\n"
msgstr "// 此处会忽略缺失文档\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:49 src/attributes/diagnostics.md:83
msgid "// Missing documentation signals a warning here\n"
msgstr "// 此处缺失文档会发出警告\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:53
msgid "// Missing documentation signals an error here\n"
msgstr "// 此处缺失文档会发出错误\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:59
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.override\\] Lint attributes can override the "
"level specified from a previous attribute, as long as the level does not "
"attempt to change a forbidden lint (except for `deny`, which is allowed "
"inside a `forbid` context, but ignored). Previous attributes are those from "
"a higher level in the syntax tree, or from a previous attribute on the same "
"entity as listed in left-to-right source order."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.override\\] 只要该级别不会试图更改已被 "
"`forbid` 的 lint（`deny` 例外，它在 `forbid` 上下文内允许使用，但会被忽略），"
"lint 属性就可以覆盖先前属性指定的级别。先前属性是指语法树中更高层级的属性，或"
"同一实体上按源码从左到右顺序列出的较早属性。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:66
msgid ""
"This example shows how one can use `allow` and `warn` to toggle a particular "
"check on and off:"
msgstr "此示例展示如何使用 `allow` 和 `warn` 开关某个特定检查："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:77
msgid ""
"// Missing documentation signals a warning here,\n"
"        // despite the allow above.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此处缺失文档会发出警告，\n"
"        // 尽管上方有 allow。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:88
msgid ""
"This example shows how one can use `forbid` to disallow uses of `allow` or "
"`expect` for that lint check:"
msgstr ""
"此示例展示如何使用 `forbid` 来禁止为该 lint 检查使用 `allow` 或 `expect`："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:94
msgid "// Attempting to toggle warning signals an error here\n"
msgstr "// 试图切换警告级别会在此处发出错误\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:96
msgid "/// Returns 2.\n"
msgstr "/// 返回 2。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:101
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` allows setting lint levels on the [command-line](../../"
"rustc/lints/levels.html#via-compiler-flag), and also supports [setting caps]"
"(../../rustc/lints/levels.html#capping-lints) on the lints that are reported."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 允许在[命令行](../../rustc/lints/levels.html#via-"
"compiler-flag)上设置 lint 级别，也支持对已报告的 lint [设置上限](../../rustc/"
"lints/levels.html#capping-lints)。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:104
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.reason\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.reason\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:105
msgid "Lint reasons"
msgstr "Lint 原因"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:107
msgid ""
"All lint attributes support an additional `reason` parameter, to give "
"context why a certain attribute was added. This reason will be displayed as "
"part of the lint message if the lint is emitted at the defined level."
msgstr ""
"所有 lint 属性都支持额外的 `reason` 参数，用于说明添加某个属性的上下文。如果"
"该 lint 按定义的级别发出，此原因会作为 lint 消息的一部分显示。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:112
msgid ""
"// `keyword_idents` is allowed by default. Here we deny it to\n"
"// avoid migration of identifiers when we update the edition.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 默认允许 `keyword_idents`。这里将其设为 deny，\n"
"// 以避免更新 edition 时迁移标识符。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:116
msgid "\"we want to avoid these idents to be future compatible\""
msgstr "\"we want to avoid these idents to be future compatible\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:118
msgid ""
"// This name was allowed in Rust's 2015 edition. We still aim to avoid\n"
"// this to be future compatible and not confuse end users.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此名称在 Rust 2015 edition 中是允许的。我们仍希望避免\n"
"// 这样做，以保持未来兼容性并避免困惑最终用户。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:124
msgid "Here is another example, where the lint is allowed with a reason:"
msgstr "这里还有一个示例，其中 lint 带有原因地被允许："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:130
msgid ""
"// The `reason` parameter on `allow` attributes acts as documentation for "
"the reader.\n"
msgstr "// `allow` 属性上的 `reason` 参数充当给读者看的文档。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:131
msgid "\"this is only modified on some platforms\""
msgstr "\"this is only modified on some platforms\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:132
msgid "\"git\""
msgstr "\"git\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:135
msgid "\"exe\""
msgstr "\"exe\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:141
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.expect\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.expect\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:142
msgid "The `#[expect]` attribute"
msgstr "`#[expect]` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:144
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.expect.intro\\] The `#[expect(C)]` attribute "
"creates a lint expectation for lint `C`. The expectation will be fulfilled, "
"if a `#[warn(C)]` attribute at the same location would result in a lint "
"emission. If the expectation is unfulfilled, because lint `C` would not be "
"emitted, the `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint will be emitted at the "
"attribute."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.expect.intro\\] `#[expect(C)]` 属性会为 lint `C` "
"创建一个 lint 期望。如果同一位置的 `#[warn(C)]` 属性会导致 lint 发出，则该期"
"望会被满足。如果由于 lint `C` 不会被发出而导致期望未满足，则会在该属性处发出 "
"`unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:153
msgid ""
"// This `#[expect]` attribute creates a lint expectation, that the "
"`unused_variables`\n"
"    // lint would be emitted by the following statement. This expectation "
"is\n"
"    // unfulfilled, since the `question` variable is used by the `println!` "
"macro.\n"
"    // Therefore, the `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint will be emitted "
"at the\n"
"    // attribute.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此 `#[expect]` 属性创建一个 lint 期望，即以下语句会发出\n"
"    // `unused_variables` lint。由于 `question` 变量被 `println!` 宏使用，\n"
"    // 此期望未满足。因此，会在该属性处发出\n"
"    // `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:159
msgid "\"who lives in a pineapple under the sea?\""
msgstr "\"who lives in a pineapple under the sea?\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:160
msgid "\"{question}\""
msgstr "\"{question}\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:162
msgid ""
"// This `#[expect]` attribute creates a lint expectation that will be "
"fulfilled, since\n"
"    // the `answer` variable is never used. The `unused_variables` lint, "
"that would usually\n"
"    // be emitted, is suppressed. No warning will be issued for the "
"statement or attribute.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此 `#[expect]` 属性创建一个会被满足的 lint 期望，因为\n"
"    // `answer` 变量从未被使用。通常会发出的 `unused_variables` lint\n"
"    // 会被抑制。该语句或属性不会产生警告。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:166
msgid "\"SpongeBob SquarePants!\""
msgstr "\"SpongeBob SquarePants!\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:170
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.expect.fulfillment\\] The lint expectation is "
"only fulfilled by lint emissions which have been suppressed by the `expect` "
"attribute. If the lint level is modified in the scope with other level "
"attributes like `allow` or `warn`, the lint emission will be handled "
"accordingly and the expectation will remain unfulfilled."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.expect.fulfillment\\] lint 期望只会由已被 "
"`expect` 属性抑制的 lint 发出满足。如果作用域中的 lint 级别被 `allow` 或 "
"`warn` 等其他级别属性修改，则该 lint 发出会按相应方式处理，而该期望仍保持未满"
"足。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:179
msgid ""
"// This will emit the `unused_variables` lint at the warn level\n"
"    // as defined by the `warn` attribute. This will not fulfill the\n"
"    // expectation above the function.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会按 `warn` 属性定义，以 warn 级别发出 `unused_variables` lint。\n"
"    // 这不会满足函数上方的期望。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:183
msgid "\"Crab Rave\""
msgstr "\"Crab Rave\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:185
msgid ""
"// The `allow` attribute suppresses the lint emission. This will not\n"
"    // fulfill the expectation as it has been suppressed by the `allow`\n"
"    // attribute and not the `expect` attribute above the function.\n"
msgstr ""
"// `allow` 属性会抑制 lint 发出。这不会满足期望，\n"
"    // 因为它是被 `allow` 属性抑制的，而不是被函数上方的\n"
"    // `expect` 属性抑制的。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:189
msgid "\"Noisestorm\""
msgstr "\"Noisestorm\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:191
msgid ""
"// This `expect` attribute will suppress the `unused_variables` lint "
"emission\n"
"    // at the variable. The `expect` attribute above the function will still "
"not\n"
"    // be fulfilled, since this lint emission has been suppressed by the "
"local\n"
"    // expect attribute.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此 `expect` 属性会在变量处抑制 `unused_variables` lint 的发出。\n"
"    // 函数上方的 `expect` 属性仍不会被满足，\n"
"    // 因为此 lint 发出已被局部 `expect` 属性抑制。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:196
msgid "\"Monstercat Release\""
msgstr "\"Monstercat Release\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:200
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.expect.independent\\] If the `expect` attribute "
"contains several lints, each one is expected separately. For a lint group "
"it's enough if one lint inside the group has been emitted:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.expect.independent\\] 如果 `expect` 属性包含多个 "
"lint，则会分别对每个 lint 建立期望。对于 lint 组，只要组内有一个 lint 已被发"
"出就足够了："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:205
msgid ""
"// This expectation will be fulfilled by the unused value inside the "
"function\n"
"// since the emitted `unused_variables` lint is inside the `unused` lint "
"group.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此期望会由函数内部的未使用值满足，\n"
"// 因为发出的 `unused_variables` lint 属于 `unused` lint 组。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:209
msgid "\"I'm running out of examples\""
msgstr "\"I'm running out of examples\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:213
msgid ""
"// This attribute creates two lint expectations. The `unused_mut` lint will "
"be\n"
"    // suppressed and with that fulfill the first expectation. The "
"`unused_variables`\n"
"    // wouldn't be emitted, since the variable is used. That expectation "
"will therefore\n"
"    // be unsatisfied, and a warning will be emitted.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此属性创建两个 lint 期望。`unused_mut` lint 会被\n"
"    // 抑制，并由此满足第一个期望。`unused_variables`\n"
"    // 不会被发出，因为该变量被使用了。因此该期望\n"
"    // 会未满足，并会发出警告。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:218
msgid "\"https://www.rust-lang.org/\""
msgstr "\"https://www.rust-lang.org/\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:220
msgid "\"Welcome to our community: {link}\""
msgstr "\"Welcome to our community: {link}\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:224
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The behavior of `#[expect(unfulfilled_lint_expectations)]` is "
"currently defined to always generate the `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` "
"lint."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `#[expect(unfulfilled_lint_expectations)]` 的行为目前定义为始终生"
"成 `unfulfilled_lint_expectations` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:227
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.group\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.group\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:228
msgid "Lint groups"
msgstr "Lint 组"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:230
msgid ""
"Lints may be organized into named groups so that the level of related lints "
"can be adjusted together. Using a named group is equivalent to listing out "
"the lints within that group."
msgstr ""
"lint 可以组织成具名组，以便一起调整相关 lint 的级别。使用具名组等价于列出该组"
"内的所有 lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:235
msgid "// This allows all lints in the \"unused\" group.\n"
msgstr "// 这允许 \"unused\" 组中的所有 lint。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:236
msgid ""
"// This overrides the \"unused_must_use\" lint from the \"unused\"\n"
"// group to deny.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会把 \"unused\" 组中的 \"unused_must_use\" lint\n"
"// 覆盖为 deny。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:241
msgid ""
"// This does not generate a warning because the \"unused_variables\"\n"
"    // lint is in the \"unused\" group.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这不会生成警告，因为 \"unused_variables\"\n"
"    // lint 位于 \"unused\" 组中。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:244
msgid ""
"// This generates an error because the result is unused and\n"
"    // \"unused_must_use\" is marked as \"deny\".\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会生成错误，因为结果未被使用，且\n"
"    // \"unused_must_use\" 被标记为 \"deny\"。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:246
msgid "\"some_file\""
msgstr "\"some_file\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:246
msgid "// ERROR: unused `Result` that must be used\n"
msgstr "// 错误：未使用必须使用的 `Result`\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:250
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.group.warnings\\] There is a special group "
"named \"warnings\" which includes all lints at the \"warn\" level. The "
"\"warnings\" group ignores attribute order and applies to all lints that "
"would otherwise warn within the entity."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.group.warnings\\] 有一个名为 \"warnings\" 的"
"特殊组，它包括所有处于 \"warn\" 级别的 lint。\"warnings\" 组会忽略属性顺序，"
"并应用于实体中所有在其他情况下会发出警告的 lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:256
msgid "// The order of these two attributes does not matter.\n"
msgstr "// 这两个属性的顺序并不重要。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:258
msgid "// The unsafe_code lint is normally \"allow\" by default.\n"
msgstr "// unsafe_code lint 通常默认为 \"allow\"。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:262
msgid ""
"// This is an error because the `unsafe_code` warning has\n"
"    // been lifted to \"deny\".\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这是错误，因为 `unsafe_code` 警告已被\n"
"    // 提升到 \"deny\"。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:264
msgid "// ERROR: use of `unsafe` block\n"
msgstr "// 错误：使用 `unsafe` 块\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:268
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.tool\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.tool\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:269
msgid "Tool lint attributes"
msgstr "工具 lint 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:271
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.tool.intro\\] Tool lints allows using scoped "
"lints, to `allow`, `warn`, `deny` or `forbid` lints of certain tools."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.tool.intro\\] 工具 lint 允许使用带作用域的 "
"lint，来对特定工具的 lint 设置 `allow`、`warn`、`deny` 或 `forbid`。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:275
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.tool.activation\\] Tool lints only get "
"checked when the associated tool is active. If a lint attribute, such as "
"`allow`, references a nonexistent tool lint, the compiler will not warn "
"about the nonexistent lint until you use the tool."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.lint.tool.activation\\] 工具 lint 只有在关联工具处"
"于活动状态时才会被检查。如果 `allow` 等 lint 属性引用了不存在的工具 lint，编"
"译器在你使用该工具之前不会对这个不存在的 lint 发出警告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:280
msgid "Otherwise, they work just like regular lint attributes:"
msgstr "除此之外，它们的工作方式与常规 lint 属性相同："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:283
msgid "// set the entire `pedantic` clippy lint group to warn\n"
msgstr "// 将整个 `pedantic` clippy lint 组设为 warn\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:284
msgid "// silence warnings from the `filter_map` clippy lint\n"
msgstr "// 静默来自 `filter_map` clippy lint 的警告\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:291
msgid "// silence the `cmp_nan` clippy lint just for this function\n"
msgstr "// 仅对这个函数静默 `cmp_nan` clippy lint\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:299
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` currently recognizes the tool lints for \"[clippy]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy)\" and \"[rustdoc](../../rustdoc/"
"lints.html)\"."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 目前识别 \"[clippy](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-"
"clippy)\" 和 \"[rustdoc](../../rustdoc/lints.html)\" 的工具 lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:302
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.deprecated\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.deprecated\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:303
msgid "The `deprecated` attribute"
msgstr "`deprecated` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:305
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.deprecated.intro\\] The _`deprecated` attribute_ "
"marks an item as deprecated. `rustc` will issue warnings on use of "
"`#[deprecated]` items. `rustdoc` will show item deprecation, including the "
"`since` version and `note`, if available."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.deprecated.intro\\] *`deprecated` 属性* 将项标记为"
"已弃用。使用 `#[deprecated]` 项时，`rustc` 会发出警告。`rustdoc` 会显示项的弃"
"用信息，包括 `since` 版本和 `note`（如果可用）。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:310
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.deprecated.syntax\\] The `deprecated` attribute "
"has several forms:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.deprecated.syntax\\] `deprecated` 属性有几种形式："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:313
msgid "`deprecated` --- Issues a generic message."
msgstr "`deprecated` --- 发出通用消息。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:314
msgid ""
"`deprecated = \"message\"` --- Includes the given string in the deprecation "
"message."
msgstr "`deprecated = \"message\"` --- 在弃用消息中包含给定字符串。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:316
msgid "\\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] syntax with two optional fields:"
msgstr "带有两个可选字段的 \\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] 语法："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:317
msgid ""
"`since` --- Specifies a version number when the item was deprecated. `rustc` "
"does not currently interpret the string, but external tools like [Clippy]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy) may check the validity of the "
"value."
msgstr ""
"`since` --- 指定项被弃用时的版本号。`rustc` 目前不会解释该字符串，但 [Clippy]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-clippy) 等外部工具可以检查该值的有效性。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:320
msgid ""
"`note` --- Specifies a string that should be included in the deprecation "
"message. This is typically used to provide an explanation about the "
"deprecation and preferred alternatives."
msgstr ""
"`note` --- 指定应包含在弃用消息中的字符串。这通常用于提供关于弃用和首选替代方"
"案的说明。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:324
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.deprecated.allowed-positions\\] The `deprecated` "
"attribute may be applied to any [item](../items.md), [trait item](../items/"
"traits.md), [enum variant](../items/enumerations.md), [struct field](../"
"items/structs.md), [external block item](../items/external-blocks.md), or "
"[macro definition](../macros-by-example.md). It cannot be applied to [trait "
"implementation items](../items/implementations.md#trait-implementations). "
"When applied to an item containing other items, such as a [module](../items/"
"modules.md) or [implementation](../items/implementations.md), all child "
"items inherit the deprecation attribute."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.deprecated.allowed-positions\\] `deprecated` 属性可"
"以应用于任何[项](../items.md)、[trait 项](../items/traits.md)、[enum 变体]"
"(../items/enumerations.md)、[struct 字段](../items/structs.md)、[外部块项]"
"(../items/external-blocks.md)或[宏定义](../macros-by-example.md)。它不能应用"
"于 [trait 实现项](../items/implementations.md#trait-implementations)。当应用"
"于包含其他项的项（如[模块](../items/modules.md)或[实现](../items/"
"implementations.md)）时，所有子项都会继承该弃用属性。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:338
msgid "\"5.2.0\""
msgstr "\"5.2.0\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:338
msgid "\"foo was rarely used. Users should instead use bar\""
msgstr "\"foo was rarely used. Users should instead use bar\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:344
msgid ""
"The [RFC](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/1270-"
"deprecation.md) contains motivations and more details."
msgstr ""
"[RFC](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/1270-"
"deprecation.md) 包含动机和更多细节。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:349
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:350
msgid "The `must_use` attribute"
msgstr "`must_use` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:352
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.intro\\] The _`must_use` [attribute](../"
"attributes.md)_ marks a value that should be used."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.intro\\] *`must_use` [属性](../"
"attributes.md)* 标记一个应当被使用的值。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:355
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.syntax\\] The `must_use` attribute uses "
"the \\[MetaWord\\] and \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntaxes."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.syntax\\] `must_use` 属性使用 \\"
"[MetaWord\\] 和 \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] 语法。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:363
msgid "\"explanation of why it should be used\""
msgstr "\"explanation of why it should be used\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:367
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.allowed-positions\\] The `must_use` "
"attribute may be applied to a:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.allowed-positions\\] `must_use` 属性可以"
"应用于："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:370
msgid "[Struct](../items/structs.md)"
msgstr "[struct](../items/structs.md)"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:371
msgid "[Enumeration](../items/enumerations.md)"
msgstr "[enum](../items/enumerations.md)"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:372
msgid "[Union](../items/unions.md)"
msgstr "[union](../items/unions.md)"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:373
msgid "\\[Function\\]"
msgstr "\\[Function\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:374
msgid "\\[Trait\\]"
msgstr "\\[Trait\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:379
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.duplicates\\] The `must_use` attribute "
"may be used only once on an item."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.duplicates\\] `must_use` 属性在一个项上只"
"能使用一次。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:385
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.message\\] The `must_use` attribute may "
"include a message by using the \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntax, e.g., "
"`#[must_use = \"example message\"]`. The message may be emitted as part of "
"the lint."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.message\\] `must_use` 属性可以使用 \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] 语法包含一条消息，例如 `#[must_use = \"example "
"message\"]`。该消息可以作为 lint 的一部分发出。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:388
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type\\] When the attribute is applied to "
"a [struct](../items/structs.md), [enumeration](../items/enumerations.md), or "
"[union](../items/unions.md), if the [expression](../expressions.md) of an "
"[expression statement](../statements.md#expression-statements) has that "
"type, the use triggers the `unused_must_use` lint."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type\\] 当该属性应用于 [struct](../items/"
"structs.md)、[enum](../items/enumerations.md) 或 [union](../items/unions.md) "
"时，如果[表达式语句](../statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../"
"expressions.md)具有该类型，则该使用会触发 `unused_must_use` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:395
msgid "// ERROR: Unused value that must be used.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：未使用必须使用的值。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:398
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type.uninhabited\\] As an exception to \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type\\], the lint does not fire for "
"`Result<(), E>` when `E` is [uninhabited](glossary.uninhabited) or for "
"`ControlFlow<B, ()>` when `B` is [uninhabited](glossary.uninhabited). A "
"`#[non_exhaustive]` type from an external crate is not considered "
"uninhabited for this purpose, because it may gain constructors in the future."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type.uninhabited\\] 作为 \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type\\] 的例外，当 `E` 是[无值的]"
"(glossary.uninhabited)时，lint 不会针对 `Result<(), E>` 触发；当 `B` 是[无值"
"的](glossary.uninhabited)时，也不会针对 `ControlFlow<B, ()>` 触发。来自外部 "
"crate 的 `#[non_exhaustive]` 类型在此目的下不被认为是无值类型，因为它将来可能"
"获得构造器。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:406 src/attributes/diagnostics.md:408
msgid "// OK: `Empty` is uninhabited.\n"
msgstr "// OK：`Empty` 是无值类型。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:411
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn\\] If the [expression](../"
"expressions.md) of an [expression statement](../statements.md#expression-"
"statements) is a [call expression](../expressions/call-expr.md) or [method "
"call expression](../expressions/method-call-expr.md) whose function operand "
"is a function to which the attribute is applied, the use triggers the "
"`unused_must_use` lint."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn\\] 如果[表达式语句](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../expressions.md)是[调用表达"
"式](../expressions/call-expr.md)或[方法调用表达式](../expressions/method-"
"call-expr.md)，且其函数操作数是应用了该属性的函数，则该使用会触发 "
"`unused_must_use` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:418 src/attributes/diagnostics.md:447
msgid "// ERROR: Unused return value that must be used.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：未使用必须使用的返回值。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:421
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait\\] If the [expression](../"
"expressions.md) of an [expression statement](../statements.md#expression-"
"statements) is a [call expression](../expressions/call-expr.md) or [method "
"call expression](../expressions/method-call-expr.md) whose function operand "
"is a function that returns an [impl trait](../types/impl-trait.md) or a [dyn "
"trait](../types/trait-object.md) type where one or more traits in the bound "
"are marked with the attribute, the use triggers the `unused_must_use` lint."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait\\] 如果[表达式语句](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../expressions.md)是[调用表达"
"式](../expressions/call-expr.md)或[方法调用表达式](../expressions/method-"
"call-expr.md)，且其函数操作数是一个返回 [impl trait](../types/impl-trait.md) "
"或 [dyn trait](../types/trait-object.md) 类型的函数，并且约束中的一个或多个 "
"trait 标记了该属性，则该使用会触发 `unused_must_use` lint。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:430
msgid "// ERROR: Unused implementor that must be used.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：未使用必须使用的实现者。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:433
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-function\\] When the attribute is "
"applied to a function in a trait declaration, the rules described in \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn\\] also apply when the function operand "
"of the [call expression](../expressions/call-expr.md) or [method call "
"expression](../expressions/method-call-expr.md) is an implementation of that "
"function."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-function\\] 当该属性应用于 trait 声"
"明中的函数时，如果[调用表达式](../expressions/call-expr.md)或[方法调用表达式]"
"(../expressions/method-call-expr.md)的函数操作数是该函数的实现，\\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn\\] 中描述的规则也适用。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:461
msgid "//          ^^^^^^^^^^^ ERROR: Unused return value that must be used.\n"
msgstr "//          ^^^^^^^^^^^ 错误：未使用必须使用的返回值。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:465
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.block-expr\\] When checking the "
"[expression](../expressions.md) of an [expression statement](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements) for \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type\\], \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn\\], \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait\\], and \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-function\\], the lint looks through "
"[block expressions](../expressions/block-expr.md) (including [`unsafe` "
"blocks](../expressions/block-expr.md#unsafe-blocks) and [labeled block "
"expressions](../expressions/block-expr.md#labeled-block-expressions)) to the "
"trailing expression of each. This applies recursively for nested block "
"expressions."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.block-expr\\] 在针对 \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type\\]、\\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn\\]、\\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait\\] 和 \\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-function\\] 检查[表达式语句](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../expressions.md)时，lint 会"
"透过[块表达式](../expressions/block-expr.md)（包括 [`unsafe` 块](../"
"expressions/block-expr.md#unsafe-blocks)和[带标签块表达式](../expressions/"
"block-expr.md#labeled-block-expressions)）查看每个块的尾随表达式。这会递归应"
"用于嵌套块表达式。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:473
msgid "// ERROR: The lint looks through block expressions.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：lint 会透过块表达式。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:474
msgid "// ERROR: The lint looks through `unsafe` blocks.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：lint 会透过 `unsafe` 块。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:475
msgid "// ERROR: The lint looks through nested blocks.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：lint 会透过嵌套块。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:478
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-impl-function\\] When used on a "
"function in a trait implementation, the attribute does nothing."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.trait-impl-function\\] 当用于 trait 实现"
"中的函数时，该属性没有效果。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:488
msgid "// This has no effect.\n"
msgstr "// 这没有效果。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:495
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` lints against use on functions in trait implementations. "
"This may become an error in the future."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 会对 trait 实现中函数上的使用发出 lint。这在将来可能会变"
"成错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:498
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.wrapping-suppression\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.wrapping-suppression\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:499
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Wrapping the result of a `#[must_use]` function in certain "
"expressions can suppress the \\[fn-based check\\]\\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn\\], because the [expression](../"
"expressions.md) of the [expression statement](../statements.md#expression-"
"statements) is not a [call expression](../expressions/call-expr.md) or "
"[method call expression](../expressions/method-call-expr.md) to a "
"`#[must_use]` function.  The \\[type-based check\\]\\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type\\] still applies if the type of the "
"overall expression is `#[must_use]`."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 将 `#[must_use]` 函数的结果包裹在某些表达式中可能会抑制 \\[基于 "
"fn 的检查\\]\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.fn\\]，因为[表达式语句](../"
"statements.md#expression-statements)的[表达式](../expressions.md)不是对 "
"`#[must_use]` 函数的[调用表达式](../expressions/call-expr.md)或[方法调用表达"
"式](../expressions/method-call-expr.md)。如果整体表达式的类型为 "
"`#[must_use]`，\\[基于类型的检查\\]\\"
"[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.type\\] 仍然适用。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:507
msgid "// The fn-based check does not fire for any of these, because the\n"
msgstr "// 对于下面这些情况，基于 fn 的检查都不会触发，因为\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:508
msgid "// expression of the expression statement is not a call to a\n"
msgstr "// 表达式语句的表达式不是对\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:509
msgid "// `#[must_use]` function.\n"
msgstr "// `#[must_use]` 函数的调用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:510
msgid "// Expression is a tuple, not a call.\n"
msgstr "// 表达式是元组，不是调用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:511
msgid "// Callee `Some` is not `#[must_use]`.\n"
msgstr "// 被调用者 `Some` 不是 `#[must_use]`。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:512
msgid "// Expression is an `if`, not a call.\n"
msgstr "// 表达式是 `if`，不是调用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:513
msgid "// Expression is a `match`, not a call.\n"
msgstr "// 表达式是 `match`，不是调用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:524
msgid "// Despite the `if` expression not being a call, the type-based check\n"
msgstr "// 尽管 `if` 表达式不是调用，基于类型的检查\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:525
msgid "// fires because the type of the expression is `MustUse`, which has\n"
msgstr "// 仍会触发，因为表达式的类型是 `MustUse`，而该类型具有\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:526
msgid "// the `#[must_use]` attribute.\n"
msgstr "// `#[must_use]` 属性。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:527
msgid "// ERROR: Must be used.\n"
msgstr "// 错误：必须使用。\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:530
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.underscore-idiom\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostics.must_use.underscore-idiom\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:531
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Using a [let statement](../statements.md#let-statements) or "
"[destructuring assignment](expr.assign.destructure) with a pattern of `_` "
"when a must-used value is purposely discarded is idiomatic."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 当有意丢弃必须使用的值时，使用带 `_` 模式的 [let 语句](../"
"statements.md#let-statements)或[解构赋值](expr.assign.destructure)是惯用做"
"法。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:542
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostic.namespace\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostic.namespace\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:543
msgid "The `diagnostic` tool attribute namespace"
msgstr "`diagnostic` 工具属性命名空间"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:545
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.namespace.intro\\] The `#[diagnostic]` attribute "
"namespace is a home for attributes to influence compile-time error messages. "
"The hints provided by these attributes are not guaranteed to be used."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.namespace.intro\\] `#[diagnostic]` 属性命名空间用于"
"放置影响编译时错误消息的属性。这些属性提供的提示不保证会被使用。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:549
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.namespace.unknown-invalid-syntax\\] Unknown "
"attributes in this namespace are accepted, though they may emit warnings for "
"unused attributes. Additionally, invalid inputs to known attributes will "
"typically be a warning (see the attribute definitions for details). This is "
"meant to allow adding or discarding attributes and changing inputs in the "
"future to allow changes without the need to keep the non-meaningful "
"attributes or options working."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.namespace.unknown-invalid-syntax\\] 此命名空间中的"
"未知属性会被接受，但它们可能会因未使用属性而发出警告。此外，对已知属性的无效"
"输入通常会是警告（详见属性定义）。这样做是为了允许未来添加或丢弃属性以及更改"
"输入，从而允许作出更改，而不需要保持无意义的属性或选项继续可用。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:554
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:555
msgid "The `diagnostic::on_unimplemented` attribute"
msgstr "`diagnostic::on_unimplemented` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:557
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.intro\\] The "
"`#[diagnostic::on_unimplemented]` attribute is a hint to the compiler to "
"supplement the error message that would normally be generated in scenarios "
"where a trait is required but not implemented on a type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.intro\\] "
"`#[diagnostic::on_unimplemented]` 属性是给编译器的提示，用于在需要某个 trait "
"但某个类型未实现它的场景中，补充通常会生成的错误消息。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:560
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.allowed-positions\\] The "
"attribute should be placed on a [trait declaration](../items/traits.md), "
"though it is not an error to be located in other positions."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.allowed-positions\\] 该属性应放在 "
"[trait 声明](../items/traits.md)上，不过位于其他位置也不是错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:563
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.syntax\\] The attribute uses the "
"\\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] syntax to specify its inputs, though any "
"malformed input to the attribute is not considered as an error to provide "
"both forwards and backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.syntax\\] 该属性使用 \\"
"[MetaListNameValueStr\\] 语法指定其输入，不过为同时提供向前和向后兼容性，任何"
"格式错误的属性输入都不被视为错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:566
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.keys\\] The following keys have "
"the given meaning:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.keys\\] 以下键具有给定含义："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:568
msgid "`message` --- The text for the top level error message."
msgstr "`message` --- 顶层错误消息的文本。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:569
msgid ""
"`label` --- The text for the label shown inline in the broken code in the "
"error message."
msgstr "`label` --- 错误消息中在出错代码内联显示的标签文本。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:570
msgid "`note` --- Provides additional notes."
msgstr "`note` --- 提供附加注释。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:572
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.note-repetition\\] The `note` "
"option can appear several times, which results in several note messages "
"being emitted."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.note-repetition\\] `note` 选项可以"
"出现多次，这会导致发出多条 note 消息。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:575
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.repetition\\] If any of the other "
"options appears several times the first occurrence of the relevant option "
"specifies the actually used value. Subsequent occurrences generates a "
"warning."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.repetition\\] 如果任何其他选项出现"
"多次，相关选项的第一次出现指定实际使用的值。后续出现会生成警告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:578
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.unknown-keys\\] A warning is "
"generated for any unknown keys."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.unknown-keys\\] 任何未知键都会生成"
"警告。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:581
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.format-string\\] All three "
"options accept a string as an argument, interpreted using the same "
"formatting as a \\[`std::fmt`\\] string."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.format-string\\] 三个选项都接受字"
"符串作为实参，并使用与 \\[`std::fmt`\\] 字符串相同的格式化方式解释。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:584
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.format-parameters\\] Format "
"parameters with the given named parameter will be replaced with the "
"following text:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.format-parameters\\] 带有给定命名"
"参数的格式参数会被替换为以下文本："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:586
msgid "`{Self}` --- The name of the type implementing the trait."
msgstr "`{Self}` --- 实现该 trait 的类型名称。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:587
msgid ""
"`{` _GenericParameterName_ `}` --- The name of the generic argument's type "
"for the given generic parameter."
msgstr ""
"`{` _GenericParameterName_ `}` --- 给定泛型参数对应的泛型实参类型名称。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:589
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.invalid-formats\\] Any other "
"format parameter will generate a warning, but will otherwise be included in "
"the string as-is."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.invalid-formats\\] 任何其他格式参"
"数都会生成警告，但除此之外会按原样包含在字符串中。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:592
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.invalid-string\\] Invalid format "
"strings may generate a warning, but are otherwise allowed, but may not "
"display as intended. Format specifiers may generate a warning, but are "
"otherwise ignored."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.on_unimplemented.invalid-string\\] 无效的格式字符串"
"可能生成警告，但除此之外是允许的，不过可能不会按预期显示。格式说明符可能生成"
"警告，但除此之外会被忽略。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:600
msgid "\"My Message for `ImportantTrait<{A}>` implemented for `{Self}`\""
msgstr "\"My Message for `ImportantTrait<{A}>` implemented for `{Self}`\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:601
msgid "\"My Label\""
msgstr "\"My Label\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:602
msgid "\"Note 1\""
msgstr "\"Note 1\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:603
msgid "\"Note 2\""
msgstr "\"Note 2\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:614
msgid "the compiler may generate an error message which looks like this:"
msgstr "编译器可能生成如下所示的错误消息："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:630
msgid "r\\[attributes.diagnostic.do_not_recommend\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.diagnostic.do_not_recommend\\]"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:631
msgid "The `diagnostic::do_not_recommend` attribute"
msgstr "`diagnostic::do_not_recommend` 属性"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:633
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.do_not_recommend.intro\\] The "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` attribute is a hint to the compiler to not "
"show the annotated trait implementation as part of a diagnostic message."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.do_not_recommend.intro\\] "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` 属性是给编译器的提示，使其不要将带注解的 "
"trait 实现作为诊断消息的一部分显示。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:636
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Suppressing the recommendation can be useful if you know that "
"the recommendation would normally not be useful to the programmer. This "
"often occurs with broad, blanket impls. The recommendation may send the "
"programmer down the wrong path, or the trait implementation may be an "
"internal detail that you don't want to expose, or the bounds may not be able "
"to be satisfied by the programmer."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 如果你知道推荐通常对程序员没有用，抑制该推荐可能很有用。这经常发"
"生在宽泛的 blanket impl 中。推荐可能会把程序员引向错误方向，或者该 trait 实现"
"可能是你不想暴露的内部细节，或者程序员可能无法满足这些约束。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:639
msgid ""
"For example, in an error message about a type not implementing a required "
"trait, the compiler may find a trait implementation that would satisfy the "
"requirements if it weren't for specific bounds in the trait implementation. "
"The compiler may tell the user that there is an impl, but the problem is the "
"bounds in the trait implementation. The `#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` "
"attribute can be used to tell the compiler to _not_ tell the user about the "
"trait implementation, and instead simply tell the user the type doesn't "
"implement the required trait."
msgstr ""
"例如，在关于某个类型未实现所需 trait 的错误消息中，编译器可能找到一个 trait "
"实现：如果不是该 trait 实现中的特定约束，它本可以满足要求。编译器可能告诉用户"
"存在一个 impl，但问题在于该 trait 实现中的约束。可以使用 "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` 属性告诉编译器 *不要* 把该 trait 实现告诉用"
"户，而只是告诉用户该类型没有实现所需 trait。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:641
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.do_not_recommend.allowed-positions\\] The "
"attribute should be placed on a [trait implementation item](../items/"
"implementations.md#trait-implementations), though it is not an error to be "
"located in other positions."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.do_not_recommend.allowed-positions\\] 该属性应放在 "
"[trait 实现项](../items/implementations.md#trait-implementations)上，不过位于"
"其他位置也不是错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:644
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.do_not_recommend.syntax\\] The attribute does not "
"accept any arguments, though unexpected arguments are not considered as an "
"error."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.diagnostic.do_not_recommend.syntax\\] 该属性不接受任何实参，不"
"过非预期实参不被视为错误。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:647
msgid ""
"In the following example, there is a trait called `AsExpression` which is "
"used for casting arbitrary types to the `Expression` type used in an SQL "
"library. There is a method called `check` which takes an `AsExpression`."
msgstr ""
"在下面的示例中，有一个名为 `AsExpression` 的 trait，用于把任意类型转换为 SQL "
"库中使用的 `Expression` 类型。有一个名为 `check` 的方法，它接受一个 "
"`AsExpression`。"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:681
msgid ""
"// Uncomment this line to change the recommendation.\n"
"// #[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]\n"
msgstr ""
"// 取消注释此行以更改推荐。\n"
"// #[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]\n"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:701 src/types/closure.md:446
#: src/types/closure.md:462 src/types/closure.md:754 src/types/closure.md:833
msgid "\"bar\""
msgstr "\"bar\""

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:705
msgid ""
"The `SelectInt` type's `check` method is expecting an `Integer` type. "
"Calling it with an i32 type works, as it gets converted to an `Integer` by "
"the `AsExpression` trait. However, calling it with a string does not, and "
"generates a an error that may look like this:"
msgstr ""
"`SelectInt` 类型的 `check` 方法期望一个 `Integer` 类型。用 i32 类型调用它可以"
"工作，因为该值会通过 `AsExpression` trait 转换为 `Integer`。然而，用字符串调"
"用它则不行，并会生成一个可能如下所示的错误："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:707
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"error[E0277]: the trait bound `&str: Expression` is not satisfied\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:53:15\n"
"   |\n"
"53 |     SelectInt.check(\"bar\");\n"
"   |               ^^^^^ the trait `Expression` is not implemented for "
"`&str`\n"
"   |\n"
"   = help: the following other types implement trait `Expression`:\n"
"             Bound<T>\n"
"             SelectInt\n"
"note: required for `&str` to implement `AsExpression<Integer>`\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:45:13\n"
"   |\n"
"45 | impl<T, ST> AsExpression<ST> for T\n"
"   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^     ^\n"
"46 | where\n"
"47 |     T: Expression<SqlType = ST>,\n"
"   |        ------------------------ unsatisfied trait bound introduced "
"here\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"error[E0277]: the trait bound `&str: Expression` is not satisfied\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:53:15\n"
"   |\n"
"53 |     SelectInt.check(\"bar\");\n"
"   |               ^^^^^ the trait `Expression` is not implemented for "
"`&str`\n"
"   |\n"
"   = help: the following other types implement trait `Expression`:\n"
"             Bound<T>\n"
"             SelectInt\n"
"note: required for `&str` to implement `AsExpression<Integer>`\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:45:13\n"
"   |\n"
"45 | impl<T, ST> AsExpression<ST> for T\n"
"   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^     ^\n"
"46 | where\n"
"47 |     T: Expression<SqlType = ST>,\n"
"   |        ------------------------ unsatisfied trait bound introduced "
"here\n"
"```"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:727
msgid ""
"By adding the `#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` attribute to the blanket "
"`impl` for `AsExpression`, the message changes to:"
msgstr ""
"通过向 `AsExpression` 的 blanket `impl` 添加 "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` 属性，消息会变为："

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:729
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"error[E0277]: the trait bound `&str: AsExpression<Integer>` is not "
"satisfied\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:53:15\n"
"   |\n"
"53 |     SelectInt.check(\"bar\");\n"
"   |               ^^^^^ the trait `AsExpression<Integer>` is not "
"implemented for `&str`\n"
"   |\n"
"   = help: the trait `AsExpression<Integer>` is not implemented for `&str`\n"
"           but trait `AsExpression<Text>` is implemented for it\n"
"   = help: for that trait implementation, expected `Text`, found `Integer`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"error[E0277]: the trait bound `&str: AsExpression<Integer>` is not "
"satisfied\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:53:15\n"
"   |\n"
"53 |     SelectInt.check(\"bar\");\n"
"   |               ^^^^^ the trait `AsExpression<Integer>` is not "
"implemented for `&str`\n"
"   |\n"
"   = help: the trait `AsExpression<Integer>` is not implemented for `&str`\n"
"           but trait `AsExpression<Text>` is implemented for it\n"
"   = help: for that trait implementation, expected `Text`, found `Integer`\n"
"```"

#: src/attributes/diagnostics.md:741
msgid ""
"The first error message includes a somewhat confusing error message about "
"the relationship of `&str` and `Expression`, as well as the unsatisfied "
"trait bound in the blanket impl. After adding "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]`, it no longer considers the blanket impl "
"for the recommendation. The message should be a little clearer, with an "
"indication that a string cannot be converted to an `Integer`."
msgstr ""
"第一条错误消息包含一段有些令人困惑的错误消息，涉及 `&str` 与 `Expression` 的"
"关系，以及 blanket impl 中未满足的 trait 约束。添加 "
"`#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` 后，它在推荐中不再考虑该 blanket impl。该消"
"息应该会清楚一些，并指出字符串不能转换为 `Integer`。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:1
msgid "r\\[attributes.codegen\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen\\]"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:2
msgid "Code generation attributes"
msgstr "代码生成属性"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:4
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) are used for controlling code "
"generation."
msgstr "以下[属性](../attributes.md)用于控制代码生成。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:7
msgid "r\\[attributes.codegen.inline\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.inline\\]"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:8
msgid "The `inline` attribute"
msgstr "`inline` 属性"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.intro\\] The _`inline` [attribute](../"
"attributes.md)_ suggests whether a copy of the attributed function's code "
"should be placed in the caller rather than generating a call to the function."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.intro\\] *`inline` [属性](../attributes.md)* 建"
"议是否应将带属性函数的代码副本放置到调用者中，而不是生成对该函数的调用。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:25
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` automatically inlines functions when doing so seems "
"worthwhile. Use this attribute carefully as poor decisions about what to "
"inline can slow down programs."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 会在认为值得时自动内联函数。请谨慎使用此属性，因为对内联"
"内容作出不佳决策可能会让程序变慢。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:28
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.syntax\\] The syntax for the `inline` "
"attribute is:"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.syntax\\] `inline` 属性的语法为："

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:38
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.allowed-positions\\] The `inline` attribute "
"may only be applied to functions with [bodies](items.fn.body) --- [closures]"
"(expr.closure), [async blocks](expr.block.async), [free functions]"
"(items.fn), [associated functions](items.associated.fn) in an [inherent impl]"
"(items.impl.inherent) or [trait impl](items.impl.trait), and associated "
"functions in a [trait definition](items.traits) when those functions have a "
"[default definition](items.traits.associated-item-decls) ."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.allowed-positions\\] `inline` 属性只能应用于具"
"有[函数体](items.fn.body)的函数 --- [闭包](expr.closure)、[async 块]"
"(expr.block.async)、[自由函数](items.fn)、[固有 impl](items.impl.inherent) "
"或 [trait impl](items.impl.trait) 中的[关联函数](items.associated.fn)，以及 "
"[trait 定义](items.traits)中那些具有[默认定义](items.traits.associated-item-"
"decls)的关联函数。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:44 src/attributes/codegen.md:108
#: src/attributes/codegen.md:874
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Though the attribute can be applied to [closures](expr.closure) "
"and [async blocks](expr.block.async), the usefulness of this is limited as "
"we do not yet support attributes on expressions."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 尽管该属性可以应用于[闭包](expr.closure)和[async 块]"
"(expr.block.async)，但其用途有限，因为我们尚不支持在表达式上使用属性。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:48
msgid "// We allow attributes on statements.\n"
msgstr "// 我们允许语句上有属性。\n"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:54
msgid "// We don't yet allow attributes on expressions.\n"
msgstr "// 我们尚不允许表达式上有属性。\n"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:58
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.duplicates\\] Only the first use of `inline` "
"on a function has effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.duplicates\\] 在一个函数上，只有第一次使用 "
"`inline` 会产生效果。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:64
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.modes\\] The `inline` attribute supports these "
"modes:"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.modes\\] `inline` 属性支持以下模式："

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:67
msgid "`#[inline]` _suggests_ performing inline expansion."
msgstr "`#[inline]` *建议*执行内联展开。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:68
msgid ""
"`#[inline(always)]` _suggests_ that inline expansion should always be "
"performed."
msgstr "`#[inline(always)]` *建议*始终执行内联展开。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:69
msgid ""
"`#[inline(never)]` _suggests_ that inline expansion should never be "
"performed."
msgstr "`#[inline(never)]` *建议*永不执行内联展开。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:71
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] In every form the attribute is a hint. The compiler may ignore "
"it."
msgstr "\\[!NOTE\\] 无论是哪种形式，该属性都是一种提示。编译器可以忽略它。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:74
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.trait\\] When `inline` is applied to a "
"function in a [trait](items.traits), it applies only to the code of the "
"[default definition](items.traits.associated-item-decls)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.trait\\] 当 `inline` 应用于 [trait]"
"(items.traits) 中的函数时，它只应用于[默认定义](items.traits.associated-item-"
"decls)的代码。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:77
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.async\\] When `inline` is applied to an [async "
"function](items.fn.async) or [async closure](expr.closure.async), it applies "
"only to the code of the generated `poll` function."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.async\\] 当 `inline` 应用于 [async 函数]"
"(items.fn.async)或 [async 闭包](expr.closure.async)时，它只应用于生成的 "
"`poll` 函数的代码。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:80
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] For more details, see [Rust issue #129347](https://github.com/"
"rust-lang/rust/issues/129347)."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 更多细节见 [Rust issue #129347](https://github.com/rust-lang/"
"rust/issues/129347)。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:83
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.externally-exported\\] The `inline` attribute "
"is ignored if the function is externally exported with [`no_mangle`]"
"(abi.no_mangle) or [`export_name`](abi.export_name)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.inline.externally-exported\\] 如果函数通过 "
"[`no_mangle`](abi.no_mangle) 或 [`export_name`](abi.export_name) 对外导出，"
"则 `inline` 属性会被忽略。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:87
msgid "r\\[attributes.codegen.cold\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.cold\\]"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:88
