"运行时使用标准库中平台特定的宏进行检查，例如 [`is_x86_feature_detected`]"
"(../../std/arch/macro.is_x86_feature_detected.html) 或 "
"[`is_aarch64_feature_detected`](../../std/arch/"
"macro.is_aarch64_feature_detected.html)。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:733
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` has a default set of features enabled for each target "
"and CPU. The CPU may be chosen with the [`-C target-cpu`](../../rustc/"
"codegen-options/index.html#target-cpu) flag. Individual features may be "
"enabled or disabled for an entire crate with the [`-C target-feature`](../../"
"rustc/codegen-options/index.html#target-feature) flag."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 会为每个目标和 CPU 默认启用一组特性。可以使用 [`-C "
"target-cpu`](../../rustc/codegen-options/index.html#target-cpu) 标志选择 "
"CPU。还可以使用 [`-C target-feature`](../../rustc/codegen-options/"
"index.html#target-feature) 标志为整个 crate 启用或禁用单独的特性。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:736
msgid "r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller\\]"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:737
msgid "The `track_caller` attribute"
msgstr "`track_caller` 属性"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:739
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.allowed-positions\\] The `track_caller` "
"attribute may be applied to any function with [`\"Rust\"` ABI](../items/"
"external-blocks.md#abi) with the exception of the entry point `fn main`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.allowed-positions\\] `track_caller` 属性"
"可以应用于任何具有 [`\"Rust\"` ABI](../items/external-blocks.md#abi) 的函数，"
"但入口点 `fn main` 除外。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:743
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.traits\\] When applied to functions and "
"methods in trait declarations, the attribute applies to all implementations. "
"If the trait provides a default implementation with the attribute, then the "
"attribute also applies to override implementations."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.traits\\] 当该属性应用于 trait 声明中的函"
"数和方法时，它会适用于所有实现。如果该 trait 提供了带有该属性的默认实现，那么"
"该属性也适用于覆盖实现。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:747
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.extern\\] When applied to a function in "
"an `extern` block the attribute must also be applied to any linked "
"implementations, otherwise undefined behavior results. When applied to a "
"function which is made available to an `extern` block, the declaration in "
"the `extern` block must also have the attribute, otherwise undefined "
"behavior results."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.extern\\] 当该属性应用于 `extern` 块中的"
"函数时，任何链接到的实现也必须应用该属性，否则会导致未定义行为。当该属性应用"
"于某个向 `extern` 块提供的函数时，`extern` 块中的声明也必须带有该属性，否则会"
"导致未定义行为。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:753
msgid "r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.behavior\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.behavior\\]"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:754
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr "行为"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:756
msgid ""
"Applying the attribute to a function `f` allows code within `f` to get a "
"hint of the [`Location`](core::panic::Location) of the \"topmost\" tracked "
"call that led to `f`'s invocation. At the point of observation, an "
"implementation behaves as if it walks up the stack from `f`'s frame to find "
"the nearest frame of an _unattributed_ function `outer`, and it returns the "
"[`Location`](core::panic::Location) of the tracked call in `outer`."
msgstr ""
"将该属性应用于函数 `f` 后，`f` 内部的代码便可以获得导致调用 `f` 的“最顶层”已"
"追踪调用的 [`Location`](core::panic::Location) 提示。在观察点上，某个实现的行"
"为如同它从 `f` 的栈帧向上遍历调用栈，找到最近的未带属性函数 `outer` 的栈帧，"
"并返回 `outer` 中该已追踪调用的 [`Location`](core::panic::Location)。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:768
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `core` provides \\[`core::panic::Location::caller`\\] for "
"observing caller locations. It wraps the \\"
"[`core::intrinsics::caller_location`\\] intrinsic implemented by `rustc`."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `core` 提供了 \\[`core::panic::Location::caller`\\] 用于观测调用"
"者位置。它封装了由 `rustc` 实现的 \\[`core::intrinsics::caller_location`\\] "
"内在函数。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:771
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Because the resulting `Location` is a hint, an implementation "
"may halt its walk up the stack early. See [Limitations](#limitations) for "
"important caveats."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 由于得到的 `Location` 只是一个提示，实现可以提前停止向上遍历调用"
"栈。重要注意事项请参见[限制](#limitations)。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:776
msgid ""
"When `f` is called directly by `calls_f`, code in `f` observes its callsite "
"within `calls_f`:"
msgstr ""
"`calls_f` 直接调用 `f` 时，`f` 中的代码会观测到它在 `calls_f` 中的调用位置："

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:784
msgid "// <-- f() prints this location\n"
msgstr "// <-- f() 打印此位置\n"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:788
msgid ""
"When `f` is called by another attributed function `g` which is in turn "
"called by `calls_g`, code in both `f` and `g` observes `g`'s callsite within "
"`calls_g`:"
msgstr ""
"当 `f` 由另一个带属性的函数 `g` 调用，而 `g` 又由 `calls_g` 调用时，`f` 和 "
"`g` 中的代码都会观测到 `g` 在 `calls_g` 中的调用位置："

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:803
msgid "// <-- g() prints this location twice, once itself and once from f()\n"
msgstr "// <-- g() 打印此位置两次：一次来自自身，一次来自 f()\n"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:807
msgid ""
"When `g` is called by another attributed function `h` which is in turn "
"called by `calls_h`, all code in `f`, `g`, and `h` observes `h`'s callsite "
"within `calls_h`:"
msgstr ""
"当 `g` 由另一个带属性的函数 `h` 调用，而 `h` 又由 `calls_h` 调用时，`f`、`g` "
"和 `h` 中的所有代码都会观测到 `h` 在 `calls_h` 中的调用位置："

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:827
msgid ""
"// <-- prints this location three times, once itself, once from g(), once "
"from f()\n"
msgstr "// <-- 打印此位置三次：一次来自自身，一次来自 g()，一次来自 f()\n"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:831
msgid "And so on."
msgstr "以此类推。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:833
msgid "r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.limits\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.limits\\]"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:834 src/types/impl-trait.md:166
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr "限制"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:836
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.hint\\] This information is a hint and "
"implementations are not required to preserve it."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.hint\\] 该信息只是提示，实现不必保留它。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:839
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.decay\\] In particular, coercing a "
"function with `#[track_caller]` to a function pointer creates a shim which "
"appears to observers to have been called at the attributed function's "
"definition site, losing actual caller information across virtual calls. A "
"common example of this coercion is the creation of a trait object whose "
"methods are attributed."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.track_caller.decay\\] 尤其是，将带有 "
"`#[track_caller]` 的函数强制转换为函数指针时，会创建一个 shim；对观察者来说，"
"它似乎是在该带属性函数的定义位置被调用的，从而在虚调用间丢失实际的调用者信"
"息。这种强制转换的一个常见例子，是创建其方法带有该属性的 trait 对象。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:845
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The aforementioned shim for function pointers is necessary "
"because `rustc` implements `track_caller` in a codegen context by appending "
"an implicit parameter to the function ABI, but this would be unsound for an "
"indirect call because the parameter is not a part of the function's type and "
"a given function pointer type may or may not refer to a function with the "
"attribute. The creation of a shim hides the implicit parameter from callers "
"of the function pointer, preserving soundness."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 上述用于函数指针的 shim 是必要的，因为 `rustc` 在代码生成上下文中"
"通过向函数 ABI 追加一个隐式参数来实现 `track_caller`，但这对于间接调用来说是"
"不健全的，因为该参数不是函数类型的一部分，而给定的函数指针类型既可能引用带有"
"该属性的函数，也可能不引用。创建 shim 会向函数指针的调用者隐藏这个隐式参数，"
"从而保持健全性。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:849
msgid "r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set\\]"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:850
msgid "The `instruction_set` attribute"
msgstr "`instruction_set` 属性"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:852
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.intro\\] The _`instruction_set` "
"[attribute](../attributes.md)_ specifies the instruction set that a function "
"will use during code generation. This allows mixing more than one "
"instruction set in a single program."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.intro\\] *`instruction_set` [属性](../"
"attributes.md)* 指定函数在代码生成期间将使用的指令集。这允许在单个程序中混用"
"多种指令集。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:865
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.syntax\\] The `instruction_set` "
"attribute uses the \\[MetaListPaths\\] syntax to specify a single path "
"consisting of the architecture family name and instruction set name."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.syntax\\] `instruction_set` 属性使用 "
"\\[MetaListPaths\\] 语法来指定单一路径，该路径由架构族名称和指令集名称组成。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:868
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.allowed-positions\\] The "
"`instruction_set` attribute may only be applied to functions with [bodies]"
"(items.fn.body) --- [closures](expr.closure), [async blocks]"
"(expr.block.async), [free functions](items.fn), [associated functions]"
"(items.associated.fn) in an [inherent impl](items.impl.inherent) or [trait "
"impl](items.impl.trait), and associated functions in a [trait definition]"
"(items.traits) when those functions have a [default definition]"
"(items.traits.associated-item-decls) ."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.allowed-positions\\] "
"`instruction_set` 属性只能应用于具有[函数体](items.fn.body)的函数 --- [闭包]"
"(expr.closure)、[async 块](expr.block.async)、[自由函数](items.fn)、[固有 "
"impl](items.impl.inherent) 或 [trait impl](items.impl.trait) 中的[关联函数]"
"(items.associated.fn)，以及 [trait 定义](items.traits)中那些具有[默认定义]"
"(items.traits.associated-item-decls)的关联函数。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:877
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.duplicates\\] The `instruction_set` "
"attribute may be used only once on a function."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.duplicates\\] `instruction_set` 属性在"
"一个函数上只能使用一次。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:880
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.target-limits\\] The "
"`instruction_set` attribute may only be used with a target that supports the "
"given value."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.target-limits\\] `instruction_set` 属"
"性只能用于支持给定值的目标。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:883
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.inline-asm\\] When the "
"`instruction_set` attribute is used, any inline assembly in the function "
"must use the specified instruction set instead of the target default."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.inline-asm\\] 当使用 "
"`instruction_set` 属性时，函数中的任何内联汇编都必须使用指定的指令集，而不是"
"目标默认指令集。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:886
msgid "r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.arm\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.codegen.instruction_set.arm\\]"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:887
msgid "`instruction_set` on ARM"
msgstr "ARM 上的 `instruction_set`"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:889
msgid ""
"When targeting the `ARMv4T` and `ARMv5te` architectures, the supported "
"values for `instruction_set` are:"
msgstr "以 `ARMv4T` 和 `ARMv5te` 架构为目标时，`instruction_set` 支持的值为："

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:891
msgid "`arm::a32` --- Generate the function as A32 \"ARM\" code."
msgstr "`arm::a32` --- 将函数生成为 A32 “ARM” 代码。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:892
msgid "`arm::t32` --- Generate the function as T32 \"Thumb\" code."
msgstr "`arm::t32` --- 将函数生成为 T32 “Thumb” 代码。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:894
msgid ""
"If the address of the function is taken as a function pointer, the low bit "
"of the address will depend on the selected instruction set:"
msgstr "如果取出该函数的地址作为函数指针，则地址的最低位将取决于所选的指令集："

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:896
msgid "For `arm::a32` (\"ARM\"), it will be 0."
msgstr "对于 `arm::a32`（“ARM”），它将为 0。"

#: src/attributes/codegen.md:897
msgid "For `arm::t32` (\"Thumb\"), it will be 1."
msgstr "对于 `arm::t32`（“Thumb”），它将为 1。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:1
msgid "r\\[attributes.limits\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.limits\\]"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:4
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) affect compile-time limits."
msgstr "以下[属性](../attributes.md)会影响编译时限制。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:6
msgid "r\\[attributes.limits.recursion_limit\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.limits.recursion_limit\\]"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:7
msgid "The `recursion_limit` attribute"
msgstr "`recursion_limit` 属性"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.recursion_limit.intro\\] The _`recursion_limit` "
"attribute_ may be applied at the [crate](../crates-and-source-files.md) "
"level to set the maximum depth for potentially infinitely-recursive compile-"
"time operations like macro expansion or auto-dereference."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.recursion_limit.intro\\] *`recursion_limit` 属性*可以应"
"用于 [crate](../crates-and-source-files.md) 级别，用于为宏展开或自动解引用等"
"潜在无限递归的编译时操作设置最大深度。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:14
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.recursion_limit.syntax\\] It uses the \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntax to specify the recursion depth."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.recursion_limit.syntax\\] 它使用 \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] 语法来指定递归深度。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:18
msgid "\\[!NOTE\\] The default in `rustc` is 128."
msgstr "\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 中的默认值是 128。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:22 src/attributes/limits.md:58
msgid "\"4\""
msgstr "\"4\""

#: src/attributes/limits.md:31
msgid ""
"// This fails to expand because it requires a recursion depth greater than "
"4.\n"
msgstr "// 这会展开失败，因为它需要大于 4 的递归深度。\n"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:37 src/destructors.md:136
msgid "\"1\""
msgstr "\"1\""

#: src/attributes/limits.md:38
msgid ""
"// This fails because it requires two recursive steps to auto-dereference.\n"
msgstr "// 这会失败，因为它需要两个递归步骤才能自动解引用。\n"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:44
msgid "r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit\\]"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:45
msgid "The `type_length_limit` attribute"
msgstr "`type_length_limit` 属性"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:47
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit.intro\\] The _`type_length_limit` "
"[attribute](../attributes.md)_ sets the maximum number of type substitutions "
"allowed when constructing a concrete type during monomorphization."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit.intro\\] *`type_length_limit` [属性]"
"(../attributes.md)* 设置在单态化期间构造具体类型时允许的类型替换最大数量。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:50
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` only enforces the limit when the nightly `-Zenforce-type-"
"length-limit` flag is active."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 只有在 nightly `-Zenforce-type-length-limit` 标志启用时，`rustc` "
"才会强制执行该限制。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:53
msgid ""
"For more information, see [Rust PR #127670](https://github.com/rust-lang/"
"rust/pull/127670)."
msgstr ""
"更多信息见 [Rust PR #127670](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/127670)。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:62
msgid "// This fails to compile because monomorphizing to\n"
msgstr "// 这会编译失败，因为单态化为\n"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:63
msgid "// `f::<((((i32,), i32), i32), i32)>` requires more\n"
msgstr "// `f::<((((i32,), i32), i32), i32)>` 需要超过 4 个\n"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:64
msgid "// than 4 type elements.\n"
msgstr "// 类型元素。\n"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:68
msgid "\\[!NOTE\\] The default value in `rustc` is `1048576`."
msgstr "\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 中的默认值是 `1048576`。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:71
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit.syntax\\] The `type_length_limit` "
"attribute uses the \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntax. The value in the string "
"must be a non-negative number."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit.syntax\\] `type_length_limit` 属性使"
"用 \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] 语法。字符串中的值必须是非负数。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:74
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit.allowed-positions\\] The "
"`type_length_limit` attribute may only be applied to the crate root."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit.allowed-positions\\] "
"`type_length_limit` 属性只能应用于 crate 根。"

#: src/attributes/limits.md:80
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit.duplicates\\] Only the first use of "
"`type_length_limit` on an item has effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.limits.type_length_limit.duplicates\\] 在一个项上，只有第一次"
"使用 `type_length_limit` 会生效。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:1
msgid "r\\[attributes.type-system\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.type-system\\]"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:2
msgid "Type system attributes"
msgstr "类型系统属性"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:4
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) are used for changing how a "
"type can be used."
msgstr "以下[属性](../attributes.md)用于改变类型可以如何被使用。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:6
msgid "r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive\\]"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:7
msgid "The `non_exhaustive` attribute"
msgstr "`non_exhaustive` 属性"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.intro\\] The _`non_exhaustive` "
"attribute_ indicates that a type or variant may have more fields or variants "
"added in the future."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.intro\\] *`non_exhaustive` 属性*表"
"示一个类型或变体将来可能会添加更多字段或变体。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.allowed-positions\\] It can be "
"applied to [`struct`s](../items/structs.md), [`enum`s](../items/"
"enumerations.md), and `enum` variants."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.allowed-positions\\] 它可以应用于 "
"[`struct`](../items/structs.md)、[`enum`](../items/enumerations.md) 和 "
"`enum` 变体。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.syntax\\] The `non_exhaustive` "
"attribute uses the \\[MetaWord\\] syntax and thus does not take any inputs."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.syntax\\] `non_exhaustive` 属性使"
"用 \\[MetaWord\\] 语法，因此不接受任何输入。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:20
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.same-crate\\] Within the defining "
"crate, `non_exhaustive` has no effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.same-crate\\] 在定义它的 crate 内，"
"`non_exhaustive` 没有效果。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:47
msgid ""
"// Non-exhaustive structs can be constructed as normal within the defining "
"crate.\n"
msgstr "// 非穷尽结构体可以在定义它的 crate 内照常构造。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:52
msgid ""
"// Non-exhaustive structs can be matched on exhaustively within the defining "
"crate.\n"
msgstr "// 非穷尽结构体可以在定义它的 crate 内被穷尽匹配。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:60
msgid ""
"// Non-exhaustive enums can be matched on exhaustively within the defining "
"crate.\n"
msgstr "// 非穷尽枚举可以在定义它的 crate 内被穷尽匹配。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:68
msgid ""
"// Non-exhaustive variants can be matched on exhaustively within the "
"defining crate.\n"
msgstr "// 非穷尽变体可以在定义它的 crate 内被穷尽匹配。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:75
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.external-crate\\] Outside of the "
"defining crate, types annotated with `non_exhaustive` have limitations that "
"preserve backwards compatibility when new fields or variants are added."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.external-crate\\] 在定义它的 crate "
"之外，带有 `non_exhaustive` 标注的类型会受到一些限制，以便在添加新字段或变体"
"时保持向后兼容性。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:79
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.construction\\] Non-exhaustive "
"types cannot be constructed outside of the defining crate:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.construction\\] 非穷尽类型不能在定"
"义它的 crate 之外构造："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:82
msgid ""
"Non-exhaustive variants ([`struct`](../items/structs.md) or [`enum` variant]"
"(../items/enumerations.md)) cannot be constructed with a \\"
"[StructExpression\\] (including with [functional update syntax](../"
"expressions/struct-expr.md#functional-update-syntax))."
msgstr ""
"非穷尽变体（[`struct`](../items/structs.md) 或 [`enum` 变体](../items/"
"enumerations.md)）不能用 \\[StructExpression\\] 构造（包括使用[函数式更新语"
"法](../expressions/struct-expr.md#functional-update-syntax)）。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:84
msgid ""
"The implicitly defined same-named constant of a [unit-like struct](../items/"
"structs.md), or the same-named constructor function of a [tuple struct](../"
"items/structs.md), has a [visibility](../visibility-and-privacy.md) no "
"greater than `pub(crate)`. That is, if the struct’s visibility is `pub`, "
"then the constant or constructor’s visibility is `pub(crate)`, and otherwise "
"the visibility of the two items is the same (as is the case without "
"`#[non_exhaustive]`)."
msgstr ""
"隐式定义的 [unit-like struct](../items/structs.md) 的同名常量，或者 [tuple "
"struct](../items/structs.md) 的同名构造函数，具有不大于 `pub(crate)` 的[可见"
"性](../visibility-and-privacy.md)。也就是说，如果该 struct 的可见性是 `pub`，"
"那么该常量或构造函数的可见性就是 `pub(crate)`；否则这两个项的可见性相同（与没"
"有 `#[non_exhaustive]` 时一样）。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:90
msgid "[`enum`](../items/enumerations.md) instances can be constructed."
msgstr "可以构造 [`enum`](../items/enumerations.md) 实例。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:92
msgid ""
"The following examples of construction do not compile when outside the "
"defining crate:"
msgstr "以下构造示例在定义它们的 crate 之外无法编译："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:96 src/attributes/type_system.md:139
msgid ""
"// These are types defined in an upstream crate that have been annotated as\n"
"// `#[non_exhaustive]`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这些类型是在上游 crate 中定义，并被标注为\n"
"// `#[non_exhaustive]`.\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:99
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Config`; if new fields were added in\n"
"// a new version of `upstream` then this would fail to compile, so it is\n"
"// disallowed.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 无法构造 `Config` 的实例；如果在\n"
"// `upstream` 的新版本中添加了新字段，那么这将编译失败，因此\n"
"// 不允许这样做。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:104
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Token`; if new fields were added, then\n"
"// it would not be a unit-like struct any more, so the same-named constant\n"
"// created by it being a unit-like struct is not public outside the crate;\n"
"// this code fails to compile.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 无法构造 `Token` 的实例；如果添加了新字段，那么\n"
"// 它将不再是类单元结构体，因此由其作为类单元结构体而创建的同名常量\n"
"// 在 crate 外部不是公有的；\n"
"// 这段代码编译失败。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:110
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Id`; if new fields were added, then\n"
"// its constructor function signature would change, so its constructor\n"
"// function is not public outside the crate; this code fails to compile.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 无法构造 `Id` 的实例；如果添加了新字段，那么\n"
"// 其构造函数签名将会改变，因此其构造\n"
"// 函数在 crate 外部不是公有的；这段代码编译失败。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:115
msgid ""
"// Can construct an instance of `Error`; new variants being introduced "
"would\n"
"// not result in this failing to compile.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 可以构造 `Error` 的实例；引入新的变体\n"
"// 不会导致这段代码编译失败。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:119
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Message::Send` or `Message::Reaction`;\n"
"// if new fields were added in a new version of `upstream` then this would\n"
"// fail to compile, so it is disallowed.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 无法构造 `Message::Send` 或 `Message::Reaction` 的实例；\n"
"// 如果在 `upstream` 的新版本中添加了新字段，那么这将\n"
"// 编译失败，因此不允许这样做。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:125
msgid ""
"// Cannot construct an instance of `Message::Quit`; if this were converted "
"to\n"
"// a tuple enum variant `upstream`, this would fail to compile.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 无法构造 `Message::Quit` 的实例；如果将其转换为\n"
"// `upstream` 中的元组枚举变体，这将编译失败。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:131
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.match\\] There are limitations "
"when matching on non-exhaustive types outside of the defining crate:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive.match\\] 在定义它们的 crate 之外对"
"非穷尽类型进行匹配时存在一些限制："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:134
msgid ""
"When pattern matching on a non-exhaustive variant ([`struct`](../items/"
"structs.md) or [`enum` variant](../items/enumerations.md)), a \\"
"[StructPattern\\] must be used which must include a `..`. A tuple enum "
"variant's constructor's [visibility](../visibility-and-privacy.md) is "
"reduced to be no greater than `pub(crate)`."
msgstr ""
"对非穷尽变体（[`struct`](../items/structs.md) 或 [`enum` 变体](../items/"
"enumerations.md)）进行模式匹配时，必须使用包含 `..` 的 \\[StructPattern\\]。"
"元组 enum 变体的构造函数的[可见性](../visibility-and-privacy.md)会降低到不大"
"于 `pub(crate)`。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:135
msgid ""
"When pattern matching on a non-exhaustive [`enum`](../items/"
"enumerations.md), matching on a variant does not contribute towards the "
"exhaustiveness of the arms. The following examples of matching do not "
"compile when outside the defining crate:"
msgstr ""
"对非穷尽 [`enum`](../items/enumerations.md) 进行模式匹配时，匹配某个变体不会"
"有助于分支的穷尽性。以下匹配示例在定义它们的 crate 之外无法编译："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:142
msgid ""
"// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive enum without including a wildcard arm.\n"
msgstr "// 如果不包含通配符分支，则无法匹配非穷尽 enum。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:147
msgid "// would compile with: `_ => {},`\n"
msgstr "// 使用 `_ => {},` 则会编译通过\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:149
msgid "// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive struct without a wildcard.\n"
msgstr "// 如果没有通配符，则无法匹配非穷尽 struct。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:152
msgid "// would compile with: `..`\n"
msgstr "// 使用 `..` 则会编译通过\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:154
msgid ""
"// Cannot match a non-exhaustive unit-like or tuple struct except by using\n"
"// braced struct syntax with a wildcard.\n"
"// This would compile as `let Token { .. } = token;`\n"
msgstr ""
"// 除非使用带通配符的大括号 struct 语法，否则无法匹配\n"
"// 非穷尽的类单元 struct 或元组 struct。\n"
"// 写成 `let Token { .. } = token;` 则会编译通过\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:158
msgid "// This would compile as `let Id { 0: id_number, .. } = id;`\n"
msgstr "// 写成 `let Id { 0: id_number, .. } = id;` 则会编译通过\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:163
msgid ""
"// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive struct enum variant without including a "
"wildcard.\n"
msgstr "// 如果不包含通配符，则无法匹配非穷尽的结构体式 enum 变体。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:165
msgid "// Cannot match on a non-exhaustive tuple or unit enum variant.\n"
msgstr "// 无法匹配非穷尽的元组或类单元 enum 变体。\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:171
msgid ""
"It's also not allowed to use numeric casts (`as`) on enums that contain any "
"non-exhaustive variants."
msgstr "也不允许对包含任何非穷尽变体的 enum 使用数值转换（`as`）。"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:173
msgid ""
"For example, the following enum can be cast because it doesn't contain any "
"non-exhaustive variants:"
msgstr "例如，以下 enum 可以转换，因为它不包含任何非穷尽变体："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:183
msgid ""
"However, if the enum contains even a single non-exhaustive variant, casting "
"will result in an error. Consider this modified version of the same enum:"
msgstr ""
"但是，如果 enum 中哪怕只包含一个非穷尽变体，转换也会导致错误。请看同一 enum "
"的这个修改版本："

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:197
msgid ""
"// Error: cannot cast an enum with a non-exhaustive variant when it's "
"defined in another crate\n"
msgstr ""
"// 错误：当 enum 定义在另一个 crate 中且具有非穷尽变体时，不能强制转换该 "
"enum\n"

#: src/attributes/type_system.md:202
msgid ""
"Non-exhaustive types are always considered inhabited in downstream crates."
msgstr "在下游 crate 中，非穷尽类型始终被视为有值。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:1
msgid "r\\[attributes.debugger\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.debugger\\]"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:2
msgid "Debugger attributes"
msgstr "调试器属性"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:4
msgid ""
"The following [attributes](../attributes.md) are used for enhancing the "
"debugging experience when using third-party debuggers like GDB or WinDbg."
msgstr ""
"以下[属性](../attributes.md)用于在使用 GDB 或 WinDbg 等第三方调试器时增强调试"
"体验。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:7
msgid "r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer\\]"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:8
msgid "The `debugger_visualizer` attribute"
msgstr "`debugger_visualizer` 属性"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.intro\\] The "
"_`debugger_visualizer` [attribute](../attributes.md)_ can be used to embed a "
"debugger visualizer file into the debug information. This improves the "
"debugger experience when displaying values."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.intro\\] *`debugger_visualizer` "
"[属性](../attributes.md)*可用于将调试器可视化器文件嵌入到调试信息中。这会改善"
"显示值时的调试器体验。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:16
msgid "\"Example.natvis\""
msgstr "\"Example.natvis\""

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:17
msgid "\"example.py\""
msgstr "\"example.py\""

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:20
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.syntax\\] The "
"`debugger_visualizer` attribute uses the \\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] syntax "
"to specify its inputs. One of the following keys must be specified:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.syntax\\] `debugger_visualizer` "
"属性使用 \\[MetaListNameValueStr\\] 语法来指定其输入。必须指定以下键之一："

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:23
msgid "\\[`natvis_file`\\]\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis\\]"
msgstr ""
"\\[`natvis_file`\\]\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis\\]"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:24
msgid ""
"\\[`gdb_script_file`\\]\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.gdb\\]"
msgstr ""
"\\[`gdb_script_file`\\]\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.gdb\\]"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:26
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.allowed-positions\\] The "
"`debugger_visualizer` attribute may only be applied to a [module](../items/"
"modules.md) or to the crate root."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.allowed-positions\\] "
"`debugger_visualizer` 属性只能应用于[模块](../items/modules.md)或 crate 根。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:29
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.duplicates\\] The "
"`debugger_visualizer` attribute may be used any number of times on a form. "
"All specified visualizer files will be loaded."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.duplicates\\] "
"`debugger_visualizer` 属性可以在一个形式上使用任意次数。所有指定的可视化器文"
"件都会被加载。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:32
msgid "r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis\\]"
msgstr "r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis\\]"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:33
msgid "Using `debugger_visualizer` with Natvis"
msgstr "将 `debugger_visualizer` 与 Natvis 一起使用"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:35
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis.intro\\] Natvis is an XML-"
"based framework for Microsoft debuggers (such as Visual Studio and WinDbg) "
"that uses declarative rules to customize the display of types. For detailed "
"information on the Natvis format, refer to Microsoft's [Natvis documentation]"
"(https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/debugger/create-custom-views-"
"of-native-objects)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis.intro\\] Natvis 是用于 "
"Microsoft 调试器（如 Visual Studio 和 WinDbg）的基于 XML 的框架，它使用声明式"
"规则来自定义类型的显示。有关 Natvis 格式的详细信息，请参阅 Microsoft 的 "
"[Natvis 文档](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/debugger/create-"
"custom-views-of-native-objects)。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:38
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis.msvc\\] This attribute "
"only supports embedding Natvis files on `-windows-msvc` targets."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis.msvc\\] 此属性只支持在 `-"
"windows-msvc` 目标上嵌入 Natvis 文件。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:41
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis.path\\] The path to the "
"Natvis file is specified with the `natvis_file` key, which is a path "
"relative to the source file."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.debugger_visualizer.natvis.path\\] Natvis 文件的路径"
"通过 `natvis_file` 键指定，该路径是相对于源文件的路径。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:46
msgid ""
"```rust ignore\n"
"#![debugger_visualizer(natvis_file = \"Rectangle.natvis\")]\n"
"\n"
"struct FancyRect {\n"
"    x: f32,\n"
"    y: f32,\n"
"    dx: f32,\n"
"    dy: f32,\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn main() {\n"
"    let fancy_rect = FancyRect { x: 10.0, y: 10.0, dx: 5.0, dy: 5.0 };\n"
"    println!(\"set breakpoint here\");\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```rust ignore\n"
