msgstr "\"hello!\""

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:189
msgid ""
"When using a debugger, invoking the `example` macro may appear as though it "
"is calling a function. That is, when you step to the invocation site, it may "
"show the macro invocation rather than the expanded code."
msgstr ""
"使用调试器时，调用 `example` 宏可能看起来像是在调用函数。也就是说，当你单步执"
"行到调用点时，它可能会显示宏调用而不是展开后的代码。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:193
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.syntax\\] The syntax for the "
"`collapse_debuginfo` attribute is:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.syntax\\] `collapse_debuginfo` 属"
"性的语法是："

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:205
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.allowed-positions\\] The "
"`collapse_debuginfo` attribute may only be applied to a [`macro_rules` "
"definition](../macros-by-example.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.allowed-positions\\] "
"`collapse_debuginfo` 属性只能应用于 [`macro_rules` 定义](../macros-by-"
"example.md)。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:208
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.duplicates\\] The "
"`collapse_debuginfo` attribute may used only once on a macro."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.duplicates\\] "
"`collapse_debuginfo` 属性只能在一个宏上使用一次。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:211
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.options\\] The "
"`collapse_debuginfo` attribute accepts these options:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.options\\] `collapse_debuginfo` 属"
"性接受以下选项："

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:214
msgid ""
"`#[collapse_debuginfo(yes)]` --- Code locations in debuginfo are collapsed."
msgstr "`#[collapse_debuginfo(yes)]` --- debuginfo 中的代码位置会被折叠。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:215
msgid ""
"`#[collapse_debuginfo(no)]` --- Code locations in debuginfo are not "
"collapsed."
msgstr "`#[collapse_debuginfo(no)]` --- debuginfo 中的代码位置不会被折叠。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:216
msgid ""
"`#[collapse_debuginfo(external)]` --- Code locations in debuginfo are "
"collapsed only if the macro comes from a different crate."
msgstr ""
"`#[collapse_debuginfo(external)]` --- 只有当宏来自不同的 crate 时，debuginfo "
"中的代码位置才会被折叠。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:218
msgid ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.default\\] The `external` "
"behavior is the default for macros that don't have this attribute unless "
"they are built-in macros. For built-in macros the default is `yes`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[attributes.debugger.collapse_debuginfo.default\\] 对于没有此属性的宏，除"
"非它们是内置宏，否则 `external` 行为是默认行为。对于内置宏，默认值是 `yes`。"

#: src/attributes/debugger.md:221
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` has a [`-C collapse-macro-debuginfo`](../../rustc/"
"codegen-options/index.html#collapse-macro-debuginfo) CLI option to override "
"both the default behavior and the values of any `#[collapse_debuginfo]` "
"attributes."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 有一个 [`-C collapse-macro-debuginfo`](../../rustc/"
"codegen-options/index.html#collapse-macro-debuginfo) CLI 选项，可覆盖默认行为"
"以及任何 `#[collapse_debuginfo]` 属性的值。"

#: src/statements-and-expressions.md:1
msgid "r\\[stmt-expr\\]"
msgstr "r\\[stmt-expr\\]"

#: src/statements-and-expressions.md:4
msgid ""
"Rust is _primarily_ an expression language. This means that most forms of "
"value-producing or effect-causing evaluation are directed by the uniform "
"syntax category of _expressions_. Each kind of expression can typically "
"_nest_ within each other kind of expression, and rules for evaluation of "
"expressions involve specifying both the value produced by the expression and "
"the order in which its sub-expressions are themselves evaluated."
msgstr ""
"Rust *主要*是一门表达式语言。这意味着，大多数产生值或造成效果的求值形式都由统"
"一的*表达式*语法类别来指导。每一种表达式通常都可以*嵌套*在其他每一种表达式之"
"内，而表达式的求值规则需要同时规定该表达式产生的值，以及其子表达式自身被求值"
"的顺序。"

#: src/statements-and-expressions.md:6
msgid ""
"In contrast, statements serve _mostly_ to contain and explicitly sequence "
"expression evaluation."
msgstr "相比之下，语句*大多*用于容纳表达式求值，并对其进行显式排序。"

#: src/statements.md:1
msgid "r\\[statement\\]"
msgstr "r\\[statement\\]"

#: src/statements.md:4
msgid "r\\[statement.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[statement.syntax\\]"

#: src/statements.md:14
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.intro\\] A _statement_ is a component of a [block](expressions/"
"block-expr.md), which is in turn a component of an outer [expression]"
"(expressions.md) or [function](items/functions.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.intro\\] *语句*是[块](expressions/block-expr.md)的组成部分，而"
"块又是外层[表达式](expressions.md)或[函数](items/functions.md)的组成部分。"

#: src/statements.md:17
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.kind\\] Rust has two kinds of statement: [declaration "
"statements](#declaration-statements) and [expression statements](#expression-"
"statements)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.kind\\] Rust 有两种语句：[声明语句](#declaration-statements)和"
"[表达式语句](#expression-statements)。"

#: src/statements.md:20
msgid "r\\[statement.decl\\]"
msgstr "r\\[statement.decl\\]"

#: src/statements.md:21
msgid "Declaration statements"
msgstr "声明语句"

#: src/statements.md:23
msgid ""
"A _declaration statement_ is one that introduces one or more _names_ into "
"the enclosing statement block. The declared names may denote new variables "
"or new [items](items.md)."
msgstr ""
"*声明语句*会向外围语句块中引入一个或多个*名称*。被声明的名称可以表示新的变量"
"或新的[项](items.md)。"

#: src/statements.md:25
msgid ""
"The two kinds of declaration statements are item declarations and `let` "
"statements."
msgstr "声明语句有两种：项声明和 `let` 语句。"

#: src/statements.md:27
msgid "r\\[statement.item\\]"
msgstr "r\\[statement.item\\]"

#: src/statements.md:28
msgid "Item declarations"
msgstr "项声明"

#: src/statements.md:30
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.item.intro\\] An _item declaration statement_ has a syntactic "
"form identical to an [item declaration](items.md) within a [module](items/"
"modules.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.item.intro\\] *项声明语句*的语法形式与[模块](items/modules.md)"
"内的[项声明](items.md)相同。"

#: src/statements.md:33
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.item.scope\\] Declaring an item within a statement block "
"restricts its [scope](names/scopes.md) to the block containing the "
"statement. The item is not given a [canonical path](paths.md#canonical-"
"paths) nor are any sub-items it may declare."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.item.scope\\] 在语句块内声明项会将其[作用域](names/scopes.md)限"
"制为包含该语句的块。该项不会被赋予[规范路径](paths.md#canonical-paths)，它可"
"能声明的任何子项也不会被赋予规范路径。"

#: src/statements.md:36
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.item.associated-scope\\] The exception to this is that "
"associated items defined by [implementations](items/implementations.md) are "
"still accessible in outer scopes as long as the item and, if applicable, "
"trait are accessible. It is otherwise identical in meaning to declaring the "
"item inside a module."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.item.associated-scope\\] 对此的例外是，由[实现](items/"
"implementations.md)定义的关联项，只要该项以及适用时的 trait 可访问，就仍可在"
"外层作用域中访问。除此之外，它的含义与在模块内声明该项相同。"

#: src/statements.md:39
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.item.outer-generics\\] There is no implicit capture of the "
"containing function's generic parameters, parameters, and local variables. "
"For example, `inner` may not access `outer_var`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.item.outer-generics\\] 不会隐式捕获所在函数的泛型参数、参数和局"
"部变量。例如，`inner` 不能访问 `outer_var`。"

#: src/statements.md:46
msgid "/* outer_var is not in scope here */"
msgstr "/* outer_var is not in scope here */"

#: src/statements.md:52
msgid "r\\[statement.let\\]"
msgstr "r\\[statement.let\\]"

#: src/statements.md:53
msgid "`let` statements"
msgstr "`let` 语句"

#: src/statements.md:55
msgid "r\\[statement.let.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[statement.let.syntax\\]"

#: src/statements.md:66
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.let.intro\\] A _`let` statement_ introduces a new set of "
"[variables](variables.md), given by a [pattern](patterns.md). The pattern is "
"followed optionally by a type annotation and then either ends, or is "
"followed by an initializer expression plus an optional `else` block."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.let.intro\\] *`let` 语句*会引入一组新的[变量](variables.md)，这"
"些变量由[模式](patterns.md)给出。模式后面可以跟随类型标注，然后要么到此结束，"
"要么跟随初始化表达式以及可选的 `else` 块。"

#: src/statements.md:69
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.let.inference\\] When no type annotation is given, the "
"compiler will infer the type, or signal an error if insufficient type "
"information is available for definite inference."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.let.inference\\] 如果未给出类型标注，编译器会推断类型；如果可用"
"于明确推断的类型信息不足，则会报错。"

#: src/statements.md:72
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.let.scope\\] Any variables introduced by a variable "
"declaration are visible from the point of declaration until the end of the "
"enclosing block scope, except when they are shadowed by another variable "
"declaration."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.let.scope\\] 由变量声明引入的任何变量，从声明点开始到外围块作用"
"域结束为止都是可见的，除非它们被另一个变量声明遮蔽。"

#: src/statements.md:75
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.let.constraint\\] If an `else` block is not present, the "
"pattern must be irrefutable. If an `else` block is present, the pattern may "
"be refutable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.let.constraint\\] 如果不存在 `else` 块，则模式必须是不可反驳"
"的。如果存在 `else` 块，则模式可以是可反驳的。"

#: src/statements.md:78
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.let.behavior\\] If the pattern does not match (this requires "
"it to be refutable), the `else` block is executed. The `else` block must "
"always diverge (evaluate to the [never type](types/never.md))."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.let.behavior\\] 如果模式不匹配（这要求它是可反驳的），则执行 "
"`else` 块。`else` 块必须始终发散（求值为 [never 类型](types/never.md)）。"

#: src/statements.md:82
msgid "// The bindings may be mut or const\n"
msgstr "// 绑定可以是 mut 或 const\n"

#: src/statements.md:83
msgid "// Refutable patterns require an else block\n"
msgstr "// 可反驳模式需要 else 块\n"

#: src/statements.md:84
msgid "// The else block must diverge\n"
msgstr "// else 块必须发散\n"

#: src/statements.md:86
msgid ""
"// This pattern is irrefutable, so the compiler\n"
"                                 // will lint as the else block is "
"redundant.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 该模式是不可反驳的，因此编译器\n"
"                                 // 会发出 lint，因为 else 块是多余的。\n"

#: src/statements.md:92
msgid "r\\[statement.expr\\]"
msgstr "r\\[statement.expr\\]"

#: src/statements.md:93
msgid "Expression statements"
msgstr "表达式语句"

#: src/statements.md:95
msgid "r\\[statement.expr.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[statement.expr.syntax\\]"

#: src/statements.md:102
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.expr.intro\\] An _expression statement_ is one that evaluates "
"an [expression](expressions.md) and ignores its result. As a rule, an "
"expression statement's purpose is to trigger the effects of evaluating its "
"expression."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.expr.intro\\] *表达式语句*会对一个[表达式](expressions.md)求值"
"并忽略其结果。通常，表达式语句的目的是触发对其表达式求值所产生的效果。"

#: src/statements.md:105
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.expr.restriction-semicolon\\] An expression that consists of "
"only a [block expression](expressions/block-expr.md) or control flow "
"expression, if used in a context where a statement is permitted, can omit "
"the trailing semicolon. This can cause an ambiguity between it being parsed "
"as a standalone statement and as a part of another expression; in this case, "
"it is parsed as a statement."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.expr.restriction-semicolon\\] 如果一个表达式仅由[块表达式]"
"(expressions/block-expr.md)或控制流表达式组成，并且用于允许语句的上下文中，则"
"可以省略尾随分号。这可能导致歧义：它既可能被解析为独立语句，也可能被解析为另"
"一个表达式的一部分；在这种情况下，它会被解析为语句。"

#: src/statements.md:108
msgid ""
"r\\[statement.expr.constraint-block\\] The type of \\[ExpressionWithBlock\\] "
"expressions when used as statements must be the unit type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[statement.expr.constraint-block\\] \\[ExpressionWithBlock\\] 表达式在用作"
"语句时，其类型必须是单元类型。"

#: src/statements.md:113
msgid "// Ignore the element returned from pop\n"
msgstr "// 忽略 pop 返回的元素\n"

#: src/statements.md:118
msgid "// Semicolon can be omitted.\n"
msgstr "// 可以省略分号。\n"

#: src/statements.md:119
msgid "// Separate expression statement, not an indexing expression.\n"
msgstr "// 独立的表达式语句，而不是索引表达式。\n"

#: src/statements.md:122
msgid "When the trailing semicolon is omitted, the result must be type `()`."
msgstr "当省略尾随分号时，结果必须是类型 `()`。"

#: src/statements.md:125
msgid ""
"// bad: the block's type is i32, not ()\n"
"// Error: expected `()` because of default return type\n"
"// if true {\n"
"//   1\n"
"// }\n"
msgstr ""
"// 错误写法：该块的类型是 i32，而不是 ()\n"
"// 错误：由于默认返回类型，预期为 `()`\n"
"// if true {\n"
"//   1\n"
"// }\n"

#: src/statements.md:130
msgid "// good: the block's type is i32\n"
msgstr "// 正确写法：该块的类型是 i32\n"

