#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:19
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.operator.intro\\] Operators are defined for built in types by the "
"Rust language."
msgstr "r\\[expr.operator.intro\\] 运算符由 Rust 语言为内置类型定义。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:22
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.operator.trait\\] Many of the following operators can also be "
"overloaded using traits in `std::ops` or `std::cmp`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.operator.trait\\] 下面许多运算符也可以使用 `std::ops` 或 `std::cmp` "
"中的 trait 进行重载。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:25
msgid "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow\\]"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:26
msgid "Overflow"
msgstr "溢出"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:28
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.intro\\] Integer operators will panic when "
"they overflow when compiled in debug mode. The `-C debug-assertions` and `-C "
"overflow-checks` compiler flags can be used to control this more directly. "
"The following things are considered to be overflow:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.intro\\] 整数运算符在调试模式编译时发生溢出将"
"会 panic。可以使用 `-C debug-assertions` 和 `-C overflow-checks` 编译器标志更"
"直接地控制此行为。以下情况被视为溢出："

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:31
msgid "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.binary-arith\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.binary-arith\\]"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:32
msgid ""
"When `+`, `*` or binary `-` create a value greater than the maximum value, "
"or less than the minimum value that can be stored."
msgstr ""
"当 `+`、`*` 或二元 `-` 产生的值大于可存储的最大值，或小于可存储的最小值时。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:34
msgid "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.unary-neg\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.unary-neg\\]"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:35
msgid ""
"Applying unary `-` to the most negative value of any signed integer type, "
"unless the operand is a [literal expression](literal-expr.md#integer-literal-"
"expressions) (or a literal expression standing alone inside one or more "
"[grouped expressions](grouped-expr.md))."
msgstr ""
"对任意有符号整数类型的最小值应用一元 `-`，除非操作数是[字面量表达式](literal-"
"expr.md#integer-literal-expressions)（或单独位于一个或多个[分组表达式]"
"(grouped-expr.md)内的字面量表达式）。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:37
msgid "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.div\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.div\\]"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:38
msgid ""
"Using `/` or `%`, where the left-hand argument is the smallest integer of a "
"signed integer type and the right-hand argument is `-1`. These checks occur "
"even when `-C overflow-checks` is disabled, for legacy reasons."
msgstr ""
"使用 `/` 或 `%` 时，左操作数是某个有符号整数类型的最小整数，且右操作数是 "
"`-1`。出于历史原因，即使禁用了 `-C overflow-checks`，也会执行这些检查。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:40
msgid "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.shift\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.operator.int-overflow.shift\\]"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:41
msgid ""
"Using `<<` or `>>` where the right-hand argument is greater than or equal to "
"the number of bits in the type of the left-hand argument, or is negative."
msgstr "使用 `<<` 或 `>>` 时，右操作数大于或等于左操作数类型的位数，或为负数。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:43
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The exception for literal expressions behind unary `-` means "
"that forms such as `-128_i8` or `let j: i8 = -(128)` never cause a panic and "
"have the expected value of -128."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 一元 `-` 后的字面量表达式例外意味着，像 `-128_i8` 或 `let j: i8 "
"= -(128)` 这样的形式永远不会导致 panic，并具有预期值 -128。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:46
msgid ""
"In these cases, the literal expression already has the most negative value "
"for its type (for example, `128_i8` has the value -128) because integer "
"literals are truncated to their type per the description in [Integer literal "
"expressions](literal-expr.md#integer-literal-expressions)."
msgstr ""
"在这些情况下，根据[整数字面量表达式](literal-expr.md#integer-literal-"
"expressions)中的说明，整数字面量会被截断为其类型，因此该字面量表达式已经具有"
"其类型的最小值（例如，`128_i8` 的值是 -128）。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:48
msgid ""
"Negation of these most negative values leaves the value unchanged due to "
"two's complement overflow conventions."
msgstr "由于二进制补码的溢出约定，对这些最小值取负会使值保持不变。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:50
msgid ""
"In `rustc`, these most negative expressions are also ignored by the "
"`overflowing_literals` lint check."
msgstr ""
"在 `rustc` 中，这些最小值表达式也会被 `overflowing_literals` lint 检查忽略。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:52
msgid "r\\[expr.operator.borrow\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.operator.borrow\\]"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:53
msgid "Borrow operators"
msgstr "借用运算符"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:55
msgid "r\\[expr.operator.borrow.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.operator.borrow.syntax\\]"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:64
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.intro\\] The `&` (shared borrow) and `&mut` "
"(mutable borrow) operators are unary prefix operators."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.intro\\] `&`（共享借用）和 `&mut`（可变借用）运算符"
"是一元前缀运算符。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:67
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.result\\] When applied to a [place expression](../"
"expressions.md#place-expressions-and-value-expressions), this expressions "
"produces a reference (pointer) to the location that the value refers to."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.result\\] 当应用于[位置表达式](../"
"expressions.md#place-expressions-and-value-expressions)时，此表达式会产生指向"
"该值所引用位置的引用（指针）。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:70
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.lifetime\\] The memory location is also placed into "
"a borrowed state for the duration of the reference. For a shared borrow "
"(`&`), this implies that the place may not be mutated, but it may be read or "
"shared again. For a mutable borrow (`&mut`), the place may not be accessed "
"in any way until the borrow expires."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.lifetime\\] 在该引用的持续期间，内存位置也会处于被借"
"用状态。对于共享借用（`&`），这意味着该位置不能被修改，但可以被读取或再次共"
"享。对于可变借用（`&mut`），在借用期结束之前，该位置不能以任何方式访问。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:73
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.mut\\] `&mut` evaluates its operand in a mutable "
"place expression context."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.mut\\] `&mut` 在可变位置表达式上下文中求值其操作数。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:76
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.temporary\\] If the `&` or `&mut` operators are "
"applied to a [value expression](../expressions.md#place-expressions-and-"
"value-expressions), then a [temporary value](../expressions.md#temporaries) "
"is created."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.operator.borrow.temporary\\] 如果 `&` 或 `&mut` 运算符应用于[值表达"
"式](../expressions.md#place-expressions-and-value-expressions)，则会创建一个"
"[临时值](../expressions.md#temporaries)。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:79
msgid "These operators cannot be overloaded."
msgstr "这些运算符不能被重载。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:83
msgid "// a temporary with value 7 is created that lasts for this scope.\n"
msgstr "// 创建一个值为 7 的临时值，它在此作用域内持续存在。\n"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:88
msgid ""
"// Mutably borrows `array` for this scope.\n"
"    // `array` may only be used through `mutable_reference`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 在此作用域内以可变方式借用 `array`。\n"
"    // `array` 只能通过 `mutable_reference` 使用。\n"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:94
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.and-and-syntax\\] Even though `&&` is a single token ([the "
"lazy 'and' operator](#lazy-boolean-operators)), when used in the context of "
"borrow expressions it works as two borrows:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.and-and-syntax\\] 尽管 `&&` 是单个 token（[惰性 “and” 运算符]"
"(#lazy-boolean-operators)），但在借用表达式上下文中使用时，它会作为两次借用工"
"作："

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:98 src/expressions/operator-expr.md:101
msgid "// same meanings:\n"
msgstr "// 含义相同：\n"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:108
msgid "r\\[expr.borrow.raw\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.borrow.raw\\]"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:109
msgid "Raw borrow operators"
msgstr "原始借用运算符"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:111
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.raw.intro\\] `&raw const` and `&raw mut` are the _raw borrow "
"operators_."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.raw.intro\\] `&raw const` 和 `&raw mut` 是*原始借用运算符*。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:114
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.raw.place\\] The operand expression of these operators is "
"evaluated in place expression context."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.raw.place\\] 这些运算符的操作数表达式在位置表达式上下文中求"
"值。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:117
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.raw.result\\] `&raw const expr` then creates a const raw "
"pointer of type `*const T` to the given place, and `&raw mut expr` creates a "
"mutable raw pointer of type `*mut T`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.raw.result\\] `&raw const expr` 会为给定位置创建类型为 "
"`*const T` 的 const 裸指针，而 `&raw mut expr` 会创建类型为 `*mut T` 的可变裸"
"指针。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:120
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.raw.invalid-ref\\] The raw borrow operators must be used "
"instead of a borrow operator whenever the place expression could evaluate to "
"a place that is not properly aligned or does not store a valid value as "
"determined by its type, or whenever creating a reference would introduce "
"incorrect aliasing assumptions. In those situations, using a borrow operator "
"would cause [undefined behavior](../behavior-considered-undefined.md) by "
"creating an invalid reference, but a raw pointer may still be constructed."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.borrow.raw.invalid-ref\\] 只要位置表达式可能求值为未正确对齐的位置、"
"按其类型判定未存储有效值的位置，或创建引用会引入不正确的别名假设，就必须使用"
"原始借用运算符，而不是借用运算符。在这些情形中，使用借用运算符会通过创建无效"
"引用而导致[未定义行为](../behavior-considered-undefined.md)，但仍可以构造裸指"
"针。"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:123
msgid ""
"The following is an example of creating a raw pointer to an unaligned place "
"through a `packed` struct:"
msgstr "下面是通过 `packed` 结构体创建指向未对齐位置的裸指针的示例："

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:132
msgid ""
"// `&packed.f2` would create an unaligned reference, and thus be undefined "
"behavior!\n"
msgstr "// `&packed.f2` 会创建未对齐的引用，因而是未定义行为！\n"

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:138
msgid ""
"The following is an example of creating a raw pointer to a place that does "
"not contain a valid value:"
msgstr "下面是创建指向不包含有效值的位置的裸指针的示例："

#: src/expressions/operator-expr.md:147
msgid ""
"// `&uninit.as_mut().field` would create a reference to an uninitialized "
"`bool`,\n"
"// and thus be undefined behavior!\n"
msgstr ""
