msgid "\"apples\""
msgstr "\"apples\""

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:176
msgid "\"cake\""
msgstr "\"cake\""

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:176
msgid "\"coffee\""
msgstr "\"coffee\""

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:179
msgid "\"I like {}.\""
msgstr "\"I like {}.\""

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:183
msgid "An example of a for loop over a series of integers:"
msgstr "对一系列整数进行 `for` 循环的示例："

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:193
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.loop.for.desugar\\] A `for` loop is equivalent to a `loop` "
"expression containing a [`match` expression](match-expr.md) as follows:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.loop.for.desugar\\] `for` 循环等价于如下包含 [`match` 表达式](match-"
"expr.md)的 `loop` 表达式："

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:223
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.loop.for.lang-items\\] `IntoIterator`, `Iterator`, and `Option` are "
"always the standard library items here, not whatever those names resolve to "
"in the current scope."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.loop.for.lang-items\\] 这里的 `IntoIterator`、`Iterator` 和 "
"`Option` 始终是标准库项，而不是这些名称在当前作用域中解析到的任何项。"

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:226
msgid ""
"The variable names `next`, `iter`, and `val` are for exposition only, they "
"do not actually have names the user can type."
msgstr ""
"变量名 `next`、`iter` 和 `val` 仅用于说明，它们实际上并没有用户可键入的名称。"

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:228
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The outer `match` is used to ensure that any [temporary values]"
"(../expressions.md#temporaries) in `iter_expr` don't get dropped before the "
"loop is finished. `next` is declared before being assigned because it "
"results in types being inferred correctly more often."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 外层 `match` 用于确保 `iter_expr` 中的任何[临时值](../"
"expressions.md#temporaries)不会在循环结束前被丢弃。`next` 在赋值前声明，是因"
"为这样更常能让类型被正确推断。"

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:231
msgid "r\\[expr.loop.label\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.loop.label\\]"

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:232
msgid "Loop labels"
msgstr "循环标签"

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:234
msgid "r\\[expr.loop.label.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.loop.label.syntax\\]"

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:239
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.loop.label.intro\\] A loop expression may optionally have a "
"_label_. The label is written as a lifetime preceding the loop expression, "
"as in `'foo: loop { break 'foo; }`, `'bar: while false {}`, `'humbug: for _ "
"in 0..0 {}`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.loop.label.intro\\] 循环表达式可以带有一个可选的*标签*。标签写作位于"
"循环表达式之前的生命周期，如 `'foo: loop { break 'foo; }`、`'bar: while "
"false {}`、`'humbug: for _ in 0..0 {}`。"

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:242
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.loop.label.control-flow\\] If a label is present, then labeled "
"`break` and `continue` expressions nested within this loop may exit out of "
"this loop or return control to its head. See [break expressions](#break-"
"expressions) and [continue expressions](#continue-expressions)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.loop.label.control-flow\\] 如果存在标签，则嵌套在此循环内的带标签 "
"`break` 和 `continue` 表达式可以退出此循环，或将控制流返回到其首部。见 "
"[break 表达式](#break-expressions)和 [continue 表达式](#continue-"
"expressions)。"

#: src/expressions/loop-expr.md:245
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.loop.label.ref\\] Labels follow the hygiene and shadowing rules of "
"local variables. For example, this code will print \"outer loop\":"
msgstr ""
