msgid "\"four\""
msgstr "\"four\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:72
msgid "\"five\""
msgstr "\"five\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:73
msgid "\"something else\""
msgstr "\"something else\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:77
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.pattern-vars\\] Variables bound within the pattern are scoped "
"to the match guard and the arm's expression."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.pattern-vars\\] 模式内绑定的变量作用域限于匹配守卫和该分支的表"
"达式。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:80
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.pattern-var-binding\\] The [binding mode](../"
"patterns.md#binding-modes) (move, copy, or reference) depends on the pattern."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.pattern-var-binding\\] [绑定模式](../patterns.md#binding-"
"modes)（移动、复制或引用）取决于模式。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:83
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.or-pattern\\] Multiple match patterns may be joined with the "
"`|` operator. Each pattern will be tested in left-to-right sequence until a "
"successful match is found."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.or-pattern\\] 多个匹配模式可以用 `|` 运算符连接。每个模式会按"
"从左到右的顺序测试，直到找到成功匹配。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:89
msgid "\"not many\""
msgstr "\"not many\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:90 src/expressions/match-expr.md:94
msgid "\"a few\""
msgstr "\"a few\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:91
msgid "\"lots\""
msgstr "\"lots\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:95
msgid "// Demonstration of pattern match order.\n"
msgstr "// 模式匹配顺序的演示。\n"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:105
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The `2..=9` is a [Range Pattern](../patterns.md#range-patterns), "
"not a [Range Expression](range-expr.md). Thus, only those types of ranges "
"supported by range patterns can be used in match arms."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `2..=9` 是[范围模式](../patterns.md#range-patterns)，而不是[范围"
"表达式](range-expr.md)。因此，只有范围模式支持的那些范围类型才能用于 match 分"
"支。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:108
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.or-patterns-restriction\\] Every binding in each `|` "
"separated pattern must appear in all of the patterns in the arm."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.or-patterns-restriction\\] 每个以 `|` 分隔的模式中的每个绑定，"
"都必须在该分支的所有模式中出现。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:111
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.binding-restriction\\] Every binding of the same name must "
"have the same type, and have the same binding mode."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.binding-restriction\\] 每个同名绑定都必须具有相同类型，并且具"
"有相同的绑定模式。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:114
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.type\\] The type of the overall `match` expression is the "
"[least upper bound](coerce.least-upper-bound) of the individual match arms."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.type\\] 整个 `match` 表达式的类型是各个 match 分支的[最小上界]"
"(coerce.least-upper-bound)。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:117
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.empty\\] If there are no match arms, then the `match` "
"expression is [diverging](divergence) and the type is [`!`](type.never)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.empty\\] 如果没有 match 分支，则 `match` 表达式是[发散的]"
"(divergence)，且类型为 [`!`](type.never)。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:132
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.diverging\\] If either the scrutinee expression or all of the "
"match arms diverge, then the entire `match` expression also diverges."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.diverging\\] 如果被匹配值表达式或所有 match 分支发散，则整个 "
"`match` 表达式也会发散。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:135
msgid "r\\[expr.match.guard\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.match.guard\\]"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:136
msgid "Match guards"
msgstr "匹配守卫"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:138
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.intro\\] Match arms can accept _match guards_ to "
"further refine the criteria for matching a case."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.intro\\] match 分支可以接受*匹配守卫*，以进一步细化匹配"
"某个情况的条件。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:141
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.condition\\] Pattern guards appear after the pattern "
"following the `if` keyword and consist of an \\[Expression\\] with a \\"
"[boolean type\\]\\[type.bool\\] or a conditional `let` match."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.condition\\] 模式守卫跟在模式后面、位于 `if` 关键字之"
"后，由具有\\[布尔类型\\]\\[type.bool\\]的 \\[Expression\\] 或条件式 `let` 匹"
"配组成。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:144
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.behavior\\] When the pattern matches successfully, the "
"pattern guard is executed. If all of the guard condition operands evaluate "
"to `true` and all of the `let` patterns successfully match their [scrutinee]"
"(../glossary.md#scrutinee)s, the match arm is successfully matched against "
"and the arm body is executed."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.behavior\\] 当模式成功匹配时，会执行模式守卫。如果所有守"
"卫条件操作数都求值为 `true`，并且所有 `let` 模式都成功匹配其[被匹配值](../"
"glossary.md#scrutinee)，则该 match 分支匹配成功，并执行分支体。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:147
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.next\\] Otherwise, the next pattern, including other "
"matches with the `|` operator in the same arm, is tested."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.next\\] 否则，会测试下一个模式，包括同一分支中使用 `|` "
"运算符的其他匹配。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:161
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Multiple matches using the `|` operator can cause the pattern "
"guard and the side effects it has to execute multiple times. For example:"
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 使用 `|` 运算符的多个匹配可能导致模式守卫及其副作用执行多次。例"
"如："

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:174
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.bound-variables\\] A pattern guard may refer to the "
"variables bound within the pattern they follow."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.bound-variables\\] 模式守卫可以引用其跟随的模式内所绑定"
"的变量。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:177
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.shared-ref\\] Before evaluating the guard, a shared "
"reference is taken to the part of the scrutinee the variable matches on. "
"While evaluating the guard, this shared reference is then used when "
"accessing the variable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.shared-ref\\] 在对守卫求值之前，会取得一个指向被匹配值中"
"该变量所匹配部分的共享引用。在对守卫求值期间，访问该变量时会使用这个共享引"
"用。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:180
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.value\\] Only when the guard evaluates successfully is "
"the value moved, or copied, from the scrutinee into the variable. This "
"allows shared borrows to be used inside guards without moving out of the "
"scrutinee in case guard fails to match."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.value\\] 只有当守卫求值并成功匹配时，才会将值从被匹配值"
"移动或复制到该变量中。这样就可以在守卫内部使用共享借用，而在守卫匹配失败时不"
"会从被匹配值中移出。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:183
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.no-mutation\\] Moreover, by holding a shared reference "
"while evaluating the guard, mutation inside guards is also prevented."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.no-mutation\\] 此外，通过在对守卫求值期间持有共享引用，"
"也会阻止守卫内部的修改。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:186
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.let\\] Guards can use `let` patterns to conditionally "
"match a scrutinee and to bind new variables into scope when the pattern "
"matches successfully."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.let\\] 守卫可以使用 `let` 模式来有条件地匹配被匹配值，并"
"在模式成功匹配时将新变量绑定到作用域中。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:189
msgid ""
"\\[!EXAMPLE\\] In this example, the guard condition `let Some(first_char) = "
"name.chars().next()` is evaluated. If the `let` pattern successfully matches "
"(i.e. the string has at least one character), the arm's body is executed. "
"Otherwise, pattern matching continues to the next arm."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EXAMPLE\\] 在此示例中，会对守卫条件 `let Some(first_char) = "
"name.chars().next()` 求值。如果 `let` 模式成功匹配（即字符串至少有一个字"
"符），则执行该分支的主体。否则，模式匹配继续到下一个分支。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:192
msgid ""
"The `let` pattern creates a new binding (`first_char`), which can be used "
"alongside the original pattern bindings (`name`) in the arm's body."
msgstr ""
"`let` 模式会创建一个新绑定（`first_char`），它可以与原始模式绑定（`name`）一"
"起在分支主体中使用。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:198
msgid "\"example\""
msgstr "\"example\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:202
msgid "// Both `name` and `first_char` are available here\n"
msgstr "// `name` 和 `first_char` 在这里都可用\n"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:203
msgid "\"Running: {name} (starts with '{first_char}')\""
msgstr "\"Running: {name} (starts with '{first_char}')\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:206
msgid "\"{name} is empty\""
msgstr "\"{name} is empty\""

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:212
msgid "r\\[expr.match.guard.chains\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.match.guard.chains\\]"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:213
msgid "Match guard chains"
msgstr "匹配守卫链"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:215
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.chains.intro\\] Multiple guard condition operands can "
"be separated with `&&`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.chains.intro\\] 多个守卫条件操作数可以用 `&&` 分隔。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:228
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.chains.order\\] Similar to a `&&` \\"
"[LazyBooleanExpression\\], each operand is evaluated from left-to-right "
"until an operand evaluates as `false` or a `let` match fails, in which case "
"the subsequent operands are not evaluated."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.chains.order\\] 类似于 `&&` \\"
"[LazyBooleanExpression\\]，每个操作数会从左到右求值，直到某个操作数求值为 "
"`false` 或某个 `let` 匹配失败；在这种情况下，后续操作数不会被求值。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:231
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.chains.bindings\\] The bindings of each `let` pattern "
"are put into scope to be available for the next condition operand and the "
"match arm body."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.chains.bindings\\] 每个 `let` 模式的绑定都会被放入作用"
"域，以供下一个条件操作数和 match 分支主体使用。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:234
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.chains.or\\] If any guard condition operand is a `let` "
"pattern, then none of the condition operands can be a `||` \\[lazy boolean "
"operator expression\\]\\[expr.bool-logic\\] due to ambiguity and precedence "
"with the `let` scrutinee."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.guard.chains.or\\] 如果任何守卫条件操作数是 `let` 模式，则由于"
"与 `let` 被匹配值之间存在歧义和优先级问题，所有条件操作数都不能是 `||` \\[惰"
"性布尔运算符表达式\\]\\[expr.bool-logic\\]。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:250
msgid "r\\[expr.match.attributes\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.match.attributes\\]"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:251
msgid "Attributes on match arms"
msgstr "match 分支上的属性"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:253
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.attributes.outer\\] Outer attributes are allowed on match "
"arms. The only attributes that have meaning on match arms are [`cfg`](../"
"conditional-compilation.md) and the [lint check attributes](../attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.attributes.outer\\] match 分支上允许使用外部属性。在 match 分"
"支上具有意义的属性只有 [`cfg`](../conditional-compilation.md) 和 [lint 检查属"
"性](../attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes)。"

#: src/expressions/match-expr.md:256
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.match.attributes.inner\\] [Inner attributes](../attributes.md) are "
"allowed directly after the opening brace of the match expression in the same "
"expression contexts as [attributes on block expressions](block-"
"expr.md#attributes-on-block-expressions)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.match.attributes.inner\\] [内部属性](../attributes.md)可以直接放在 "
"match 表达式的左花括号之后，允许出现的表达式上下文与[块表达式上的属性](block-"
"expr.md#attributes-on-block-expressions)相同。"

#: src/expressions/return-expr.md:1
msgid "r\\[expr.return\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.return\\]"

#: src/expressions/return-expr.md:2
msgid "`return` expressions"
msgstr "`return` 表达式"

#: src/expressions/return-expr.md:4
msgid "r\\[expr.return.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.return.syntax\\]"

#: src/expressions/return-expr.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.return.intro\\] Return expressions are denoted with the keyword "
"`return`."
msgstr "r\\[expr.return.intro\\] 返回表达式用关键字 `return` 表示。"

#: src/expressions/return-expr.md:12
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.return.behavior\\] Evaluating a `return` expression moves its "
"argument into the designated output location for the current function call, "
"destroys the current function activation frame, and transfers control to the "
"caller frame."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.return.behavior\\] 对 `return` 表达式求值会将其实参移动到当前函数调"
"用的指定输出位置，销毁当前函数激活帧，并将控制转移到调用者帧。"

#: src/expressions/return-expr.md:15
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.return.diverging\\] A `return` expression is [diverging]"
"(divergence) and has a type of [`!`](type.never)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.return.diverging\\] `return` 表达式是[发散的](divergence)，并具有 "
"[`!`](type.never) 类型。"

#: src/expressions/return-expr.md:18
msgid "An example of a `return` expression:"
msgstr "`return` 表达式的示例："

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:1
msgid "r\\[expr.await\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.await\\]"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:4
msgid "r\\[expr.await.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.await.syntax\\]"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.await.intro\\] An `await` expression is a syntactic construct for "
"suspending a computation provided by an implementation of "
"`std::future::IntoFuture` until the given future is ready to produce a value."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.await.intro\\] `await` 表达式是一种语法构造，用于挂起由 "
"`std::future::IntoFuture` 的某个实现提供的计算，直到给定 future 准备好产生"
"值。"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:12
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.await.construct\\] The syntax for an await expression is an "
"expression with a type that implements the [`IntoFuture`]"
"(std::future::IntoFuture) trait, called the _future operand_, then the token "
"`.`, and then the `await` keyword."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.await.construct\\] await 表达式的语法是：一个类型实现了 "
"[`IntoFuture`](std::future::IntoFuture) trait 的表达式，称为 *future 操作数"
"*，后跟 token `.`，再后跟 `await` 关键字。"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:15
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.await.allowed-positions\\] Await expressions are legal only within "
"an [async context](../expressions/block-expr.md#async-context), like an "
"[`async fn`](../items/functions.md#async-functions), [`async` closure]"
"(closure-expr.md#async-closures), or [`async` block](block-expr.md#async-"
"blocks)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[expr.await.allowed-positions\\] await 表达式仅在 [async 上下文](../"
"expressions/block-expr.md#async-context)中合法，例如在 [`async fn`](../items/"
"functions.md#async-functions)、[`async` 闭包](closure-expr.md#async-closures)"
"或 [`async` 块](block-expr.md#async-blocks)中。"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:18
msgid ""
"r\\[expr.await.effects\\] More specifically, an await expression has the "
"following effect."
msgstr "r\\[expr.await.effects\\] 更具体地说，await 表达式具有以下效果。"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:21
msgid ""
"Create a future by calling [`IntoFuture::into_future`]"
"(std::future::IntoFuture::into_future) on the future operand."
msgstr ""
"通过在 future 操作数上调用 [`IntoFuture::into_future`]"
"(std::future::IntoFuture::into_future) 创建一个 future。"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:22
msgid "Evaluate the future to a [future](std::future::Future) `tmp`;"
msgstr "将该 future 求值为一个 [future](std::future::Future) `tmp`；"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:23
msgid "Pin `tmp` using [`Pin::new_unchecked`](std::pin::Pin::new_unchecked);"
msgstr ""
"使用 [`Pin::new_unchecked`](std::pin::Pin::new_unchecked) 对 `tmp` 进行固定；"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:24
msgid ""
"This pinned future is then polled by calling the [`Future::poll`]"
"(std::future::Future::poll) method and passing it the current [task context]"
"(#task-context);"
msgstr ""
"随后通过调用 [`Future::poll`](std::future::Future::poll) 方法并向其传入当前"
"[任务上下文](#task-context)来轮询这个已固定的 future；"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:25
msgid ""
"If the call to `poll` returns [`Poll::Pending`](std::task::Poll::Pending), "
"then the future returns `Poll::Pending`, suspending its state so that, when "
"the surrounding async context is re-polled, execution returns to step 3;"
msgstr ""
"如果对 `poll` 的调用返回 [`Poll::Pending`](std::task::Poll::Pending)，则该 "
"future 返回 `Poll::Pending`，并挂起其状态，以便在外围 async 上下文再次被轮询"
"时，执行返回到步骤 3；"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:26
msgid ""
"Otherwise the call to `poll` must have returned [`Poll::Ready`]"
"(std::task::Poll::Ready), in which case the value contained in the "
"[`Poll::Ready`](std::task::Poll::Ready) variant is used as the result of the "
"`await` expression itself."
msgstr ""
"否则，对 `poll` 的调用必定已返回 [`Poll::Ready`](std::task::Poll::Ready)，在"
"这种情况下，[`Poll::Ready`](std::task::Poll::Ready) 变体中包含的值会用作 "
"`await` 表达式本身的结果。"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:28
msgid "r\\[expr.await.edition2018\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.await.edition2018\\]"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:29
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] Await expressions are only available beginning with Rust "
"2018."
msgstr "\\[!EDITION-2018\\] await 表达式仅从 Rust 2018 开始可用。"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:32
msgid "r\\[expr.await.task\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.await.task\\]"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:33
msgid "Task context"
msgstr "任务上下文"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:35
msgid ""
"The task context refers to the [`Context`](std::task::Context) which was "
"supplied to the current [async context](../expressions/block-expr.md#async-"
"context) when the async context itself was polled. Because `await` "
"expressions are only legal in an async context, there must be some task "
"context available."
msgstr ""
"任务上下文指当前 [async 上下文](../expressions/block-expr.md#async-context)本"
"身被轮询时提供给它的 [`Context`](std::task::Context)。因为 `await` 表达式只"
"在 async 上下文中合法，所以必须有某个任务上下文可用。"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:37
msgid "r\\[expr.await.desugar\\]"
msgstr "r\\[expr.await.desugar\\]"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:38
msgid "Approximate desugaring"
msgstr "近似脱糖"

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:40
msgid ""
"Effectively, an await expression is roughly equivalent to the following non-"
"normative desugaring:"
msgstr "实际上，await 表达式大致等价于以下非规范性的脱糖形式："

#: src/expressions/await-expr.md:55
msgid ""
"where the `yield` pseudo-code returns `Poll::Pending` and, when re-invoked, "
"resumes execution from that point. The variable `current_context` refers to "
"the context taken from the async environment."
msgstr ""
"其中 `yield` 伪代码返回 `Poll::Pending`，并在再次被调用时从该点恢复执行。变"
"量 `current_context` 指的是从 async 环境取得的上下文。"

