#: src/patterns.md:119
msgid "r\\[patterns.refutable\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.refutable\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:120
msgid "Refutability"
msgstr "可反驳性"

#: src/patterns.md:122
msgid ""
"A pattern is said to be _refutable_ when it has the possibility of not being "
"matched by the value it is being matched against. _Irrefutable_ patterns, on "
"the other hand, always match the value they are being matched against. "
"Examples:"
msgstr ""
"当一个模式有可能不匹配它所匹配的值时，称该模式是*可反驳的*。另一方面，*不可反"
"驳的*模式始终匹配它所匹配的值。示例："

#: src/patterns.md:125
msgid "// \"(x, y)\" is an irrefutable pattern\n"
msgstr "// \"(x, y)\" 是不可驳模式\n"

#: src/patterns.md:127
msgid "// \"(a, 3)\" is refutable, and will not match\n"
msgstr "// \"(a, 3)\" 是可驳模式，并且不会匹配\n"

#: src/patterns.md:128
msgid "\"Shouldn't reach here\""
msgstr "\"Shouldn't reach here\""

#: src/patterns.md:129
msgid "// \"(a, 4)\" is refutable, and will match\n"
msgstr "// \"(a, 4)\" 是可驳模式，并且会匹配\n"

#: src/patterns.md:130
msgid "\"Matched ({}, 4)\""
msgstr "\"Matched ({}, 4)\""

#: src/patterns.md:134
msgid "r\\[patterns.literal\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.literal\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:135
msgid "Literal patterns"
msgstr "字面量模式"

#: src/patterns.md:137
msgid "r\\[patterns.literal.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.literal.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:142
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.literal.intro\\] _Literal patterns_ match exactly the same "
"value as what is created by the literal. Since negative numbers are not "
"[literals](expressions/literal-expr.md), literals in patterns may be "
"prefixed by an optional minus sign, which acts like the negation operator."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.literal.intro\\] *字面量模式*精确匹配由该字面量创建的同一个值。"
"由于负数不是[字面量](expressions/literal-expr.md)，模式中的字面量可以带有一个"
"可选的前置减号，其作用类似于取负运算符。"

#: src/patterns.md:145
msgid ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] C string and raw C string literals are accepted in literal "
"patterns, but `&CStr` doesn't implement structural equality (`#[derive(Eq, "
"PartialEq)]`) and therefore any such `match` on a `&CStr` will be rejected "
"with a type error."
msgstr ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] 字面量模式接受 C 字符串和原始 C 字符串字面量，但 `&CStr` 没有"
"实现结构相等性（`#[derive(Eq, PartialEq)]`），因此任何这类针对 `&CStr` 的 "
"`match` 都会因类型错误而被拒绝。"

#: src/patterns.md:148
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.literal.refutable\\] Literal patterns are always refutable."
msgstr "r\\[patterns.literal.refutable\\] 字面量模式始终是可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:156
msgid "\"It's minus one\""
msgstr "\"It's minus one\""

#: src/patterns.md:157
msgid "\"It's a one\""
msgstr "\"It's a one\""

#: src/patterns.md:158
msgid "\"It's either a two or a four\""
msgstr "\"It's either a two or a four\""

#: src/patterns.md:159
msgid "\"Matched none of the arms\""
msgstr "\"Matched none of the arms\""

#: src/patterns.md:164
msgid "r\\[patterns.ident\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ident\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:165
msgid "Identifier patterns"
msgstr "标识符模式"

#: src/patterns.md:167
msgid "r\\[patterns.ident.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ident.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:172
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.intro\\] Identifier patterns bind the value they match to "
"a variable in the [value namespace](names.namespaces.kinds)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.intro\\] 标识符模式会把它们匹配的值绑定到[值命名空间]"
"(names.namespaces.kinds)中的一个变量。"

#: src/patterns.md:175
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.unique\\] The identifier must be unique within the "
"pattern."
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ident.unique\\] 该标识符在模式中必须是唯一的。"

#: src/patterns.md:178
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.scope\\] The variable will shadow any variables of the "
"same name in scope. The [scope](names/scopes.md) of the new binding depends "
"on the context of where the pattern is used (such as a `let` binding or a "
"`match` arm)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.scope\\] 该变量会遮蔽作用域内任何同名变量。新绑定的[作用"
"域](names/scopes.md)取决于模式使用位置的上下文（例如 `let` 绑定或 `match` 分"
"支）。"

#: src/patterns.md:181
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.bare\\] Patterns that consist of only an identifier, "
"possibly with a `mut`, match any value and bind it to that identifier. This "
"is the most commonly used pattern in variable declarations and parameters "
"for functions and closures."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.bare\\] 仅由一个标识符组成、可能带有 `mut` 的模式会匹配任"
"何值，并将其绑定到该标识符。这是变量声明以及函数和闭包参数中最常用的模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:191
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.scrutinized\\] To bind the matched value of a pattern to "
"a variable, use the syntax `variable @ subpattern`. For example, the "
"following binds the value 2 to `e` (not the entire range: the range here is "
"a range subpattern)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.scrutinized\\] 若要把模式匹配到的值绑定到变量，请使用语法 "
"`variable @ subpattern`。例如，以下代码会把值 2 绑定到 `e`（不是整个范围：这"
"里的范围是一个范围子模式）。"

#: src/patterns.md:198
msgid "\"got a range element {}\""
msgstr "\"got a range element {}\""

#: src/patterns.md:199
msgid "\"anything\""
msgstr "\"anything\""

#: src/patterns.md:203
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.move\\] By default, identifier patterns bind a variable "
"to a copy of or move from the matched value depending on whether the matched "
"value implements [`Copy`](special-types-and-traits.md#copy)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.move\\] 默认情况下，标识符模式会根据被匹配值是否实现 "
"[`Copy`](special-types-and-traits.md#copy)，把变量绑定到被匹配值的副本，或者"
"从被匹配值移动而来。"

#: src/patterns.md:206
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.ref\\] This can be changed to bind to a reference by "
"using the `ref` keyword, or to a mutable reference using `ref mut`. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.ref\\] 可以使用 `ref` 关键字将其改为绑定到引用，或使用 "
"`ref mut` 绑定到可变引用。例如："

#: src/patterns.md:222
msgid ""
"In the first match expression, the value is copied (or moved). In the second "
"match, a reference to the same memory location is bound to the variable "
"value. This syntax is needed because in destructuring subpatterns the `&` "
"operator can't be applied to the value's fields. For example, the following "
"is not valid:"
msgstr ""
"在第一个 match 表达式中，该值会被复制（或移动）。在第二个 match 中，指向同一"
"内存位置的引用会被绑定到变量 value。需要这种语法，是因为在解构子模式中，`&` "
"运算符不能应用到值的字段。例如，以下代码无效："

#: src/patterns.md:233
msgid "To make it valid, write the following:"
msgstr "若要使其有效，请写成以下形式："

#: src/patterns.md:244
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.ref-ignored\\] Thus, `ref` is not something that is being "
"matched against. Its objective is exclusively to make the matched binding a "
"reference, instead of potentially copying or moving what was matched."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.ref-ignored\\] 因此，`ref` 并不是被匹配的内容。它的目的仅"
"仅是让匹配到的绑定成为引用，而不是可能复制或移动被匹配的内容。"

#: src/patterns.md:247
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.precedent\\] [Path patterns](#path-patterns) take "
"precedence over identifier patterns."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.precedent\\] [路径模式](#path-patterns)优先于标识符模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:250
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] When a pattern is a single-segment identifier, the grammar is "
"ambiguous whether it means an \\[IdentifierPattern\\] or a \\"
"[PathPattern\\]. This ambiguity can only be resolved after [name resolution]"
"(names/name-resolution.md)."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 当一个模式是单段标识符时，语法上无法确定它表示 \\"
"[IdentifierPattern\\] 还是 \\[PathPattern\\]。这种歧义只能在[名称解析](names/"
"name-resolution.md)之后解决。"

#: src/patterns.md:255
msgid "//    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ That this constant is in scope affects how the\n"
msgstr "//    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ 此常量在作用域内会影响\n"

#: src/patterns.md:256
msgid "//                   patterns below are treated.\n"
msgstr "//                   以下模式会被处理。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:261
msgid "//  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ Parsed as a `PathPattern` that resolves to\n"
msgstr "//  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ 被解析为一个 `PathPattern`，其解析为\n"

#: src/patterns.md:262
msgid "//                 the constant `42`.\n"
msgstr "//                 常量 `42`。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:264
msgid "//  ^^^^^^^^^^^ Parsed as an `IdentifierPattern`.\n"
msgstr "//  ^^^^^^^^^^^ 被解析为一个 `IdentifierPattern`。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:268
msgid "// If `EXPECTED_VALUE` were treated as an `IdentifierPattern` above,\n"
msgstr "// 如果上面的 `EXPECTED_VALUE` 被视为一个 `IdentifierPattern`，\n"

#: src/patterns.md:269
msgid "// that pattern would always match, making the function always return\n"
msgstr "// 那么该模式总会匹配，使函数总是返回\n"

#: src/patterns.md:270
msgid "// `Ok(_) regardless of the input.\n"
msgstr "// `Ok(_)`，无论输入是什么。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:275
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.constraint\\] It is an error if `ref` or `ref mut` is "
"specified and the identifier shadows a constant."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.constraint\\] 如果指定了 `ref` 或 `ref mut`，且该标识符遮"
"蔽了一个常量，则这是错误。"

#: src/patterns.md:278
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.refutable\\] Identifier patterns are irrefutable if the "
"`@` subpattern is irrefutable or the subpattern is not specified."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.refutable\\] 如果 `@` 子模式不可反驳，或者未指定该子模式，"
"则标识符模式是不可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:281
msgid "r\\[patterns.ident.binding\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ident.binding\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:282
msgid "Binding modes"
msgstr "绑定模式"

#: src/patterns.md:284
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.intro\\] To service better ergonomics, patterns "
"operate in different _binding modes_ in order to make it easier to bind "
"references to values. When a reference value is matched by a non-reference "
"pattern, it will be automatically treated as a `ref` or `ref mut` binding. "
"Example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.intro\\] 为了改善易用性，模式会以不同的*绑定模式*"
"运行，以便更容易将引用绑定到值。当一个引用值由非引用模式匹配时，它会被自动视"
"为 `ref` 或 `ref mut` 绑定。示例："

#: src/patterns.md:290
msgid "// y was converted to `ref y` and its type is &i32\n"
msgstr "// y 被转换为 `ref y`，其类型为 &i32\n"

#: src/patterns.md:294
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.non-reference\\] _Non-reference patterns_ include "
"all patterns except bindings, [wildcard patterns](#wildcard-pattern) (`_`), "
"[`const` patterns](#path-patterns) of reference types, and [reference "
"patterns](#reference-patterns)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.non-reference\\] *非引用模式*包括除绑定、[通配符模"
"式](#wildcard-pattern)（`_`）、引用类型的 [`const` 模式](#path-patterns)以及"
"[引用模式](#reference-patterns)之外的所有模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:297
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.default-mode\\] If a binding pattern does not "
"explicitly have `ref`, `ref mut`, or `mut`, then it uses the _default "
"binding mode_ to determine how the variable is bound."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.default-mode\\] 如果一个绑定型模式没有显式带有 "
"`ref`、`ref mut` 或 `mut`，则它会使用*默认绑定模式*来确定变量如何绑定。"

#: src/patterns.md:300
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.move\\] The default binding mode starts in "
"\"move\" mode which uses move semantics."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.move\\] 默认绑定模式从 \"move\" 模式开始，该模式使"
"用移动语义。"

#: src/patterns.md:303
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.top-down\\] When matching a pattern, the compiler "
"starts from the outside of the pattern and works inwards."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.top-down\\] 匹配模式时，编译器会从模式外层开始并向"
"内处理。"

#: src/patterns.md:306
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.auto-deref\\] Each time a reference is matched "
"using a non-reference pattern, it will automatically dereference the value "
"and update the default binding mode."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.auto-deref\\] 每当使用非引用模式匹配一个引用时，它"
"都会自动解引用该值并更新默认绑定模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:309
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.ref\\] References will set the default binding "
"mode to `ref`."
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ident.binding.ref\\] 引用会将默认绑定模式设为 `ref`。"

#: src/patterns.md:312
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.ref-mut\\] Mutable references will set the mode "
"to `ref mut` unless the mode is already `ref` in which case it remains `ref`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.ref-mut\\] 可变引用会将模式设为 `ref mut`，除非该"
"模式已经是 `ref`，在这种情况下它会保持为 `ref`。"

#: src/patterns.md:315
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.nested-references\\] If the automatically "
"dereferenced value is still a reference, it is dereferenced and this process "
"repeats."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.nested-references\\] 如果自动解引用后的值仍然是引"
"用，则会继续解引用，并重复此过程。"

#: src/patterns.md:318
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mode-limitations-binding\\] The binding pattern "
"may only explicitly specify a `ref` or `ref mut` binding mode, or specify "
"mutability with `mut`, when the default binding mode is \"move\". For "
"example, these are not accepted:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mode-limitations-binding\\] 只有当默认绑定模式为 "
"\"move\" 时，绑定型模式才可以显式指定 `ref` 或 `ref mut` 绑定模式，或用 "
"`mut` 指定可变性。例如，以下形式不被接受："

#: src/patterns.md:327
msgid "r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mode-limitations.edition2024\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mode-limitations.edition2024\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:328
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] Before the 2024 edition, bindings could explicitly "
"specify a `ref` or `ref mut` binding mode even when the default binding mode "
"was not \"move\", and they could specify mutability on such bindings with "
"`mut`. In these editions, specifying `mut` on a binding set the binding mode "
"to \"move\" regardless of the current default binding mode."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] 在 2024 edition 之前，即使默认绑定模式不是 \"move\"，绑定"
"也可以显式指定 `ref` 或 `ref mut` 绑定模式，并且可以在这类绑定上用 `mut` 指定"
"可变性。在这些 edition 中，无论当前默认绑定模式如何，在绑定上指定 `mut` 都会"
"把绑定模式设为 \"move\"。"

#: src/patterns.md:331
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mode-limitations-reference\\] Similarly, a "
"reference pattern may only appear when the default binding mode is \"move\". "
"For example, this is not accepted:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mode-limitations-reference\\] 类似地，引用模式只可"
"以在默认绑定模式为 \"move\" 时出现。例如，以下形式不被接受："

#: src/patterns.md:338
msgid "r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mode-limitations-reference.edition2024\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mode-limitations-reference.edition2024\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:339
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] Before the 2024 edition, reference patterns could appear "
"even when the default binding mode was not \"move\", and had both the effect "
"of matching against the scrutinee and of causing the default binding mode to "
"be reset to \"move\"."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] 在 2024 edition 之前，即使默认绑定模式不是 \"move\"，引用"
"模式也可以出现，并且同时具有匹配被匹配值以及导致默认绑定模式重置为 \"move\" "
"的效果。"

#: src/patterns.md:342
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mixed\\] Move bindings and reference bindings can "
"be mixed together in the same pattern. Doing so will result in partial move "
"of the object bound to and the object cannot be used afterwards. This "
"applies only if the type cannot be copied."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ident.binding.mixed\\] 移动绑定和引用绑定可以混合出现在同一个模"
"式中。这样做会导致被绑定对象发生部分移动，该对象之后不能再使用。只有当该类型"
"不能被复制时，这一点才适用。"

#: src/patterns.md:345
msgid ""
"In the example below, `name` is moved out of `person`. Trying to use "
"`person` as a whole or `person.name` would result in an error because of "
"_partial move_."
msgstr ""
"在下面的示例中，`name` 被从 `person` 中移出。尝试把 `person` 作为整体使用或使"
"用 `person.name` 会因为*部分移动*而导致错误。"

#: src/patterns.md:354
msgid "// `name` is moved from person and `age` referenced\n"
msgstr "// `name` 从 person 移出，`age` 被引用\n"

#: src/patterns.md:359
msgid "r\\[patterns.wildcard\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.wildcard\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:360
msgid "Wildcard pattern"
msgstr "通配符模式"

#: src/patterns.md:362
msgid "r\\[patterns.wildcard.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.wildcard.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:367
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.wildcard.intro\\] The _wildcard pattern_ (an underscore symbol) "
"matches any value. It is used to ignore values when they don't matter."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.wildcard.intro\\] *通配符模式*（下划线符号）匹配任何值。它用于忽"
"略无关紧要的值。"

#: src/patterns.md:370
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.wildcard.struct-matcher\\] Inside other patterns, it matches a "
"single data field (as opposed to the `..`, which matches the remaining "
"fields)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.wildcard.struct-matcher\\] 在其他模式内部，它匹配单个数据字段"
"（相对于匹配剩余字段的 `..`）。"

#: src/patterns.md:373
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.wildcard.no-binding\\] Unlike identifier patterns, it does not "
"copy, move, or borrow the value it matches."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.wildcard.no-binding\\] 不同于标识符模式，它不会复制、移动或借用"
"它所匹配的值。"

#: src/patterns.md:380
msgid "// the x is always matched by _\n"
msgstr "// x 总是由 _ 匹配\n"

#: src/patterns.md:382
msgid "// ignore a function/closure param\n"
msgstr "// 忽略函数/闭包参数\n"

#: src/patterns.md:385
msgid "// ignore a field from a struct\n"
msgstr "// 忽略 struct 中的一个字段\n"

#: src/patterns.md:398
msgid "// accept any Some, with any value\n"
msgstr "// 接受任何 Some，带有任何值\n"

#: src/patterns.md:404
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.wildcard.refutable\\] The wildcard pattern is always "
"irrefutable."
msgstr "r\\[patterns.wildcard.refutable\\] 通配符模式始终是不可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:407
msgid "r\\[patterns.rest\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.rest\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:408
msgid "Rest pattern"
msgstr "剩余模式"

#: src/patterns.md:410
msgid "r\\[patterns.rest.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.rest.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:415
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.rest.intro\\] The _rest pattern_ (the `..` token) acts as a "
"variable-length pattern which matches zero or more elements that haven't "
"been matched already before and after."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.rest.intro\\] *剩余模式*（`..` token）作为可变长度模式，匹配其前"
"后尚未被匹配的零个或多个元素。"

#: src/patterns.md:418
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.rest.allowed-patterns\\] It may only be used in [tuple](#tuple-"
"patterns), [tuple struct](#tuple-struct-patterns), and [slice](#slice-"
"patterns) patterns, and may only appear once as one of the elements in those "
"patterns. It is also allowed in an [identifier pattern](#identifier-"
"patterns) for [slice patterns](#slice-patterns) only."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.rest.allowed-patterns\\] 它只可以用于[元组](#tuple-patterns)、"
"[元组结构体](#tuple-struct-patterns)和[切片](#slice-patterns)模式，并且在这些"
"模式中只能作为其中一个元素出现一次。它也允许出现在[标识符模式](#identifier-"
"patterns)中，但仅限于[切片模式](#slice-patterns)。"

#: src/patterns.md:421
msgid "r\\[patterns.rest.refutable\\] The rest pattern is always irrefutable."
msgstr "r\\[patterns.rest.refutable\\] 剩余模式始终是不可反驳的。"

