#: src/patterns.md:641
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.range.refutable\\] Range patterns for fix-width integer and "
"`char` types are irrefutable when they span the entire set of possible "
"values of a type. For example, `0u8..=255u8` is irrefutable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.range.refutable\\] 对于固定宽度整数和 `char` 类型，如果范围模式"
"覆盖某个类型的整个可能值集合，则它们是不可反驳的。例如，`0u8..=255u8` 是不可"
"反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:644
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.range.refutable-integer\\] The range of values for an integer "
"type is the closed range from its minimum to maximum value."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.range.refutable-integer\\] 整数类型的取值范围是从其最小值到最大"
"值的闭区间。"

#: src/patterns.md:647
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.range.refutable-char\\] The range of values for a `char` type "
"are precisely those ranges containing all Unicode Scalar Values: "
"`'\\u{0000}'..='\\u{D7FF}'` and `'\\u{E000}'..='\\u{10FFFF}'`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.range.refutable-char\\] `char` 类型的取值范围恰好是包含所有 "
"Unicode 标量值的那些范围：`'\\u{0000}'..='\\u{D7FF}'` 和 "
"`'\\u{E000}'..='\\u{10FFFF}'`。"

#: src/patterns.md:650
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.range.constraint-slice\\] \\[RangeFromPattern\\] cannot be used "
"as a top-level pattern for subpatterns in [slice patterns](#slice-patterns). "
"For example, the pattern `[1.., _]` is not a valid pattern."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.range.constraint-slice\\] \\[RangeFromPattern\\] 不能用作[切片模"
"式](#slice-patterns)中子模式的顶层模式。例如，模式 `[1.., _]` 不是有效模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:653
msgid "r\\[patterns.range.edition2021\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.range.edition2021\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:654
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2021\\] Before the 2021 edition, range patterns with both a "
"lower and upper bound may also be written using `...` in place of `..=`, "
"with the same meaning."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2021\\] 在 2021 edition 之前，同时具有下界和上界的范围模式也可以"
"使用 `...` 代替 `..=` 来书写，含义相同。"

#: src/patterns.md:657
msgid "r\\[patterns.ref\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ref\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:658
msgid "Reference patterns"
msgstr "引用模式"

#: src/patterns.md:660
msgid "r\\[patterns.ref.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ref.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:665
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ref.intro\\] Reference patterns dereference the pointers that "
"are being matched and, thus, borrow them."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ref.intro\\] 引用模式会解引用正在被匹配的指针，并因此借用它们。"

#: src/patterns.md:668
msgid "For example, these two matches on `x: &i32` are equivalent:"
msgstr "例如，以下两个针对 `x: &i32` 的匹配是等价的："

#: src/patterns.md:673 src/patterns.md:674
msgid "\"zero\""
msgstr "\"zero\""

#: src/patterns.md:673 src/patterns.md:674
msgid "\"some\""
msgstr "\"some\""

#: src/patterns.md:679
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ref.ref-ref\\] The grammar production for reference patterns "
"has to match the token `&&` to match a reference to a reference because it "
"is a token by itself, not two `&` tokens."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ref.ref-ref\\] 引用模式的语法产生式必须匹配 token `&&` 才能匹配"
"对引用的引用，因为它本身就是一个 token，而不是两个 `&` token。"

#: src/patterns.md:682
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ref.mut\\] Adding the `mut` keyword dereferences a mutable "
"reference. The mutability must match the mutability of the reference."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.ref.mut\\] 添加 `mut` 关键字会解引用可变引用。可变性必须与该引用"
"的可变性匹配。"

#: src/patterns.md:685
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.ref.refutable\\] Reference patterns are always irrefutable."
msgstr "r\\[patterns.ref.refutable\\] 引用模式始终是不可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:688
msgid "r\\[patterns.struct\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.struct\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:689
msgid "Struct patterns"
msgstr "结构体模式"

#: src/patterns.md:691
msgid "r\\[patterns.struct.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.struct.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:716
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.intro\\] Struct patterns match struct, enum, and union "
"values that match all criteria defined by its subpatterns. They are also "
"used to [destructure](#destructuring) a struct, enum, or union value."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.intro\\] 结构体模式匹配满足其子模式所定义全部条件的 "
"struct、enum 和 union 值。它们也用于[解构](#destructuring) struct、enum 或 "
"union 值。"

#: src/patterns.md:719
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.ignore-rest\\] On a struct pattern, the fields are "
"referenced by name, index (in the case of tuple structs) or ignored by use "
"of `..`:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.ignore-rest\\] 在结构体模式中，字段通过名称、索引（对于元"
"组结构体）引用，或通过使用 `..` 忽略："

#: src/patterns.md:731 src/patterns.md:744
msgid "// order doesn't matter\n"
msgstr "// 顺序无关紧要\n"

#: src/patterns.md:762
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.constraint-struct\\] If `..` is not used, a struct "
"pattern used to match a struct is required to specify all fields:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.constraint-struct\\] 如果未使用 `..`，则用于匹配 struct "
"的结构体模式必须指定所有字段："

#: src/patterns.md:771 src/patterns.md:774 src/patterns.md:775
#: src/patterns.md:776 src/patterns.md:777 src/patterns.md:794
msgid "'X'"
msgstr "'X'"

#: src/patterns.md:782
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.constraint-union\\] A struct pattern used to match a "
"union must specify exactly one field (see [Pattern matching on unions](items/"
"unions.md#pattern-matching-on-unions))."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.constraint-union\\] 用于匹配 union 的结构体模式必须恰好指"
"定一个字段（见 [union 上的模式匹配](items/unions.md#pattern-matching-on-"
"unions)）。"

#: src/patterns.md:785
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.binding-shorthand\\] The \\[IDENTIFIER\\] syntax matches "
"any value and binds it to a variable with the same name as the given field. "
"It is a shorthand for `fieldname: fieldname`. The `ref` and `mut` qualifiers "
"can be included with the behavior as described in \\[patterns.ident.ref\\]."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.binding-shorthand\\] \\[IDENTIFIER\\] 语法匹配任何值，并"
"将其绑定到与给定字段同名的变量。它是 `fieldname: fieldname` 的简写。可以包含 "
"`ref` 和 `mut` 限定符，其行为如 \\[patterns.ident.ref\\] 所述。"

#: src/patterns.md:799
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.refutable\\] A struct pattern is refutable if the \\"
"[PathInExpression\\] resolves to a constructor of an enum with more than one "
"variant, or one of its subpatterns is refutable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.refutable\\] 如果 \\[PathInExpression\\] 解析到具有多个变"
"体的 enum 的构造器，或者其某个子模式是可反驳的，则结构体模式是可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:802
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.namespace\\] A struct pattern matches against the "
"struct, union, or enum variant whose constructor is resolved from \\"
"[PathInExpression\\] in the [type namespace](names.namespaces.kinds). See \\"
"[patterns.tuple-struct.namespace\\] for more details."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.struct.namespace\\] 结构体模式匹配其构造器由 \\"
"[PathInExpression\\] 在[类型命名空间](names.namespaces.kinds)中解析得到的 "
"struct、union 或 enum 变体。更多细节见 \\[patterns.tuple-"
"struct.namespace\\]。"

#: src/patterns.md:805
msgid "r\\[patterns.tuple-struct\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.tuple-struct\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:806
msgid "Tuple struct patterns"
msgstr "元组结构体模式"

#: src/patterns.md:808
msgid "r\\[patterns.tuple-struct.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.tuple-struct.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:815
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple-struct.intro\\] Tuple struct patterns match tuple struct "
"and enum values that match all criteria defined by its subpatterns. They are "
"also used to [destructure](#destructuring) a tuple struct or enum value."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple-struct.intro\\] 元组结构体模式匹配满足其子模式所定义全部条"
"件的元组结构体和 enum 值。它们也用于[解构](#destructuring)元组结构体或 enum "
"值。"

#: src/patterns.md:818
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple-struct.refutable\\] A tuple struct pattern is refutable "
"if the \\[PathInExpression\\] resolves to a constructor of an enum with more "
"than one variant, or one of its subpatterns is refutable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple-struct.refutable\\] 如果 \\[PathInExpression\\] 解析到具有"
"多个变体的 enum 的构造器，或者其某个子模式是可反驳的，则元组结构体模式是可反"
"驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:821
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple-struct.namespace\\] A tuple struct pattern matches "
"against the tuple struct or [tuple-like enum variant](items.enum.tuple-expr) "
"whose constructor is resolved from \\[PathInExpression\\] in the [value "
"namespace](names.namespaces.kinds)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple-struct.namespace\\] 元组结构体模式匹配其构造器由 \\"
"[PathInExpression\\] 在[值命名空间](names.namespaces.kinds)中解析得到的元组结"
"构体或[类元组 enum 变体](items.enum.tuple-expr)。"

#: src/patterns.md:824
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Conversely, a struct pattern for a tuple struct or [tuple-like "
"enum variant](items.enum.tuple-expr), e.g. `S { 0: _ }`, matches against the "
"tuple struct or variant whose constructor is resolved in the [type namespace]"
"(names.namespaces.kinds)."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 反过来，用于元组结构体或[类元组 enum 变体](items.enum.tuple-expr)"
"的结构体模式，例如 `S { 0: _ }`，会匹配其构造器在[类型命名空间]"
"(names.namespaces.kinds)中解析得到的元组结构体或变体。"

#: src/patterns.md:831
msgid "// Import `E1::V` from the type namespace only.\n"
msgstr "// 仅从类型命名空间导入 `E1::V`。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:833 src/patterns.md:840
msgid "// For namespace masking.\n"
msgstr "// 用于命名空间遮蔽。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:838
msgid "// Import `E2::V` from the value namespace only.\n"
msgstr "// 仅从值命名空间导入 `E2::V`。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:846
msgid "// This struct pattern matches against the tuple-like\n"
msgstr "// 此结构体模式匹配类元组形式的 enum 变体，\n"

#: src/patterns.md:847
msgid "// enum variant whose constructor was found in the type\n"
msgstr "// 其构造器是在类型\n"

#: src/patterns.md:848 src/patterns.md:852
msgid "// namespace.\n"
msgstr "// 命名空间中找到的。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:850
msgid "// This tuple struct pattern matches against the tuple-like\n"
msgstr "// 此元组结构体模式匹配类元组形式的 enum 变体，\n"

#: src/patterns.md:851
msgid "// enum variant whose constructor was found in the value\n"
msgstr "// 其构造器是在值\n"

#: src/patterns.md:855
msgid "// Required due to the odd behavior of `super` within functions.\n"
msgstr "// 这是必需的，因为 `super` 在函数内的行为比较特殊。\n"

#: src/patterns.md:859
msgid ""
"The Lang team has made certain decisions, such as in [PR #138458](https://"
"github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/138458), that raise questions about the "
"desirability of using the value namespace in this way for patterns, as "
"described in [PR #140593](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/"
"140593#issuecomment-2972338457). It might be prudent to not intentionally "
"rely on this nuance in your code."
msgstr ""
"语言团队（Lang team）已作出某些决定，例如 [PR #138458](https://github.com/"
"rust-lang/rust/pull/138458) 中的决定，这些决定引发了关于在模式中以这种方式使"
"用值命名空间是否可取的问题，如 [PR #140593](https://github.com/rust-lang/"
"rust/pull/140593#issuecomment-2972338457) 所述。在你的代码中不刻意依赖这种细"
"微行为，可能是较为谨慎的做法。"

#: src/patterns.md:861
msgid "r\\[patterns.tuple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.tuple\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:862
msgid "Tuple patterns"
msgstr "元组模式"

#: src/patterns.md:864
msgid "r\\[patterns.tuple.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.tuple.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:874
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple.intro\\] Tuple patterns match tuple values that match all "
"criteria defined by its subpatterns. They are also used to [destructure]"
"(#destructuring) a tuple."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple.intro\\] 元组模式匹配满足其子模式所定义全部条件的元组值。"
"它们也用于[解构](#destructuring)元组。"

#: src/patterns.md:877
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple.rest-syntax\\] The form `(..)` with a single \\"
"[RestPattern\\] is a special form that does not require a comma, and matches "
"a tuple of any size."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple.rest-syntax\\] 带有单个 \\[RestPattern\\] 的形式 `(..)` 是"
"一种特殊形式，它不需要逗号，并匹配任意大小的元组。"

#: src/patterns.md:880
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple.refutable\\] The tuple pattern is refutable when one of "
"its subpatterns is refutable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.tuple.refutable\\] 当元组模式的某个子模式可反驳时，该元组模式是"
"可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:883
msgid "An example of using tuple patterns:"
msgstr "使用元组模式的示例："

#: src/patterns.md:893
msgid "r\\[patterns.paren\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.paren\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:894
msgid "Grouped patterns"
msgstr "分组模式"

#: src/patterns.md:896
msgid "r\\[patterns.paren.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.paren.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:901
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.paren.intro\\] Enclosing a pattern in parentheses can be used "
"to explicitly control the precedence of compound patterns. For example, a "
"reference pattern next to a range pattern such as `&0..=5` is ambiguous and "
"is not allowed, but can be expressed with parentheses."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.paren.intro\\] 将模式括在圆括号中可以用于显式控制复合模式的优先"
"级。例如，像 `&0..=5` 这样引用模式紧邻范围模式的形式是有歧义的，因而不允许使"
"用，但可以用圆括号表达。"

#: src/patterns.md:912
msgid "r\\[patterns.slice\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.slice\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:913
msgid "Slice patterns"
msgstr "切片模式"

#: src/patterns.md:915
msgid "r\\[patterns.slice.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.slice.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:922
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.slice.intro\\] Slice patterns can match both arrays of fixed "
"size and slices of dynamic size."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.slice.intro\\] 切片模式既可以匹配固定大小的数组，也可以匹配动态"
"大小的切片。"

#: src/patterns.md:926
msgid "// Fixed size\n"
msgstr "// 固定大小\n"

#: src/patterns.md:929
msgid "\"starts with one\""
msgstr "\"starts with one\""

#: src/patterns.md:930
msgid "\"starts with something else\""
msgstr "\"starts with something else\""

#: src/patterns.md:934
msgid "// Dynamic size\n"
msgstr "// 动态大小\n"

#: src/patterns.md:937
msgid "/* this arm will not apply because the length doesn't match */"
msgstr "/* this arm will not apply because the length doesn't match */"

#: src/patterns.md:938
msgid "/* this arm will apply */"
msgstr "/* this arm will apply */"

#: src/patterns.md:939
msgid ""
"/* this wildcard is required, since the length is not known statically */"
msgstr ""
"/* this wildcard is required, since the length is not known statically */"

#: src/patterns.md:943
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.slice.refutable-array\\] Slice patterns are irrefutable when "
"matching an array as long as each element is irrefutable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.slice.refutable-array\\] 匹配数组时，只要每个元素都是不可反驳"
"的，切片模式就是不可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:946
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.slice.refutable-slice\\] When matching a slice, it is "
"irrefutable only in the form with a single `..` \\[rest pattern\\]\\"
"[patterns.rest\\] or [identifier pattern](#identifier-patterns) with the "
"`..` rest pattern as a subpattern."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.slice.refutable-slice\\] 匹配切片时，只有带有单个 `..` \\[剩余模"
"式\\]\\[patterns.rest\\]的形式，或以 `..` 剩余模式作为子模式的[标识符模式]"
"(#identifier-patterns)，才是不可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:949
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.slice.restriction\\] Within a slice, a range pattern without "
"both lower and upper bound must be enclosed in parentheses, as in `(a..)`, "
"to clarify it is intended to match against a single slice element. A range "
"pattern with both lower and upper bound, like `a..=b`, is not required to be "
"enclosed in parentheses."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.slice.restriction\\] 在切片内部，没有同时具备下界和上界的范围模"
"式必须括在圆括号中，如 `(a..)`，以明确它意在匹配单个切片元素。像 `a..=b` 这样"
"同时具有下界和上界的范围模式不需要括在圆括号中。"

#: src/patterns.md:952
msgid "r\\[patterns.path\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.path\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:953
msgid "Path patterns"
msgstr "路径模式"

#: src/patterns.md:955
msgid "r\\[patterns.path.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.path.syntax\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:960
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.path.intro\\] _Path patterns_ are patterns that refer either to "
"constant values or to structs or enum variants that have no fields."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.path.intro\\] *路径模式*是指向常量值，或者指向没有字段的 struct "
"或 enum 变体的模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:963
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.path.unqualified\\] Unqualified path patterns can refer to:"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.path.unqualified\\] 非限定路径模式可以指向："

#: src/patterns.md:966
msgid "enum variants"
msgstr "enum 变体"

#: src/patterns.md:967
msgid "structs"
msgstr "struct"

#: src/patterns.md:968
msgid "constants"
msgstr "常量"

#: src/patterns.md:969
msgid "associated constants"
msgstr "关联常量"

#: src/patterns.md:971
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.path.qualified\\] Qualified path patterns can only refer to "
"associated constants."
msgstr "r\\[patterns.path.qualified\\] 限定路径模式只能指向关联常量。"

#: src/patterns.md:974
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.path.refutable\\] Path patterns are irrefutable when they refer "
"to structs or an enum variant when the enum has only one variant or a "
"constant whose type is irrefutable. They are refutable when they refer to "
"refutable constants or enum variants for enums with multiple variants."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.path.refutable\\] 当路径模式指向 struct、仅有一个变体的 enum 的"
"某个 enum 变体，或类型不可反驳的常量时，它们是不可反驳的。当它们指向可反驳常"
"量，或具有多个变体的 enum 的 enum 变体时，它们是可反驳的。"

#: src/patterns.md:977
msgid "r\\[patterns.const\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.const\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:978
msgid "Constant patterns"
msgstr "常量模式"

#: src/patterns.md:980
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.const.partial-eq\\] When a constant `C` of type `T` is used as "
"a pattern, we first check that `T: PartialEq`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.const.partial-eq\\] 当类型为 `T` 的常量 `C` 被用作模式时，我们首"
"先检查 `T: PartialEq`。"

#: src/patterns.md:983
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.const.structural-equality\\] Furthermore we require that the "
"value of `C` _has (recursive) structural equality_, which is defined "
"recursively as follows:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.const.structural-equality\\] 此外，我们要求 `C` 的值*具有（递归"
"的）结构相等性*，其递归定义如下："

#: src/patterns.md:986
msgid "r\\[patterns.const.primitive\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.const.primitive\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:987
msgid ""
"Integers as well as `str`, `bool` and `char` values always have structural "
"equality."
msgstr "整数以及 `str`、`bool` 和 `char` 值始终具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:989
msgid "r\\[patterns.const.builtin-aggregate\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.const.builtin-aggregate\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:990
msgid ""
"Tuples, arrays, and slices have structural equality if all their fields/"
"elements have structural equality. (In particular, `()` and `[]` always have "
"structural equality.)"
msgstr ""
"如果元组、数组和切片的所有字段/元素都具有结构相等性，则它们具有结构相等性。"
"（特别是，`()` 和 `[]` 始终具有结构相等性。）"

#: src/patterns.md:992
msgid "r\\[patterns.const.ref\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.const.ref\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:993
msgid ""
"References have structural equality if the value they point to has "
"structural equality."
msgstr "如果引用所指向的值具有结构相等性，则该引用具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:995
msgid "r\\[patterns.const.aggregate\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.const.aggregate\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:996
msgid ""
"A value of `struct` or `enum` type has structural equality if its "
"`PartialEq` instance is derived via `#[derive(PartialEq)]`, and all fields "
"(for enums: of the active variant) have structural equality."
msgstr ""
"如果 `struct` 或 `enum` 类型的值的 `PartialEq` 实例是通过 "
"`#[derive(PartialEq)]` 派生的，并且所有字段（对于 enum：活动变体的所有字段）"
"都具有结构相等性，则该值具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:998
msgid "r\\[patterns.const.pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.const.pointer\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:999
msgid ""
"A raw pointer has structural equality if it was defined as a constant "
"integer (and then cast/transmuted)."
msgstr ""
"如果原始指针被定义为常量整数（然后被强制转换/transmute），则它具有结构相等"
"性。"

#: src/patterns.md:1001
msgid "r\\[patterns.const.float\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.const.float\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:1002
msgid "A float value has structural equality if it is not a `NaN`."
msgstr "如果浮点数值不是 `NaN`，则它具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:1004
msgid "r\\[patterns.const.exhaustive\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.const.exhaustive\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:1005
msgid "Nothing else has structural equality."
msgstr "其他任何东西都不具有结构相等性。"

#: src/patterns.md:1007
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.const.generic\\] In particular, the value of `C` must be known "
"at pattern-building time (which is pre-monomorphization). This means that "
"associated consts that involve generic parameters cannot be used as patterns."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.const.generic\\] 特别是，`C` 的值必须在模式构建时已知（即单态化"
"前，pre-monomorphization）。这意味着涉及泛型参数的关联 const 不能用作模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:1010
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.const.immutable\\] The value of `C` must not contain any "
"references to mutable statics (`static mut` items or interior mutable "
"`static` items) or `extern` statics."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.const.immutable\\] `C` 的值不得包含任何指向可变静态项（`static "
"mut` 项或内部可变的 `static` 项）或 `extern` 静态项的引用。"

#: src/patterns.md:1013
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.const.translation\\] After ensuring all conditions are met, the "
"constant value is translated into a pattern, and now behaves exactly as-if "
"that pattern had been written directly. In particular, it fully participates "
"in exhaustiveness checking. (For raw pointers, constants are the only way to "
"write such patterns. Only `_` is ever considered exhaustive for these types.)"
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.const.translation\\] 在确保所有条件都满足之后，该常量值会被转换"
"为一个模式，并且现在的行为完全如同直接写出了该模式一样。特别是，它会完整参与"
"穷尽性检查。（对于原始指针，常量是书写这类模式的唯一方式。对于这些类型，只有 "
"`_` 会被认为是穷尽的。）"

#: src/patterns.md:1016
msgid "r\\[patterns.or\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.or\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:1017
msgid "Or-patterns"
msgstr "Or-patterns（或模式）"

#: src/patterns.md:1019
msgid ""
"_Or-patterns_ are patterns that match on one of two or more sub-patterns "
"(for example `A | B | C`). They can nest arbitrarily. Syntactically, or-"
"patterns are allowed in any of the places where other patterns are allowed "
"(represented by the \\[Pattern\\] production), with the exceptions of "
"`let`\\-bindings and function and closure parameters (represented by the \\"
"[PatternNoTopAlt\\] production)."
msgstr ""
"*Or-patterns（或模式）*是匹配两个或多个子模式之一的模式（例如 `A | B | C`）。"
"它们可以任意嵌套。在语法上，or-patterns 可以出现在允许其他模式出现的任何位置"
"（由 \\[Pattern\\] 产生式表示），但 `let`\\-绑定以及函数和闭包参数例外（由 \\"
"[PatternNoTopAlt\\] 产生式表示）。"

#: src/patterns.md:1021
msgid "r\\[patterns.constraints\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.constraints\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:1022
msgid "Static semantics"
msgstr "静态语义"

#: src/patterns.md:1024
msgid "r\\[patterns.constraints.pattern\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.constraints.pattern\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:1025
msgid ""
"Given a pattern `p | q` at some depth for some arbitrary patterns `p` and "
"`q`, the pattern is considered ill-formed if:"
msgstr ""
"给定某个深度处的模式 `p | q`，其中 `p` 和 `q` 是任意模式；如果满足以下情况，"
"则该模式被认为是形式不良的："

#: src/patterns.md:1027
msgid ""
"the type inferred for `p` does not unify with the type inferred for `q`, or"
msgstr "为 `p` 推断出的类型不能与为 `q` 推断出的类型合一，或"

#: src/patterns.md:1028
msgid "the same set of bindings are not introduced in `p` and `q`, or"
msgstr "`p` 和 `q` 中引入的不是同一组绑定，或"

#: src/patterns.md:1029
msgid ""
"the type of any two bindings with the same name in `p` and `q` do not unify "
"with respect to types or binding modes."
msgstr "`p` 和 `q` 中任何两个同名绑定的类型在类型或绑定模式方面不能合一。"

#: src/patterns.md:1031
msgid ""
"Unification of types is in all instances aforementioned exact and implicit "
"[type coercions](type-coercions.md) do not apply."
msgstr ""
"上述所有情况下，类型合一都是精确的，隐式[类型强制转换](type-coercions.md)不适"
"用。"

#: src/patterns.md:1033
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.constraints.match-type-check\\] 2. When type checking an "
"expression `match e_s { a_1 => e_1, ... a_n => e_n }`, for each match arm "
"`a_i` which contains a pattern of form `p_i | q_i`, the pattern `p_i | q_i` "
"is considered ill formed if, at the depth `d` where it exists the fragment "
"of `e_s` at depth `d`, the type of the expression fragment does not unify "
"with `p_i | q_i`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.constraints.match-type-check\\] 2. 对表达式 `match e_s { a_1 => "
"e_1, ... a_n => e_n }` 进行类型检查时，对于每个包含 `p_i | q_i` 形式模式的 "
"match 分支 `a_i`，如果在它所在的深度 `d` 处，`e_s` 在深度 `d` 的表达式片段的"
"类型不能与 `p_i | q_i` 合一，则模式 `p_i | q_i` 被认为是形式不良的。"

#: src/patterns.md:1036
msgid ""
"r\\[patterns.constraints.exhaustiveness-or-pattern\\] 3. With respect to "
"exhaustiveness checking, a pattern `p | q` is considered to cover `p` as "
"well as `q`. For some constructor `c(x, ..)` the distributive law applies "
"such that `c(p | q, ..rest)` covers the same set of value as `c(p, ..rest) | "
"c(q, ..rest)` does. This can be applied recursively until there are no more "
"nested patterns of form `p | q` other than those that exist at the top level."
msgstr ""
"r\\[patterns.constraints.exhaustiveness-or-pattern\\] 3. 就穷尽性检查而言，模"
"式 `p | q` 被认为既覆盖 `p`，也覆盖 `q`。对于某个构造器 `c(x, ..)`，分配律适"
"用，使得 `c(p | q, ..rest)` 覆盖与 `c(p, ..rest) | c(q, ..rest)` 相同的值集"
"合。这可以递归应用，直到除了位于顶层的 `p | q` 形式模式之外，不再存在嵌套的这"
"类模式。"

#: src/patterns.md:1039
msgid ""
"Note that by _\"constructor\"_ we do not refer to tuple struct patterns, but "
"rather we refer to a pattern for any product type. This includes enum "
"variants, tuple structs, structs with named fields, arrays, tuples, and "
"slices."
msgstr ""
"注意，所谓 *\"构造器\"* 并不是指元组结构体模式，而是指任何积类型的模式。这包"
"括 enum 变体、元组结构体、带命名字段的 struct、数组、元组和切片。"

#: src/patterns.md:1041
msgid "r\\[patterns.behavior\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.behavior\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:1042
msgid "Dynamic semantics"
msgstr "动态语义"

#: src/patterns.md:1044
msgid "r\\[patterns.behavior.nested-or-patterns\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.behavior.nested-or-patterns\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:1045
msgid ""
"The dynamic semantics of pattern matching a scrutinee expression `e_s` "
"against a pattern `c(p | q, ..rest)` at depth `d` where `c` is some "
"constructor, `p` and `q` are arbitrary patterns, and `rest` is optionally "
"any remaining potential factors in `c`, is defined as being the same as that "
"of `c(p, ..rest) | c(q, ..rest)`."
msgstr ""
"在深度 `d` 处，将被匹配值表达式 `e_s` 与模式 `c(p | q, ..rest)` 进行模式匹配"
"的动态语义，被定义为与 `c(p, ..rest) | c(q, ..rest)` 的动态语义相同；其中 "
"`c` 是某个构造器，`p` 和 `q` 是任意模式，`rest` 可选地表示 `c` 中任何剩余的潜"
"在因子。"

#: src/patterns.md:1047
msgid "r\\[patterns.precedence\\]"
msgstr "r\\[patterns.precedence\\]"

#: src/patterns.md:1048
msgid "Precedence with other undelimited patterns"
msgstr "与其他无定界模式的优先级"

#: src/patterns.md:1050
msgid ""
"As shown elsewhere in this chapter, there are several types of patterns that "
"are syntactically undelimited, including identifier patterns, reference "
"patterns, and or-patterns. Or-patterns always have the lowest-precedence. "
"This allows us to reserve syntactic space for a possible future type "
"ascription feature and also to reduce ambiguity. For example, `x @ A(..) | "
"B(..)` will result in an error that `x` is not bound in all patterns. `&A(x) "
"| B(x)` will result in a type mismatch between `x` in the different "
"subpatterns."
msgstr ""
"如本章其他地方所示，有几类模式在语法上是无定界的，包括标识符模式、引用模式和 "
"or-patterns（或模式）。Or-patterns 始终具有最低优先级。这使我们能够为未来可能"
"的类型标注特性保留语法空间，也能减少歧义。例如，`x @ A(..) | B(..)` 会导致错"
"误，因为 `x` 并未在所有模式中绑定。`&A(x) | B(x)` 会导致不同子模式中的 `x` 之"
"间出现类型不匹配。"

#: src/types.md:1
msgid "r\\[type\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type\\]"

#: src/types.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.intro\\] Every variable, item, and value in a Rust program has a "
"type. The _type_ of a _value_ defines the interpretation of the memory "
"holding it and the operations that may be performed on the value."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.intro\\] Rust 程序中的每个变量、项和值都有类型。*值* 的 *类型* 定义"
"了如何解释保存该值的内存，以及可以对该值执行哪些操作。"

#: src/types.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[type.builtin\\] Built-in types are tightly integrated into the language, "
"in nontrivial ways that are not possible to emulate in user-defined types."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.builtin\\] 内置类型以非平凡的方式紧密集成到语言中，这些方式无法用用"
"户定义类型来模拟。"

#: src/types.md:10
