"represent every memory address in the process."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.numeric.int.size.usize\\] `usize` 类型是一种无符号整数类型，其位数与"
"平台的指针类型相同。它可以表示进程中的每个内存地址。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:40
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] While a `usize` can represent every _address_, converting a "
"_pointer_ to a `usize` is not necessarily a reversible operation. For more "
"information, see the documentation for [type cast expressions](../"
"expressions/operator-expr.md#type-cast-expressions), \\[`std::ptr`\\], and \\"
"[provenance\\]\\[std::ptr#provenance\\] in particular."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 虽然 `usize` 可以表示每个*地址*，但将*指针*转换为 `usize` 不一定"
"是可逆操作。更多信息请参见[类型转换表达式](../expressions/operator-"
"expr.md#type-cast-expressions)、\\[`std::ptr`\\]，尤其是 \\[provenance（来"
"源）\\]\\[std::ptr#provenance\\] 的文档。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:43
msgid ""
"r\\[type.numeric.int.size.isize\\] The `isize` type is a signed two's "
"complement integer type with the same number of bits as the platform's "
"pointer type. The theoretical upper bound on object and array size is the "
"maximum `isize` value. This ensures that `isize` can be used to calculate "
"differences between pointers into an object or array and can address every "
"byte within an object along with one byte past the end."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.numeric.int.size.isize\\] `isize` 类型是一种有符号二进制补码整数类"
"型，其位数与平台的指针类型相同。对象和数组大小的理论上限是 `isize` 的最大值。"
"这确保 `isize` 可用于计算指向对象或数组内部的指针之间的差值，并且能够寻址对象"
"内的每个字节以及末尾之后一个字节。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:46
msgid ""
"r\\[type.numeric.int.size.minimum\\] `usize` and `isize` are at least 16-"
"bits wide."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.numeric.int.size.minimum\\] `usize` 和 `isize` 至少为 16 位宽。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:49
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Many pieces of Rust code may assume that pointers, `usize`, and "
"`isize` are either 32-bit or 64-bit. As a consequence, 16-bit pointer "
"support is limited and may require explicit care and acknowledgment from a "
"library to support."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 许多 Rust 代码可能假定指针、`usize` 和 `isize` 要么是 32 位，要么"
"是 64 位。因此，对 16 位指针的支持是有限的，并且可能需要库显式谨慎处理并确认"
"支持。"

#: src/types/numeric.md:52
msgid "r\\[type.numeric.validity\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.numeric.validity\\]"

#: src/types/numeric.md:55
msgid ""
"For every numeric type, `T`, the bit validity of `T` is equivalent to the "
"bit validity of `[u8; size_of::<T>()]`. An uninitialized byte is not a valid "
"`u8`."
msgstr ""
"对于每种数值类型 `T`，`T` 的位有效性等价于 `[u8; size_of::<T>()]` 的位有效"
"性。未初始化字节不是有效的 `u8`。"

#: src/types/char.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.char\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.char\\]"

#: src/types/char.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.char.intro\\] The `char` type represents a single [Unicode scalar "
"value](http://www.unicode.org/glossary/#unicode_scalar_value) (i.e., a code "
"point that is not a surrogate)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.char.intro\\] `char` 类型表示单个 [Unicode 标量值](http://"
"www.unicode.org/glossary/#unicode_scalar_value)（即不是代理项的码点）。"

#: src/types/char.md:10
msgid "'😀'"
msgstr "'😀'"

#: src/types/char.md:11
msgid "'\\u{1F600}'"
msgstr "'\\u{1F600}'"

#: src/types/char.md:14
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] See \\[the standard library docs\\]\\[`char`\\] for information "
"on the impls of the `char` type."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 有关 `char` 类型的 impl 信息，请参见 \\[标准库文档\\]\\"
"[`char`\\]。"

#: src/types/char.md:17
msgid ""
"r\\[type.char.value\\] A value of type `char` is represented as a 32-bit "
"unsigned word in the 0x0000 to 0xD7FF or 0xE000 to 0x10FFFF range. It is "
"immediate [undefined behavior](../behavior-considered-undefined.md) to "
"create a `char` that falls outside this range."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.char.value\\] `char` 类型的值表示为一个 32 位无符号字，位于 0x0000 "
"到 0xD7FF 或 0xE000 到 0x10FFFF 范围内。创建落在此范围之外的 `char` 会立即导"
"致 [未定义行为](../behavior-considered-undefined.md)。"

#: src/types/char.md:20
msgid ""
"r\\[type.char.layout\\] `char` is guaranteed to have the same size and "
"alignment as `u32` on all platforms."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.char.layout\\] 保证 `char` 在所有平台上都具有与 `u32` 相同的大小和对"
"齐。"

#: src/types/char.md:23
msgid ""
"r\\[type.char.validity\\] Every byte of a `char` is guaranteed to be "
"initialized. In other words, `transmute::<char, [u8; size_of::"
"<char>()]>(...)` is always sound -- but since some bit patterns are invalid "
"`char`s, the inverse is not always sound."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.char.validity\\] 保证 `char` 的每个字节都已初始化。换言之，"
"`transmute::<char, [u8; size_of::<char>()]>(...)` 始终是健全的，但由于某些位"
"模式是无效的 `char`，其逆向转换并不总是健全的。"

#: src/types/str.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.str\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.str\\]"

#: src/types/str.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.str.intro\\] The string slice (`str`) type represents a sequence of "
"characters."
msgstr "r\\[type.str.intro\\] 字符串切片（`str`）类型表示一个字符序列。"

#: src/types/str.md:9
msgid "\"你好，世界\""
msgstr "\"你好，世界\""

#: src/types/str.md:12
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] See \\[the standard library docs\\]\\[`str`\\] for information "
"on the impls of the `str` type."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 有关 `str` 类型的 impl 信息，请参见 \\[标准库文档\\]\\[`str`\\]。"

#: src/types/str.md:15
msgid ""
"r\\[type.str.value\\] A value of type `str` is represented in the same way "
"as `[u8]`, a slice of 8-bit unsigned bytes."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.str.value\\] `str` 类型的值以与 `[u8]` 相同的方式表示，即一个 8 位无"
"符号字节的切片。"

#: src/types/str.md:18
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The standard library makes extra assumptions about `str`: "
"methods working on `str` assume and ensure that the data it contains is "
"valid UTF-8. Calling a `str` method with a non-UTF-8 buffer can cause "
"[undefined behavior](../behavior-considered-undefined.md) now or in the "
"future."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 标准库对 `str` 作出额外假设：作用于 `str` 的方法会假设并确保它包"
"含的数据是有效的 UTF-8。现在或将来，使用非 UTF-8 缓冲区调用 `str` 方法都可能"
"导致 [未定义行为](../behavior-considered-undefined.md)。"

#: src/types/str.md:21
msgid ""
"r\\[type.str.unsized\\] A `str` is a [dynamically sized type](../dynamically-"
"sized-types.md). It can only be instantiated through a pointer type, such as "
"`&str`. The layout of `&str` is the same as the layout of `&[u8]`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.str.unsized\\] `str` 是一种 [动态大小类型](../dynamically-sized-"
"types.md)。它只能通过指针类型来实例化，例如 `&str`。`&str` 的布局与 `&[u8]` "
"的布局相同。"

#: src/types/never.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.never\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.never\\]"

#: src/types/never.md:4
msgid "r\\[type.never.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.never.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/never.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[type.never.intro\\] The never type `!` is a type with no values, "
"representing the result of computations that never complete."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.never.intro\\] never 类型 `!` 是一种没有值的类型，表示永不完成的计算"
"的结果。"

#: src/types/never.md:12
msgid ""
"r\\[type.never.coercion\\] Expressions of type `!` can be coerced into any "
"other type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.never.coercion\\] 类型为 `!` 的表达式可以被强制转换为任何其他类型。"

#: src/types/never.md:15
msgid ""
"r\\[type.never.constraint\\] The `!` type can **only** appear in function "
"return types presently, indicating it is a diverging function that never "
"returns."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.never.constraint\\] 目前，`!` 类型**只能**出现在函数返回类型中，表示"
"该函数是一个永不返回的发散函数。"

#: src/types/never.md:20
msgid "\"This call never returns.\""
msgstr "\"This call never returns.\""

#: src/types/tuple.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.tuple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.tuple\\]"

#: src/types/tuple.md:4
msgid "r\\[type.tuple.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.tuple.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/tuple.md:11
msgid ""
"r\\[type.tuple.intro\\] _Tuple types_ are a family of structural types[^1] "
"for heterogeneous lists of other types."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.tuple.intro\\] *元组类型*是一族结构类型[^1]，用于由其他类型组成的异"
"构列表。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:14
msgid ""
"The syntax for a tuple type is a parenthesized, comma-separated list of "
"types."
msgstr "元组类型的语法是一个用括号括起、以逗号分隔的类型列表。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[type.tuple.restriction\\] 1-ary tuples require a comma after their "
"element type to be disambiguated with a [parenthesized type](../"
"types.md#parenthesized-types)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.tuple.restriction\\] 一元元组要求在其元素类型后带有逗号，以便与[带括"
"号类型](../types.md#parenthesized-types)区分开。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:19
msgid ""
"r\\[type.tuple.field-number\\] A tuple type has a number of fields equal to "
"the length of the list of types. This number of fields determines the "
"_arity_ of the tuple. A tuple with `n` fields is called an _n-ary tuple_. "
"For example, a tuple with 2 fields is a 2-ary tuple."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.tuple.field-number\\] 元组类型的字段数等于类型列表的长度。该字段数决"
"定元组的*元数*。具有 `n` 个字段的元组称为 *n 元元组*。例如，具有 2 个字段的元"
"组是二元元组。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:22
msgid ""
"r\\[type.tuple.field-name\\] Fields of tuples are named using increasing "
"numeric names matching their position in the list of types. The first field "
"is `0`. The second field is `1`. And so on. The type of each field is the "
"type of the same position in the tuple's list of types."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.tuple.field-name\\] 元组的字段使用与它们在类型列表中位置相匹配的递增"
"数字名称来命名。第一个字段是 `0`。第二个字段是 `1`。以此类推。每个字段的类型"
"是元组类型列表中相同位置的类型。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:25
msgid ""
"r\\[type.tuple.unit\\] For convenience and historical reasons, the tuple "
"type with no fields (`()`) is often called _unit_ or _the unit type_. Its "
"one value is also called _unit_ or _the unit value_."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.tuple.unit\\] 出于便利和历史原因，没有字段的元组类型（`()`）通常称"
"为 _unit_ 或 _the unit type_（单元类型）。它的唯一值也称为 _unit_ 或 _the "
"unit value_（单元值）。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:28
msgid "Some examples of tuple types:"
msgstr "元组类型的一些示例："

#: src/types/tuple.md:31
msgid "`(i32,)` (1-ary tuple)"
msgstr "`(i32,)`（1-ary 元组）"

#: src/types/tuple.md:33
msgid "`(String, i32)`"
msgstr "`(String, i32)`"

#: src/types/tuple.md:34
msgid "`(i32, String)` (different type from the previous example)"
msgstr "`(i32, String)`（与前一个示例是不同的类型）"

#: src/types/tuple.md:35
msgid "`(i32, f64, Vec<String>, Option<bool>)`"
msgstr "`(i32, f64, Vec<String>, Option<bool>)`"

#: src/types/tuple.md:37
msgid ""
"r\\[type.tuple.constructor\\] Values of this type are constructed using a "
"[tuple expression](../expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-expressions). "
"Furthermore, various expressions will produce the unit value if there is no "
"other meaningful value for it to evaluate to."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.tuple.constructor\\] 此类型的值使用[元组表达式](../expressions/"
"tuple-expr.md#tuple-expressions)构造。此外，当没有其他有意义的求值结果时，各"
"种表达式会产生单元值。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:40
msgid ""
"r\\[type.tuple.access\\] Tuple fields can be accessed by either a [tuple "
"index expression](../expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions) "
"or [pattern matching](../patterns.md#tuple-patterns)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.tuple.access\\] 元组字段可以通过[元组索引表达式](../expressions/"
"tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions)或[模式匹配](../patterns.md#tuple-"
"patterns)访问。"

#: src/types/tuple.md:43
msgid ""
"Structural types are always equivalent if their internal types are "
"equivalent. For a nominal version of tuples, see [tuple structs](./"
"struct.md)."
msgstr ""
"如果结构类型的内部类型等价，那么它们总是等价的。关于元组的名义版本，请参见 "
"[元组结构体](./struct.md)。"

#: src/types/array.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.array\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.array\\]"

#: src/types/array.md:4
msgid "r\\[type.array.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.array.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/array.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[type.array.intro\\] An array is a fixed-size sequence of `N` elements of "
"type `T`. The array type is written as `[T; N]`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.array.intro\\] 数组是由 `N` 个 `T` 类型元素组成的固定大小序列。数组"
"类型写作 `[T; N]`。"

#: src/types/array.md:12
msgid ""
"r\\[type.array.constraint\\] The size is a [constant expression](../"
"const_eval.md#constant-expressions) that evaluates to a [`usize`]"
"(numeric.md#machine-dependent-integer-types)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.array.constraint\\] 大小是一个 [常量表达式](../"
"const_eval.md#constant-expressions)，其求值结果为 [`usize`]"
"(numeric.md#machine-dependent-integer-types)。"

#: src/types/array.md:18
msgid "// A stack-allocated array\n"
msgstr "// 栈上分配的数组\n"

#: src/types/array.md:20 src/types/slice.md:22
msgid "// A heap-allocated array, coerced to a slice\n"
msgstr "// 堆上分配的数组，被强制转换为切片\n"

#: src/types/array.md:25
msgid ""
"r\\[type.array.index\\] All elements of arrays are always initialized, and "
"access to an array is always bounds-checked in safe methods and operators."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.array.index\\] 数组的所有元素始终已初始化，并且在安全方法和运算符中"
"访问数组始终会进行边界检查。"

#: src/types/array.md:28
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The \\[`Vec<T>`\\] standard library type provides a heap-"
"allocated resizable array type."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] \\[`Vec<T>`\\] 标准库类型提供了一种堆分配的可调整大小数组类型。"

#: src/types/slice.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.slice\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.slice\\]"

#: src/types/slice.md:4
msgid "r\\[type.slice.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.slice.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/slice.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[type.slice.intro\\] A slice is a [dynamically sized type](../dynamically-"
"sized-types.md) representing a 'view' into a sequence of elements of type "
"`T`. The slice type is written as `[T]`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.slice.intro\\] 切片是一种 [动态大小类型](../dynamically-sized-"
"types.md)，表示对 `T` 类型元素序列的一个“视图”。切片类型写作 `[T]`。"

#: src/types/slice.md:12
msgid ""
"r\\[type.slice.unsized\\] Slice types are generally used through pointer "
"types. For example:"
msgstr "r\\[type.slice.unsized\\] 切片类型通常通过指针类型使用。例如："

#: src/types/slice.md:15
msgid ""
"`&[T]`: a 'shared slice', often just called a 'slice'. It doesn't own the "
"data it points to; it borrows it."
msgstr ""
"`&[T]`：一个“共享切片”，通常简称为“切片”。它不拥有其所指向的数据；它借用了这"
"些数据。"

#: src/types/slice.md:16
msgid ""
"`&mut [T]`: a 'mutable slice'. It mutably borrows the data it points to."
msgstr "`&mut [T]`：一个“可变切片”。它可变地借用其所指向的数据。"

#: src/types/slice.md:17
msgid "`Box<[T]>`: a 'boxed slice'"
msgstr "`Box<[T]>`：一个“装箱切片”"

#: src/types/slice.md:24
msgid "// A (shared) slice into an array\n"
msgstr "// 数组的（共享）切片\n"

#: src/types/slice.md:29
msgid ""
"r\\[type.slice.safe\\] All elements of slices are always initialized, and "
"access to a slice is always bounds-checked in safe methods and operators."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.slice.safe\\] 切片的所有元素始终已初始化，并且在安全方法和运算符中访"
"问切片始终会进行边界检查。"

#: src/types/struct.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.struct\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.struct\\]"

#: src/types/struct.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.struct.intro\\] A `struct` _type_ is a heterogeneous product of "
"other types, called the _fields_ of the type.[^structtype]"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.struct.intro\\] `struct` *类型*是其他类型的异构积，这些其他类型称为"
"该类型的*字段*。[^structtype]"

#: src/types/struct.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[type.struct.constructor\\] New instances of a `struct` can be "
"constructed with a [struct expression](../expressions/struct-expr.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.struct.constructor\\] 可以使用[结构体表达式](../expressions/struct-"
"expr.md)构造 `struct` 的新实例。"

#: src/types/struct.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[type.struct.layout\\] The memory layout of a `struct` is undefined by "
"default to allow for compiler optimizations like field reordering, but it "
"can be fixed with the [`repr` attribute](../type-layout.md#representations). "
"In either case, fields may be given in any order in a corresponding struct "
"_expression_; the resulting `struct` value will always have the same memory "
"layout."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.struct.layout\\] `struct` 的内存布局默认未定义，以允许字段重排等编译"
"器优化，但可以通过 [`repr` 属性](../type-layout.md#representations)固定其布"
"局。在任一情况下，都可以在相应的 struct *表达式*中以任意顺序给出字段；生成的 "
"`struct` 值始终具有相同的内存布局。"

#: src/types/struct.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[type.struct.field-visibility\\] The fields of a `struct` may be "
"qualified by [visibility modifiers](../visibility-and-privacy.md), to allow "
"access to data in a struct outside a module."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.struct.field-visibility\\] `struct` 的字段可以由[可见性修饰符](../"
"visibility-and-privacy.md)限定，以允许在模块外部访问结构体中的数据。"

#: src/types/struct.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[type.struct.tuple\\] A _tuple struct_ type is just like a struct type, "
"except that the fields are anonymous."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.struct.tuple\\] *元组结构体*类型与结构体类型类似，只是字段是匿名的。"

#: src/types/struct.md:19
msgid ""
"r\\[type.struct.unit\\] A _unit-like struct_ type is like a struct type, "
"except that it has no fields. The one value constructed by the associated "
"[struct expression](../expressions/struct-expr.md) is the only value that "
"inhabits such a type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.struct.unit\\] *类单元结构体*类型与结构体类型类似，只是它没有字段。"
"由关联的[结构体表达式](../expressions/struct-expr.md)构造的那一个值，是这种类"
"型唯一拥有的值。"

#: src/types/struct.md:22
msgid ""
"`struct` types are analogous to `struct` types in C, the _record_ types of "
"the ML family, or the _struct_ types of the Lisp family."
msgstr ""
"`struct` 类型类似于 C 中的 `struct` 类型、ML 家族中的 _record_ 类型，或 Lisp "
"家族中的 _struct_ 类型。"

#: src/types/enum.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.enum\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.enum\\]"

#: src/types/enum.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.enum.intro\\] An _enumerated type_ is a nominal, heterogeneous "
"disjoint union type, denoted by the name of an [`enum` item](../items/"
"enumerations.md). [^enumtype]"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.enum.intro\\] *枚举类型*是一种名义的异构不交联合类型，由 [`enum` 项]"
"(../items/enumerations.md)的名称表示。[^enumtype]"

#: src/types/enum.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[type.enum.declaration\\] An [`enum` item](../items/enumerations.md) "
"declares both the type and a number of _variants_, each of which is "
"independently named and has the syntax of a struct, tuple struct or unit-"
"like struct."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.enum.declaration\\] 一个 [`enum` 项](../items/enumerations.md)同时声"
"明类型和若干*变体*，每个变体都有独立名称，并具有结构体、元组结构体或类单元结"
"构体的语法。"

#: src/types/enum.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[type.enum.constructor\\] New instances of an `enum` can be constructed "
"with a [struct expression](../expressions/struct-expr.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.enum.constructor\\] 可以使用 [结构体表达式](../expressions/struct-"
"expr.md)构造 `enum` 的新实例。"

#: src/types/enum.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[type.enum.value\\] Any `enum` value consumes as much memory as the "
"largest variant for its corresponding `enum` type, as well as the size "
"needed to store a discriminant."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.enum.value\\] 任何 `enum` 值消耗的内存都等于其对应 `enum` 类型中最大"
"变体所需的内存，再加上存储判别值所需的大小。"

#: src/types/enum.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[type.enum.name\\] Enum types cannot be denoted _structurally_ as types, "
"but must be denoted by named reference to an [`enum` item](../items/"
"enumerations.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.enum.name\\] 枚举类型不能作为类型被*结构性地*表示，而必须通过对 "
"[`enum` 项](../items/enumerations.md)的具名引用来表示。"

#: src/types/enum.md:19
msgid ""
"The `enum` type is analogous to a `data` constructor declaration in Haskell, "
"or a _pick ADT_ in Limbo."
msgstr ""
"`enum` 类型类似于 Haskell 中的 `data` 构造器声明，或 Limbo 中的 _pick ADT_。"

#: src/types/union.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.union\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.union\\]"

#: src/types/union.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.union.intro\\] A _union type_ is a nominal, heterogeneous C-like "
"union, denoted by the name of a [`union` item](../items/unions.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.union.intro\\] *联合体类型*是一种名义的异构类 C union，由 [`union` "
"项](../items/unions.md)的名称表示。"

#: src/types/union.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[type.union.access\\] Unions have no notion of an \"active field\". "
"Instead, every union access transmutes parts of the content of the union to "
"the type of the accessed field."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.union.access\\] 联合体没有“活动字段”的概念。相反，每次访问联合体时，"
"都会将联合体内容的一部分 transmute 为被访问字段的类型。"

#: src/types/union.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[type.union.safety\\] Since transmutes can cause unexpected or undefined "
"behaviour, `unsafe` is required to read from a union field."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.union.safety\\] 由于 transmute 可能导致意外行为或未定义行为，从联合"
"体字段读取需要 `unsafe`。"

#: src/types/union.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[type.union.constraint\\] Union field types are also restricted to a "
"subset of types which ensures that they never need dropping. See the [item]"
"(../items/unions.md) documentation for further details."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.union.constraint\\] 联合体字段类型也被限制为类型的一个子集，以确保它"
"们永远不需要析构。更多细节请参见[项](../items/unions.md)文档。"

#: src/types/union.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[type.union.layout\\] The memory layout of a `union` is undefined by "
"default (in particular, fields do _not_ have to be at offset 0), but the "
"`#[repr(...)]` attribute can be used to fix a layout."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.union.layout\\] `union` 的内存布局默认未定义（特别是，字段*不*必须位"
"于偏移量 0），但可以使用 `#[repr(...)]` 属性来固定布局。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.fn-item\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.fn-item\\]"

#: src/types/function-item.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.intro\\] When referred to, a function item, or the "
"constructor of a tuple-like struct or enum variant, yields a [zero-sized]"
"(glossary.zst) value of its _function item type_."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.intro\\] 在被引用时，函数项，或者类元组结构体或枚举变体的构"
"造器，会产生一个其*函数项类型*的[零大小](glossary.zst)值。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.unique\\] That type explicitly identifies the function - "
"its name, its type arguments, and its early-bound lifetime arguments (but "
"not its late-bound lifetime arguments, which are only assigned when the "
"function is called) - so the value does not need to contain an actual "
"function pointer, and no indirection is needed when the function is called."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.unique\\] 该类型会显式标识该函数，即它的名称、类型实参以及早"
"绑定生命周期实参（但不包括晚绑定生命周期实参，后者只有在调用函数时才会被赋"
"值），因此该值不需要包含实际的函数指针，并且调用函数时也不需要间接访问。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.name\\] There is no syntax that directly refers to a "
"function item type, but the compiler will display the type as something like "
"`fn(u32) -> i32 {fn_name}` in error messages."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.name\\] 没有语法可以直接引用函数项类型，但编译器会在错误消息"
"中将该类型显示为类似 `fn(u32) -> i32 {fn_name}` 的形式。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:13
msgid ""
"Because the function item type explicitly identifies the function, the item "
"types of different functions - different items, or the same item with "
"different generics - are distinct, and mixing them will create a type error:"
msgstr ""
"由于函数项类型会显式标识该函数，不同函数的项类型，即不同项，或同一项带有不同"
"泛型的情况，彼此是不同的；混用它们会产生类型错误："

#: src/types/function-item.md:18
msgid "//~ ERROR mismatched types\n"
msgstr "//~ ERROR mismatched types\n"

#: src/types/function-item.md:21
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.coercion\\] However, there is a [coercion](../type-"
"coercions.md) from function items to [function pointers](function-"
"pointer.md) with the same signature, which is triggered not only when a "
"function item is used when a function pointer is directly expected, but also "
"when different function item types with the same signature meet in different "
"arms of the same `if` or `match`:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.coercion\\] 不过，存在一种从函数项到具有相同签名的[函数指针]"
"(function-pointer.md)的[强制转换](../type-coercions.md)。这种转换不仅会在直接"
"期望函数指针却使用函数项时触发，也会在具有相同签名的不同函数项类型出现在同一"
"个 `if` 或 `match` 的不同分支中时触发："

#: src/types/function-item.md:27
msgid "// `foo_ptr_1` has function pointer type `fn()` here\n"
msgstr "// `foo_ptr_1` 在这里具有函数指针类型 `fn()`\n"

#: src/types/function-item.md:30
msgid "// ... and so does `foo_ptr_2` - this type-checks.\n"
msgstr "// ... `foo_ptr_2` 也是如此 - 这能通过类型检查。\n"

#: src/types/function-item.md:39
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.traits\\] All function items implement [`Copy`](../special-"
"types-and-traits.md#copy), [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone), "
"[`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send), and [`Sync`](../special-types-"
"and-traits.md#sync)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-item.traits\\] 所有函数项都实现 [`Copy`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#copy)、[`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone)、[`Send`]"
"(../special-types-and-traits.md#send) 和 [`Sync`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#sync)。"

#: src/types/function-item.md:42
msgid ""
"\\[`Fn`\\], \\[`FnMut`\\], and \\[`FnOnce`\\] are implemented unless the "
"function has any of the following:"
msgstr ""
"\\[`Fn`\\]、\\[`FnMut`\\] 和 \\[`FnOnce`\\] 会被实现，除非函数具有以下任一"
"项："

#: src/types/function-item.md:44
msgid "an \\[`unsafe`\\]\\[unsafe.fn\\] qualifier"
msgstr "一个 \\[`unsafe`\\]\\[unsafe.fn\\] 限定符"

#: src/types/function-item.md:45
msgid ""
"a \\[`target_feature` attribute\\]\\[attributes.codegen.target_feature\\]"
msgstr ""
"一个 \\[`target_feature` 属性\\]\\[attributes.codegen.target_feature\\]"

#: src/types/function-item.md:46
msgid "an \\[ABI\\]\\[items.fn.extern\\] other than `\"Rust\"`"
msgstr "一个不是 `\"Rust\"` 的 \\[ABI\\]\\[items.fn.extern\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.closure\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.intro\\] A [closure expression](../expressions/closure-"
"expr.md) produces a closure value with a unique, anonymous type that cannot "
"be written out. A closure type is approximately equivalent to a struct which "
"contains the captured values. For instance, the following closure:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.intro\\] [闭包表达式](../expressions/closure-expr.md)会产生"
"一个闭包值，其类型唯一、匿名且无法写出。闭包类型大致等价于一个包含被捕获值的 "
"struct。例如，以下闭包："

#: src/types/closure.md:26
msgid "// Prints \"Point { x: 2, y: 1 }\".\n"
msgstr "// 打印 \"Point { x: 2, y: 1 }\"。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:29
msgid "generates a closure type roughly like the following:"
msgstr "会生成大致如下的闭包类型："

#: src/types/closure.md:33
msgid ""
"// Note: This is not exactly how it is translated, this is only for\n"
"// illustration.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 注意：实际转换并非完全如此，这里仅用于\n"
"// 演示。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:43 src/types/closure.md:779
msgid "\"rust-call\""
msgstr "\"rust-call\""

#: src/types/closure.md:51
msgid "so that the call to `f` works as if it were:"
msgstr "因此，对 `f` 的调用会像下面这样工作："

#: src/types/closure.md:58
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:61
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.intro\\] A _capture mode_ determines how a [place "
"expression](../expressions.md#place-expressions-and-value-expressions) from "
"the environment is borrowed or moved into the closure. The capture modes are:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.intro\\] *捕获模式* 决定环境中的[位置表达式](../"
"expressions.md#place-expressions-and-value-expressions)如何被借用或移动进闭"
"包。捕获模式包括："

#: src/types/closure.md:64
msgid ""
"Immutable borrow (`ImmBorrow`) --- The place expression is captured as a "
"[shared reference](pointer.md#references--and-mut)."
msgstr ""
"不可变借用（`ImmBorrow`）--- 位置表达式会作为[共享引用]"
"(pointer.md#references--and-mut)被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:65
msgid ""
"Unique immutable borrow (`UniqueImmBorrow`) --- This is similar to an "
"immutable borrow, but must be unique as described [below](#unique-immutable-"
"borrows-in-captures)."
msgstr ""
"唯一不可变借用（`UniqueImmBorrow`）--- 这类似于不可变借用，但必须如[下文]"
"(#unique-immutable-borrows-in-captures)所述保持唯一。"

#: src/types/closure.md:66
msgid ""
"Mutable borrow (`MutBorrow`) --- The place expression is captured as a "
"[mutable reference](pointer.md#mutable-references-mut)."
msgstr ""
"可变借用（`MutBorrow`）--- 位置表达式会作为[可变引用](pointer.md#mutable-"
"references-mut)被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:67
msgid ""
"Move (`ByValue`) --- The place expression is captured by [moving the value]"
"(../expressions.md#moved-and-copied-types) into the closure."
msgstr ""
"移动（`ByValue`）--- 位置表达式通过将[值移动](../expressions.md#moved-and-"
"copied-types)进闭包来捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:69
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precedence\\] Place expressions from the "
"environment are captured from the first mode that is compatible with how the "
"captured value is used inside the closure body. The mode is not affected by "
"the code surrounding the closure, such as the lifetimes of involved "
"variables or fields, or of the closure itself."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precedence\\] 来自环境的位置表达式会按第一个与被捕获"
"值在闭包体内使用方式兼容的模式被捕获。该模式不受闭包周围代码影响，例如相关变"
"量、字段或闭包自身的生命周期。"

#: src/types/closure.md:77
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.copy\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.copy\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:78
msgid "`Copy` values"
msgstr "`Copy` 值"

#: src/types/closure.md:80
msgid ""
"Values that implement [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy) that are "
"moved into the closure are captured with the `ImmBorrow` mode."
msgstr ""
"被移动进闭包且实现 [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy) 的值，会以 "
"`ImmBorrow` 模式捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:85
msgid "// x captured by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// x 以 ImmBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:89
msgid "r\\[type.closure.async.input\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.async.input\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:90
msgid "Async input capture"
msgstr "async 输入捕获"

#: src/types/closure.md:92
msgid ""
"Async closures always capture all input arguments, regardless of whether or "
"not they are used within the body."
msgstr "async 闭包总是捕获所有输入实参，无论它们是否在闭包体内使用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:94
msgid "Capture precision"
msgstr "捕获精度"

#: src/types/closure.md:96
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.capture-path\\] A _capture path_ is a "
"sequence starting with a variable from the environment followed by zero or "
"more place projections from that variable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.capture-path\\] *捕获路径* 是一个序列，它"
"以环境中的变量开头，后接从该变量出发的零个或多个位置投影。"

#: src/types/closure.md:99
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.place-projection\\] A _place projection_ "
"is a [field access](../expressions/field-expr.md), [tuple index](../"
"expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions), [dereference](../"
"expressions/operator-expr.md#the-dereference-operator) (and automatic "
"dereferences), [array or slice index](../expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-"
"slice-indexing-expressions) expression, or [pattern destructuring]"
"(patterns.destructure) applied to a variable."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.place-projection\\] *位置投影* 是应用于变"
"量的[字段访问](../expressions/field-expr.md)、[元组索引](../expressions/"
"tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions)、[解引用](../expressions/operator-"
"expr.md#the-dereference-operator)（以及自动解引用）、[数组或切片索引](../"
"expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-slice-indexing-expressions)表达式，或[模"
"式解构](patterns.destructure)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:102
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] In `rustc`, pattern destructuring desugars into a series of "
"dereferences and field or element accesses."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 在 `rustc` 中，模式解构会脱糖为一系列解引用以及字段或元素访问。"

#: src/types/closure.md:105
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.intro\\] The closure borrows or moves the "
"capture path, which may be truncated based on the rules described below."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.intro\\] 闭包会借用或移动捕获路径，而该路"
"径可能会根据下文描述的规则被截断。"

#: src/types/closure.md:117
msgid "// s.f1.1 captured by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// s.f1.1 以 ImmBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:122
msgid ""
"Here the capture path is the local variable `s`, followed by a field access "
"`.f1`, and then a tuple index `.1`. This closure captures an immutable "
"borrow of `s.f1.1`."
msgstr ""
"这里的捕获路径是局部变量 `s`，后接字段访问 `.f1`，再后接元组索引 `.1`。此闭包"
"捕获的是对 `s.f1.1` 的不可变借用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:130
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.shared-prefix\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.shared-prefix\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:131
msgid "Shared prefix"
msgstr "共享前缀"

#: src/types/closure.md:133
msgid ""
"In the case where a capture path and one of the ancestors of that path are "
"both captured by a closure, the ancestor path is captured with the highest "
"capture mode among the two captures, `CaptureMode = max(AncestorCaptureMode, "
"DescendantCaptureMode)`, using the strict weak ordering:"
msgstr ""
"当一个捕获路径及该路径的某个祖先路径都被同一闭包捕获时，祖先路径会使用两次捕"
"获中较高的捕获模式来捕获，即 `CaptureMode = max(AncestorCaptureMode, "
"DescendantCaptureMode)`，其中采用以下严格弱序："

#: src/types/closure.md:135
msgid "`ImmBorrow < UniqueImmBorrow < MutBorrow < ByValue`"
msgstr "`ImmBorrow < UniqueImmBorrow < MutBorrow < ByValue`"

#: src/types/closure.md:137
msgid "Note that this might need to be applied recursively."
msgstr "注意，这可能需要递归应用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:140
msgid ""
"// In this example, there are three different capture paths with a shared "
"ancestor:\n"
msgstr "// 在此示例中，有三条不同的捕获路径拥有一个共享祖先：\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:142 src/paths.md:141
msgid "\"S\""
msgstr "\"S\""

#: src/types/closure.md:143
msgid "\"T\""
msgstr "\"T\""

#: src/types/closure.md:144
msgid "\"U\""
msgstr "\"U\""

#: src/types/closure.md:147
msgid "// u captured by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// u 以 ImmBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:148
msgid "// u.1 captured by MutBorrow\n"
msgstr "// u.1 以 MutBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:149
msgid "// u.0.0 captured by ByValue\n"
msgstr "// u.0.0 以 ByValue 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:154
msgid "Overall this closure will capture `u` by `ByValue`."
msgstr "总体而言，此闭包会以 `ByValue` 捕获 `u`。"

#: src/types/closure.md:156
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.dereference-shared\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.dereference-shared\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:157
msgid "Rightmost shared reference truncation"
msgstr "最右共享引用截断"

#: src/types/closure.md:159
msgid ""
"The capture path is truncated at the rightmost dereference in the capture "
"path if the dereference is applied to a shared reference."
msgstr ""
"如果捕获路径中的解引用应用于共享引用，则捕获路径会在其中最右侧的此类解引用处"
"截断。"

#: src/types/closure.md:161
msgid ""
"This truncation is allowed because fields that are read through a shared "
"reference will always be read via a shared reference or a copy. This helps "
"reduce the size of the capture when the extra precision does not yield any "
"benefit from a borrow checking perspective."
msgstr ""
"允许这种截断，是因为通过共享引用读取的字段始终会经由共享引用或副本来读取。当"
"额外的精度从借用检查角度看并无收益时，这有助于减小捕获的大小。"

#: src/types/closure.md:163
msgid ""
"The reason it is the _rightmost_ dereference is to help avoid a shorter "
"lifetime than is necessary. Consider the following example:"
msgstr ""
"之所以选择*最右侧*解引用，是为了帮助避免生命周期短于必要范围。考虑以下示例："

#: src/types/closure.md:180
msgid ""
"If this were to capture `m`, then the closure would no longer outlive "
"`'static`, since `m` is constrained to `'a`. Instead, it captures "
"`(*(*m).a)` by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"如果这里捕获 `m`，则该闭包将不再比 `'static` 活得更久，因为 `m` 受限于 `'a`。"
"相反，它会以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `(*(*m).a)`。"

#: src/types/closure.md:182
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:183
msgid "Wildcard pattern bindings"
msgstr "通配符模式绑定"

#: src/types/closure.md:185
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.reads\\] Closures only capture "
"data that needs to be read. Binding a value with a [wildcard pattern](../"
"patterns.md#wildcard-pattern) does not read the value, so the place is not "
"captured."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.reads\\] 闭包只捕获需要读取的数"
"据。使用[通配符模式](../patterns.md#wildcard-pattern)绑定某个值并不会读取该"
"值，因此该位置不会被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:189 src/types/closure.md:208 src/types/closure.md:250
#: src/types/closure.md:264 src/types/closure.md:294 src/types/closure.md:311
msgid "// A non-`Copy` type.\n"
msgstr "// 一个非 `Copy` 类型。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:192 src/types/closure.md:195 src/types/closure.md:213
#: src/types/closure.md:221 src/types/closure.md:230 src/types/closure.md:240
#: src/types/closure.md:330 src/types/closure.md:431
msgid "// Does not capture `x`.\n"
msgstr "// 不捕获 `x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:197 src/types/closure.md:215 src/types/closure.md:223
#: src/types/closure.md:232 src/types/closure.md:242 src/types/closure.md:332
#: src/types/closure.md:434
msgid "// OK: `x` can be moved here.\n"
msgstr "// OK：`x` 可以在这里被移动。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:201
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.destructuring\\] Destructuring "
"tuples, structs, and single-variant enums does not, by itself, cause a read "
"or the place to be captured."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.destructuring\\] 解构元组、"
"struct 和单变体 enum，本身不会导致读取，也不会导致该位置被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:204
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Enums marked with \\[`#[non_exhaustive]`\\]\\[attributes.type-"
"system.non_exhaustive\\] are always treated as having multiple variants. See "
"_\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.non_exhaustive\\]_."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 带有 \\[`#[non_exhaustive]`\\]\\[attributes.type-"
"system.non_exhaustive\\] 标记的 enum 总是被视为具有多个变体。参见 _\\"
"[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.non_exhaustive\\]_。"

#: src/types/closure.md:209
msgid "// Destructuring tuples does not cause a read or capture.\n"
msgstr "// 解构元组不会导致读取或捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:217
msgid "// Destructuring unit structs does not cause a read or capture.\n"
msgstr "// 解构单元 struct 不会导致读取或捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:225
msgid "// Destructuring structs does not cause a read or capture.\n"
msgstr "// 解构 struct 不会导致读取或捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:234
msgid ""
"// Destructuring single-variant enums does not cause a read\n"
"// or capture.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 解构单变体 enum 不会导致读取\n"
"// 或捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:246
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.fields\\] Fields matched against "
"\\[RestPattern\\] (`..`) or \\[StructPatternEtCetera\\] (also `..`) are not "
"read, and those fields are not captured."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.fields\\] 由 \\[RestPattern\\]"
"（`..`）或 \\[StructPatternEtCetera\\]（同样是 `..`）匹配的字段不会被读取，且"
"这些字段不会被捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:253
msgid "// Captures `x.0` by `ByValue`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ByValue` 捕获 `x.0`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:254
msgid "// Only the first tuple field was captured by the closure.\n"
msgstr "// 闭包只捕获了第一个元组字段。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:256 src/types/closure.md:319
msgid "// OK: `x.1` can be moved here.\n"
msgstr "// OK：`x.1` 可以在这里被移动。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:260
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.array-slice\\] Partial captures "
"of arrays and slices are not supported; the entire slice or array is always "
"captured even if used with wildcard pattern matching, indexing, or sub-"
"slicing."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.array-slice\\] 不支持对数组和切片"
"进行部分捕获；即使使用通配符模式匹配、索引或子切片，也总是捕获整个切片或数"
"组。"

#: src/types/closure.md:267
msgid "// Captures all of `x` by `ByValue`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ByValue` 捕获整个 `x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:269
msgid "// ERROR: Borrow of moved value.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：借用了已移动的值。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:272
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.initialized\\] Values that are "
"matched with wildcards must still be initialized."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.wildcard.initialized\\] 与通配符匹配的值仍"
"然必须已初始化。"

#: src/types/closure.md:278
msgid "// ERROR: Binding `x` isn't initialized.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：绑定 `x` 未初始化。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:284
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:285
msgid "Capturing for discriminant reads"
msgstr "针对判别值读取的捕获"

#: src/types/closure.md:287
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.reads\\] If pattern "
"matching reads a discriminant, the place containing that discriminant is "
"captured by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.reads\\] 如果模式匹配会读取"
"判别值，则包含该判别值的位置会以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:290
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.multiple-variant\\] "
"Matching against a variant of an enum that has more than one variant reads "
"the discriminant, capturing the place by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.multiple-variant\\] 匹配具有"
"多个变体的 enum 的某个变体会读取判别值，并以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获该位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:297
msgid ""
"//   ^^^^\n"
"// This pattern requires reading the discriminant, which\n"
"// causes `x.0` to be captured by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr ""
"//   ^^^^\n"
"// 此模式需要读取判别值，这会\n"
"// 导致 `x.0` 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:303
msgid ""
"// ERROR: Cannot borrow `x.0` as mutable.\n"
"//           ^^^\n"
"// The closure is still live, so `x.0` is still immutably\n"
"// borrowed here.\n"
msgstr ""
"// ERROR：不能将 `x.0` 作为可变对象借用。\n"
"//           ^^^\n"
"// 闭包仍然存活，因此 `x.0` 在这里仍然被\n"
"// 不可变借用。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:313
msgid "// Captures `x.0` by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `x.0`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:316
msgid ""
"// Though `x.0` is captured due to the discriminant read,\n"
"// `x.1` is not captured.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 虽然 `x.0` 因判别值读取而被捕获，\n"
"// 但 `x.1` 不会被捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:323
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.single-variant\\] Matching "
"against the only variant of a single-variant enum does not read the "
"discriminant and does not capture the place."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.single-variant\\] 匹配单变"
"体 enum 的唯一变体不会读取判别值，也不会捕获该位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:327
msgid "// A single-variant enum.\n"
msgstr "// 一个单变体 enum。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:336
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.non_exhaustive\\] If \\"
"[`#[non_exhaustive]`\\]\\[attributes.type-system.non_exhaustive\\] is "
"applied to an enum, the enum is treated as having multiple variants for the "
"purpose of deciding whether a read occurs, even if it actually has only one "
"variant."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.non_exhaustive\\] 如果对 "
"enum 应用了 \\[`#[non_exhaustive]`\\]\\[attributes.type-"
"system.non_exhaustive\\]，则在判定是否发生读取时，该 enum 会被视为具有多个变"
"体，即使它实际上只有一个变体。"

#: src/types/closure.md:339
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.uninhabited-variants\\] "
"Even if all variants but the one being matched against are uninhabited, "
"making the pattern \\[irrefutable\\]\\[patterns.refutable\\], the "
"discriminant is still read if it otherwise would be."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.discriminants.uninhabited-variants\\] 即使"
"除被匹配的变体之外所有变体都不可能有值，从而使该模式\\[不可反驳\\]\\"
"[patterns.refutable\\]，只要在其他情况下会读取判别值，这里仍然会读取判别值。"

#: src/types/closure.md:346 src/types/closure.md:362
msgid "// Captures `x` by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:348 src/types/closure.md:364
msgid "// ERROR: Cannot borrow `x` as mutable.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：不能将 `x` 作为可变对象借用。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:353
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.range-patterns\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.range-patterns\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:354
msgid "Capturing and range patterns"
msgstr "捕获与范围模式"

#: src/types/closure.md:356
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.range-patterns.reads\\] Matching against "
"a \\[range pattern\\]\\[patterns.range\\] reads the place being matched, "
"even if the range includes all possible values of the type, and captures the "
"place by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.range-patterns.reads\\] 匹配\\[范围模式\\]"
"\\[patterns.range\\]会读取被匹配的位置，即使该范围包含该类型的所有可能值，并"
"且会以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获该位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:368
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.slice-patterns\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.slice-patterns\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:369
msgid "Capturing and slice patterns"
msgstr "捕获与切片模式"

#: src/types/closure.md:371
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.slice-patterns.slices\\] Matching a slice "
"against a \\[slice pattern\\]\\[patterns.slice\\] other than one with only a "
"single \\[rest pattern\\]\\[patterns.rest\\] (i.e. `[..]`) is treated as a "
"read of the length from the slice and captures the slice by `ImmBorrow`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.slice-patterns.slices\\] 用\\[切片模式\\]"
"\\[patterns.slice\\]匹配切片时，除只含单个\\[剩余模式\\]\\[patterns.rest\\]的"
"模式（即 `[..]`）之外，都会被视为从该切片读取长度，并以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获该切"
"片。"

#: src/types/closure.md:376
msgid "// Captures `*x` by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `*x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:377
msgid ""
"//       ^^\n"
"// This matches a slice of exactly zero elements. To know whether the\n"
"// scrutinee matches, the length must be read, causing the slice to\n"
"// be captured.\n"
msgstr ""
"//       ^^\n"
"// 这会匹配恰好有零个元素的切片。要知道\n"
"// 被匹配值是否匹配，必须读取长度，从而导致\n"
"// 该切片被捕获。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:384
msgid "// ERROR: Cannot borrow `*x` as mutable.\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：不能将 `*x` 作为可变对象借用。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:390
msgid "// Does not capture `*x`.\n"
msgstr "// 不捕获 `*x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:391
msgid "//   ^^ Rest pattern.\n"
msgstr "//   ^^ 剩余模式。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:394
msgid "// OK: `*x` can be borrow here.\n"
msgstr "// OK：可以在这里借用 `*x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:398
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Perhaps surprisingly, even though the length is contained in the "
"(wide) _pointer_ to the slice, it is the place of the _pointee_ (the slice) "
"that is treated as read and is captured."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 也许令人意外的是，虽然长度包含在指向切片的（宽）*指针* 中，但被视"
"为读取并被捕获的是 *被指向对象*（切片）的位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:403
msgid "// The closure outlives `'l` because it captures `**x`. If\n"
msgstr "// 该闭包比 `'l` 活得更久，因为它捕获 `**x`。如果\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:404
msgid "// instead it captured `*x`, it would not live long enough\n"
msgstr "// 它转而捕获 `*x`，则它就不会活得足够久，\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:405
msgid "// to satisfy the `impl Fn() + 'l` bound.\n"
msgstr "// 无法满足 `impl Fn() + 'l` 约束。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:406 src/types/closure.md:417
msgid "// Captures `**x` by `ImmBorrow`.\n"
msgstr "// 以 `ImmBorrow` 捕获 `**x`。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:413
msgid ""
"In this way, the behavior is consistent with dereferencing to the slice in "
"the scrutinee."
msgstr "这样一来，其行为就与在被匹配值中解引用到切片一致。"

#: src/types/closure.md:424
msgid ""
"For details, see [Rust PR #138961](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/"
"138961)."
msgstr ""
"详情请参见 [Rust PR #138961](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/138961)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:426
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.slice-patterns.arrays\\] As the length of "
"an array is fixed by its type, matching an array against a slice pattern "
"does not by itself capture the place."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.slice-patterns.arrays\\] 由于数组长度由其"
"类型固定，用切片模式匹配数组本身不会捕获该位置。"

#: src/types/closure.md:432
msgid "// Length is fixed.\n"
msgstr "// 长度是固定的。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:438
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.move-dereference\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.move-dereference\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:439
msgid "Capturing references in move contexts"
msgstr "在 move 上下文中捕获引用"

#: src/types/closure.md:441
msgid ""
"Because it is not allowed to move fields out of a reference, `move` closures "
"will only capture the prefix of a capture path that runs up to, but not "
"including, the first dereference of a reference. The reference itself will "
"be moved into the closure."
msgstr ""
"由于不允许从引用中移出字段，`move` 闭包只会捕获捕获路径的前缀，直到但不包括对"
"引用的第一次解引用。该引用本身会被移动进闭包。"

#: src/types/closure.md:449
msgid "// captures `t_mut_ref` ByValue\n"
msgstr "// 以 ByValue 捕获 `t_mut_ref`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:454
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.raw-pointer-dereference\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.raw-pointer-dereference\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:455
msgid "Raw pointer dereference"
msgstr "裸指针解引用"

#: src/types/closure.md:457
msgid ""
"Because it is `unsafe` to dereference a raw pointer, closures will only "
"capture the prefix of a capture path that runs up to, but not including, the "
"first dereference of a raw pointer."
msgstr ""
"由于解引用裸指针是 `unsafe` 的，闭包只会捕获捕获路径的前缀，直到但不包括对裸"
"指针的第一次解引用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:466
msgid "// captures `t_ptr` by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `t_ptr`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:471
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.union\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.union\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:472
msgid "Union fields"
msgstr "union 字段"

#: src/types/closure.md:474
msgid ""
"Because it is `unsafe` to access a union field, closures will only capture "
"the prefix of a capture path that runs up to the union itself."
msgstr ""
"由于访问 union 字段是 `unsafe` 的，闭包只会捕获捕获路径中直到 union 本身为止"
"的前缀。"

#: src/types/closure.md:484
msgid "// captures `u` ByValue\n"
msgstr "// 以 ByValue 捕获 `u`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:487
msgid "// This also includes writing to fields.\n"
msgstr "// 这也包括写入字段。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:492
msgid "// captures `u` with MutBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 MutBorrow 捕获 `u`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:497
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.unaligned\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.unaligned\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:498
msgid "Reference into unaligned `struct`s"
msgstr "指向未对齐 `struct` 的引用"

#: src/types/closure.md:500
msgid ""
"Because it is [undefined behavior](../behavior-considered-undefined.md) to "
"create references to unaligned fields in a structure, closures will only "
"capture the prefix of the capture path that runs up to, but not including, "
"the first field access into a structure that uses [the `packed` "
"representation](../type-layout.md#the-alignment-modifiers). This includes "
"all fields, even those that are aligned, to protect against compatibility "
"concerns should any of the fields in the structure change in the future."
msgstr ""
"由于为结构中未对齐的字段创建引用是[未定义行为](../behavior-considered-"
"undefined.md)，闭包只会捕获捕获路径的前缀，直到但不包括对使用 [`packed` 表示]"
"(../type-layout.md#the-alignment-modifiers)的结构进行的第一次字段访问。这包括"
"所有字段，即使是已对齐的字段也包括在内，以防结构中的任何字段将来发生变化时引"
"发兼容性问题。"

#: src/types/closure.md:508 src/types/closure.md:523
msgid "// captures `t` with ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `t`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:509
msgid "// Copies out of `t` are ok.\n"
msgstr "// 可以从 `t` 中复制出值。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:515
msgid ""
"Similarly, taking the address of an unaligned field also captures the entire "
"struct:"
msgstr "类似地，取得未对齐字段的地址也会捕获整个 struct："

#: src/types/closure.md:525
msgid "// ERROR: cannot move out of `t.0` because it is borrowed\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：不能移出 `t.0`，因为它已被借用\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:529
msgid ""
"but the above works if it is not packed since it captures the field "
"precisely:"
msgstr "但如果它不是 packed 的，上述代码就可以工作，因为它会精确捕获该字段："

#: src/types/closure.md:536
msgid "// captures `t.1` with ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `t.1`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:537
msgid "// The move here is allowed.\n"
msgstr "// 这里的移动是允许的。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:546
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.box-deref\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.box-deref\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:547
msgid "`Box` vs other `Deref` implementations"
msgstr "`Box` 与其他 `Deref` 实现"

#: src/types/closure.md:549
msgid ""
"The implementation of the [`Deref`](../special-types-and-traits.md#deref-and-"
"derefmut) trait for [`Box`](../special-types-and-traits.md#boxt) is treated "
"differently from other `Deref` implementations, as it is considered a "
"special entity."
msgstr ""
"[`Box`](../special-types-and-traits.md#boxt) 的 [`Deref`](../special-types-"
"and-traits.md#deref-and-derefmut) trait 实现会被区别于其他 `Deref` 实现来处"
"理，因为它被认为是一个特殊实体。"

#: src/types/closure.md:551
msgid ""
"For example, let us look at examples involving `Rc` and `Box`. The `*rc` is "
"desugared to a call to the trait method `deref` defined on `Rc`, but since "
"`*box` is treated differently, it is possible to do a precise capture of the "
"contents of the `Box`."
msgstr ""
"例如，来看涉及 `Rc` 和 `Box` 的示例。`*rc` 会脱糖为对 `Rc` 上定义的 trait 方"
"法 `deref` 的调用，但由于 `*box` 会被区别处理，因此可以精确捕获 `Box` 的内"
"容。"

#: src/types/closure.md:556
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.box-non-move.not-moved\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.box-non-move.not-moved\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:557
msgid "`Box` with non-`move` closure"
msgstr "非 `move` 闭包中的 `Box`"

#: src/types/closure.md:559
msgid ""
"In a non-`move` closure, if the contents of the `Box` are not moved into the "
"closure body, the contents of the `Box` are precisely captured."
msgstr ""
"在非 `move` 闭包中，如果 `Box` 的内容没有被移动进闭包体，则 `Box` 的内容会被"
"精确捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:566
msgid "// captures `(*b).0` by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `(*b).0`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:569
msgid "// Contrast `Box` with another type that implements Deref:\n"
msgstr "// 将 `Box` 与另一种实现 Deref 的类型进行对比：\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:573
msgid "// captures `r` by ImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// 以 ImmBorrow 捕获 `r`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:578
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.box-non-move.moved\\] However, if the "
"contents of the `Box` are moved into the closure, then the box is entirely "
"captured. This is done so the amount of data that needs to be moved into the "
"closure is minimized."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.box-non-move.moved\\] 然而，如果 `Box` 的"
"内容被移动进闭包，则整个 box 都会被捕获。这样做是为了最小化需要移动进闭包的数"
"据量。"

#: src/types/closure.md:582
msgid ""
"// This is the same as the example above except the closure\n"
"// moves the value instead of taking a reference to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这与上面的示例相同，只是闭包会移动该值，\n"
"// 而不是取得对它的引用。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:589 src/types/closure.md:604
msgid "// captures `b` with ByValue\n"
msgstr "// 以 ByValue 捕获 `b`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:594
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.box-move.read\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.box-move.read\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:595
msgid "`Box` with move closure"
msgstr "move 闭包中的 `Box`"

#: src/types/closure.md:597
msgid ""
"Similarly to moving contents of a `Box` in a non-`move` closure, reading the "
"contents of a `Box` in a `move` closure will capture the `Box` entirely."
msgstr ""
"与在非 `move` 闭包中移动 `Box` 的内容类似，在 `move` 闭包中读取 `Box` 的内容"
"会捕获整个 `Box`。"

#: src/types/closure.md:608
msgid "r\\[type.closure.unique-immutable\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.unique-immutable\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:609
msgid "Unique immutable borrows in captures"
msgstr "捕获中的唯一不可变借用"

#: src/types/closure.md:611
msgid ""
"Captures can occur by a special kind of borrow called a _unique immutable "
"borrow_, which cannot be used anywhere else in the language and cannot be "
"written out explicitly. It occurs when modifying the referent of a mutable "
"reference, as in the following example:"
msgstr ""
"捕获可以通过一种称为*唯一不可变借用*的特殊借用发生，这种借用不能在语言的其他"
"任何地方使用，也不能显式写出。它会在修改可变引用的被引用对象时发生，如以下示"
"例所示："

#: src/types/closure.md:617
msgid "// An ImmBorrow and a MutBorrow of `x`.\n"
msgstr "// 对 `x` 的一个 ImmBorrow 和一个 MutBorrow。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:619
msgid "// `x` captured by UniqueImmBorrow\n"
msgstr "// `x` 以 UniqueImmBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:620
msgid ""
"// The following line is an error:\n"
"// let y = &x;\n"
msgstr ""
"// 下面这一行会出错：\n"
"// let y = &x;\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:623
msgid "// However, the following is OK.\n"
msgstr "// 然而，下面这样是 OK 的。\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:628
msgid ""
"In this case, borrowing `x` mutably is not possible, because `x` is not "
"`mut`. But at the same time, borrowing `x` immutably would make the "
"assignment illegal, because a `& &mut` reference might not be unique, so it "
"cannot safely be used to modify a value. So a unique immutable borrow is "
"used: it borrows `x` immutably, but like a mutable borrow, it must be unique."
msgstr ""
"在此情况下，不可能可变借用 `x`，因为 `x` 不是 `mut`。但与此同时，不可变借用 "
"`x` 又会使赋值非法，因为 `& &mut` 引用可能不是唯一的，所以不能安全地用于修改"
"值。因此会使用唯一不可变借用：它以不可变方式借用 `x`，但像可变借用一样，它必"
"须是唯一的。"

#: src/types/closure.md:630
msgid ""
"In the above example, uncommenting the declaration of `y` will produce an "
"error because it would violate the uniqueness of the closure's borrow of "
"`x`; the declaration of z is valid because the closure's lifetime has "
"expired at the end of the block, releasing the borrow."
msgstr ""
"在上面的示例中，如果取消 `y` 的声明的注释，将会产生错误，因为这会违反闭包对 "
"`x` 的借用的唯一性；z 的声明是有效的，因为闭包的生命周期已在块的末尾结束，从"
"而释放了该借用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:632
msgid "r\\[type.closure.call\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.call\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:633
msgid "Call traits and coercions"
msgstr "调用 trait 与强制转换"

#: src/types/closure.md:635
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.call.intro\\] Closure types all implement \\[`FnOnce`\\], "
"indicating that they can be called once by consuming ownership of the "
"closure. Additionally, some closures implement more specific call traits:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.call.intro\\] 所有闭包类型都实现 \\[`FnOnce`\\]，表示它们可"
"以通过消耗闭包的所有权来调用一次。此外，某些闭包会实现更具体的调用 trait："

#: src/types/closure.md:638
msgid "r\\[type.closure.call.fn-mut\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.call.fn-mut\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:639
msgid ""
"A closure which does not move out of any captured variables implements \\"
"[`FnMut`\\], indicating that it can be called by mutable reference."
msgstr ""
"不会移出任何被捕获变量的闭包实现 \\[`FnMut`\\]，表示它可以通过可变引用调用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:641
msgid "r\\[type.closure.call.fn\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.call.fn\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:642
msgid ""
"A closure which does not mutate or move out of any captured variables "
"implements \\[`Fn`\\], indicating that it can be called by shared reference."
msgstr ""
"不会修改或移出任何被捕获变量的闭包实现 \\[`Fn`\\]，表示它可以通过共享引用调"
"用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:644
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `move` closures may still implement \\[`Fn`\\] or \\[`FnMut`\\], "
"even though they capture variables by move. This is because the traits "
"implemented by a closure type are determined by what the closure does with "
"captured values, not how it captures them."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `move` 闭包仍然可以实现 \\[`Fn`\\] 或 \\[`FnMut`\\]，即使它们通过"
"移动来捕获变量。这是因为闭包类型实现哪些 trait 取决于闭包如何处理被捕获值，而"
"不是它如何捕获这些值。"

#: src/types/closure.md:647
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.non-capturing\\] _Non-capturing closures_ are closures that "
"don't capture anything from their environment. Non-async, non-capturing "
"closures can be coerced to function pointers (e.g., `fn()`) with the "
"matching signature."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.non-capturing\\] *非捕获闭包* 是不从其环境捕获任何内容的闭"
"包。非 async 的非捕获闭包可以被强制转换为具有匹配签名的函数指针（例如 "
"`fn()`）。"

#: src/types/closure.md:660
msgid "r\\[type.closure.async.traits\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.async.traits\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:661
msgid "Async closure traits"
msgstr "async 闭包 trait"

#: src/types/closure.md:663
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.async.traits.fn-family\\] Async closures have a further "
"restriction of whether or not they implement \\[`FnMut`\\] or \\[`Fn`\\]."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.async.traits.fn-family\\] async 闭包对于是否实现 \\"
"[`FnMut`\\] 或 \\[`Fn`\\] 还有进一步限制。"

#: src/types/closure.md:666
msgid ""
"The \\[`Future`\\] returned by the async closure has similar capturing "
"characteristics as a closure. It captures place expressions from the async "
"closure based on how they are used. The async closure is said to be "
"_lending_ to its \\[`Future`\\] if it has either of the following properties:"
msgstr ""
"async 闭包返回的 \\[`Future`\\] 具有与闭包类似的捕获特性。它会根据使用方式从 "
"async 闭包中捕获位置表达式。如果 async 闭包具有以下任一性质，则称它向其 \\"
"[`Future`\\] *借出*："

#: src/types/closure.md:668
msgid "The `Future` includes a mutable capture."
msgstr "`Future` 包含可变捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:669
msgid ""
"The async closure captures by value, except when the value is accessed with "
"a dereference projection."
msgstr "async 闭包按值捕获，但通过解引用投影访问该值时除外。"

#: src/types/closure.md:671
msgid ""
"If the async closure is lending to its `Future`, then \\[`FnMut`\\] and \\"
"[`Fn`\\] are _not_ implemented. \\[`FnOnce`\\] is always implemented."
msgstr ""
"如果 async 闭包向其 `Future` 借出，则 *不会* 实现 \\[`FnMut`\\] 和 \\"
"[`Fn`\\]。\\[`FnOnce`\\] 总是会实现。"

#: src/types/closure.md:673
msgid ""
"**Example**: The first clause for a mutable capture can be illustrated with "
"the following:"
msgstr "**示例**：关于可变捕获的第一项条件可以用下面的代码说明："

#: src/types/closure.md:681
msgid "// x captured with MutBorrow\n"
msgstr "// x 以 MutBorrow 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:683
msgid "// ERROR: async closure does not implement `FnMut`\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：async 闭包未实现 `FnMut`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:687
msgid ""
"The second clause for a regular value capture can be illustrated with the "
"following:"
msgstr "关于常规值捕获的第二项条件可以用下面的代码说明："

#: src/types/closure.md:695
msgid "// x captured ByValue\n"
msgstr "// x 以 ByValue 捕获\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:697
msgid "// ERROR: async closure does not implement `Fn`\n"
msgstr "// ERROR：async 闭包未实现 `Fn`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:701
msgid ""
"The exception of the the second clause can be illustrated by using a "
"dereference, which does allow `Fn` and `FnMut` to be implemented:"
msgstr ""
"第二项条件的例外可以通过使用解引用来说明，这种方式确实允许实现 `Fn` 和 "
"`FnMut`："

#: src/types/closure.md:711
msgid "// OK: implements `Fn`\n"
msgstr "// OK：实现 `Fn`\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:715
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.async.traits.async-family\\] Async closures implement \\"
"[`AsyncFn`\\], \\[`AsyncFnMut`\\], and \\[`AsyncFnOnce`\\] in an analogous "
"way as regular closures implement \\[`Fn`\\], \\[`FnMut`\\], and \\"
"[`FnOnce`\\]; that is, depending on the use of the captured variables in its "
"body."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.async.traits.async-family\\] async 闭包实现 \\"
"[`AsyncFn`\\]、\\[`AsyncFnMut`\\] 和 \\[`AsyncFnOnce`\\] 的方式，类似于普通闭"
"包实现 \\[`Fn`\\]、\\[`FnMut`\\] 和 \\[`FnOnce`\\] 的方式；也就是说，取决于其"
"闭包体中对被捕获变量的使用。"

#: src/types/closure.md:718
msgid "r\\[type.closure.traits\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.traits\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:719
msgid "Other traits"
msgstr "其他 trait"

#: src/types/closure.md:721
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.traits.intro\\] All closure types implement [`Sized`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#sized). Additionally, closure types implement "
"the following traits if allowed to do so by the types of the captures it "
"stores:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.traits.intro\\] 所有闭包类型都实现 [`Sized`](../special-"
"types-and-traits.md#sized)。此外，如果其存储的捕获项的类型允许，闭包类型还会"
"实现以下 trait："

#: src/types/closure.md:724
msgid "[`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone)"
msgstr "[`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone)"

#: src/types/closure.md:725
msgid "[`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)"
msgstr "[`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)"

#: src/types/closure.md:726
msgid "[`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)"
msgstr "[`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)"

#: src/types/closure.md:727
msgid "[`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send)"
msgstr "[`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send)"

#: src/types/closure.md:729
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.traits.behavior\\] The rules for [`Send`](../special-types-"
"and-traits.md#send) and [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync) match "
"those for normal struct types, while [`Clone`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#clone) and [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy) behave as "
"if [derived](../attributes/derive.md). For [`Clone`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#clone), the order of cloning of the captured values is left "
"unspecified."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.traits.behavior\\] [`Send`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#send) 和 [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync) 的规则与普"
"通 struct 类型的规则一致，而 [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone) "
"和 [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy) 的行为就像是[派生](../"
"attributes/derive.md)得到的一样。对于 [`Clone`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#clone)，被捕获值的克隆顺序是未指定的。"

#: src/types/closure.md:732
msgid ""
"Because captures are often by reference, the following general rules arise:"
msgstr "由于捕获通常通过引用进行，因此会得到以下一般规则："

#: src/types/closure.md:734
msgid ""
"A closure is [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync) if all captured "
"values are [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)."
msgstr ""
"如果所有被捕获值都是 [`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)，则闭包是 "
"[`Sync`](../special-types-and-traits.md#sync)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:735
msgid ""
"A closure is [`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send) if all values "
"captured by non-unique immutable reference are [`Sync`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#sync), and all values captured by unique immutable or mutable "
"reference, copy, or move are [`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send)."
msgstr ""
"如果所有通过非唯一不可变引用捕获的值都是 [`Sync`](../special-types-and-"
"traits.md#sync)，且所有通过唯一不可变引用、可变引用、复制或移动捕获的值都是 "
"[`Send`](../special-types-and-traits.md#send)，则闭包是 [`Send`](../special-"
"types-and-traits.md#send)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:736
msgid ""
"A closure is [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone) or [`Copy`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#copy) if it does not capture any values by "
"unique immutable or mutable reference, and if all values it captures by copy "
"or move are [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone) or [`Copy`](../"
"special-types-and-traits.md#copy), respectively."
msgstr ""
"如果闭包没有通过唯一不可变引用或可变引用捕获任何值，并且它通过复制或移动捕获"
"的所有值分别都是 [`Clone`](../special-types-and-traits.md#clone) 或 [`Copy`]"
"(../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)，则该闭包是 [`Clone`](../special-types-"
"and-traits.md#clone) 或 [`Copy`](../special-types-and-traits.md#copy)。"

#: src/types/closure.md:746
msgid "r\\[type.closure.drop-order\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.drop-order\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:747
msgid "Drop order"
msgstr "丢弃顺序"

#: src/types/closure.md:749
msgid ""
"If a closure captures a field of a composite types such as structs, tuples, "
"and enums by value, the field's lifetime would now be tied to the closure. "
"As a result, it is possible for disjoint fields of a composite types to be "
"dropped at different times."
msgstr ""
"如果闭包按值捕获复合类型（例如 struct、元组和 enum）的某个字段，则该字段的生"
"命周期现在会与闭包绑定。因此，复合类型中互不重叠的字段可能会在不同时间被丢"
"弃。"

#: src/types/closure.md:754
msgid "// --+\n"
msgstr "// --+\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:755
msgid "//                                               |\n"
msgstr "//                                               |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:756
msgid ""
"// ----------------------------+  |\n"
"            // tuple.0 is captured into the closure |  |\n"
msgstr ""
"// ----------------------------+  |\n"
"            // tuple.0 被捕获到闭包中 |  |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:758
msgid "//                       |  |\n"
msgstr "//                       |  |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:759
msgid "//                                       |  |\n"
msgstr "//                                       |  |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:760
msgid "// 'c' and 'tuple.0' dropped here ------------+  |\n"
msgstr "// 'c' 和 'tuple.0' 在此处被丢弃 ------------+  |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:761
msgid "// tuple.1 dropped here -----------------------------+\n"
msgstr "// tuple.1 在此处被丢弃 -----------------------------+\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:764
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.entirety\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.entirety\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:765
msgid "Edition 2018 and before"
msgstr "2018 edition 及以前版本"

#: src/types/closure.md:767
msgid "Closure types difference"
msgstr "闭包类型差异"

#: src/types/closure.md:769
msgid ""
"In Edition 2018 and before, closures always capture a variable in its "
"entirety, without its precise capture path. This means that for the example "
"used in the [Closure types](#closure-types) section, the generated closure "
"type would instead look something like this:"
msgstr ""
"在 2018 edition 及以前版本中，闭包总是整体捕获变量，而不会使用其精确捕获路"
"径。这意味着对于[闭包类型](#closure-types)一节中的示例，生成的闭包类型会改为"
"大致如下："

#: src/types/closure.md:787
msgid "and the call to `f` would work as follows:"
msgstr "而对 `f` 的调用会按如下方式工作："

#: src/types/closure.md:794
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.composite\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.composite\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:795
msgid "Capture precision difference"
msgstr "捕获精度差异"

#: src/types/closure.md:797
msgid ""
"Composite types such as structs, tuples, and enums are always captured in "
"its entirety, not by individual fields. As a result, it may be necessary to "
"borrow into a local variable in order to capture a single field:"
msgstr ""
"复合类型（例如 struct、元组和 enum）总是被整体捕获，而不是按单个字段捕获。因"
"此，为了捕获单个字段，可能需要先借用到局部变量中："

#: src/types/closure.md:817
msgid ""
"If, instead, the closure were to use `self.vec` directly, then it would "
"attempt to capture `self` by mutable reference. But since `self.set` is "
"already borrowed to iterate over, the code would not compile."
msgstr ""
"如果该闭包改为直接使用 `self.vec`，则它会尝试通过可变引用捕获 `self`。但由于 "
"`self.set` 已经被借用来进行迭代，这段代码将无法编译。"

#: src/types/closure.md:819
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.move\\] If the `move` keyword "
"is used, then all captures are by move or, for `Copy` types, by copy, "
"regardless of whether a borrow would work. The `move` keyword is usually "
"used to allow the closure to outlive the captured values, such as if the "
"closure is being returned or used to spawn a new thread."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.move\\] 如果使用 `move` 关键"
"字，则所有捕获都会通过移动进行；对于 `Copy` 类型，则通过复制进行，而不考虑借"
"用是否可行。`move` 关键字通常用于让闭包比被捕获值活得更久，例如闭包被返回或用"
"于生成新线程时。"

#: src/types/closure.md:822
msgid ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.wildcard\\] Regardless of if "
"the data will be read by the closure, i.e. in case of wild card patterns, if "
"a variable defined outside the closure is mentioned within the closure the "
"variable will be captured in its entirety."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.wildcard\\] 无论闭包是否会读取"
"数据，即在通配符模式的情况下，只要闭包内提到在闭包外定义的变量，该变量就会被"
"整体捕获。"

#: src/types/closure.md:825
msgid "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.drop-order\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.closure.capture.precision.edition2018.drop-order\\]"

#: src/types/closure.md:826
msgid "Drop order difference"
msgstr "丢弃顺序差异"

#: src/types/closure.md:828
msgid ""
"As composite types are captured in their entirety, a closure which captures "
"one of those composite types by value would drop the entire captured "
"variable at the same time as the closure gets dropped."
msgstr ""
"由于复合类型会被整体捕获，按值捕获其中某个复合类型的闭包，会在闭包被丢弃的同"
"时丢弃整个被捕获变量。"

#: src/types/closure.md:835
msgid ""
"// --------------------------+\n"
"            // tuple is captured into the closure |\n"
msgstr ""
"// --------------------------+\n"
"            // tuple 被捕获到闭包中 |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:837
msgid "//                     |\n"
msgstr "//                     |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:838
msgid "//                                     |\n"
msgstr "//                                     |\n"

#: src/types/closure.md:839
msgid "// 'c' and 'tuple' dropped here ------------+\n"
msgstr "// 'c' 和 'tuple' 在此处被丢弃 ------------+\n"

#: src/types/pointer.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.intro\\] All pointers are explicit first-class values. They "
"can be moved or copied, stored into data structs, and returned from "
"functions."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.intro\\] 所有指针都是显式的一等值。它们可以被移动或复制，可"
"以存储到数据结构中，也可以从函数返回。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:7
msgid "r\\[type.pointer.reference\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer.reference\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:8
msgid "References (`&` and `&mut`)"
msgstr "引用（`&` 和 `&mut`）"

#: src/types/pointer.md:10
msgid "r\\[type.pointer.reference.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer.reference.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:15
msgid "r\\[type.pointer.reference.shared\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer.reference.shared\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:16
msgid "Shared references (`&`)"
msgstr "共享引用（`&`）"

#: src/types/pointer.md:18
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.shared.intro\\] Shared references point to memory "
"which is owned by some other value."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.shared.intro\\] 共享引用指向由某个其他值拥有的内"
"存。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:21
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.shared.constraint-mutation\\] When a shared "
"reference to a value is created, it prevents direct mutation of the value. "
"[Interior mutability](../interior-mutability.md) provides an exception for "
"this in certain circumstances. As the name suggests, any number of shared "
"references to a value may exist. A shared reference type is written `&type`, "
"or `&'a type` when you need to specify an explicit lifetime."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.shared.constraint-mutation\\] 创建指向某个值的共享"
"引用后，它会阻止对该值的直接变更。[内部可变性](../interior-mutability.md)在某"
"些情况下为此提供例外。顾名思义，可以存在任意数量的指向同一个值的共享引用。共"
"享引用类型写作 `&type`，在需要指定显式生命周期时写作 `&'a type`。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:24
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.shared.copy\\] Copying a reference is a "
"\"shallow\" operation: it involves only copying the pointer itself, that is, "
"pointers are `Copy`. Releasing a reference has no effect on the value it "
"points to, but referencing of a [temporary value](../"
"expressions.md#temporaries) will keep it alive during the scope of the "
"reference itself."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.shared.copy\\] 复制引用是一种“浅”操作：它只涉及复"
"制指针本身，也就是说，指针是 `Copy` 的。释放一个引用不会影响它所指向的值，但"
"对[临时值](../expressions.md#temporaries)的引用会让该临时值在引用本身的作用域"
"期间保持存活。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:27
msgid "r\\[type.pointer.reference.mut\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer.reference.mut\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:28
msgid "Mutable references (`&mut`)"
msgstr "可变引用（`&mut`）"

#: src/types/pointer.md:30
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.mut.intro\\] Mutable references point to memory "
"which is owned by some other value. A mutable reference type is written "
"`&mut type` or `&'a mut type`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.mut.intro\\] 可变引用指向由某个其他值拥有的内存。"
"可变引用类型写作 `&mut type` 或 `&'a mut type`。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:33
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.mut.copy\\] A mutable reference (that hasn't been "
"borrowed) is the only way to access the value it points to, so is not `Copy`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.reference.mut.copy\\] 一个（尚未被借用的）可变引用是访问其所"
"指向值的唯一方式，因此它不是 `Copy` 的。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:36
msgid "r\\[type.pointer.raw\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer.raw\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:37
msgid "Raw pointers (`*const` and `*mut`)"
msgstr "裸指针（`*const` 和 `*mut`）"

#: src/types/pointer.md:39
msgid "r\\[type.pointer.raw.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer.raw.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:44
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.intro\\] Raw pointers are pointers without safety or "
"liveness guarantees. Raw pointers are written as `*const T` or `*mut T`. For "
"example `*const i32` means a raw pointer to a 32-bit integer."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.intro\\] 裸指针是没有安全性或存活性保证的指针。裸指针写"
"作 `*const T` 或 `*mut T`。例如，`*const i32` 表示指向 32 位整数的裸指针。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:47
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.copy\\] Copying or dropping a raw pointer has no effect "
"on the lifecycle of any other value."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.copy\\] 复制或丢弃裸指针不会影响任何其他值的生命周期。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:50
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.safety\\] Dereferencing a raw pointer is an [`unsafe` "
"operation](../unsafety.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.safety\\] 解引用裸指针是一种 [`unsafe` 操作](../"
"unsafety.md)。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:53
msgid ""
"This can also be used to convert a raw pointer to a reference by reborrowing "
"it (`&*` or `&mut *`). Raw pointers are generally discouraged; they exist to "
"support interoperability with foreign code, and writing performance-critical "
"or low-level functions."
msgstr ""
"这也可以通过重新借用裸指针（`&*` 或 `&mut *`）来将它转换为引用。通常不鼓励使"
"用裸指针；它们的存在是为了支持与外部代码的互操作，以及编写性能关键或低层级函"
"数。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:55
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.cmp\\] When comparing raw pointers they are compared by "
"their address, rather than by what they point to. When comparing raw "
"pointers to [dynamically sized types](../dynamically-sized-types.md) they "
"also have their additional data compared."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.cmp\\] 比较裸指针时，比较的是它们的地址，而不是它们所指"
"向的内容。比较指向[动态大小类型](../dynamically-sized-types.md)的裸指针时，还"
"会比较它们的附加数据。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:58
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.constructor\\] Raw pointers can be created directly "
"using `&raw const` for `*const` pointers and `&raw mut` for `*mut` pointers."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.raw.constructor\\] 可以直接使用 `&raw const` 创建 `*const` "
"指针，使用 `&raw mut` 创建 `*mut` 指针。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:61
msgid "r\\[type.pointer.smart\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer.smart\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:62
msgid "Smart pointers"
msgstr "智能指针"

#: src/types/pointer.md:64
msgid ""
"The standard library contains additional 'smart pointer' types beyond "
"references and raw pointers."
msgstr "除了引用和裸指针之外，标准库还包含额外的“智能指针”类型。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:66
msgid "r\\[type.pointer.validity\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.pointer.validity\\]"

#: src/types/pointer.md:69
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.validity.pointer-fragment\\] Despite pointers and "
"references being similar to `usize`s in the machine code emitted on most "
"platforms, the semantics of transmuting a reference or pointer type to a non-"
"pointer type is currently undecided. Thus, it may not be valid to transmute "
"a pointer or reference type, `P`, to a `[u8; size_of::<P>()]`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.validity.pointer-fragment\\] 尽管在大多数平台生成的机器码"
"中，指针和引用与 `usize` 类似，但将引用或指针类型转换为非指针类型的语义目前尚"
"未确定。因此，将指针或引用类型 `P` 转换为 `[u8; size_of::<P>()]` 可能无效。"

#: src/types/pointer.md:72
msgid ""
"r\\[type.pointer.validity.raw\\] For thin raw pointers (i.e., for `P = "
"*const T` or `P = *mut T` for `T: Sized`), the inverse direction "
"(transmuting from an integer or array of integers to `P`) is always valid. "
"However, the pointer produced via such a transmutation may not be "
"dereferenced (not even if `T` has [size zero](glossary.zst))."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.pointer.validity.raw\\] 对于薄裸指针（即当 `T: Sized` 时，`P = "
"*const T` 或 `P = *mut T`），反方向（从整数或整数数组转换为 `P`）始终是有效"
"的。不过，通过这种转换生成的指针不得被解引用（即使 `T` 具有[零大小]"
"(glossary.zst)也不行）。"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.fn-pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.fn-pointer\\]"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:4
msgid "r\\[type.fn-pointer.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.fn-pointer.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:27
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-pointer.intro\\] A function pointer type, written using the `fn` "
"keyword, refers to a function whose identity is not necessarily known at "
"compile-time."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-pointer.intro\\] 函数指针类型使用 `fn` 关键字书写，指代一个其身份"
"不一定在编译时已知的函数。"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:30
msgid "An example where `Binop` is defined as a function pointer type:"
msgstr "下面是将 `Binop` 定义为函数指针类型的示例："

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:44
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-pointer.coercion\\] Function pointers can be created via a "
"coercion from both [function items](function-item.md) and non-capturing, non-"
"async [closures](closure.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-pointer.coercion\\] 函数指针可以通过从[函数项](function-item.md)"
"以及非捕获、非 async 的[闭包](closure.md)进行强制转换来创建。"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:47
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-pointer.qualifiers\\] The `unsafe` qualifier indicates that the "
"type's value is an [unsafe function](../unsafe-keyword.md), and the `extern` "
"qualifier indicates it is an [extern function](../items/functions.md#extern-"
"function-qualifier)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-pointer.qualifiers\\] `unsafe` 限定符表示该类型的值是一个 "
"[unsafe 函数](../unsafe-keyword.md)，而 `extern` 限定符表示它是一个 [extern "
"函数](../items/functions.md#extern-function-qualifier)。"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:50
msgid ""
"r\\[type.fn-pointer.constraint-variadic\\] For the function to be variadic, "
"its `extern` ABI must be one of those listed in \\"
"[items.extern.variadic.conventions\\]."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.fn-pointer.constraint-variadic\\] 要使函数成为变参函数，它的 "
"`extern` ABI 必须是 \\[items.extern.variadic.conventions\\] 中列出的 ABI 之"
"一。"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:53
msgid "r\\[type.fn-pointer.attributes\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.fn-pointer.attributes\\]"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:54
msgid "Attributes on function pointer parameters"
msgstr "函数指针形参上的属性"

#: src/types/function-pointer.md:56
msgid ""
"Attributes on function pointer parameters follow the same rules and "
"restrictions as [regular function parameters](../items/"
"functions.md#attributes-on-function-parameters)."
msgstr ""
"函数指针形参上的属性遵循与[常规函数形参](../items/functions.md#attributes-on-"
"function-parameters)相同的规则和限制。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.trait-object\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.trait-object\\]"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:2
msgid "Trait objects"
msgstr "trait 对象"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:4
msgid "r\\[type.trait-object.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.trait-object.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:11
msgid ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.intro\\] A _trait object_ is an opaque value of "
"another type that implements a set of traits. The set of traits is made up "
"of a [dyn compatible](../items/traits.md#dyn-compatibility) _base trait_ "
"plus any number of [auto traits](../special-types-and-traits.md#auto-traits)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.intro\\] *trait 对象*是实现一组 trait 的某个其他类型的"
"不透明值。这组 trait 由一个 [dyn 兼容](../items/traits.md#dyn-compatibility)"
"的*基 trait* 加任意数量的 [auto trait](../special-types-and-traits.md#auto-"
"traits)组成。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:14
msgid ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.impls\\] Trait objects implement the base trait, its "
"auto traits, and any [supertraits](../items/traits.md#supertraits) of the "
"base trait."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.impls\\] trait 对象会实现基 trait、它的 auto trait，以"
"及基 trait 的任何 [supertrait](../items/traits.md#supertraits)。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:17
msgid ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.name\\] Trait objects are written as the keyword `dyn` "
"followed by a set of trait bounds, but with the following restrictions on "
"the trait bounds."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.name\\] trait 对象写作关键字 `dyn` 后跟一组 trait 约"
"束，但这些 trait 约束有以下限制。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:20
msgid ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.constraint\\] There may not be more than one non-auto "
"trait, no more than one lifetime, and opt-out bounds (e.g. `?Sized`) are not "
"allowed. Furthermore, paths to traits may be parenthesized."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.constraint\\] 非 auto trait 不得超过一个，生命周期不得"
"超过一个，并且不允许使用选择退出的约束（例如 `?Sized`）。此外，指向 trait 的"
"路径可以加括号。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:23
msgid ""
"For example, given a trait `Trait`, the following are all trait objects:"
msgstr "例如，给定一个 trait `Trait`，以下都是 trait 对象："

#: src/types/trait-object.md:25 src/syntax-index.md:240
msgid "`dyn Trait`"
msgstr "[trait 对象类型](types/trait-object.md#r-type.trait-object)"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:26
msgid "`dyn Trait + Send`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait + Send`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:27
msgid "`dyn Trait + Send + Sync`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait + Send + Sync`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:28
msgid "`dyn Trait + 'static`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait + 'static`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:29
msgid "`dyn Trait + Send + 'static`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait + Send + 'static`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:30
msgid "`dyn Trait +`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait +`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:31
msgid "`dyn 'static + Trait`."
msgstr "`dyn 'static + Trait`."

#: src/types/trait-object.md:32
msgid "`dyn (Trait)`"
msgstr "`dyn (Trait)`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:34
msgid "r\\[type.trait-object.syntax-edition2021\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.trait-object.syntax-edition2021\\]"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:35
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2021\\] Before the 2021 edition, the `dyn` keyword may be "
"omitted."
msgstr "\\[!EDITION-2021\\] 在 2021 edition 之前，`dyn` 关键字可以省略。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:38
msgid "r\\[type.trait-object.syntax-edition2018\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.trait-object.syntax-edition2018\\]"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:39
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] In the 2015 edition, if the first bound of the trait "
"object is a path that starts with `::`, then the `dyn` will be treated as a "
"part of the path. The first path can be put in parenthesis to get around "
"this. As such, if you want a trait object with the trait "
"`::your_module::Trait`, you should write it as `dyn (::your_module::Trait)`."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] 在 2015 edition 中，如果 trait 对象的第一个约束是以 `::` "
"开头的路径，那么 `dyn` 会被视为该路径的一部分。可以将第一个路径放入括号中来绕"
"过这一点。因此，如果你想要一个带有 trait `::your_module::Trait` 的 trait 对"
"象，应写作 `dyn (::your_module::Trait)`。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:42
msgid ""
"Beginning in the 2018 edition, `dyn` is a true keyword and is not allowed in "
"paths, so the parentheses are not necessary."
msgstr ""
"自 2018 edition 起，`dyn` 是真正的关键字，且不允许出现在路径中，因此括号不再"
"必要。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:44
msgid ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.alias\\] Two trait object types alias each other if "
"the base traits alias each other and if the sets of auto traits are the same "
"and the lifetime bounds are the same. For example, `dyn Trait + Send + "
"UnwindSafe` is the same as `dyn Trait + UnwindSafe + Send`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.alias\\] 如果基 trait 互为别名，auto trait 的集合相同，"
"并且生命周期约束相同，则两个 trait 对象类型互为别名。例如，`dyn Trait + Send "
"+ UnwindSafe` 与 `dyn Trait + UnwindSafe + Send` 相同。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:47
msgid ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.unsized\\] Due to the opaqueness of which concrete "
"type the value is of, trait objects are [dynamically sized types](../"
"dynamically-sized-types.md). Like all <abbr title=\"dynamically sized "
"types\">DSTs</abbr>, trait objects are used behind some type of pointer; for "
"example `&dyn SomeTrait` or `Box<dyn SomeTrait>`. Each instance of a pointer "
"to a trait object includes:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.trait-object.unsized\\] 由于该值属于哪个具体类型是不透明的，trait 对"
"象是[动态大小类型](../dynamically-sized-types.md)。与所有 <abbr "
"title=\"dynamically sized types\">DST</abbr> 一样，trait 对象通过某种指针间接"
"使用；例如 `&dyn SomeTrait` 或 `Box<dyn SomeTrait>`。指向 trait 对象的指针的"
"每个实例都包含："

#: src/types/trait-object.md:50
msgid "a pointer to an instance of a type `T` that implements `SomeTrait`"
msgstr "一个指向类型 `T` 的实例的指针，该类型实现了 `SomeTrait`"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:51
msgid ""
"a _virtual method table_, often just called a _vtable_, which contains, for "
"each method of `SomeTrait` and its [supertraits](../items/"
"traits.md#supertraits) that `T` implements, a pointer to `T`'s "
"implementation (i.e. a function pointer)."
msgstr ""
"一个*虚方法表*，通常直接称为 _vtable_，它针对 `T` 所实现的 `SomeTrait` 及其 "
"[supertrait](../items/traits.md#supertraits) 的每个方法，包含一个指向 `T` 的"
"实现的指针（即函数指针）。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:53
msgid ""
"The purpose of trait objects is to permit \"late binding\" of methods. "
"Calling a method on a trait object results in virtual dispatch at runtime: "
"that is, a function pointer is loaded from the trait object vtable and "
"invoked indirectly. The actual implementation for each vtable entry can vary "
"on an object-by-object basis."
msgstr ""
"trait 对象的目的是允许方法的“后期绑定”。在 trait 对象上调用方法会在运行时产生"
"虚分派：也就是说，从 trait 对象的 vtable 中加载一个函数指针，并间接调用它。每"
"个 vtable 条目的实际实现可以因对象而异。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:55
msgid "An example of a trait object:"
msgstr "trait 对象的示例："

#: src/types/trait-object.md:75
msgid ""
"In this example, the trait `Printable` occurs as a trait object in both the "
"type signature of `print`, and the cast expression in `main`."
msgstr ""
"在此示例中，trait `Printable` 在 `print` 的类型签名和 `main` 中的转换表达式里"
"都作为 trait 对象出现。"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:77
msgid "r\\[type.trait-object.lifetime-bounds\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.trait-object.lifetime-bounds\\]"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:78
msgid "Trait object lifetime bounds"
msgstr "trait 对象生命周期约束"

#: src/types/trait-object.md:80
msgid ""
"Since a trait object can contain references, the lifetimes of those "
"references need to be expressed as part of the trait object. This lifetime "
"is written as `Trait + 'a`. There are [defaults](../lifetime-"
"elision.md#default-trait-object-lifetimes) that allow this lifetime to "
"usually be inferred with a sensible choice."
msgstr ""
"由于 trait 对象可以包含引用，这些引用的生命周期需要作为 trait 对象的一部分表"
"达出来。这个生命周期写作 `Trait + 'a`。存在一些[默认值](../lifetime-"
"elision.md#default-trait-object-lifetimes)，使得该生命周期通常可以被推断为一"
"个合理的选择。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:2
msgid "Impl trait"
msgstr "impl Trait"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:4
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:11
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.intro\\] `impl Trait` provides ways to specify unnamed "
"but concrete types that implement a specific trait. It can appear in two "
"sorts of places: argument position (where it can act as an anonymous type "
"parameter to functions), and return position (where it can act as an "
"abstract return type)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.intro\\] `impl Trait` 提供了指定未命名但具体、且实现某个"
"特定 trait 的类型的方式。它可以出现在两类位置：实参位置（此时它可以充当函数的"
"匿名类型形参）和返回位置（此时它可以充当抽象返回类型）。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:17
msgid "// argument position: anonymous type parameter\n"
msgstr "// 实参位置：匿名类型形参\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:21
msgid "// return position: abstract return type\n"
msgstr "// 返回位置：抽象返回类型\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:26
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.param\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.param\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:27
msgid "Anonymous type parameters"
msgstr "匿名类型形参"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:29
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] This is often called \"impl Trait in argument position\". (The "
"term \"parameter\" is more correct here, but \"impl Trait in argument "
"position\" is the phrasing used during the development of this feature, and "
"it remains in parts of the implementation.)"
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 这通常称为“实参位置中的 impl Trait”。（这里使用“形参”这个术语更准"
"确，但“实参位置中的 impl Trait”是此特性开发期间使用的表述，并且仍保留在部分实"
"现中。）"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:32
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.param.intro\\] Functions can use `impl` followed by a "
"set of trait bounds to declare a parameter as having an anonymous type. The "
"caller must provide a type that satisfies the bounds declared by the "
"anonymous type parameter, and the function can only use the methods "
"available through the trait bounds of the anonymous type parameter."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.param.intro\\] 函数可以使用 `impl` 后跟一组 trait 约束，"
"将一个形参声明为具有匿名类型。调用者必须提供满足该匿名类型形参所声明约束的类"
"型，而函数只能使用通过该匿名类型形参的 trait 约束可用的方法。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:35
msgid "For example, these two forms are almost equivalent:"
msgstr "例如，这两种形式几乎等价："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:39
msgid "// generic type parameter\n"
msgstr "// 泛型类型形参\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:43
msgid "// impl Trait in argument position\n"
msgstr "// 实参位置中的 impl Trait\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:49
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.param.generic\\] That is, `impl Trait` in argument "
"position is syntactic sugar for a generic type parameter like `<T: Trait>`, "
"except that the type is anonymous and doesn't appear in the \\"
"[GenericParams\\] list."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.param.generic\\] 也就是说，实参位置中的 `impl Trait` 是类"
"似 `<T: Trait>` 的泛型类型形参的语法糖，只不过该类型是匿名的，并且不会出现在 "
"\\[GenericParams\\] 列表中。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:52
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] For function parameters, generic type parameters and `impl "
"Trait` are not exactly equivalent. With a generic parameter such as `<T: "
"Trait>`, the caller has the option to explicitly specify the generic "
"argument for `T` at the call site using \\[GenericArgs\\], for example, "
"`foo::<usize>(1)`. Changing a parameter from either one to the other can "
"constitute a breaking change for the callers of a function, since this "
"changes the number of generic arguments."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 对于函数形参，泛型类型形参和 `impl Trait` 并不完全等价。对于像 "
"`<T: Trait>` 这样的泛型形参，调用者可以选择在调用点使用 \\[GenericArgs\\] 显"
"式指定 `T` 的泛型实参，例如 `foo::<usize>(1)`。将一个形参从其中一种形式改为另"
"一种形式，可能构成对函数调用者的破坏性变更，因为这会改变泛型实参的数量。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:55
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.return\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.return\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:56
msgid "Abstract return types"
msgstr "抽象返回类型"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:58
msgid "\\[!NOTE\\] This is often called \"impl Trait in return position\"."
msgstr "\\[!NOTE\\] 这通常称为“返回位置中的 impl Trait”。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:61
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.return.intro\\] Functions can use `impl Trait` to return "
"an abstract return type. These types stand in for another concrete type "
"where the caller may only use the methods declared by the specified `Trait`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.return.intro\\] 函数可以使用 `impl Trait` 来返回抽象返回"
"类型。这些类型代表另一个具体类型，而调用者只能使用由指定 `Trait` 声明的方法。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:64
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.return.constraint-body\\] Each possible return value "
"from the function must resolve to the same concrete type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.return.constraint-body\\] 函数中每一个可能的返回值都必须"
"解析为同一个具体类型。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:67
msgid ""
"`impl Trait` in return position allows a function to return an unboxed "
"abstract type. This is particularly useful with [closures](closure.md) and "
"iterators. For example, closures have a unique, un-writable type. "
"Previously, the only way to return a closure from a function was to use a "
"[trait object](trait-object.md):"
msgstr ""
"返回位置中的 `impl Trait` 允许函数返回未装箱的抽象类型。这对[闭包]"
"(closure.md)和迭代器特别有用。例如，闭包具有唯一且无法写出的类型。以前，从函"
"数返回闭包的唯一方式是使用 [trait 对象](trait-object.md)："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:75
msgid ""
"This could incur performance penalties from heap allocation and dynamic "
"dispatch. It wasn't possible to fully specify the type of the closure, only "
"to use the `Fn` trait. That means that the trait object is necessary. "
"However, with `impl Trait`, it is possible to write this more simply:"
msgstr ""
"这可能因堆分配和动态分派而带来性能损耗。以前无法完整指定闭包的类型，只能使用 "
"`Fn` trait。这意味着 trait 对象是必要的。然而，使用 `impl Trait` 可以更简单地"
"写成："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:83
msgid "which also avoids the drawbacks of using a boxed trait object."
msgstr "这也避免了使用装箱 trait 对象的缺点。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:85
msgid ""
"Similarly, the concrete types of iterators could become very complex, "
"incorporating the types of all previous iterators in a chain. Returning "
"`impl Iterator` means that a function only exposes the `Iterator` trait as a "
"bound on its return type, instead of explicitly specifying all of the other "
"iterator types involved."
msgstr ""
"类似地，迭代器的具体类型可能变得非常复杂，包含链中所有先前迭代器的类型。返回 "
"`impl Iterator` 意味着函数只在其返回类型上暴露 `Iterator` trait 作为约束，而"
"不是显式指定所涉及的所有其他迭代器类型。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:87
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.return-in-trait\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.return-in-trait\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:88
msgid "Return-position `impl Trait` in traits and trait implementations"
msgstr "trait 和 trait 实现中的返回位置 `impl Trait`"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:90
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.return-in-trait.intro\\] Functions in traits may also "
"use `impl Trait` as a syntax for an anonymous associated type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.return-in-trait.intro\\] trait 中的函数也可以使用 `impl "
"Trait` 作为匿名关联类型的语法。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:93
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.return-in-trait.desugaring\\] Every `impl Trait` in the "
"return type of an associated function in a trait is desugared to an "
"anonymous associated type. The return type that appears in the "
"implementation's function signature is used to determine the value of the "
"associated type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.return-in-trait.desugaring\\] trait 中关联函数返回类型里"
"的每个 `impl Trait` 都会被脱糖为一个匿名关联类型。实现的函数签名中出现的返回"
"类型用于确定该关联类型的值。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:96
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-captures\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-captures\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:97
msgid "Capturing"
msgstr "捕获"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:99
msgid ""
"Behind each return-position `impl Trait` abstract type is some hidden "
"concrete type.  For this concrete type to use a generic parameter, that "
"generic parameter must be _captured_ by the abstract type."
msgstr ""
"每个返回位置 `impl Trait` 抽象类型背后都有某个隐藏的具体类型。要让这个具体类"
"型使用某个泛型形参，该泛型形参必须被该抽象类型 *捕获*。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:101
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.auto\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.auto\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:102
msgid "Automatic capturing"
msgstr "自动捕获"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:104
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.auto.intro\\] Return-position `impl "
"Trait` abstract types automatically capture all in-scope generic parameters, "
"including generic type, const, and lifetime parameters (including higher-"
"ranked ones)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.auto.intro\\] 返回位置 `impl Trait` 抽象"
"类型会自动捕获所有作用域内泛型形参，包括泛型类型、const 和生命周期形参（包括"
"高阶生命周期形参）。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:107
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.edition2024\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.edition2024\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:108
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] Before the 2024 edition, on free functions and on "
"associated functions and methods of inherent impls, generic lifetime "
"parameters that do not appear in the bounds of the abstract return type are "
"not automatically captured."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] 在 2024 edition 之前，对于自由函数以及固有 impl 的关联函"
"数和方法，未出现在抽象返回类型约束中的泛型生命周期形参不会被自动捕获。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:111
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:112
msgid "Precise capturing"
msgstr "精确捕获"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:114
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.use\\] The set of generic "
"parameters captured by a return-position `impl Trait` abstract type may be "
"explicitly controlled with a [`use<..>` bound](../trait-bounds.md#use-"
"bounds).  If present, only the generic parameters listed in the `use<..>` "
"bound will be captured.  E.g.:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.use\\] 返回位置 `impl Trait` 抽象"
"类型所捕获的泛型形参集合，可以通过 [`use<..>` 约束](../trait-bounds.md#r-"
"bound.use)显式控制。如果存在该约束，则只有列在 `use<..>` 约束中的泛型形参会被"
"捕获。例如："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:119
msgid ""
"//                                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"  //                                     Captures `'a` and `T` only.\n"
msgstr ""
"//                                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"  //                                     只捕获 `'a` 和 `T`。\n"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:125
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.constraint-single\\] Currently, "
"only one `use<..>` bound may be present in a bounds list, all in-scope type "
"and const generic parameters must be included, and all lifetime parameters "
"that appear in other bounds of the abstract type must be included."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.constraint-single\\] 目前，一个约"
"束列表中最多只能出现一个 `use<..>` 约束，必须包含所有作用域内类型和 const 泛"
"型形参，并且必须包含所有出现在该抽象类型其他约束中的生命周期形参。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:128
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.constraint-lifetime\\] Within "
"the `use<..>` bound, any lifetime parameters present must appear before all "
"type and const generic parameters, and the elided lifetime (`'_`) may be "
"present if it is otherwise allowed to appear within the `impl Trait` return "
"type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.constraint-lifetime\\] 在 "
"`use<..>` 约束内，任何出现的生命周期形参都必须位于所有类型和 const 泛型形参之"
"前；如果省略生命周期 (`'_`) 原本允许出现在 `impl Trait` 返回类型内，那么它可"
"以出现。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:131
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.constraint-param-impl-trait\\] "
"Because all in-scope type parameters must be included by name, a `use<..>` "
"bound may not be used in the signature of items that use argument-position "
"`impl Trait`, as those items have anonymous type parameters in scope."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.constraint-param-impl-trait\\] 由"
"于所有作用域内类型形参都必须按名称包含，`use<..>` 约束不得用于使用实参位置 "
"`impl Trait` 的项的签名中，因为这些项的作用域内有匿名类型形参。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:134
msgid ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.constraint-in-trait\\] Any "
"`use<..>` bound that is present in an associated function in a trait "
"definition must include all generic parameters of the trait, including the "
"implicit `Self` generic type parameter of the trait."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.impl-trait.generic-capture.precise.constraint-in-trait\\] trait 定义"
"中的关联函数里出现的任何 `use<..>` 约束，都必须包含该 trait 的所有泛型形参，"
"包括该 trait 隐式的 `Self` 泛型类型形参。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:137
msgid "Differences between generics and `impl Trait` in return position"
msgstr "返回位置中泛型与 `impl Trait` 的差异"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:139
msgid ""
"In argument position, `impl Trait` is very similar in semantics to a generic "
"type parameter. However, there are significant differences between the two "
"in return position. With `impl Trait`, unlike with a generic type parameter, "
"the function chooses the return type, and the caller cannot choose the "
"return type."
msgstr ""
"在实参位置，`impl Trait` 在语义上非常类似于泛型类型形参。然而，二者在返回位置"
"中存在显著差异。使用 `impl Trait` 时，与使用泛型类型形参不同，函数会选择返回"
"类型，而调用者不能选择返回类型。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:141 src/types/impl-trait.md:153
msgid "The function:"
msgstr "函数："

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:151
msgid ""
"allows the caller to determine the return type, `T`, and the function "
"returns that type."
msgstr "允许调用者确定返回类型 `T`，并且该函数返回该类型。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:163
msgid ""
"doesn't allow the caller to determine the return type. Instead, the function "
"chooses the return type, but only promises that it will implement `Trait`."
msgstr ""
"不允许调用者确定返回类型。相反，该函数会选择返回类型，但只承诺它会实现 "
"`Trait`。"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:165
msgid "r\\[type.impl-trait.constraint\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.impl-trait.constraint\\]"

#: src/types/impl-trait.md:168
msgid ""
"`impl Trait` can only appear as a parameter or return type of a non-`extern` "
"function. It cannot be the type of a `let` binding, field type, or appear "
"inside a type alias."
msgstr ""
"`impl Trait` 只能作为非 `extern` 函数的形参或返回类型出现。它不能作为 `let` "
"绑定的类型、字段类型，也不能出现在类型别名内部。"

#: src/types/parameters.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.generic\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.generic\\]"

#: src/types/parameters.md:4
msgid ""
"Within the body of an item that has type parameter declarations, the names "
"of its type parameters are types:"
msgstr "在具有类型参数声明的项的主体内，其类型参数的名称就是类型："

#: src/types/parameters.md:18
msgid ""
"Here, `first` has type `A`, referring to `to_vec`'s `A` type parameter; and "
"`rest` has type `Vec<A>`, a vector with element type `A`."
msgstr ""
"这里，`first` 的类型为 `A`，指代 `to_vec` 的 `A` 类型参数；而 `rest` 的类型"
"为 `Vec<A>`，即元素类型为 `A` 的 vector。"

#: src/types/inferred.md:1
msgid "r\\[type.inferred\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.inferred\\]"

#: src/types/inferred.md:4
msgid "r\\[type.inferred.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[type.inferred.syntax\\]"

#: src/types/inferred.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[type.inferred.intro\\] The inferred type asks the compiler to infer the "
"type if possible based on the surrounding information available."
msgstr ""
"r\\[type.inferred.intro\\] 推断类型要求编译器在可能时基于周围可用的信息推断类"
"型。"

#: src/types/inferred.md:12
msgid "\\[!EXAMPLE\\] The inferred type is often used in generic arguments:"
msgstr "\\[!EXAMPLE\\] 推断类型常用于泛型实参："

#: src/types/inferred.md:19
msgid ""
"r\\[type.inferred.constraint\\] The inferred type cannot be used in item "
"signatures."
msgstr "r\\[type.inferred.constraint\\] 推断类型不能用于项签名。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:1
msgid "r\\[dynamic-sized\\]"
msgstr "r\\[dynamic-sized\\]"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[dynamic-sized.intro\\] Most types have a fixed size that is known at "
"compile time and implement the trait [`Sized`](special-types-and-"
"traits.md#sized). A type with a size that is known only at run-time is "
"called a _dynamically sized type_ (_DST_) or, informally, an unsized type.  "
"[Slices](types/slice.md), [trait objects](types/trait-object.md), and [str]"
"(types/str.md) are examples of <abbr title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</"
"abbr>."
msgstr ""
"r\\[dynamic-sized.intro\\] 大多数类型都有在编译时已知的固定大小，并实现 "
"trait [`Sized`](special-types-and-traits.md#sized)。大小只有在运行时才知道的"
"类型称为*动态大小类型*（_DST_），非正式地也称为 unsized 类型。[切片](types/"
"slice.md)、[trait 对象](types/trait-object.md) 和 [str](types/str.md) 是 "
"<abbr title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr> 的例子。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[dynamic-sized.restriction\\] Such types can only be used in certain "
"cases:"
msgstr "r\\[dynamic-sized.restriction\\] 这类类型只能在某些情况下使用："

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:10
msgid "r\\[dynamic-sized.pointer-types\\]"
msgstr "r\\[dynamic-sized.pointer-types\\]"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:11
msgid ""
"[Pointer types](types/pointer.md) to <abbr title=\"dynamically sized "
"types\">DSTs</abbr> are sized but have twice the size of pointers to sized "
"types"
msgstr ""
"指向 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr> 的[指针类型](types/"
"pointer.md) 是有大小的，但其大小是指向有大小类型的指针的两倍"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:12
msgid "Pointers to slices and `str` also store the number of elements."
msgstr "指向切片和 `str` 的指针还会存储元素数量。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:13
msgid "Pointers to trait objects also store a pointer to a vtable."
msgstr "指向 trait 对象的指针还会存储一个指向 vtable 的指针。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:15
msgid "r\\[dynamic-sized.question-sized\\]"
msgstr "r\\[dynamic-sized.question-sized\\]"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:16
msgid ""
"<abbr title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr> can be provided as type "
"arguments to generic type parameters having the special `?Sized` bound. They "
"can also be used for associated type definitions when the corresponding "
"associated type declaration has a `?Sized` bound. By default, any type "
"parameter or associated type has a `Sized` bound, unless it is relaxed using "
"`?Sized`."
msgstr ""
"<abbr title=\"dynamically sized types\">DSTs</abbr> 可以作为类型实参提供给具"
"有特殊 `?Sized` 边界的泛型类型形参。当对应的关联类型声明具有 `?Sized` 边界"
"时，它们也可以用于关联类型定义。默认情况下，任何类型形参或关联类型都有 "
"`Sized` 边界，除非使用 `?Sized` 将其放宽。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:18
msgid "r\\[dynamic-sized.trait-impl\\]"
msgstr "r\\[dynamic-sized.trait-impl\\]"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:19
msgid ""
"Traits may be implemented for <abbr title=\"dynamically sized\n"
"types\">DSTs</abbr>. Unlike with generic type parameters, `Self: ?Sized` is "
"the default in trait definitions."
msgstr ""
"可以为 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized\n"
"types\">DSTs</abbr> 实现 trait。与泛型类型形参不同，在 trait 定义中 `Self: ?"
"Sized` 是默认情况。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:22
msgid "r\\[dynamic-sized.struct-field\\]"
msgstr "r\\[dynamic-sized.struct-field\\]"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:23
msgid ""
"Structs may contain a <abbr title=\"dynamically sized type\">DST</abbr> as "
"the last field; this makes the struct itself a <abbr title=\"dynamically "
"sized type\">DST</abbr>."
msgstr ""
"结构体可以包含一个 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized type\">DST</abbr> 作为最后"
"一个字段；这会使该结构体本身成为一个 <abbr title=\"dynamically sized "
"type\">DST</abbr>。"

#: src/dynamically-sized-types.md:25
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] [Variables](variables.md), function parameters, [const](items/"
"constant-items.md) items, and [static](items/static-items.md) items must be "
"`Sized`."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] [变量](variables.md)、函数形参、[const](items/constant-items.md) "
"项和 [static](items/static-items.md) 项必须是 `Sized`。"

#: src/type-layout.md:1
msgid "r\\[layout\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.intro\\] The layout of a type is its size, alignment, and the "
"relative offsets of its fields. For enums, how the discriminant is laid out "
"and interpreted is also part of type layout."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.intro\\] 类型的布局包括它的大小、对齐以及其字段的相对偏移量。对于 "
"enum，判别值如何布局和解释也属于类型布局的一部分。"

#: src/type-layout.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.guarantees\\] Type layout can be changed with each compilation. "
"Instead of trying to document exactly what is done, we only document what is "
"guaranteed today."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.guarantees\\] 类型布局可能随每次编译而改变。我们不试图记录实际具体"
"做了什么，而只记录目前保证的内容。"

#: src/type-layout.md:10
msgid ""
"Note that even types with the same layout can still differ in how they are "
"passed across function boundaries. For function call ABI compatibility of "
"types, see [here](../core/primitive.fn.md#abi-compatibility)."
msgstr ""
"注意，即使两个类型具有相同布局，它们跨函数边界传递的方式仍可能不同。关于类型"
"的函数调用 ABI 兼容性，见[这里](../core/primitive.fn.md#abi-compatibility)。"

#: src/type-layout.md:12
msgid "r\\[layout.properties\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.properties\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:13
msgid "Size and alignment"
msgstr "大小和对齐"

#: src/type-layout.md:15
msgid "All values have an alignment and size."
msgstr "所有值都有对齐和大小。"

#: src/type-layout.md:17
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.properties.align\\] The _alignment_ of a value specifies what "
"addresses are valid to store the value at. A value of alignment `n` must "
"only be stored at an address that is a multiple of n. For example, a value "
"with an alignment of 2 must be stored at an even address, while a value with "
"an alignment of 1 can be stored at any address. Alignment is measured in "
"bytes, and must be at least 1, and always a power of 2. The alignment of a "
"value can be checked with the [`align_of_val`](std::mem::align_of_val) "
"function."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.properties.align\\] 值的 *对齐* 指定了哪些地址可用于存储该值。对齐"
"为 `n` 的值只能存储在地址值为 n 的倍数的地址处。例如，对齐为 2 的值必须存储在"
"偶数地址，而对齐为 1 的值可以存储在任意地址。对齐以字节为单位，必须至少为 1，"
"并且始终是 2 的幂。可以使用 [`align_of_val`](std::mem::align_of_val) 函数检查"
"值的对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:20
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.properties.size\\] The _size_ of a value is the offset in bytes "
"between successive elements in an array with that item type including "
"alignment padding. The size of a value is always a multiple of its "
"alignment. Note that some types are [zero-sized](glossary.zst); 0 is "
"considered a multiple of any alignment (for example, on some platforms, the "
"type `[u16; 0]` has size 0 and alignment 2). The size of a value can be "
"checked with the [`size_of_val`](std::mem::size_of_val) function."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.properties.size\\] 值的 *大小* 是具有该元素类型的数组中相邻元素之"
"间的字节偏移量，包括对齐填充。值的大小始终是其对齐的倍数。注意，某些类型是[零"
"大小](glossary.zst)；0 被视为任何对齐的倍数（例如，在某些平台上，类型 `[u16; "
"0]` 的大小为 0、对齐为 2）。可以使用 [`size_of_val`](std::mem::size_of_val) "
"函数检查值的大小。"

#: src/type-layout.md:23
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.properties.sized\\] Types where all values have the same size and "
"alignment, and both are known at compile time, implement the [`Sized`]"
"(std::marker::Sized) trait and can be checked with the [`size_of`]"
"(std::mem::size_of) and [`align_of`](std::mem::align_of) functions. Types "
"that are not [`Sized`](std::marker::Sized) are known as [dynamically sized "
"types](dynamically-sized-types.md). Since all values of a `Sized` type share "
"the same size and alignment, we refer to those shared values as the size of "
"the type and the alignment of the type respectively."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.properties.sized\\] 所有值都具有相同大小和对齐，且二者在编译时已知"
"的类型，实现 [`Sized`](std::marker::Sized) trait，并可用 [`size_of`]"
"(std::mem::size_of) 和 [`align_of`](std::mem::align_of) 函数检查。不是 "
"[`Sized`](std::marker::Sized) 的类型称为[动态大小类型](dynamically-sized-"
"types.md)。由于 `Sized` 类型的所有值共享相同的大小和对齐，我们分别将这些共享"
"的量称为该类型的大小和该类型的对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:26
msgid "r\\[layout.primitive\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.primitive\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:27
msgid "Primitive data layout"
msgstr "原始数据布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:29
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.size\\] The size of most primitives is given in this "
"table."
msgstr "r\\[layout.primitive.size\\] 大多数原始类型的大小见下表。"

#: src/type-layout.md:32
msgid "`size_of::<Type>()`"
msgstr "`size_of::<Type>()`"

#: src/type-layout.md:34 src/type-layout.md:35
msgid "1"
msgstr "1"

#: src/type-layout.md:35
msgid "`u8` / `i8`"
msgstr "`u8` / `i8`"

#: src/type-layout.md:36
msgid "`u16` / `i16`"
msgstr "`u16` / `i16`"

#: src/type-layout.md:36
msgid "2"
msgstr "2"

#: src/type-layout.md:37
msgid "`u32` / `i32`"
msgstr "`u32` / `i32`"

#: src/type-layout.md:37 src/type-layout.md:41 src/type-layout.md:43
msgid "4"
msgstr "4"

#: src/type-layout.md:38
msgid "`u64` / `i64`"
msgstr "`u64` / `i64`"

#: src/type-layout.md:38 src/type-layout.md:42
msgid "8"
msgstr "8"

#: src/type-layout.md:39
msgid "`u128` / `i128`"
msgstr "`u128` / `i128`"

#: src/type-layout.md:39
msgid "16"
msgstr "16"

#: src/type-layout.md:40
msgid "`usize` / `isize`"
msgstr "`usize` / `isize`"

#: src/type-layout.md:40
msgid "See below"
msgstr "见下文"

#: src/type-layout.md:41 src/inline-assembly.md:680 src/inline-assembly.md:685
msgid "`f32`"
msgstr "`f32`"

#: src/type-layout.md:42 src/inline-assembly.md:681 src/inline-assembly.md:686
msgid "`f64`"
msgstr "`f64`"

#: src/type-layout.md:45
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.size-minimum\\] `usize` and `isize` have a size big "
"enough to contain every address on the target platform. For example, on a 32 "
"bit target, this is 4 bytes, and on a 64 bit target, this is 8 bytes."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.size-minimum\\] `usize` 和 `isize` 的大小足以容纳目标平"
"台上的每个地址。例如，在 32 位目标上为 4 字节，在 64 位目标上为 8 字节。"

#: src/type-layout.md:48
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.size-align\\] `usize` and `isize` have the same size "
"and alignment."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.size-align\\] `usize` 和 `isize` 具有相同的大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:51
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.platform-specific-alignment\\] The alignment of "
"primitives is platform-specific. In most cases, their alignment is equal to "
"their size, but it may be less. In particular, `i128` and `u128` are often "
"aligned to 4 or 8 bytes even though their size is 16, and on many 32-bit "
"platforms, `i64`, `u64`, and `f64` are only aligned to 4 bytes, not 8."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.platform-specific-alignment\\] 原始类型的对齐是平台特定"
"的。大多数情况下，它们的对齐等于其大小，但也可能更小。特别是，`i128` 和 "
"`u128` 虽然大小为 16，却通常按 4 或 8 字节对齐；在许多 32 位平台上，`i64`、"
"`u64` 和 `f64` 只按 4 字节而不是 8 字节对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:54
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.integer-alignment\\] Alignment is guaranteed to be the "
"same for fixed-width signed and unsigned integer variants of the same "
"indicated size --- that is, for a given size `N`, `align_of::<uN>() == "
"align_of::<iN>()`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.primitive.integer-alignment\\] 保证同一指定位宽的定宽有符号和无符"
"号整数变体具有相同对齐——也就是说，对于给定大小 `N`，`align_of::<uN>() == "
"align_of::<iN>()`。"

#: src/type-layout.md:57
msgid "r\\[layout.pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.pointer\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:58
msgid "Pointers and references layout"
msgstr "指针和引用布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:60
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.pointer.intro\\] Pointers and references have the same layout. "
"Mutability of the pointer or reference does not change the layout."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.pointer.intro\\] 指针和引用具有相同布局。指针或引用的可变性不会改"
"变布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:63
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.pointer.thin\\] Pointers to sized types have the same size and "
"alignment as `usize`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.pointer.thin\\] 指向有大小类型的指针具有与 `usize` 相同的大小和对"
"齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:66
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.pointer.unsized\\] Pointers to unsized types are sized. The size "
"and alignment of a pointer to an unsized type are each guaranteed to be "
"greater than or equal to those of a pointer to a sized type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.pointer.unsized\\] 指向无大小类型的指针是有大小的。保证指向无大小"
"类型的指针的大小和对齐分别大于或等于指向有大小类型的指针的大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:69
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Though you should not rely on this, all pointers to <abbr "
"title=\"Dynamically Sized Types\">DSTs</abbr> are currently twice the size "
"of the size of `usize` and have the same alignment."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 尽管你不应依赖这一点，但目前所有指向 <abbr title=\"Dynamically "
"Sized Types\">DSTs</abbr> 的指针的大小都是 `usize` 大小的两倍，并具有相同的对"
"齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:72
msgid "r\\[layout.array\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.array\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:73
msgid "Array layout"
msgstr "数组布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:75
msgid ""
"An array of `[T; N]` has a size of `size_of::<T>() * N` and the same "
"alignment of `T`. Arrays are laid out so that the zero-based `nth` element "
"of the array is offset from the start of the array by `n * size_of::<T>()` "
"bytes."
msgstr ""
"`[T; N]` 数组的大小为 `size_of::<T>() * N`，并具有与 `T` 相同的对齐。数组的布"
"局使得数组中从零开始计数的 `nth` 元素相对于数组开头的偏移量为 `n * size_of::"
"<T>()` 字节。"

#: src/type-layout.md:77
msgid "r\\[layout.slice\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.slice\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:78
msgid "Slice layout"
msgstr "切片布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:80
msgid "Slices have the same layout as the section of the array they slice."
msgstr "切片与其切取的数组区段具有相同布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:82
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] This is about the raw `[T]` type, not pointers (`&[T]`, "
"`Box<[T]>`, etc.) to slices."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 这里说的是原始 `[T]` 类型，而不是指向切片的指针（`&[T]`、"
"`Box<[T]>` 等）。"

#: src/type-layout.md:85
msgid "r\\[layout.str\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.str\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:86
msgid "`str` Layout"
msgstr "`str` 布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:88
msgid ""
"String slices are a UTF-8 representation of characters that have the same "
"layout as slices of type `[u8]`. A reference `&str` has the same layout as a "
"reference `&[u8]`."
msgstr ""
"字符串切片是字符的 UTF-8 表示，其布局与类型 `[u8]` 的切片相同。引用 `&str` 与"
"引用 `&[u8]` 具有相同布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:90
msgid "r\\[layout.tuple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.tuple\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:91
msgid "Tuple layout"
msgstr "元组布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:93
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.tuple.def\\] Tuples are laid out according to the [`Rust` "
"representation](#the-rust-representation)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.tuple.def\\] 元组按照 [`Rust` 表示](#the-rust-representation)进行"
"布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:96
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.tuple.unit\\] The exception to this is the unit tuple (`()`), "
"which is guaranteed as a [zero-sized type](glossary.zst) to have a size of 0 "
"and an alignment of 1."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.tuple.unit\\] 例外是单元元组（`()`），保证它作为[零大小类型]"
"(glossary.zst)具有大小 0 和对齐 1。"

#: src/type-layout.md:99
msgid "r\\[layout.trait-object\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.trait-object\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:100
msgid "Trait object layout"
msgstr "trait 对象布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:102
msgid "Trait objects have the same layout as the value the trait object is of."
msgstr "trait 对象与其所表示的值具有相同布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:104
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] This is about the raw trait object types, not pointers (`&dyn "
"Trait`, `Box<dyn Trait>`, etc.) to trait objects."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 这里说的是原始 trait 对象类型，而不是指向 trait 对象的指针"
"（`&dyn Trait`、`Box<dyn Trait>` 等）。"

#: src/type-layout.md:107
msgid "r\\[layout.closure\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.closure\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:108
msgid "Closure layout"
msgstr "闭包布局"

#: src/type-layout.md:110
msgid "Closures have no layout guarantees."
msgstr "闭包没有布局保证。"

#: src/type-layout.md:112
msgid "r\\[layout.repr\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:113
msgid "Representations"
msgstr "表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:115
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.intro\\] All user-defined composite types (`struct`s, "
"`enum`s, and `union`s) have a _representation_ that specifies what the "
"layout is for the type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.intro\\] 所有用户定义的复合类型（`struct`、`enum` 和 "
"`union`）都有一个 *表示*，用于指定该类型的布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:118
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.kinds\\] The possible representations for a type are:"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.kinds\\] 类型可能具有的表示有："

#: src/type-layout.md:121
msgid "[`Rust`](#the-rust-representation) (default)"
msgstr "[`Rust`](#the-rust-representation)（默认）"

#: src/type-layout.md:122
msgid "[`C`](#the-c-representation)"
msgstr "[`C`](#the-c-representation)"

#: src/type-layout.md:123
msgid "The [primitive representations](#primitive-representations)"
msgstr "[原始表示](#primitive-representations)"

#: src/type-layout.md:124
msgid "[`transparent`](#the-transparent-representation)"
msgstr "[`transparent`](#the-transparent-representation)"

#: src/type-layout.md:126
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.attribute\\] The representation of a type can be changed by "
"applying the `repr` attribute to it. The following example shows a struct "
"with a `C` representation."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.attribute\\] 可以通过对类型应用 `repr` 属性来改变类型的表示。"
"下面的示例展示了一个具有 `C` 表示的 struct。"

#: src/type-layout.md:138
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.align-packed\\] The alignment may be raised or lowered with "
"the `align` and `packed` modifiers respectively. They alter the "
"representation specified in the attribute. If no representation is "
"specified, the default one is altered."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.align-packed\\] 可以分别使用 `align` 和 `packed` 修饰符提高或"
"降低对齐。它们会更改属性中指定的表示。如果未指定表示，则会更改默认表示。"

#: src/type-layout.md:142
msgid "// Default representation, alignment lowered to 2.\n"
msgstr "// 默认表示，对齐降低为 2。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:149
msgid "// C representation, alignment raised to 8\n"
msgstr "// C 表示，对齐提高为 8\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:159
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] As a consequence of the representation being an attribute on the "
"item, the representation does not depend on generic parameters. Any two "
"types with the same name have the same representation. For example, "
"`Foo<Bar>` and `Foo<Baz>` both have the same representation."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 由于表示是项上的属性，表示不依赖于泛型参数。任何两个具有相同名称"
"的类型都有相同表示。例如，`Foo<Bar>` 和 `Foo<Baz>` 都具有相同表示。"

#: src/type-layout.md:162
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.inter-field\\] The representation of a type can change the "
"padding between fields, but does not change the layout of the fields "
"themselves. For example, a struct with a `C` representation that contains a "
"struct `Inner` with the `Rust` representation will not change the layout of "
"`Inner`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.inter-field\\] 类型的表示可以改变字段之间的填充，但不会改变字"
"段本身的布局。例如，一个具有 `C` 表示的 struct，如果包含一个具有 `Rust` 表示"
"的 struct `Inner`，则不会改变 `Inner` 的布局。"

#: src/type-layout.md:165
msgid "<a id=\"the-default-representation\"></a> r\\[layout.repr.rust\\]"
msgstr "<a id=\"the-default-representation\"></a> r\\[layout.repr.rust\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:167
msgid "The `Rust` representation"
msgstr "`Rust` 表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:169
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.rust.intro\\] The `Rust` representation is the default "
"representation for nominal types without a `repr` attribute. Using this "
"representation explicitly through a `repr` attribute is guaranteed to be the "
"same as omitting the attribute entirely."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.rust.intro\\] `Rust` 表示是没有 `repr` 属性的名义类型的默认表"
"示。通过 `repr` 属性显式使用此表示，保证与完全省略该属性相同。"

#: src/type-layout.md:172
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.rust.layout\\] The only data layout guarantees made by this "
"representation are those required for soundness. These are:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.rust.layout\\] 此表示作出的数据布局保证只有健全性所要求的那"
"些。它们是："

#: src/type-layout.md:175
msgid "The offset of a field is divisible by that field's alignment."
msgstr "字段的偏移量可被该字段的对齐整除。"

#: src/type-layout.md:176
msgid ""
"The alignment of the type is at least the maximum alignment of its fields."
msgstr "类型的对齐至少是其字段的最大对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:178
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.rust.layout.struct\\] For [structs](items/structs.md), it is "
"further guaranteed that the fields do not overlap. That is, the fields can "
"be ordered such that the offset plus the size of any field is less than or "
"equal to the offset of the next field in the ordering. The ordering does not "
"have to be the same as the order in which the fields are specified in the "
"declaration of the type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.rust.layout.struct\\] 对于 [struct](items/structs.md)，还进一"
"步保证字段不重叠。也就是说，可以对字段排序，使得任意字段的偏移量加上其大小小"
"于或等于该排序中下一个字段的偏移量。该排序不必与类型声明中指定字段的顺序相"
"同。"

#: src/type-layout.md:181
msgid ""
"Be aware that this guarantee does not imply that the fields have distinct "
"addresses: [zero-sized types](glossary.zst) may have the same address as "
"other fields in the same struct."
msgstr ""
"注意，此保证并不意味着字段具有不同地址：[零大小类型](glossary.zst)可能与同一 "
"struct 中的其他字段具有相同地址。"

#: src/type-layout.md:183
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.rust.unspecified\\] There are no other guarantees of data "
"layout made by this representation."
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.rust.unspecified\\] 此表示不作其他数据布局保证。"

#: src/type-layout.md:186
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.c\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.c\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:187
msgid "The `C` representation"
msgstr "`C` 表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:189
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.intro\\] The `C` representation is designed for dual "
"purposes. One purpose is for creating types that are interoperable with the "
"C Language. The second purpose is to create types that you can soundly "
"perform operations on that rely on data layout such as reinterpreting values "
"as a different type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.intro\\] `C` 表示有双重目的。一个目的是创建可与 C 语言互操"
"作的类型。第二个目的是创建可以健全地在其上执行依赖数据布局的操作（例如将值重"
"新解释为不同类型）的类型。"

#: src/type-layout.md:192
msgid ""
"Because of this dual purpose, it is possible to create types that are not "
"useful for interfacing with the C programming language."
msgstr "由于这种双重目的，可以创建出不适合与 C 编程语言交互的类型。"

#: src/type-layout.md:194
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.constraint\\] This representation can be applied to "
"structs, unions, and enums. The exception is [zero-variant enums](items/"
"enumerations.md#zero-variant-enums) for which the `C` representation is an "
"error."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.constraint\\] 此表示可以应用于 struct、union 和 enum。例外"
"是[零变体枚举](items/enumerations.md#zero-variant-enums)，对它们使用 `C` 表示"
"会出错。"

#: src/type-layout.md:197
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.c.struct\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.c.struct\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:198
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` Structs"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` struct"

#: src/type-layout.md:200
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.struct.align\\] The alignment of the struct is the "
"alignment of the most-aligned field in it, or one if there are no fields."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.struct.align\\] struct 的对齐是其中对齐要求最高的字段的对"
"齐；如果没有字段，则为 1。"

#: src/type-layout.md:203
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.struct.size-field-offset\\] The size and offset of fields "
"is determined by the following algorithm."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.struct.size-field-offset\\] 字段的大小和偏移量由以下算法确"
"定。"

#: src/type-layout.md:206
msgid "Start with a current offset of 0 bytes."
msgstr "从当前偏移量 0 字节开始。"

#: src/type-layout.md:208
msgid ""
"For each field in declaration order in the struct, first determine the size "
"and alignment of the field. If the current offset is not a multiple of the "
"field's alignment, then add padding bytes to the current offset until it is "
"a multiple of the field's alignment. The offset for the field is what the "
"current offset is now. Then increase the current offset by the size of the "
"field."
msgstr ""
"对于 struct 中按声明顺序排列的每个字段，首先确定该字段的大小和对齐。如果当前"
"偏移量不是该字段对齐的倍数，则向当前偏移量添加填充字节，直到它成为该字段对齐"
"的倍数。该字段的偏移量就是此时的当前偏移量。然后将当前偏移量增加该字段的大"
"小。"

#: src/type-layout.md:210
msgid ""
"Finally, the size of the struct is the current offset rounded up to the "
"nearest multiple of the struct's alignment."
msgstr ""
"最后，struct 的大小是将当前偏移量向上取整到最接近的 struct 对齐倍数后的值。"

#: src/type-layout.md:212
msgid "Here is this algorithm described in pseudocode."
msgstr "下面用伪代码描述此算法。"

#: src/type-layout.md:216
msgid ""
"/// Returns the amount of padding needed after `offset` to ensure that the\n"
"/// following address will be aligned to `alignment`.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// 返回 `offset` 之后所需的填充量，以确保\n"
"/// 后续地址将按 `alignment` 对齐。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:221
msgid "// round up to next multiple of `alignment`\n"
msgstr "// 向上取整到下一个 `alignment` 的倍数\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:224
msgid "// already a multiple of `alignment`\n"
msgstr "// 已经是 `alignment` 的倍数\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:234
msgid ""
"// Increase the current offset so that it's a multiple of the alignment\n"
"    // of this field. For the first field, this will always be zero.\n"
"    // The skipped bytes are called padding bytes.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 增加当前偏移量，使其成为此字段对齐的倍数。\n"
"    // 对第一个字段，这始终为零。\n"
"    // 跳过的字节称为填充字节。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:247
msgid ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] This pseudocode uses a naive algorithm that ignores overflow "
"issues for the sake of clarity. To perform memory layout computations in "
"actual code, use [`Layout`](std::alloc::Layout)."
msgstr ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] 为了清晰起见，此伪代码使用了一个会忽略溢出问题的朴素算法。要在"
"实际代码中执行内存布局计算，请使用 [`Layout`](std::alloc::Layout)。"

#: src/type-layout.md:250
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] This algorithm can produce [zero-sized](glossary.zst) structs. "
"In C, an empty struct declaration like `struct Foo { }` is illegal. However, "
"both gcc and clang support options to enable such structs, and assign them "
"size zero. C++, in contrast, gives empty structs a size of 1, unless they "
"are inherited from or they are fields that have the `[[no_unique_address]]` "
"attribute, in which case they do not increase the overall size of the struct."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 此算法可以产生[零大小](glossary.zst) struct。在 C 中，像 `struct "
"Foo { }` 这样的空 struct 声明是非法的。不过，gcc 和 clang 都支持启用这类 "
"struct 的选项，并赋予它们零大小。相比之下，C++ 会给空 struct 大小 1，除非它们"
"作为基类被继承，或者它们是具有 `[[no_unique_address]]` 属性的字段；在这些情况"
"下，它们不会增加 struct 的整体大小。"

#: src/type-layout.md:253
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.c.union\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.c.union\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:254
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` Unions"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` union"

#: src/type-layout.md:256
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.union.intro\\] A union declared with `#[repr(C)]` will "
"have the same size and alignment as an equivalent C union declaration in the "
"C language for the target platform."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.union.intro\\] 使用 `#[repr(C)]` 声明的 union 将具有与目标"
"平台上 C 语言中等价的 C union 声明相同的大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:259
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.union.size-align\\] The union will have a size of the "
"maximum size of all of its fields rounded to its alignment, and an alignment "
"of the maximum alignment of all of its fields. These maximums may come from "
"different fields. Each field lives at byte offset 0 from the beginning of "
"the union."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.union.size-align\\] union 的大小是其所有字段最大大小按其对"
"齐向上取整后的值，对齐是其所有字段的最大对齐。这两个最大值可能来自不同字段。"
"每个字段都位于从 union 开头起的字节偏移量 0 处。"

#: src/type-layout.md:269
msgid "// From f2\n"
msgstr "// 来自 f2\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:270
msgid "// From f1\n"
msgstr "// 来自 f1\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:281
msgid ""
"// Size of 6 from b,\n"
"                                                      // rounded up to 8 "
"from\n"
"                                                      // alignment of a.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 大小 6 来自 b，\n"
"                                                      // 根据 a 的对齐\n"
"                                                      // 向上取整到 8。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:284
msgid "// From a\n"
msgstr "// 来自 a\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:290
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.c.enum\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.c.enum\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:291
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` Field-less Enums"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` 无字段 enum"

#: src/type-layout.md:293
msgid ""
"For [field-less enums](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum), the `C` "
"representation has the size and alignment of the default `enum` size and "
"alignment for the target platform's C ABI."
msgstr ""
"对于[无字段枚举](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum)，`C` 表示的大小和对齐"
"等同于目标平台 C ABI 中默认的 `enum` 大小和对齐。"

#: src/type-layout.md:295
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The enum representation in C is implementation defined, so this "
"is really a \"best guess\". In particular, this may be incorrect when the C "
"code of interest is compiled with certain flags."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] C 中的 enum 表示由实现定义，因此这实际上只是“最佳猜测”。特别是，"
"当相关 C 代码使用某些标志编译时，这可能不正确。"

#: src/type-layout.md:298
msgid ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] There are crucial differences between an `enum` in the C "
"language and Rust's [field-less enums](items/enumerations.md#field-less-"
"enum) with this representation. An `enum` in C is mostly a `typedef` plus "
"some named constants; in other words, an object of an `enum` type can hold "
"any integer value. For example, this is often used for bitflags in `C`. In "
"contrast, Rust’s [field-less enums](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum) "
"can only legally hold the discriminant values, everything else is [undefined "
"behavior](behavior-considered-undefined.md). Therefore, using a field-less "
"enum in FFI to model a C `enum` is often wrong."
msgstr ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] C 语言中的 `enum` 与 Rust 中使用此表示的[无字段枚举](items/"
"enumerations.md#field-less-enum)之间存在关键差异。C 中的 `enum` 大多是一个 "
"`typedef` 加上一些具名常量；换句话说，`enum` 类型的对象可以持有任何整数值。例"
"如，这在 `C` 中常用于 bitflags。相比之下，Rust 的[无字段枚举](items/"
"enumerations.md#field-less-enum)只能合法地持有判别值，其他一切都是[未定义行"
"为](behavior-considered-undefined.md)。因此，在 FFI 中使用无字段枚举来模拟 C "
"`enum` 往往是错误的。"

#: src/type-layout.md:301
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.c.adt\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.c.adt\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:302
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` Enums With Fields"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` 带字段 enum"

#: src/type-layout.md:304
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.adt.intro\\] The representation of a `repr(C)` enum with "
"fields is a `repr(C)` struct with two fields, also called a \"tagged union\" "
"in C:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.c.adt.intro\\] 带字段的 `repr(C)` enum 的表示是一个有两个字段"
"的 `repr(C)` struct，在 C 中也称为“tagged union”："

#: src/type-layout.md:307
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.c.adt.tag\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.c.adt.tag\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:308
msgid "a `repr(C)` version of the enum with all fields removed (\"the tag\")"
msgstr "该 enum 移除所有字段后的 `repr(C)` 版本（“标签”）"

#: src/type-layout.md:310
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.c.adt.fields\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.c.adt.fields\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:311
msgid ""
"a `repr(C)` union of `repr(C)` structs for the fields of each variant that "
"had them (\"the payload\")"
msgstr ""
"由每个带字段变体的字段所对应的 `repr(C)` struct 构成的 `repr(C)` union（“载"
"荷”）"

#: src/type-layout.md:313
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Due to the representation of `repr(C)` structs and unions, if a "
"variant has a single field there is no difference between putting that field "
"directly in the union or wrapping it in a struct; any system which wishes to "
"manipulate such an `enum`'s representation may therefore use whichever form "
"is more convenient or consistent for them."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 由于 `repr(C)` struct 和 union 的表示，如果某个变体只有一个字段，"
"那么将该字段直接放入 union 与将其包装在 struct 中没有区别；因此，任何希望操作"
"这种 `enum` 表示的系统都可以使用对它们来说更方便或更一致的形式。"

#: src/type-layout.md:317
msgid "// This Enum has the same representation as ...\n"
msgstr "// 此 Enum 具有与以下内容相同的表示...\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:325
msgid "// ... this struct.\n"
msgstr "// ...这个 struct。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:332 src/type-layout.md:405
msgid "// This is the discriminant enum.\n"
msgstr "// 这是判别值 enum。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:336
msgid "// This is the variant union.\n"
msgstr "// 这是变体 union。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:357
msgid ""
"// This struct could be omitted (it is a zero-sized type), and it must be "
"in\n"
"// C/C++ headers.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 此 struct 可以省略（它是零大小类型），且它必须位于\n"
"// C/C++ 头文件中。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:365
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.primitive\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.primitive\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:366
msgid "Primitive representations"
msgstr "原始表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:368
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.primitive.intro\\] The _primitive representations_ are the "
"representations with the same names as the primitive integer types. That is: "
"`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`, `usize`, `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, "
"`i128`, and `isize`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.primitive.intro\\] *原始表示* 是与原始整数类型同名的表示。也"
"就是：`u8`、`u16`、`u32`、`u64`、`u128`、`usize`、`i8`、`i16`、`i32`、`i64`、"
"`i128` 和 `isize`。"

#: src/type-layout.md:371
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.primitive.constraint\\] Primitive representations can only "
"be applied to enumerations and have different behavior whether the enum has "
"fields or no fields. It is an error for [zero-variant enums](items/"
"enumerations.md#zero-variant-enums) to have a primitive representation. "
"Combining two primitive representations together is an error."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.primitive.constraint\\] 原始表示只能应用于枚举，并且根据 "
"enum 是否有字段而有不同的行为。对[零变体枚举](items/enumerations.md#zero-"
"variant-enums)使用原始表示是错误。将两个原始表示组合在一起是错误。"

#: src/type-layout.md:374
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.primitive.enum\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.primitive.enum\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:375
msgid "Primitive representation of field-less enums"
msgstr "无字段枚举的原始表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:377
msgid ""
"For [field-less enums](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum), primitive "
"representations set the size and alignment to be the same as the primitive "
"type of the same name. For example, a field-less enum with a `u8` "
"representation can only have discriminants between 0 and 255 inclusive."
msgstr ""
"对于[无字段枚举](items/enumerations.md#field-less-enum)，原始表示会将大小和对"
"齐设为与同名原始类型相同。例如，具有 `u8` 表示的无字段枚举只能具有 0 到 255"
"（含）之间的判别值。"

#: src/type-layout.md:379
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.primitive.adt\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.primitive.adt\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:380
msgid "Primitive representation of enums with fields"
msgstr "带字段枚举的原始表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:382
msgid ""
"The representation of a primitive representation enum is a `repr(C)` union "
"of `repr(C)` structs for each variant with a field. The first field of each "
"struct in the union is the primitive representation version of the enum with "
"all fields removed (\"the tag\") and the remaining fields are the fields of "
"that variant."
msgstr ""
"原始表示枚举的表示是一个 `repr(C)` union，其中包含每个带字段变体对应的 "
"`repr(C)` struct。union 中每个 struct 的第一个字段是该 enum 移除所有字段后的"
"原始表示版本（“标签”），其余字段是该变体的字段。"

#: src/type-layout.md:384
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] This representation is unchanged if the tag is given its own "
"member in the union, should that make manipulation more clear for you "
"(although to follow the C++ standard the tag member should be wrapped in a "
"`struct`)."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 如果将标签作为自己的成员放在 union 中，此表示不变；如果这能让操作"
"对你更清晰的话可以这样做（不过，为了遵循 C++ 标准，标签成员应包装在 `struct` "
"中）。"

#: src/type-layout.md:388
msgid "// This enum has the same representation as ...\n"
msgstr "// 此 enum 具有与以下内容相同的表示...\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:396
msgid "// ... this union.\n"
msgstr "// ...这个 union。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:428
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.primitive-c\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.primitive-c\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:429
msgid ""
"Combining primitive representations of enums with fields and `#[repr(C)]`"
msgstr "组合带字段枚举的原始表示和 `#[repr(C)]`"

#: src/type-layout.md:431
msgid ""
"For enums with fields, it is also possible to combine `repr(C)` and a "
"primitive representation (e.g., `repr(C, u8)`). This modifies the [`repr(C)`]"
"(#reprc-enums-with-fields) by changing the representation of the "
"discriminant enum to the chosen primitive instead. So, if you chose the `u8` "
"representation, then the discriminant enum would have a size and alignment "
"of 1 byte."
msgstr ""
"对于带字段枚举，也可以组合 `repr(C)` 和原始表示（例如 `repr(C, u8)`）。这会修"
"改 [`repr(C)`](#reprc-enums-with-fields)，将判别值 enum 的表示改为所选原始表"
"示。因此，如果选择 `u8` 表示，判别值 enum 的大小和对齐将为 1 字节。"

#: src/type-layout.md:433
msgid ""
"The discriminant enum from the example [earlier](#reprc-enums-with-fields) "
"then becomes:"
msgstr "前面[示例](#reprc-enums-with-fields)中的判别值 enum 随后变为："

#: src/type-layout.md:436
msgid "// `u8` was added\n"
msgstr "// 添加了 `u8`\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:446
msgid "// So `u8` is used here instead of `C`\n"
msgstr "// 因此这里使用 `u8` 而不是 `C`\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:452
msgid ""
"For example, with a `repr(C, u8)` enum it is not possible to have 257 unique "
"discriminants (\"tags\") whereas the same enum with only a `repr(C)` "
"attribute will compile without any problems."
msgstr ""
"例如，对于 `repr(C, u8)` enum，不可能有 257 个唯一判别值（“标签”）；而同一个 "
"enum 如果只有 `repr(C)` 属性，则会顺利编译。"

#: src/type-layout.md:454
msgid ""
"Using a primitive representation in addition to `repr(C)` can change the "
"size of an enum from the `repr(C)` form:"
msgstr ""
"除了 `repr(C)` 之外再使用原始表示，可能会改变 enum 相对于 `repr(C)` 形式的大"
"小："

#: src/type-layout.md:474
msgid "// The size of the C representation is platform dependent\n"
msgstr "// C 表示的大小依赖平台\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:476
msgid ""
"// One byte for the discriminant and one byte for the value in "
"Enum8::Variant0\n"
msgstr "// 判别值一个字节，Enum8::Variant0 中的值一个字节\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:478
msgid ""
"// Two bytes for the discriminant and one byte for the value in "
"Enum16::Variant0\n"
"// plus one byte of padding.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 判别值两个字节，Enum16::Variant0 中的值一个字节，\n"
"// 再加一个字节的填充。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:486
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.alignment\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.alignment\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:487
msgid "The alignment modifiers"
msgstr "对齐修饰符"

#: src/type-layout.md:489
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.intro\\] The `align` and `packed` modifiers can be "
"used to respectively raise or lower the alignment of `struct`s and `union`s. "
"`packed` may also alter the padding between fields (although it will not "
"alter the padding inside of any field). On their own, `align` and `packed` "
"do not provide guarantees about the order of fields in the layout of a "
"struct or the layout of an enum variant, although they may be combined with "
"representations (such as `C`) which do provide such guarantees."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.intro\\] `align` 和 `packed` 修饰符可分别用于提高或"
"降低 `struct` 和 `union` 的对齐。`packed` 也可能改变字段之间的填充（不过它不"
"会改变任何字段内部的填充）。`align` 和 `packed` 本身不保证 struct 布局或 "
"enum 变体布局中字段的顺序，不过它们可以与确实提供此类保证的表示（如 `C`）组合"
"使用。"

#: src/type-layout.md:492
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.constraint-alignment\\] The alignment is specified "
"as an integer parameter in the form of `#[repr(align(x))]` or "
"`#[repr(packed(x))]`. The alignment value must be a power of two from 1 up "
"to 2<sup>29</sup>. For `packed`, if no value is given, as in "
"`#[repr(packed)]`, then the value is 1."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.constraint-alignment\\] 对齐以 `#[repr(align(x))]` "
"或 `#[repr(packed(x))]` 形式的整数参数指定。对齐值必须是从 1 到 2<sup>29</"
"sup> 的 2 的幂。对于 `packed`，如果未给出值，如 `#[repr(packed)]`，则该值为 "
"1。"

#: src/type-layout.md:495
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.align\\] For `align`, if the specified alignment "
"is less than the alignment of the type without the `align` modifier, then "
"the alignment is unaffected."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.align\\] 对于 `align`，如果指定的对齐小于没有 "
"`align` 修饰符时该类型的对齐，则对齐不受影响。"

#: src/type-layout.md:498
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.packed\\] For `packed`, if the specified alignment "
"is greater than the type's alignment without the `packed` modifier, then the "
"alignment and layout is unaffected."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.packed\\] 对于 `packed`，如果指定的对齐大于没有 "
"`packed` 修饰符时该类型的对齐，则对齐和布局不受影响。"

#: src/type-layout.md:501
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.packed-fields\\] The alignments of each field, for "
"the purpose of positioning fields, is the smaller of the specified alignment "
"and the alignment of the field's type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.packed-fields\\] 为放置字段而使用的每个字段的对齐，"
"是指定对齐和该字段类型对齐两者中的较小者。"

#: src/type-layout.md:504
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.packed-padding\\] Inter-field padding is "
"guaranteed to be the minimum required in order to satisfy each field's "
"(possibly altered) alignment (although note that, on its own, `packed` does "
"not provide any guarantee about field ordering). An important consequence of "
"these rules is that a type with `#[repr(packed(1))]` (or `#[repr(packed)]`) "
"will have no inter-field padding."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.packed-padding\\] 保证字段间填充是满足每个字段（可"
"能已更改的）对齐所需的最小填充（不过请注意，`packed` 本身不提供任何字段排序保"
"证）。这些规则的一个重要后果是，具有 `#[repr(packed(1))]`（或 "
"`#[repr(packed)]`）的类型没有字段间填充。"

#: src/type-layout.md:507
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.constraint-exclusive\\] The `align` and `packed` "
"modifiers cannot be applied on the same type and a `packed` type cannot "
"transitively contain another `align`ed type. `align` and `packed` may only "
"be applied to the [`Rust`](#the-rust-representation) and [`C`](#the-c-"
"representation) representations."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.constraint-exclusive\\] `align` 和 `packed` 修饰符"
"不能应用于同一类型，且 `packed` 类型不能传递地包含另一个已 `align` 的类型。"
"`align` 和 `packed` 只能应用于 [`Rust`](#the-rust-representation) 和 [`C`]"
"(#the-c-representation) 表示。"

#: src/type-layout.md:510
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.enum\\] The `align` modifier can also be applied "
"on an `enum`. When it is, the effect on the `enum`'s alignment is the same "
"as if the `enum` was wrapped in a newtype `struct` with the same `align` "
"modifier."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.alignment.enum\\] `align` 修饰符也可以应用于 `enum`。这样做"
"时，它对 `enum` 对齐的影响，就像将该 `enum` 包装在具有相同 `align` 修饰符的 "
"newtype `struct` 中一样。"

#: src/type-layout.md:513
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] References to unaligned fields are not allowed because it is "
"[undefined behavior](behavior-considered-undefined.md). When fields are "
"unaligned due to an alignment modifier, consider the following options for "
"using references and dereferences:"
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 不允许引用未对齐字段，因为这是[未定义行为](behavior-considered-"
"undefined.md)。当字段因对齐修饰符而未对齐时，使用引用和解引用可考虑以下选项："

#: src/type-layout.md:523
msgid ""
"// Instead of creating a reference to a field, copy the value to a local "
"variable.\n"
msgstr "// 不要创建指向字段的引用，而是将值复制到局部变量。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:525
msgid ""
"// Or in situations like `println!` which creates a reference, use braces\n"
msgstr "// 或者在 `println!` 这类会创建引用的情形中，使用花括号\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:526
msgid "// to change it to a copy of the value.\n"
msgstr "// 将它改为值的副本。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:528
msgid ""
"// Or if you need a pointer, use the unaligned methods for reading and "
"writing\n"
msgstr "// 或者如果需要指针，使用用于读写的未对齐方法，\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:529
msgid "// instead of dereferencing the pointer directly.\n"
msgstr "// 而不是直接解引用指针。\n"

#: src/type-layout.md:536
msgid "r\\[layout.repr.transparent\\]"
msgstr "r\\[layout.repr.transparent\\]"

#: src/type-layout.md:537
msgid "The `transparent` representation"
msgstr "`transparent` 表示"

#: src/type-layout.md:539
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.transparent.constraint-field\\] The `transparent` "
"representation can only be used on a [`struct`](items/structs.md) or an "
"[`enum`](items/enumerations.md) with a single variant that has:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.transparent.constraint-field\\] `transparent` 表示只能用于 "
"[`struct`](items/structs.md)，或用于具有单个变体的 [`enum`](items/"
"enumerations.md)，并且其具有："

#: src/type-layout.md:541
msgid ""
"any number of fields with size 0 and alignment 1 (e.g. [`PhantomData<T>`]"
"(special-types-and-traits.md#phantomdatat)), and"
msgstr ""
"任意数量大小为 0 且对齐为 1 的字段（例如 [`PhantomData<T>`](special-types-"
"and-traits.md#phantomdatat)），以及"

#: src/type-layout.md:542
msgid "at most one other field."
msgstr "至多一个其他字段。"

#: src/type-layout.md:544
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.transparent.layout-abi\\] Structs and enums with this "
"representation have the same layout and ABI as the only non-size 0 non-"
"alignment 1 field, if present, or unit otherwise."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.transparent.layout-abi\\] 具有此表示的 struct 和 enum，如果存"
"在唯一一个不属于大小 0 且对齐 1 的字段，则具有与该字段相同的布局和 ABI；否则"
"具有与单元类型相同的布局和 ABI。"

#: src/type-layout.md:547
msgid ""
"This is different than the `C` representation because a struct with the `C` "
"representation will always have the ABI of a `C` `struct` while, for "
"example, a struct with the `transparent` representation with a primitive "
"field will have the ABI of the primitive field."
msgstr ""
"这不同于 `C` 表示，因为具有 `C` 表示的 struct 总是具有 `C` `struct` 的 ABI；"
"而例如，具有 `transparent` 表示且包含原始字段的 struct 将具有该原始字段的 "
"ABI。"

#: src/type-layout.md:549
msgid ""
"r\\[layout.repr.transparent.constraint-exclusive\\] Because this "
"representation delegates type layout to another type, it cannot be used with "
"any other representation."
msgstr ""
"r\\[layout.repr.transparent.constraint-exclusive\\] 由于此表示将类型布局委托"
"给另一个类型，因此不能与任何其他表示一起使用。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:1
msgid "r\\[interior-mut\\]"
msgstr "r\\[interior-mut\\]"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[interior-mut.intro\\] Sometimes a type needs to be mutated while having "
"multiple aliases. In Rust this is achieved using a pattern called _interior "
"mutability_."
msgstr ""
"r\\[interior-mut.intro\\] 有时，一个类型需要在具有多个别名的同时被修改。在 "
"Rust 中，这是通过一种称为*内部可变性*的模式实现的。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[interior-mut.shared-ref\\] A type has interior mutability if its "
"internal state can be changed through a [shared reference](types/"
"pointer.md#shared-references-) to it."
msgstr ""
"r\\[interior-mut.shared-ref\\] 如果一个类型的内部状态可以通过指向它的[共享引"
"用](types/pointer.md#shared-references-) 来改变，则该类型具有内部可变性。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[interior-mut.no-constraint\\] This goes against the usual [requirement]"
"(behavior-considered-undefined.md) that the value pointed to by a shared "
"reference is not mutated."
msgstr ""
"r\\[interior-mut.no-constraint\\] 这违背了通常的[要求](behavior-considered-"
"undefined.md)：共享引用所指向的值不会被修改。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[interior-mut.unsafe-cell\\] \\[`std::cell::UnsafeCell<T>`\\] type is the "
"only allowed way to disable this requirement. When `UnsafeCell<T>` is "
"immutably aliased, it is still safe to mutate, or obtain a mutable reference "
"to, the `T` it contains."
msgstr ""
"r\\[interior-mut.unsafe-cell\\] \\[`std::cell::UnsafeCell<T>`\\] 类型是唯一允"
"许用来禁用此要求的方式。当 `UnsafeCell<T>` 被不可变地别名化时，修改其包含的 "
"`T`，或取得指向该 `T` 的可变引用，仍然是安全的。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[interior-mut.mut-unsafe-cell\\] As with all other types, it is undefined "
"behavior to have multiple `&mut UnsafeCell<T>` aliases."
msgstr ""
"r\\[interior-mut.mut-unsafe-cell\\] 与所有其他类型一样，拥有多个 `&mut "
"UnsafeCell<T>` 别名是未定义行为。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:19
msgid ""
"r\\[interior-mut.abstraction\\] Other types with interior mutability can be "
"created by using `UnsafeCell<T>` as a field. The standard library provides a "
"variety of types that provide safe interior mutability APIs."
msgstr ""
"r\\[interior-mut.abstraction\\] 可以通过将 `UnsafeCell<T>` 用作字段来创建其他"
"具有内部可变性的类型。标准库提供了多种提供安全内部可变性 API 的类型。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:22
msgid ""
"r\\[interior-mut.ref-cell\\] For example, \\[`std::cell::RefCell<T>`\\] uses "
"run-time borrow checks to ensure the usual rules around multiple references."
msgstr ""
"r\\[interior-mut.ref-cell\\] 例如，\\[`std::cell::RefCell<T>`\\] 使用运行时借"
"用检查来确保关于多个引用的通常规则。"

#: src/interior-mutability.md:25
msgid ""
"r\\[interior-mut.atomic\\] The \\[`std::sync::atomic`\\] module contains "
"types that wrap a value that is only accessed with atomic operations, "
"allowing the value to be shared and mutated across threads."
msgstr ""
"r\\[interior-mut.atomic\\] \\[`std::sync::atomic`\\] 模块包含一些类型，它们包"
"装只能通过原子操作访问的值，从而允许该值在线程之间共享和修改。"

#: src/subtyping.md:1
msgid "r\\[subtype\\]"
msgstr "r\\[subtype\\]"

#: src/subtyping.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[subtype.intro\\] Subtyping is implicit and can occur at any stage in "
"type checking or inference."
msgstr ""
"r\\[subtype.intro\\] 子类型化是隐式的，可以发生在类型检查或推断的任何阶段。"

#: src/subtyping.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[subtype.kinds\\] Subtyping is restricted to two cases: variance with "
"respect to lifetimes and between types with higher ranked lifetimes. If we "
"were to erase lifetimes from types, then the only subtyping would be due to "
"type equality."
msgstr ""
"r\\[subtype.kinds\\] 子类型化仅限于两种情况：关于生命周期的型变，以及具有高阶"
"生命周期的类型之间的子类型化。如果从类型中擦除生命周期，那么唯一的子类型化将"
"来自类型相等。"

#: src/subtyping.md:10
msgid ""
"Consider the following example: string literals always have `'static` "
"lifetime. Nevertheless, we can assign `s` to `t`:"
msgstr ""
"考虑以下示例：字符串字面量始终具有 `'static` 生命周期。尽管如此，我们仍可以"
"将 `s` 赋给 `t`："

#: src/subtyping.md:14
msgid "\"hi\""
msgstr "\"hi\""

#: src/subtyping.md:19
msgid ""
"Since `'static` outlives the lifetime parameter `'a`, `&'static str` is a "
"subtype of `&'a str`."
msgstr ""
"由于 `'static` 比生命周期参数 `'a` 存活得更久，`&'static str` 是 `&'a str` 的"
"子类型。"

#: src/subtyping.md:21
msgid ""
"r\\[subtype.higher-ranked\\] [Higher-ranked](../nomicon/hrtb.html) [function "
"pointers](types/function-pointer.md) and [trait objects](types/trait-"
"object.md) have another subtype relation. They are subtypes of types that "
"are given by substitutions of the higher-ranked lifetimes. Some examples:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[subtype.higher-ranked\\] [高阶](../nomicon/hrtb.html)[函数指针](types/"
"function-pointer.md)和 [trait 对象](types/trait-object.md)具有另一种子类型关"
"系。它们是由替换高阶生命周期所给出的类型的子类型。一些示例："

#: src/subtyping.md:25
msgid "// Here 'a is substituted for 'static\n"
msgstr "// 这里用 'a 替换 'static\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:28
msgid "// This works similarly for trait objects\n"
msgstr "// 对 trait 对象也类似\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:32
msgid "// We can also substitute one higher-ranked lifetime for another\n"
msgstr "// 我们也可以用一个高阶生命周期替换另一个\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:38
msgid "r\\[subtyping.variance\\]"
msgstr "r\\[subtyping.variance\\]"

#: src/subtyping.md:39
msgid "Variance"
msgstr "型变"

#: src/subtyping.md:41
msgid ""
"r\\[subtyping.variance.intro\\] Variance is a property that generic types "
"have with respect to their arguments. A generic type's _variance_ in a "
"parameter is how the subtyping of the parameter affects the subtyping of the "
"type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[subtyping.variance.intro\\] 型变是泛型类型相对于其实参所具有的属性。泛型"
"类型在某个参数上的 *型变*，表示该参数的子类型化如何影响该类型的子类型化。"

#: src/subtyping.md:44
msgid "r\\[subtyping.variance.covariant\\]"
msgstr "r\\[subtyping.variance.covariant\\]"

#: src/subtyping.md:45
msgid ""
"`F<T>` is _covariant_ over `T` if `T` being a subtype of `U` implies that "
"`F<T>` is a subtype of `F<U>` (subtyping \"passes through\")"
msgstr ""
"如果 `T` 是 `U` 的子类型会推出 `F<T>` 是 `F<U>` 的子类型，则 `F<T>` 对 `T` 是"
"*协变* 的（子类型化“传递通过”）"

#: src/subtyping.md:47
msgid "r\\[subtyping.variance.contravariant\\]"
msgstr "r\\[subtyping.variance.contravariant\\]"

#: src/subtyping.md:48
msgid ""
"`F<T>` is _contravariant_ over `T` if `T` being a subtype of `U` implies "
"that `F<U>` is a subtype of `F<T>`"
msgstr ""
"如果 `T` 是 `U` 的子类型会推出 `F<U>` 是 `F<T>` 的子类型，则 `F<T>` 对 `T` 是"
"*逆变* 的"

#: src/subtyping.md:50
msgid "r\\[subtyping.variance.invariant\\]"
msgstr "r\\[subtyping.variance.invariant\\]"

#: src/subtyping.md:51
msgid ""
"`F<T>` is _invariant_ over `T` otherwise (no subtyping relation can be "
"derived)"
msgstr "否则，`F<T>` 对 `T` 是 *不变* 的（无法导出子类型关系）"

#: src/subtyping.md:53
msgid ""
"r\\[subtyping.variance.builtin-types\\] Variance of types is automatically "
"determined as follows"
msgstr "r\\[subtyping.variance.builtin-types\\] 类型的型变按如下方式自动确定"

#: src/subtyping.md:56
msgid "Variance in `'a`"
msgstr "在 `'a` 上的型变"

#: src/subtyping.md:56
msgid "Variance in `T`"
msgstr "在 `T` 上的型变"

#: src/subtyping.md:58
msgid "`&'a T`"
msgstr "`&'a T`"

#: src/subtyping.md:58 src/subtyping.md:59 src/subtyping.md:60
#: src/subtyping.md:62 src/subtyping.md:63 src/subtyping.md:66
#: src/subtyping.md:67
msgid "covariant"
msgstr "协变"

#: src/subtyping.md:59
msgid "`&'a mut T`"
msgstr "`&'a mut T`"

#: src/subtyping.md:59 src/subtyping.md:61 src/subtyping.md:65
#: src/subtyping.md:67
msgid "invariant"
msgstr "不变"

#: src/subtyping.md:60 src/type-coercions.md:159
msgid "`*const T`"
msgstr "`*const T`"

#: src/subtyping.md:61 src/type-coercions.md:160
msgid "`*mut T`"
msgstr "`*mut T`"

#: src/subtyping.md:62
msgid "`[T]` and `[T; n]`"
msgstr "`[T]` 和 `[T; n]`"

#: src/subtyping.md:63
msgid "`fn() -> T`"
msgstr "`fn() -> T`"

#: src/subtyping.md:64
msgid "`fn(T) -> ()`"
msgstr "`fn(T) -> ()`"

#: src/subtyping.md:64
msgid "contravariant"
msgstr "逆变"

#: src/subtyping.md:65
msgid "`std::cell::UnsafeCell<T>`"
msgstr "`std::cell::UnsafeCell<T>`"

#: src/subtyping.md:66
msgid "`std::marker::PhantomData<T>`"
msgstr "`std::marker::PhantomData<T>`"

#: src/subtyping.md:67
msgid "`dyn Trait<T> + 'a`"
msgstr "`dyn Trait<T> + 'a`"

#: src/subtyping.md:69
msgid ""
"r\\[subtyping.variance.user-composite-types\\] The variance of other "
"`struct`, `enum`, and `union` types is decided by looking at the variance of "
"the types of their fields. If the parameter is used in positions with "
"different variances then the parameter is invariant. For example the "
"following struct is covariant in `'a` and `T` and invariant in `'b`, `'c`, "
"and `U`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[subtyping.variance.user-composite-types\\] 其他 `struct`、`enum` 和 "
"`union` 类型的型变，通过查看其字段类型的型变来决定。如果参数被用在具有不同型"
"变的位置中，则该参数是不变的。例如，以下结构体在 `'a` 和 `T` 上是协变的，在 "
"`'b`、`'c` 和 `U` 上是不变的。"

#: src/subtyping.md:75
msgid ""
"// This makes `Variance` covariant in 'a, and would\n"
"                            // make it covariant in U, but U is used later\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这使 `Variance` 在 'a 上协变，并且本会使它\n"
"                            // 在 U 上协变，但 U 稍后还会被使用\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:77
msgid "// Covariant in T\n"
msgstr "// 在 T 上协变\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:78
msgid "// Invariant in 'b\n"
msgstr "// 在 'b 上不变\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:79
msgid "// Invariant in U, makes the whole struct invariant\n"
msgstr "// 在 U 上不变，使整个结构体不变\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:81
msgid ""
"// Both co- and contravariant, makes 'c invariant\n"
"                            // in the struct.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 同时协变和逆变，使 'c 在该结构体中\n"
"                            // 不变。\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:86
msgid ""
"r\\[subtyping.variance.builtin-composite-types\\] When used outside of an "
"`struct`, `enum`, or `union`, the variance for parameters is checked at each "
"location separately."
msgstr ""
"r\\[subtyping.variance.builtin-composite-types\\] 当在 `struct`、`enum` 或 "
"`union` 之外使用时，参数的型变会在每个位置分别检查。"

#: src/subtyping.md:92
msgid ""
"// 'long is used inside of a tuple in both a co- and invariant position.\n"
msgstr "// 'long 在元组内同时用于协变位置和不变位置。\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:95
msgid ""
"// As the variance at these positions is computed separately,\n"
"    // we can freely shrink 'long in the covariant position.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 由于这些位置上的型变是分别计算的，\n"
"    // 我们可以在协变位置自由缩短 'long。\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:101
msgid "// 'middle is used in both a co- and contravariant position.\n"
msgstr "// 'middle 同时用于协变位置和逆变位置。\n"

#: src/subtyping.md:104
msgid ""
"// As the variance at these positions is computed separately,\n"
"    // we can freely shrink 'middle in the covariant position\n"
"    // and extend it in the contravariant position.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 由于这些位置上的型变是分别计算的，\n"
"    // 我们可以在协变位置自由缩短 'middle，\n"
"    // 并在逆变位置扩展它。\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:1
msgid "r\\[bound\\]"
msgstr "r\\[bound\\]"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:4
msgid "r\\[bound.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[bound.syntax\\]"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:33
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.intro\\] [Trait](items/traits.md#trait-bounds) and lifetime bounds "
"provide a way for [generic items](items/generics.md) to restrict which types "
"and lifetimes are used as their parameters. Bounds can be provided on any "
"type in a [where clause](items/generics.md#where-clauses). There are also "
"shorter forms for certain common cases:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.intro\\] [Trait](items/traits.md#trait-bounds) 约束和生命周期约束为"
"[泛型项](items/generics.md)提供了一种方式，用于限制哪些类型和生命周期可用作其"
"参数。约束可以在 [where 子句](items/generics.md#where-clauses)中的任何类型上"
"给出。对于某些常见情况，也有较短的形式："

#: src/trait-bounds.md:36
msgid ""
"Bounds written after declaring a [generic parameter](items/generics.md): `fn "
"f<A: Copy>() {}` is the same as `fn f<A>() where A: Copy {}`."
msgstr ""
"写在声明[泛型形参](items/generics.md)之后的约束：`fn f<A: Copy>() {}` 与 `fn "
"f<A>() where A: Copy {}` 相同。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:37
msgid ""
"In trait declarations as [supertraits](items/traits.md#supertraits): `trait "
"Circle : Shape {}` is equivalent to `trait Circle where Self : Shape {}`."
msgstr ""
"在 trait 声明中作为 [supertrait](items/traits.md#supertraits)：`trait "
"Circle : Shape {}` 等价于 `trait Circle where Self : Shape {}`。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:38
msgid ""
"In trait declarations as bounds on [associated types](items/associated-"
"items.md#associated-types): `trait A { type B: Copy; }` is equivalent to "
"`trait A where Self::B: Copy { type B; }`."
msgstr ""
"在 trait 声明中作为[关联类型](items/associated-items.md#associated-types)上的"
"约束：`trait A { type B: Copy; }` 等价于 `trait A where Self::B: Copy { type "
"B; }`。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:40
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.satisfaction\\] Bounds on an item must be satisfied when using the "
"item. When type checking and borrow checking a generic item, the bounds can "
"be used to determine that a trait is implemented for a type. For example, "
"given `Ty: Trait`"
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.satisfaction\\] 使用某个项时，必须满足该项上的约束。在对泛型项进行"
"类型检查和借用检查时，可以使用这些约束来判定某个类型实现了某个 trait。例如，"
"给定 `Ty: Trait`"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:43
msgid ""
"In the body of a generic function, methods from `Trait` can be called on "
"`Ty` values. Likewise associated constants on the `Trait` can be used."
msgstr ""
"在泛型函数体中，可以在 `Ty` 值上调用来自 `Trait` 的方法。同样，也可以使用 "
"`Trait` 上的关联常量。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:44
msgid "Associated types from `Trait` can be used."
msgstr "可以使用来自 `Trait` 的关联类型。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:45
msgid ""
"Generic functions and types with a `T: Trait` bounds can be used with `Ty` "
"being used for `T`."
msgstr ""
"带有 `T: Trait` 约束的泛型函数和类型可以在以 `Ty` 作为 `T` 的情况下使用。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:55
msgid "// Can call method because T: Shape\n"
msgstr "// 可以调用方法，因为 T: Shape\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:60
msgid "// doesn't move sh because T: Copy\n"
msgstr "// 不会移动 sh，因为 T: Copy\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:61
msgid "// Can use generic function because T: Shape\n"
msgstr "// 可以使用泛型函数，因为 T: Shape\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:67
msgid "// Type Figure<U> is well-formed because U: Shape\n"
msgstr "// 类型 Figure<U> 是良构的，因为 U: Shape\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:70
msgid "\"Figure of two {}\""
msgstr "\"两个 {} 组成的 Figure\""

#: src/trait-bounds.md:71
msgid "// Can use associated function\n"
msgstr "// 可以使用关联函数\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:76
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.trivial\\] Bounds that don't use the item's parameters or [higher-"
"ranked lifetimes](#higher-ranked-trait-bounds) are checked when the item is "
"defined. It is an error for such a bound to be false."
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.trivial\\] 不使用该项的参数或[高阶生命周期](#higher-ranked-trait-"
"bounds)的约束，会在定义该项时被检查。这样的约束若为假，则是错误。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:79
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.special\\] \\[`Copy`\\], \\[`Clone`\\], and \\[`Sized`\\] bounds "
"are also checked for certain generic types when using the item, even if the "
"use does not provide a concrete type. It is an error to have `Copy` or "
"`Clone` as a bound on a mutable reference, [trait object](types/trait-"
"object.md), or [slice](types/slice.md). It is an error to have `Sized` as a "
"bound on a trait object or slice."
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.special\\] 使用该项时，对于某些泛型类型也会检查 \\[`Copy`\\]、\\"
"[`Clone`\\] 和 \\[`Sized`\\] 约束，即使该使用没有提供具体类型。在可变引用、"
"[trait 对象](types/trait-object.md)或[切片](types/slice.md)上以 `Copy` 或 "
"`Clone` 作为约束是错误的。在 trait 对象或切片上以 `Sized` 作为约束也是错误"
"的。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:86
msgid "// Error: `i32` is not an iterator\n"
msgstr "// 错误：`i32` 不是迭代器\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:87
msgid "// (at use) Error: the trait bound is not satisfied\n"
msgstr "// （使用时）错误：未满足 trait 约束\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:88
msgid "// (at use) Error: size cannot be known at compilation\n"
msgstr "// （使用时）错误：无法在编译时知道大小\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:95
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.trait-object\\] Trait and lifetime bounds are also used to name "
"[trait objects](types/trait-object.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.trait-object\\] Trait 约束和生命周期约束也用于命名 [trait 对象]"
"(types/trait-object.md)。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:98
msgid "r\\[bound.sized\\]"
msgstr "r\\[bound.sized\\]"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:99
msgid "`?Sized`"
msgstr "`?Sized`"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:101
msgid ""
"`?` is only used to relax the implicit \\[`Sized`\\] trait bound for [type "
"parameters](types/parameters.md) or [associated types](items/associated-"
"items.md#associated-types). `?Sized` may not be used as a bound for other "
"types."
msgstr ""
"`?` 只用于放宽[类型形参](types/parameters.md)或[关联类型](items/associated-"
"items.md#associated-types)的隐式 \\[`Sized`\\] trait 约束。`?Sized` 不得用作"
"其他类型的约束。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:103
msgid "r\\[bound.lifetime\\]"
msgstr "r\\[bound.lifetime\\]"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:104
msgid "Lifetime bounds"
msgstr "生命周期约束"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:106
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.lifetime.intro\\] Lifetime bounds can be applied to types or to "
"other lifetimes."
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.lifetime.intro\\] 生命周期约束可以应用于类型，也可以应用于其他生命"
"周期。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:109
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.lifetime.outlive-lifetime\\] The bound `'a: 'b` is usually read as "
"`'a` _outlives_ `'b`. `'a: 'b` means that `'a` lasts at least as long as "
"`'b`, so a reference `&'a ()` is valid whenever `&'b ()` is valid."
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.lifetime.outlive-lifetime\\] 约束 `'a: 'b` 通常读作 `'a` "
"_outlives_ `'b`。`'a: 'b` 表示 `'a` 至少与 `'b` 一样长，因此只要 `&'b ()` 有"
"效，引用 `&'a ()` 就有效。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:114
msgid "// &'a i32 is a subtype of &'b i32 because 'a: 'b\n"
msgstr "// &'a i32 是 &'b i32 的子类型，因为 'a: 'b\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:115
msgid "// &'b &'a i32 is well formed because 'a: 'b\n"
msgstr "// &'b &'a i32 是良构的，因为 'a: 'b\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:119
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.lifetime.outlive-type\\] `T: 'a` means that all lifetime "
"parameters of `T` outlive `'a`. For example, if `'a` is an unconstrained "
"lifetime parameter, then `i32: 'static` and `&'static str: 'a` are "
"satisfied, but `Vec<&'a ()>: 'static` is not."
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.lifetime.outlive-type\\] `T: 'a` 表示 `T` 的所有生命周期参数都至少"
"与 `'a` 一样长。例如，如果 `'a` 是一个未受约束的生命周期参数，那么 `i32: "
"'static` 和 `&'static str: 'a` 得到满足，但 `Vec<&'a ()>: 'static` 不满足。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:122
msgid "r\\[bound.higher-ranked\\]"
msgstr "r\\[bound.higher-ranked\\]"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:123
msgid "Higher-ranked trait bounds"
msgstr "高阶 trait 约束"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:125
msgid "r\\[bound.higher-ranked.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[bound.higher-ranked.syntax\\]"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:130
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.higher-ranked.intro\\] Trait bounds may be _higher ranked_ over "
"lifetimes. These bounds specify a bound that is true _for all_ lifetimes. "
"For example, a bound such as `for<'a> &'a T: PartialEq<i32>` would require "
"an implementation like"
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.higher-ranked.intro\\] Trait 约束可以在生命周期上是*高阶*的。这些约"
"束指定了对*所有*生命周期都为真的约束。例如，像 `for<'a> &'a T: "
"PartialEq<i32>` 这样的约束会要求有如下实现"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:141
msgid ""
"and could then be used to compare a `&'a T` with any lifetime to an `i32`."
msgstr "然后可用于将具有任意生命周期的 `&'a T` 与 `i32` 进行比较。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:143
msgid ""
"Only a higher-ranked bound can be used here, because the lifetime of the "
"reference is shorter than any possible lifetime parameter on the function:"
msgstr ""
"这里只能使用高阶约束，因为该引用的生命周期短于函数上任何可能的生命周期参数："

#: src/trait-bounds.md:152
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.higher-ranked.trait\\] Higher-ranked lifetimes may also be "
"specified just before the trait: the only difference is the [scope](names/"
"scopes.md#higher-ranked-trait-bound-scopes) of the lifetime parameter, which "
"extends only to the end of the following trait instead of the whole bound. "
"This function is equivalent to the last one."
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.higher-ranked.trait\\] 高阶生命周期也可以正好指定在 trait 之前：唯"
"一的区别是生命周期参数的[作用域](names/scopes.md#higher-ranked-trait-bound-"
"scopes)，它只延伸到后续 trait 的末尾，而不是整个约束的末尾。此函数等价于上一"
"个函数。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:162
msgid "r\\[bound.implied\\]"
msgstr "r\\[bound.implied\\]"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:163
msgid "Implied bounds"
msgstr "隐含约束"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:165
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.implied.intro\\] Lifetime bounds required for types to be well-"
"formed are sometimes inferred."
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.implied.intro\\] 类型成为良构类型所需的生命周期约束有时会被推断出"
"来。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:172
msgid ""
"The type parameter `T` is required to outlive `'a` for the type `&'a T` to "
"be well-formed. This is inferred because the function signature contains the "
"type `&'a T` which is only valid if `T: 'a` holds."
msgstr ""
"为了使类型 `&'a T` 成为良构类型，类型参数 `T` 必须至少与 `'a` 一样长。这会被"
"推断出来，因为函数签名包含类型 `&'a T`，而该类型只有在 `T: 'a` 成立时才有效。"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:174
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.implied.context\\] Implied bounds are added for all parameters and "
"outputs of functions. Inside of `requires_t_outlives_a` you can assume `T: "
"'a` to hold even if you don't explicitly specify this:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.implied.context\\] 隐含约束会为函数的所有参数和输出添加。在 "
"`requires_t_outlives_a` 内部，即使没有显式指定这一点，也可以假定 `T: 'a` 成"
"立："

#: src/trait-bounds.md:181
msgid ""
"// This compiles, because `T: 'a` is implied by\n"
"    // the reference type `&'a T`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这可以编译，因为 `T: 'a` 由\n"
"    // 引用类型 `&'a T` 隐含。\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:190
msgid ""
"// This errors, because `T: 'a` is not implied by\n"
"    // the function signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会出错，因为 `T: 'a` 并不由\n"
"    // 函数签名隐含。\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:196
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.implied.trait\\] Only lifetime bounds are implied, trait bounds "
"still have to be explicitly added. The following example therefore causes an "
"error:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.implied.trait\\] 只有生命周期约束会被隐含，trait 约束仍然必须显式添"
"加。因此，下面的示例会导致错误："

#: src/trait-bounds.md:201
msgid "// error[E0277]: `T` doesn't implement `Debug`\n"
msgstr "// error[E0277]：`T` 未实现 `Debug`\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:206
msgid ""
"r\\[bound.implied.def\\] Lifetime bounds are also inferred for type "
"definitions and impl blocks for any type:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[bound.implied.def\\] 也会为类型定义以及任何类型的 impl 块推断生命周期约"
"束："

#: src/trait-bounds.md:211
msgid ""
"// This requires `T: 'a` to be well-formed\n"
"    // which is inferred by the compiler.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这要求满足 `T: 'a`，该类型才是良构的，\n"
"    // 这一点由编译器推断。\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:217
msgid ""
"// This requires `T: 'a` to be well-formed,\n"
"    // which is inferred by the compiler.\n"
"    //\n"
"    // Note that `T: 'a` is required even when only\n"
"    // using `Enum::OtherVariant`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这要求满足 `T: 'a`，该类型才是良构的，\n"
"    // 这一点由编译器推断。\n"
"    //\n"
"    // 注意，即使只使用 `Enum::OtherVariant`，\n"
"    // 也要求 `T: 'a`。\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:227
msgid ""
"// This would error because `T: 'a` is not implied by any type\n"
"// in the impl header.\n"
"//     impl<'a, T> Trait<'a, T> for () {}\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这会出错，因为 `T: 'a` 不由 impl 头部中的\n"
"// 任何类型隐含。\n"
"//     impl<'a, T> Trait<'a, T> for () {}\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:231
msgid "// This compiles as `T: 'a` is implied by the self type `&'a T`.\n"
msgstr "// 这可以编译，因为 `T: 'a` 由 self 类型 `&'a T` 隐含。\n"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:236
msgid "r\\[bound.use\\]"
msgstr "r\\[bound.use\\]"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:237
msgid "Use bounds"
msgstr "Use 约束"

#: src/trait-bounds.md:239
msgid ""
"Certain bounds lists may include a `use<..>` bound to control which generic "
"parameters are captured by the `impl Trait` [abstract return type](types/"
"impl-trait.md#abstract-return-types).  See [precise capturing](types/impl-"
"trait.md#precise-capturing) for more details."
msgstr ""
"某些约束列表可以包含 `use<..>` 约束，用于控制哪些泛型参数会被 `impl Trait` "
"[抽象返回类型](types/impl-trait.md#abstract-return-types)捕获。更多细节请参见"
"[精确捕获](types/impl-trait.md#precise-capturing)。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:1
msgid "r\\[coerce\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.intro\\] **Type coercions** are implicit operations that change "
"the type of a value. They happen automatically at specific locations and are "
"highly restricted in what types actually coerce."
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.intro\\] **类型强制转换**是改变值的类型的隐式操作。它们会在特定位"
"置自动发生，并且对于实际可强制转换的类型有很严格的限制。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.as\\] Any conversions allowed by coercion can also be explicitly "
"performed by the [type cast operator](expressions/operator-expr.md#type-cast-"
"expressions), `as`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.as\\] 任何可由强制转换允许的转换，也都可以通过[类型转换运算符]"
"(expressions/operator-expr.md#type-cast-expressions) `as` 显式执行。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:10
msgid ""
"Coercions are originally defined in [RFC 401](https://github.com/rust-lang/"
"rfcs/blob/master/text/0401-coercions.md) and expanded upon in [RFC 1558]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/1558-closure-to-fn-"
"coercion.md)."
msgstr ""
"强制转换最初在 [RFC 401](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/"
"0401-coercions.md) 中定义，并在 [RFC 1558](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/"
"blob/master/text/1558-closure-to-fn-coercion.md) 中得到扩展。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:12
msgid "r\\[coerce.site\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:13
msgid "Coercion sites"
msgstr "强制转换位置"

#: src/type-coercions.md:15
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.site.intro\\] A coercion can only occur at certain coercion sites "
"in a program; these are typically places where the desired type is explicit "
"or can be derived by propagation from explicit types (without type "
"inference). Possible coercion sites are:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.site.intro\\] 强制转换只能发生在程序中的某些强制转换位置；这些位置"
"通常是期望类型显式给出，或可以从显式类型传播推导出来（不经过类型推断）的地"
"方。可能的强制转换位置包括："

#: src/type-coercions.md:18
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.let\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.let\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:19
msgid "`let` statements where an explicit type is given."
msgstr "给出了显式类型的 `let` 语句。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:21 src/type-coercions.md:35 src/type-coercions.md:50
msgid "For example, `&mut 42` is coerced to have type `&i8` in the following:"
msgstr "例如，在下面的代码中，`&mut 42` 被强制转换为类型 `&i8`："

#: src/type-coercions.md:27
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.value\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.value\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:28
msgid "`static` and `const` item declarations (similar to `let` statements)."
msgstr "`static` 和 `const` 项声明（类似于 `let` 语句）。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:30
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.argument\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.argument\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:31
msgid "Arguments for function calls"
msgstr "函数调用的实参"

#: src/type-coercions.md:33
msgid ""
"The value being coerced is the actual parameter, and it is coerced to the "
"type of the formal parameter."
msgstr "被强制转换的值是实际参数，它会被强制转换为形式参数的类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:45
msgid ""
"For method calls, the receiver (`self` parameter) type is coerced "
"differently, see the documentation on [method-call expressions](expressions/"
"method-call-expr.md) for details."
msgstr ""
"对于方法调用，接收者（`self` 参数）的类型会以不同方式强制转换；详情见[方法调"
"用表达式](expressions/method-call-expr.md)的文档。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:47
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.constructor\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.constructor\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:48
msgid "Instantiations of struct, union, or enum variant fields"
msgstr "结构体、联合体或枚举变体字段的实例化"

#: src/type-coercions.md:60
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.return\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.return\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:61
msgid ""
"Function results—either the final line of a block if it is not semicolon-"
"terminated or any expression in a `return` statement"
msgstr ""
"函数结果，即块中未以分号结束时的最后一行，或 `return` 语句中的任何表达式"

#: src/type-coercions.md:63
msgid ""
"For example, `x` is coerced to have type `&dyn Display` in the following:"
msgstr "例如，在下面的代码中，`x` 被强制转换为类型 `&dyn Display`："

#: src/type-coercions.md:72
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.assignment\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.assignment\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:73
msgid "Assigned value operands in assignment expressions"
msgstr "赋值表达式中被赋的值操作数"

#: src/type-coercions.md:75
msgid "For example, `y` is coerced to have type `&i8` in the following:"
msgstr "例如，在下面的代码中，`y` 被强制转换为类型 `&i8`："

#: src/type-coercions.md:82
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.site.subexpr\\] If the expression in one of these coercion sites "
"is a coercion-propagating expression, then the relevant sub-expressions in "
"that expression are also coercion sites. Propagation recurses from these new "
"coercion sites. Propagating expressions and their relevant sub-expressions "
"are:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.site.subexpr\\] 如果这些强制转换位置之一中的表达式是会传播强制转换"
"的表达式，那么该表达式中的相关子表达式也会成为强制转换位置。传播会从这些新的"
"强制转换位置递归进行。会传播的表达式及其相关子表达式如下："

#: src/type-coercions.md:85
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.array\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.array\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:86
msgid ""
"Array literals, where the array has type `[U; n]`. Each sub-expression in "
"the array literal is a coercion site for coercion to type `U`."
msgstr ""
"数组字面量，其中数组具有类型 `[U; n]`。数组字面量中的每个子表达式都是强制转换"
"到类型 `U` 的强制转换位置。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:88
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.repeat\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.repeat\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:89
msgid ""
"Array literals with repeating syntax, where the array has type `[U; n]`. The "
"repeated sub-expression is a coercion site for coercion to type `U`."
msgstr ""
"带有重复语法的数组字面量，其中数组具有类型 `[U; n]`。被重复的子表达式是强制转"
"换到类型 `U` 的强制转换位置。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:91
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.tuple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.tuple\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:92
msgid ""
"Tuples, where a tuple is a coercion site to type `(U_0, U_1, ..., U_n)`. "
"Each sub-expression is a coercion site to the respective type, e.g. the "
"zeroth sub-expression is a coercion site to type `U_0`."
msgstr ""
"元组，其中元组是强制转换到类型 `(U_0, U_1, ..., U_n)` 的强制转换位置。每个子"
"表达式都是强制转换到对应类型的强制转换位置，例如第零个子表达式是强制转换到类"
"型 `U_0` 的强制转换位置。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:94
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.parenthesis\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.parenthesis\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:95
msgid ""
"Parenthesized sub-expressions (`(e)`): if the expression has type `U`, then "
"the sub-expression is a coercion site to `U`."
msgstr ""
"带括号的子表达式（`(e)`）：如果表达式具有类型 `U`，则该子表达式是强制转换到 "
"`U` 的强制转换位置。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:97
msgid "r\\[coerce.site.block\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.site.block\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:98
msgid ""
"Blocks: if a block has type `U`, then the last expression in the block (if "
"it is not semicolon-terminated) is a coercion site to `U`. This includes "
"blocks which are part of control flow statements, such as `if`/`else`, if "
"the block has a known type."
msgstr ""
"块：如果块具有类型 `U`，则块中的最后一个表达式（如果它未以分号结束）是强制转"
"换到 `U` 的强制转换位置。如果作为控制流语句一部分的块具有已知类型，这也包括例"
"如 `if`/`else` 中的块。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:100
msgid "r\\[coerce.types\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:101
msgid "Coercion types"
msgstr "强制转换类型"

#: src/type-coercions.md:103
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.types.intro\\] Coercion is allowed between the following types:"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.intro\\] 下列类型之间允许强制转换："

#: src/type-coercions.md:106
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.reflexive\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.reflexive\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:107
msgid ""
"`T` to `U` if `T` is a [subtype](subtyping.md) of `U` (_reflexive case_)"
msgstr ""
"如果 `T` 是 `U` 的[子类型](subtyping.md)，则从 `T` 到 `U`（*自反情形*）"

#: src/type-coercions.md:109
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.transitive\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.transitive\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:110
msgid ""
"`T_1` to `T_3` where `T_1` coerces to `T_2` and `T_2` coerces to `T_3` "
"(_transitive case_)"
msgstr ""
"从 `T_1` 到 `T_3`，其中 `T_1` 强制转换到 `T_2`，且 `T_2` 强制转换到 `T_3`（*"
"传递情形*）"

#: src/type-coercions.md:112
msgid "Note that this is not fully supported yet."
msgstr "注意，这尚未得到完全支持。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:114
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.mut-reborrow\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.mut-reborrow\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:115
msgid "`&mut T` to `&T`"
msgstr "从 `&mut T` 到 `&T`"

#: src/type-coercions.md:117
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.mut-pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.mut-pointer\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:118
msgid "`*mut T` to `*const T`"
msgstr "从 `*mut T` 到 `*const T`"

#: src/type-coercions.md:120
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.ref-to-pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.ref-to-pointer\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:121
msgid "`&T` to `*const T`"
msgstr "从 `&T` 到 `*const T`"

#: src/type-coercions.md:123
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.mut-to-pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.mut-to-pointer\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:124
msgid "`&mut T` to `*mut T`"
msgstr "从 `&mut T` 到 `*mut T`"

#: src/type-coercions.md:126
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.deref\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.deref\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:127
msgid ""
"`&T` or `&mut T` to `&U` if `T` implements `Deref<Target = U>`. For example:"
msgstr ""
"如果 `T` 实现了 `Deref<Target = U>`，则从 `&T` 或 `&mut T` 到 `&U`。例如："

#: src/type-coercions.md:147
msgid "'y'"
msgstr "'y'"

#: src/type-coercions.md:148
msgid "//&mut CharContainer is coerced to &char.\n"
msgstr "//&mut CharContainer 被强制转换为 &char。\n"

#: src/type-coercions.md:152
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.deref-mut\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.deref-mut\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:153
msgid "`&mut T` to `&mut U` if `T` implements `DerefMut<Target = U>`."
msgstr "如果 `T` 实现了 `DerefMut<Target = U>`，则从 `&mut T` 到 `&mut U`。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:155
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.unsize\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.unsize\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:156
msgid "TyCtor(`T`) to TyCtor(`U`), where TyCtor(`T`) is one of"
msgstr "从 TyCtor(`T`) 到 TyCtor(`U`)，其中 TyCtor(`T`) 是下列之一："

#: src/type-coercions.md:157
msgid "`&T`"
msgstr "`&T`"

#: src/type-coercions.md:158
msgid "`&mut T`"
msgstr "`&mut T`"

#: src/type-coercions.md:161 src/special-types-and-traits.md:8
msgid "`Box<T>`"
msgstr "`Box<T>`"

#: src/type-coercions.md:163
msgid ""
"and where `U` can be obtained from `T` by [unsized coercion](#unsized-"
"coercions)."
msgstr "且其中 `U` 可以通过[非定长强制转换](#unsized-coercions)从 `T` 获得。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:169
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.fn\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.fn\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:170
msgid "Function item types to `fn` pointers"
msgstr "函数项类型到 `fn` 指针"

#: src/type-coercions.md:172
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.closure\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.closure\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:173
msgid "Non capturing closures to `fn` pointers"
msgstr "非捕获闭包到 `fn` 指针"

#: src/type-coercions.md:175
msgid "r\\[coerce.types.never\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.types.never\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:176
msgid "`!` to any `T`"
msgstr "`!` 到任意 `T`"

#: src/type-coercions.md:178
msgid "r\\[coerce.unsize\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.unsize\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:179
msgid "Unsized coercions"
msgstr "非定长强制转换"

#: src/type-coercions.md:181
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.unsize.intro\\] The following coercions are called `unsized "
"coercions`, since they relate to converting types to unsized types, and are "
"permitted in a few cases where other coercions are not, as described above. "
"They can still happen anywhere else a coercion can occur."
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.unsize.intro\\] 以下强制转换称为 `unsized coercions`（非定长强制转"
"换），因为它们涉及将类型转换为非定长类型，并且如上所述，在少数其他强制转换不"
"被允许的情形中也被允许。它们仍然可以在强制转换可以发生的其他任何位置发生。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:184
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.unsize.trait\\] Two traits, [`Unsize`](std::marker::Unsize) and "
"[`CoerceUnsized`](std::ops::CoerceUnsized), are used to assist in this "
"process and expose it for library use. The following coercions are built-ins "
"and, if `T` can be coerced to `U` with one of them, then an implementation "
"of `Unsize<U>` for `T` will be provided:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.unsize.trait\\] 两个 trait，[`Unsize`](std::marker::Unsize) 和 "
"[`CoerceUnsized`](std::ops::CoerceUnsized)，用于辅助这一过程，并将其暴露给库"
"使用。以下强制转换是内建的；如果 `T` 可以通过其中之一强制转换为 `U`，则会为 "
"`T` 提供 `Unsize<U>` 的实现："

#: src/type-coercions.md:187
msgid "r\\[coerce.unsize.slice\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.unsize.slice\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:188
msgid "`[T; n]` to `[T]`."
msgstr "`[T; n]` 到 `[T]`。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:190
msgid "r\\[coerce.unsize.trait-object\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.unsize.trait-object\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:191
msgid ""
"`T` to `dyn U`, when `T` implements `U + Sized`, and `U` is [dyn compatible]"
"(items/traits.md#dyn-compatibility)."
msgstr ""
"当 `T` 实现 `U + Sized`，且 `U` 是 [dyn 兼容](items/traits.md#dyn-"
"compatibility)的，则 `T` 到 `dyn U`。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:193
msgid "r\\[coerce.unsize.trait-upcast\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.unsize.trait-upcast\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:194
msgid ""
"`dyn T` to `dyn U`, when `U` is one of `T`'s [supertraits](items/"
"traits.md#supertraits)."
msgstr ""
"当 `U` 是 `T` 的[父 trait](items/traits.md#supertraits) 之一时，`dyn T` 到 "
"`dyn U`。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:195
msgid ""
"This allows dropping auto traits, i.e. `dyn T + Auto` to `dyn U` is allowed."
msgstr "这允许丢弃 auto trait，即允许从 `dyn T + Auto` 到 `dyn U` 的强制转换。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:196
msgid ""
"This allows adding auto traits if the principal trait has the auto trait as "
"a super trait, i.e. given `trait T: U + Send {}`, `dyn T` to `dyn T + Send` "
"or to `dyn U + Send` coercions are allowed."
msgstr ""
"如果主 trait 将该 auto trait 作为父 trait，则这允许添加 auto trait，即给定 "
"`trait T: U + Send {}`，允许从 `dyn T` 到 `dyn T + Send` 或到 `dyn U + Send` "
"的强制转换。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:198
msgid "r\\[coerce.unsized.composite\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.unsized.composite\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:199
msgid "`Foo<..., T, ...>` to `Foo<..., U, ...>`, when:"
msgstr "在满足以下条件时，`Foo<..., T, ...>` 到 `Foo<..., U, ...>`："

#: src/type-coercions.md:200
msgid "`Foo` is a struct."
msgstr "`Foo` 是一个结构体。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:201
msgid "`T` implements `Unsize<U>`."
msgstr "`T` 实现 `Unsize<U>`。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:202
msgid "The last field of `Foo` has a type involving `T`."
msgstr "`Foo` 的最后一个字段具有涉及 `T` 的类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:203
msgid ""
"If that field has type `Bar<T>`, then `Bar<T>` implements `Unsize<Bar<U>>`."
msgstr "如果该字段的类型为 `Bar<T>`，则 `Bar<T>` 实现 `Unsize<Bar<U>>`。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:204
msgid "T is not part of the type of any other fields."
msgstr "T 不是任何其他字段类型的一部分。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:206
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.unsized.pointer\\] Additionally, a type `Foo<T>` can implement "
"`CoerceUnsized<Foo<U>>` when `T` implements `Unsize<U>` or "
"`CoerceUnsized<Foo<U>>`. This allows it to provide an unsized coercion to "
"`Foo<U>`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.unsized.pointer\\] 此外，当 `T` 实现 `Unsize<U>` 或 "
"`CoerceUnsized<Foo<U>>` 时，类型 `Foo<T>` 可以实现 `CoerceUnsized<Foo<U>>`。"
"这允许它提供到 `Foo<U>` 的非定长强制转换。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:209
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] While the definition of the unsized coercions and their "
"implementation has been stabilized, the traits themselves are not yet stable "
"and therefore can't be used directly in stable Rust."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 虽然非定长强制转换的定义及其实现已经稳定，但这些 trait 本身尚未稳"
"定，因此不能在 stable Rust 中直接使用。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:212
msgid "r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:213
msgid "Least upper bound coercions"
msgstr "最小上界强制转换"

#: src/type-coercions.md:215
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.intro\\] In some contexts, the compiler must "
"coerce together multiple types to try and find the most general type. This "
"is called a \"Least Upper Bound\" coercion. LUB coercion is used and only "
"used in the following situations:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.intro\\] 在某些上下文中，编译器必须将多个类型共"
"同强制转换，以尝试寻找最通用的类型。这称为“最小上界”（Least Upper Bound）强制"
"转换。LUB 强制转换仅在以下情形中使用："

#: src/type-coercions.md:218
msgid "To find the common type for a series of if branches."
msgstr "为一系列 if 分支寻找共同类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:219
msgid "To find the common type for a series of match arms."
msgstr "为一系列 match 分支寻找共同类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:220
msgid "To find the common type for array elements."
msgstr "为数组元素寻找共同类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:221
msgid ""
"To find the common type for a [labeled block expression](expr.loop.block-"
"labels) among the break operands and the final block operand."
msgstr ""
"为[带标签块表达式](expr.loop.block-labels)在 break 操作数和最终块操作数之间寻"
"找共同类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:222
msgid ""
"To find the common type for an [`loop` expression with break expressions]"
"(expr.loop.break-value) among the break operands."
msgstr ""
"为[带 break 表达式的 `loop` 表达式](expr.loop.break-value)在各 break 操作数之"
"间寻找共同类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:223
msgid ""
"To find the type for the return type of a closure with multiple return "
"statements."
msgstr "为具有多个 return 语句的闭包的返回类型寻找类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:224
msgid ""
"To check the type for the return type of a function with multiple return "
"statements."
msgstr "为具有多个 return 语句的函数的返回类型检查类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:226
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.target\\] In each such case, there are a set of "
"types `T0..Tn` to be mutually coerced to some target type `T_t`, which is "
"unknown to start."
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.target\\] 在每一种这样的情形中，都有一组类型 "
"`T0..Tn` 需要相互强制转换到某个目标类型 `T_t`，而该目标类型起初是未知的。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:229
msgid ""
"r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.computation\\] Computing the LUB coercion is "
"done iteratively. The target type `T_t` begins as the type `T0`. For each "
"new type `Ti`, we consider whether"
msgstr ""
"r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.computation\\] LUB 强制转换的计算以迭代方式完"
"成。目标类型 `T_t` 初始为类型 `T0`。对于每个新类型 `Ti`，会考虑是否"

#: src/type-coercions.md:232
msgid "r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.computation-identity\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.computation-identity\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:233
msgid ""
"If `Ti` can be coerced to the current target type `T_t`, then no change is "
"made."
msgstr "如果 `Ti` 可以强制转换为当前目标类型 `T_t`，则不做更改。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:235
msgid "r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.computation-replace\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.computation-replace\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:236
msgid ""
"Otherwise, check whether `T_t` can be coerced to `Ti`; if so, the `T_t` is "
"changed to `Ti`. (This check is also conditioned on whether all of the "
"source expressions considered thus far have implicit coercions.)"
msgstr ""
"否则，检查 `T_t` 是否可以强制转换为 `Ti`；如果可以，则将 `T_t` 改为 `Ti`。"
"（此检查还以到目前为止所考虑的所有源表达式是否都有隐式强制转换为条件。）"

#: src/type-coercions.md:238
msgid "r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.computation-unify\\]"
msgstr "r\\[coerce.least-upper-bound.computation-unify\\]"

#: src/type-coercions.md:239
msgid ""
"If not, try to compute a mutual supertype of `T_t` and `Ti`, which will "
"become the new target type."
msgstr ""
"如果不可以，则尝试计算 `T_t` 和 `Ti` 的共同超类型，它将成为新的目标类型。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:244
msgid "// For if branches\n"
msgstr "// 对于 if 分支\n"

#: src/type-coercions.md:253
msgid "// For match arms\n"
msgstr "// 对于 match 分支\n"

#: src/type-coercions.md:260
msgid "// For array elements\n"
msgstr "// 对于数组元素\n"

#: src/type-coercions.md:263
msgid "// For closure with multiple return statements\n"
msgstr "// 对于带有多个 return 语句的闭包\n"

#: src/type-coercions.md:275
msgid "// For type checking of function with multiple return statements\n"
msgstr "// 用于对具有多个 return 语句的函数进行类型检查\n"

#: src/type-coercions.md:287
msgid ""
"In these examples, types of the `ba*` are found by LUB coercion. And the "
"compiler checks whether LUB coercion result of `a`, `b`, `c` is `i32` in the "
"processing of the function `foo`."
msgstr ""
"在这些示例中，`ba*` 的类型由 LUB 强制转换确定。并且在处理函数 `foo` 时，编译"
"器会检查 `a`、`b`、`c` 的 LUB 强制转换结果是否为 `i32`。"

#: src/type-coercions.md:289
msgid "Caveat"
msgstr "注意事项"

#: src/type-coercions.md:291
msgid ""
"This description is obviously informal. Making it more precise is expected "
"to proceed as part of a general effort to specify the Rust type checker more "
"precisely."
msgstr ""
"这一描述显然是非正式的。预计会将其进一步精确化，作为更精确地规定 Rust 类型检"
"查器这一整体工作的一部分。"

#: src/divergence.md:1
msgid "r\\[divergence\\]"
msgstr "r\\[divergence\\]"

#: src/divergence.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[divergence.intro\\] A _diverging expression_ is an expression that never "
"completes normal execution."
msgstr "r\\[divergence.intro\\] *发散表达式*是永远不会完成正常执行的表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:9
msgid "\"This function never returns!\""
msgstr "\"This function never returns!\""

#: src/divergence.md:13
msgid "// This line never completes.\n"
msgstr "// 这一行永不完成。\n"

#: src/divergence.md:14
msgid "\"This is never printed: {x}\""
msgstr "\"This is never printed: {x}\""

#: src/divergence.md:18
msgid "See the following rules for specific expression divergence behavior:"
msgstr "有关特定表达式发散行为，请参见以下规则："

#: src/divergence.md:20
msgid "\\[expr.block.diverging\\] --- Block expressions."
msgstr "\\[expr.block.diverging\\] --- 块表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:21
msgid "\\[expr.if.diverging\\] --- `if` expressions."
msgstr "\\[expr.if.diverging\\] --- `if` 表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:22
msgid ""
"\\[expr.loop.block-labels.type\\] --- Labeled block expressions with `break`."
msgstr "\\[expr.loop.block-labels.type\\] --- 带有 `break` 的带标签块表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:23
msgid ""
"\\[expr.loop.break-value.diverging\\] --- `loop` expressions with `break`."
msgstr ""
"\\[expr.loop.break-value.diverging\\] --- 带有 `break` 的 `loop` 表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:24
msgid "\\[expr.loop.break.diverging\\] --- `break` expressions."
msgstr "\\[expr.loop.break.diverging\\] --- `break` 表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:25
msgid "\\[expr.loop.continue.diverging\\] --- `continue` expressions."
msgstr "\\[expr.loop.continue.diverging\\] --- `continue` 表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:26
msgid "\\[expr.loop.infinite.diverging\\] --- Infinite `loop` expressions."
msgstr "\\[expr.loop.infinite.diverging\\] --- 无限 `loop` 表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:27
msgid "\\[expr.match.diverging\\] --- `match` expressions."
msgstr "\\[expr.match.diverging\\] --- `match` 表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:28
msgid "\\[expr.match.empty\\] --- Empty `match` expressions."
msgstr "\\[expr.match.empty\\] --- 空 `match` 表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:29
msgid "\\[expr.return.diverging\\] --- `return` expressions."
msgstr "\\[expr.return.diverging\\] --- `return` 表达式。"

#: src/divergence.md:30
msgid "\\[type.never.constraint\\] --- Function calls returning `!`."
msgstr "\\[type.never.constraint\\] --- 返回 `!` 的函数调用。"

#: src/divergence.md:32
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The \\[`panic!`\\] macro and related panic-generating macros "
"like \\[`unreachable!`\\] also have the type [`!`](type.never) and are "
"diverging."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] \\[`panic!`\\] 宏以及像 \\[`unreachable!`\\] 这样的相关 panic 生"
"成宏也具有 [`!`](type.never) 类型，并且是发散的。"

#: src/divergence.md:35
msgid ""
"r\\[divergence.never\\] Any expression of type [`!`](type.never) is a "
"diverging expression. However, diverging expressions are not limited to type "
"[`!`](type.never); expressions of other types may also diverge (e.g., "
"`Some(loop {})` has type `Option<!>`)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[divergence.never\\] 任何类型为 [`!`](type.never) 的表达式都是发散表达式。"
"不过，发散表达式并不限于类型 [`!`](type.never)；其他类型的表达式也可能发散"
"（例如，`Some(loop {})` 的类型是 `Option<!>`）。"

#: src/divergence.md:38
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Though `!` is considered an uninhabited type, a type being "
"uninhabited is not sufficient for it to diverge."
msgstr "\\[!NOTE\\] 虽然 `!` 被视为无值类型，但一个类型无值并不足以使其发散。"

#: src/divergence.md:47
msgid "// This has a type of `!`.\n"
msgstr "// 这具有 `!` 类型。\n"

#: src/divergence.md:48
msgid "// So, the entire function is considered diverging.\n"
msgstr "// 因此，整个函数被视为发散。\n"

#: src/divergence.md:50
msgid "// OK: The type of the body is `!` which matches the return type.\n"
msgstr "// OK：主体的类型是 `!`，与返回类型匹配。\n"

#: src/divergence.md:53
