#: src/destructors.md:349
msgid "r\\[destructors.scope.operands\\]"
msgstr "r\\[destructors.scope.operands\\]"

#: src/destructors.md:350
msgid "Operands"
msgstr "操作数"

#: src/destructors.md:352
msgid ""
"Temporaries are also created to hold the result of operands to an expression "
"while the other operands are evaluated. The temporaries are associated to "
"the scope of the expression with that operand. Since the temporaries are "
"moved from once the expression is evaluated, dropping them has no effect "
"unless one of the operands to an expression breaks out of the expression, "
"returns, or [panics](panic.md)."
msgstr ""
"在对其他操作数求值期间，也会创建临时值来保存表达式操作数的结果。这些临时值关"
"联到包含该操作数的表达式的作用域。由于表达式一经求值完成就会从这些临时值中移"
"出，因此丢弃它们没有效果，除非该表达式的某个操作数跳出该表达式、返回，或发生 "
"[panic](panic.md)。"

#: src/destructors.md:362
msgid ""
"// Tuple expression doesn't finish evaluating so operands drop in reverse "
"order\n"
msgstr "// 元组表达式未完成求值，因此操作数按逆序丢弃\n"

#: src/destructors.md:364
msgid "\"Outer tuple first\""
msgstr "\"外层元组第一个\""

#: src/destructors.md:365
msgid "\"Outer tuple second\""
msgstr "\"外层元组第二个\""

#: src/destructors.md:367
msgid "\"Inner tuple first\""
msgstr "\"内层元组第一个\""

#: src/destructors.md:368
msgid "\"Inner tuple second\""
msgstr "\"内层元组第二个\""

#: src/destructors.md:371
msgid "\"Never created\""
msgstr "\"从未创建\""

#: src/destructors.md:376
msgid "r\\[destructors.scope.const-promotion\\]"
msgstr "r\\[destructors.scope.const-promotion\\]"

#: src/destructors.md:377
msgid "Constant promotion"
msgstr "常量提升"

#: src/destructors.md:379
msgid ""
"Promotion of a value expression to a `'static` slot occurs when the "
"expression could be written in a constant and borrowed, and that borrow "
"could be dereferenced where the expression was originally written, without "
"changing the runtime behavior. That is, the promoted expression can be "
"evaluated at compile-time and the resulting value does not contain [interior "
"mutability](interior-mutability.md) or [destructors](destructors.md) (these "
"properties are determined based on the value where possible, e.g. `&None` "
"always has the type `&'static Option<_>`, as it contains nothing disallowed)."
msgstr ""
"当一个值表达式可以写在常量中并被借用，而且该借用可以在该表达式原本所在的位置"
"被解引用且不改变运行时行为时，就会发生到 `'static` 存储槽的提升。也就是说，被"
"提升的表达式可以在编译时求值，并且所得值不包含[内部可变性](interior-"
"mutability.md)或[析构器](destructors.md)（这些性质会在可能时基于该值确定，例"
"如 `&None` 始终具有类型 `&'static Option<_>`，因为它不包含任何被禁止的内"
"容）。"

#: src/destructors.md:381
msgid "r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension\\]"
msgstr "r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension\\]"

#: src/destructors.md:382
msgid "Temporary lifetime extension"
msgstr "临时生命周期延长"

#: src/destructors.md:384
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The exact rules for temporary lifetime extension are subject to "
"change. This is describing the current behavior only."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 临时生命周期延长的确切规则可能会改变。这里描述的只是当前行为。"

#: src/destructors.md:387
msgid ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.let\\] The temporary scopes for "
"expressions in `let` statements are sometimes _extended_ to the scope of the "
"block containing the `let` statement. This is done when the usual temporary "
"scope would be too small, based on certain syntactic rules. For example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.let\\] `let` 语句中表达式的临时作用"
"域有时会被 *延长* 到包含该 `let` 语句的块的作用域。基于某些语法规则，当通常的"
"临时作用域过小时，就会这样做。例如："

#: src/destructors.md:391
msgid ""
"// Usually a temporary would be dropped by now, but the temporary for `0` "
"lives\n"
"// to the end of the block.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 通常临时值到这里已经会被丢弃，但 `0` 的临时值会存活\n"
"// 到块的末尾。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:397
msgid ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.static\\] Lifetime extension also "
"applies to `static` and `const` items, where it makes temporaries live until "
"the end of the program. For example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.static\\] 生命周期延长也适用于 "
"`static` 和 `const` 项，在这些项中它会让临时值存活到程序结束。例如："

#: src/destructors.md:401
msgid ""
"// Usually this would be a dangling reference as the `Vec` would only\n"
"// exist inside the initializer expression of `C`, but instead the\n"
"// borrow gets lifetime-extended so it effectively has `'static` lifetime.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 通常这会成为悬垂引用，因为该 `Vec` 只会存在于 `C` 的\n"
"// 初始化器表达式内部，但这里该借用会被生命周期延长，\n"
"// 因而实际上具有 `'static` 生命周期。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:408
msgid ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.sub-expressions\\] If a [borrow]"
"(expr.operator.borrow), [dereference](expressions/operator-expr.md#the-"
"dereference-operator), [field](expressions/field-expr.md), or [tuple "
"indexing expression](expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions) "
"has an extended temporary scope, then so does its operand. If an [indexing "
"expression](expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-slice-indexing-expressions) "
"has an extended temporary scope, then the indexed expression also has an "
"extended temporary scope."
msgstr ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.sub-expressions\\] 如果[借用]"
"(expr.operator.borrow)、[解引用](expressions/operator-expr.md#the-"
"dereference-operator)、[字段](expressions/field-expr.md)或[元组索引表达式]"
"(expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions)具有被延长的临时作用"
"域，那么它的操作数也如此。如果[索引表达式](expressions/array-expr.md#array-"
"and-slice-indexing-expressions)具有被延长的临时作用域，那么被索引的表达式也具"
"有被延长的临时作用域。"

#: src/destructors.md:411
msgid "r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.patterns\\]"
msgstr "r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.patterns\\]"

#: src/destructors.md:412
msgid "Extending based on patterns"
msgstr "基于模式的延长"

#: src/destructors.md:414
msgid ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.patterns.extending\\] An _extending "
"pattern_ is either:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.patterns.extending\\] *延长模式* 是"
"以下两者之一："

#: src/destructors.md:417
msgid ""
"An [identifier pattern](patterns.md#identifier-patterns) that binds by "
"reference or mutable reference."
msgstr ""
"通过引用或可变引用绑定的[标识符模式](patterns.md#identifier-patterns)。"

#: src/destructors.md:421
msgid "// Binds by reference.\n"
msgstr "// 通过引用绑定。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:423
msgid "// Binds by mutable reference.\n"
msgstr "// 通过可变引用绑定。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:427
msgid ""
"A [struct](patterns.md#struct-patterns), [tuple](patterns.md#tuple-"
"patterns), [tuple struct](patterns.md#tuple-struct-patterns), [slice]"
"(patterns.md#slice-patterns), or [or-pattern](patterns.md#or-patterns) where "
"at least one of the direct subpatterns is an extending pattern."
msgstr ""
"至少一个直接子模式是延长模式的[结构体](patterns.md#struct-patterns)、[元组]"
"(patterns.md#tuple-patterns)、[元组结构体](patterns.md#tuple-struct-"
"patterns)、[切片](patterns.md#slice-patterns)或 [or-pattern（或模式）]"
"(patterns.md#or-patterns)。"

#: src/destructors.md:434
msgid "// Struct pattern.\n"
msgstr "// 结构体模式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:436
msgid "// Tuple struct pattern.\n"
msgstr "// 元组结构体模式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:438
msgid "// Tuple pattern.\n"
msgstr "// 元组模式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:440
msgid "// Slice pattern.\n"
msgstr "// 切片模式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:442
msgid "// Or pattern.\n"
msgstr "// Or 模式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:444 src/names/name-resolution.md:61
#: src/names/name-resolution.md:64
msgid "//\n"
msgstr "//\n"

#: src/destructors.md:445
msgid "// All of the temporaries above are still live here.\n"
msgstr "// 以上所有临时值在这里仍然存活。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:449
msgid ""
"So `ref x`, `V(ref x)` and `[ref x, y]` are all extending patterns, but `x`, "
"`&ref x` and `&(ref x,)` are not."
msgstr ""
"因此 `ref x`、`V(ref x)` 和 `[ref x, y]` 都是延长模式，但 `x`、`&ref x` 和 "
"`&(ref x,)` 不是。"

#: src/destructors.md:451
msgid ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.patterns.let\\] If the pattern in a "
"`let` statement is an extending pattern then the temporary scope of the "
"initializer expression is extended."
msgstr ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.patterns.let\\] 如果 `let` 语句中的"
"模式是延长模式，则初始化器表达式的临时作用域会被延长。"

#: src/destructors.md:455
msgid "// This is an extending pattern, so the temporary scope is extended.\n"
msgstr "// 这是延长模式，因此临时作用域会被延长。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:462
msgid ""
"// This is neither an extending pattern nor an extending expression,\n"
"// so the temporary is dropped at the semicolon.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这既不是延长模式，也不是延长表达式，\n"
"// 因此临时值会在分号处丢弃。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:470
msgid ""
"// This is not an extending pattern but it is an extending expression,\n"
"// so the temporary lives beyond the `let` statement.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 这不是延长模式，但它是延长表达式，\n"
"// 因此临时值会存活到 `let` 语句之后。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:477
msgid "r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.exprs\\]"
msgstr "r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.exprs\\]"

#: src/destructors.md:478
msgid "Extending based on expressions"
msgstr "基于表达式的延长"

#: src/destructors.md:480
msgid ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.exprs.extending\\] For a let "
"statement with an initializer, an _extending expression_ is an expression "
"which is one of the following:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.exprs.extending\\] 对于带初始化器的 "
"let 语句，*延长表达式* 是以下表达式之一："

#: src/destructors.md:483
msgid "The initializer expression."
msgstr "初始化器表达式。"

#: src/destructors.md:484
msgid "The operand of an extending [borrow](expr.operator.borrow) expression."
msgstr "延长[借用](expr.operator.borrow)表达式的操作数。"

#: src/destructors.md:485
msgid ""
"The [super operands](expr.super-macros) of an extending [super macro call]"
"(expr.super-macros) expression."
msgstr ""
"延长 [super 宏调用](expr.super-macros)表达式的 [super 操作数](expr.super-"
"macros)。"

#: src/destructors.md:486
msgid ""
"The operand(s) of an extending [array](expressions/array-expr.md#array-"
"expressions), [cast](expressions/operator-expr.md#type-cast-expressions), "
"[braced struct](expressions/struct-expr.md), or [tuple](expressions/tuple-"
"expr.md#tuple-expressions) expression."
msgstr ""
"延长[数组](expressions/array-expr.md#array-expressions)、[类型转换]"
"(expressions/operator-expr.md#type-cast-expressions)、[大括号结构体]"
"(expressions/struct-expr.md)或[元组](expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-"
"expressions)表达式的操作数。"

#: src/destructors.md:487
msgid ""
"The arguments to an extending [tuple struct](type.struct.tuple) or [tuple "
"enum variant](type.enum.declaration) constructor expression."
msgstr ""
"延长[元组结构体](type.struct.tuple)或[元组枚举变体](type.enum.declaration)构"
"造器表达式的实参。"

#: src/destructors.md:488
msgid ""
"The final expression of an extending [block expression](expressions/block-"
"expr.md) except for an [async block expression](expr.block.async)."
msgstr ""
"延长[块表达式](expressions/block-expr.md)的末尾表达式，但 [async 块表达式]"
"(expr.block.async)除外。"

#: src/destructors.md:489
msgid ""
"The final expression of an extending [`if`](expressions/if-expr.md#if-"
"expressions) expression's consequent, `else if`, or `else` block."
msgstr ""
"延长 [`if`](expressions/if-expr.md#if-expressions) 表达式的后件、`else if` "
"或 `else` 块的末尾表达式。"

#: src/destructors.md:490
msgid ""
"An arm expression of an extending [`match`](expressions/match-expr.md) "
"expression."
msgstr "延长 [`match`](expressions/match-expr.md) 表达式的分支表达式。"

#: src/destructors.md:492
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The desugaring of a [destructuring assignment]"
"(expr.assign.destructure) makes its assigned value operand (the RHS) an "
"extending expression within a newly-introduced block. For details, see \\"
"[expr.assign.destructure.tmp-ext\\]."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] [解构赋值](expr.assign.destructure)的脱糖会使其被赋值操作数"
"（RHS）成为新引入块内的延长表达式。详情见 \\[expr.assign.destructure.tmp-"
"ext\\]。"

#: src/destructors.md:495
msgid ""
"So the borrow expressions in `&mut 0`, `(&1, &mut 2)`, and `Some(&mut 3)` "
"are all extending expressions. The borrows in `&0 + &1` and `f(&mut 0)` are "
"not."
msgstr ""
"因此，`&mut 0`、`(&1, &mut 2)` 和 `Some(&mut 3)` 中的借用表达式都是延长表达"
"式。`&0 + &1` 和 `f(&mut 0)` 中的借用则不是。"

#: src/destructors.md:497
msgid ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.exprs.borrows\\] The operand of an "
"extending [borrow](expr.operator.borrow) expression has its [temporary scope]"
"(destructors.scope.temporary) [extended](destructors.scope.lifetime-"
"extension)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.exprs.borrows\\] 延长[借用]"
"(expr.operator.borrow)表达式的操作数，其[临时作用域]"
"(destructors.scope.temporary)会被[延长](destructors.scope.lifetime-"
"extension)。"

#: src/destructors.md:500
msgid ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.exprs.super-macros\\] The [super "
"temporaries](expr.super-macros) of an extending [super macro call]"
"(expr.super-macros) expression have their [scopes]"
"(destructors.scope.temporary) [extended](destructors.scope.lifetime-"
"extension)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[destructors.scope.lifetime-extension.exprs.super-macros\\] 延长 [super 宏"
"调用](expr.super-macros)表达式的 [super 临时值](expr.super-macros)，其[作用"
"域](destructors.scope.temporary)会被[延长](destructors.scope.lifetime-"
"extension)。"

#: src/destructors.md:503
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` does not treat [array repeat operands](expr.array.repeat-"
"operand) of extending [array](types/array.md) expressions as extending "
"expressions. Whether it should is an open question."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 不会把延长[数组](types/array.md)表达式的[数组重复操作数]"
"(expr.array.repeat-operand)视为延长表达式。是否应当如此仍是开放问题。"

#: src/destructors.md:506
msgid ""
"For details, see [Rust issue #146092](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"issues/146092)."
msgstr ""
"详情见 [Rust issue #146092](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/"
"146092)。"

#: src/destructors.md:510
msgid ""
"Here are some examples where expressions have extended temporary scopes:"
msgstr "下面是一些表达式具有被延长的临时作用域的示例："

#: src/destructors.md:519
msgid "// Operand of borrow.\n"
msgstr "// 借用的操作数。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:521
msgid "// Operand of raw borrow.\n"
msgstr "// 原始借用的操作数。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:523
msgid "// Operand of cast.\n"
msgstr "// 类型转换的操作数。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:525
msgid "// Operand of tuple constructor.\n"
msgstr "// 元组构造器的操作数。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:528
msgid "// Argument to tuple struct constructor.\n"
msgstr "// 元组结构体构造器的实参。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:530
msgid "// Argument to tuple enum variant constructor.\n"
msgstr "// 元组枚举变体构造器的实参。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:532
msgid "// Final expr of block.\n"
msgstr "// 块的末尾表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:534
msgid "// Final expr of `const` block.\n"
msgstr "// `const` 块的末尾表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:536
msgid "// Final expr of `unsafe` block.\n"
msgstr "// `unsafe` 块的末尾表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:538
msgid ""
"//              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"//           Final exprs of `if`/`else` blocks.\n"
msgstr ""
"//              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"//           `if`/`else` 块的末尾表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:542
msgid "// `match` arm expression.\n"
msgstr "// `match` 分支表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:544
msgid "// Super operand of super macro call expression.\n"
msgstr "// super 宏调用表达式的 super 操作数。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:549
msgid ""
"//\n"
"// All of the temporaries above are still live here.\n"
msgstr ""
"//\n"
"// 以上所有临时值在这里仍然存活。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:555
msgid ""
"Here are some examples where expressions don't have extended temporary "
"scopes:"
msgstr "下面是一些表达式不具有被延长的临时作用域的示例："

#: src/destructors.md:558
msgid ""
"// Arguments to function calls are not extending expressions. The\n"
"// temporary is dropped at the semicolon.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 函数调用的实参不是延长表达式。\n"
"// 临时值会在分号处丢弃。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:568
msgid "// Receivers of method calls are not extending expressions.\n"
msgstr "// 方法调用的接收者不是延长表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:575
msgid "// Scrutinees of match expressions are not extending expressions.\n"
msgstr "// match 表达式的被匹配值不是延长表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:582
msgid "// Final expressions of `async` blocks are not extending expressions.\n"
msgstr "// `async` 块的末尾表达式不是延长表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:589
msgid "// Final expressions of closures are not extending expressions.\n"
msgstr "// 闭包的末尾表达式不是延长表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:596
msgid "// Operands of loop breaks are not extending expressions.\n"
msgstr "// loop break 的操作数不是延长表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:603
msgid "// Operands of breaks to labels are not extending expressions.\n"
msgstr "// 到标签的 break 的操作数不是延长表达式。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:611
msgid ""
"// The argument to `pin!` is only an extending expression if the call\n"
"// is an extending expression. Since it's not, the inner block is not\n"
"// an extending expression, so the temporaries in its trailing\n"
"// expression are dropped immediately.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 只有当 `pin!` 调用本身是延长表达式时，传给 `pin!` 的实参\n"
"// 才是延长表达式。由于这里不是，内部块也不是延长表达式，\n"
"// 所以其尾随表达式中的临时值会立即丢弃。\n"

#: src/destructors.md:625
msgid "r\\[destructors.forget\\]"
msgstr "r\\[destructors.forget\\]"

#: src/destructors.md:626
msgid "Not running destructors"
msgstr "不运行析构器"

#: src/destructors.md:628
msgid "r\\[destructors.manually-suppressing\\]"
msgstr "r\\[destructors.manually-suppressing\\]"

#: src/destructors.md:629
msgid "Manually suppressing destructors"
msgstr "手动抑制析构器"

#: src/destructors.md:631
msgid ""
"\\[`core::mem::forget`\\] can be used to prevent the destructor of a "
"variable from being run, and \\[`core::mem::ManuallyDrop`\\] provides a "
"wrapper to prevent a variable or field from being dropped automatically."
msgstr ""
"\\[`core::mem::forget`\\] 可用于防止变量的析构器运行，而 \\"
"[`core::mem::ManuallyDrop`\\] 提供了一个包装器，用于防止变量或字段被自动丢"
"弃。"

#: src/destructors.md:633
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Preventing a destructor from being run via \\"
"[`core::mem::forget`\\] or other means is safe even if it has a type that "
"isn't `'static`. Besides the places where destructors are guaranteed to run "
"as defined by this document, types may _not_ safely rely on a destructor "
"being run for soundness."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 通过 \\[`core::mem::forget`\\] 或其他方式防止析构器运行是安全的，"
"即使相关值的类型不是 `'static` 也是如此。除了本文档定义的保证析构器会运行的位"
"置之外，类型不能为了健全性而依赖析构器会运行。"

#: src/destructors.md:636
msgid "r\\[destructors.process-termination\\]"
msgstr "r\\[destructors.process-termination\\]"

#: src/destructors.md:637
msgid "Process termination without unwinding"
msgstr "不展开而终止进程"

#: src/destructors.md:639
msgid ""
"There are some ways to terminate the process without [unwinding]"
"(panic.md#unwinding), in which case destructors will not be run."
msgstr ""
"有一些方式会在不[展开](panic.md#unwinding)的情况下终止进程，此时析构器不会运"
"行。"

#: src/destructors.md:641
msgid ""
"The standard library provides \\[`std::process::exit`\\] and \\"
"[`std::process::abort`\\] to do this explicitly. Additionally, if the \\"
"[panic handler\\]\\[panic.panic_handler.std\\] is set to `abort`, panicking "
"will always terminate the process without destructors being run."
msgstr ""
"标准库提供了 \\[`std::process::exit`\\] 和 \\[`std::process::abort`\\] 来显式"
"执行这种终止。此外，如果 \\[panic 处理器\\]\\[panic.panic_handler.std\\] 被设"
"置为 `abort`，则 panic 始终会在不运行析构器的情况下终止进程。"

#: src/destructors.md:643
msgid ""
"There is one additional case to be aware of: when a panic reaches a [non-"
"unwinding ABI boundary](items/functions.md#unwinding), either no destructors "
"will run, or all destructors up until the ABI boundary will run."
msgstr ""
"还有一种额外情况需要注意：当 panic 到达[非展开式 ABI 边界](items/"
"functions.md#unwinding)时，要么不会运行任何析构器，要么会运行直到该 ABI 边界"
"为止的所有析构器。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:1
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:4
msgid ""
"Rust has rules that allow lifetimes to be elided in various places where the "
"compiler can infer a sensible default choice."
msgstr ""
"Rust 有一些规则，允许在编译器可以推断出合理默认选择的各种位置省略生命周期。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:6
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.function\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.function\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:7
msgid "Lifetime elision in functions"
msgstr "函数中的生命周期省略"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:9
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.intro\\] In order to make common patterns more "
"ergonomic, lifetime arguments can be _elided_ in [function item](types/"
"function-item.md), [function pointer](types/function-pointer.md), and "
"[closure trait](types/closure.md) signatures. The following rules are used "
"to infer lifetime parameters for elided lifetimes."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.intro\\] 为了让常见模式更易用，可以在 "
"[function item](types/function-item.md)、[function pointer](types/function-"
"pointer.md) 和 [closure trait](types/closure.md) 签名中*省略*生命周期实参。以"
"下规则用于为被省略的生命周期推断生命周期参数。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:12
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.lifetimes-not-inferred\\] It is an error to "
"elide lifetime parameters that cannot be inferred."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.lifetimes-not-inferred\\] 省略无法推断的生命周"
"期参数是错误的。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:15
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.explicit-placeholder\\] The placeholder "
"lifetime, `'_`, can also be used to have a lifetime inferred in the same "
"way. For lifetimes in paths, using `'_` is preferred."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.explicit-placeholder\\] 占位生命周期 `'_` 也可"
"以用于以相同方式推断生命周期。对于路径中的生命周期，优先使用 `'_`。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:18
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.only-functions\\] Trait object lifetimes "
"follow different rules discussed [below](#default-trait-object-lifetimes)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.only-functions\\] trait object 生命周期遵循[下"
"文](#r-lifetime-elision.trait-object)讨论的不同规则。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:21
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.function.implicit-lifetime-parameters\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.function.implicit-lifetime-parameters\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:22
msgid ""
"Each elided lifetime in the parameters becomes a distinct lifetime parameter."
msgstr "参数中每个被省略的生命周期都会成为一个不同的生命周期参数。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:24
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.function.output-lifetime\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.function.output-lifetime\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:25
msgid ""
"If there is exactly one lifetime used in the parameters (elided or not), "
"that lifetime is assigned to _all_ elided output lifetimes."
msgstr ""
"如果参数中恰好使用了一个生命周期（无论是否被省略），该生命周期会被赋给*所有*"
"被省略的输出生命周期。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:27
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.receiver-lifetime\\] In method signatures "
"there is another rule"
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.function.receiver-lifetime\\] 在方法签名中还有另一条规则"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:30
msgid ""
"If the receiver has type `&Self`  or `&mut Self`, then the lifetime of that "
"reference to `Self` is assigned to all elided output lifetime parameters."
msgstr ""
"如果接收者的类型为 `&Self`  或 `&mut Self`，则该指向 `Self` 的引用的生命周期"
"会被赋给所有被省略的输出生命周期参数。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:41 src/lifetime-elision.md:45
#: src/lifetime-elision.md:48 src/lifetime-elision.md:51
#: src/lifetime-elision.md:54 src/lifetime-elision.md:57
#: src/lifetime-elision.md:61 src/lifetime-elision.md:65
#: src/lifetime-elision.md:68
msgid "// elided\n"
msgstr "// 已省略\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:42
msgid "// also elided\n"
msgstr "// 也是已省略\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:43 src/lifetime-elision.md:46
#: src/lifetime-elision.md:49 src/lifetime-elision.md:52
#: src/lifetime-elision.md:55 src/lifetime-elision.md:58
#: src/lifetime-elision.md:62 src/lifetime-elision.md:66
#: src/lifetime-elision.md:69
msgid "// expanded\n"
msgstr "// 已展开\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:60
msgid "// elided - preferred\n"
msgstr "// 已省略 - 首选形式\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:73
msgid ""
"// The following examples show situations where it is not allowed to elide "
"the\n"
"// lifetime parameter.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 以下示例展示不允许省略\n"
"// 生命周期参数的情况。\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:76
msgid "// Cannot infer, because there are no parameters to infer from.\n"
msgstr "// 无法推断，因为没有可供推断的参数。\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:78 src/lifetime-elision.md:81
msgid "// ILLEGAL\n"
msgstr "// 非法\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:79
msgid ""
"// Cannot infer, ambiguous if it is borrowed from the first or second "
"parameter.\n"
msgstr "// 无法推断，不明确它是从第一个参数还是第二个参数借用而来。\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:85
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:86
msgid "Default trait object lifetimes"
msgstr "默认 trait object 生命周期"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:88
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.intro\\] The assumed lifetime of "
"references held by a [trait object](types/trait-object.md) is called its "
"_default object lifetime bound_. These were defined in [RFC 599](https://"
"github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/0599-default-object-bound.md) and "
"amended in [RFC 1156](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/"
"1156-adjust-default-object-bounds.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.intro\\] [trait object](types/trait-"
"object.md) 所持有引用的假定生命周期称为其*默认对象生命周期约束*。这些约束在 "
"[RFC 599](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/0599-default-"
"object-bound.md) 中定义，并在 [RFC 1156](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/"
"blob/master/text/1156-adjust-default-object-bounds.md) 中修订。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:91
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.explicit-bound\\] These default object "
"lifetime bounds are used instead of the lifetime parameter elision rules "
"defined above when the lifetime bound is omitted entirely."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.explicit-bound\\] 当生命周期约束被完全省略"
"时，会使用这些默认对象生命周期约束，而不是上面定义的生命周期参数省略规则。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:94
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.explicit-placeholder\\] If `'_` is used as "
"the lifetime bound then the bound follows the usual elision rules."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.explicit-placeholder\\] 如果将 `'_` 用作生"
"命周期约束，则该约束遵循通常的省略规则。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:97
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.containing-type\\] If the trait object is "
"used as a type argument of a generic type then the containing type is first "
"used to try to infer a bound."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.containing-type\\] 如果 trait object 被用作"
"泛型类型的类型实参，则会先使用包含它的类型来尝试推断约束。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:100
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.containing-type-unique\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.containing-type-unique\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:101
msgid ""
"If there is a unique bound from the containing type then that is the default."
msgstr "如果从包含类型得到唯一约束，则该约束就是默认值。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:103
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.containing-type-explicit\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.containing-type-explicit\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:104
msgid ""
"If there is more than one bound from the containing type then an explicit "
"bound must be specified."
msgstr "如果从包含类型得到多个约束，则必须指定显式约束。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:106
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.trait-bounds\\] If neither of those rules "
"apply, then the bounds on the trait are used:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.trait-bounds\\] 如果上述规则都不适用，则使"
"用 trait 上的约束："

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:109
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.trait-unique\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.trait-unique\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:110
msgid ""
"If the trait is defined with a single lifetime _bound_ then that bound is "
"used."
msgstr "如果 trait 定义时带有单个生命周期*约束*，则使用该约束。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:112
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.static-lifetime\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.static-lifetime\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:113
msgid "If `'static` is used for any lifetime bound then `'static` is used."
msgstr "如果任一生命周期约束使用了 `'static`，则使用 `'static`。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:115
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.default\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.default\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:116
msgid ""
"If the trait has no lifetime bounds, then the lifetime is inferred in "
"expressions and is `'static` outside of expressions."
msgstr ""
"如果 trait 没有生命周期约束，则生命周期在表达式中被推断，而在表达式之外为 "
"`'static`。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:119 src/lifetime-elision.md:156
msgid "// For the following trait...\n"
msgstr "// 对于以下 trait...\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:121
msgid "// These two are the same because Box<T> has no lifetime bound on T\n"
msgstr "// 这二者相同，因为 Box<T> 对 T 没有生命周期约束\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:125 src/lifetime-elision.md:162
msgid "// ...and so are these:\n"
msgstr "// ...这些也是如此：\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:129
msgid "// ...so are these, because &'a T requires T: 'a\n"
msgstr "// ...这些也是如此，因为 &'a T 要求 T: 'a\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:133
msgid "// std::cell::Ref<'a, T> also requires T: 'a, so these are the same\n"
msgstr "// std::cell::Ref<'a, T> 也要求 T: 'a，所以这些相同\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:140
msgid "// This is an example of an error.\n"
msgstr "// 这是一个错误示例。\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:147
msgid ""
"//                                  ^^^^^^^\n"
"// Error: the lifetime bound for this object type cannot be deduced from "
"context\n"
msgstr ""
"//                                  ^^^^^^^\n"
"// 错误：无法从上下文推断此对象类型的生命周期约束\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:152
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.innermost-type\\] Note that the innermost "
"object sets the bound, so `&'a Box<dyn Foo>` is still `&'a Box<dyn Foo + "
"'static>`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.trait-object.innermost-type\\] 注意，最内层对象会决定约"
"束，因此 `&'a Box<dyn Foo>` 仍然是 `&'a Box<dyn Foo + 'static>`。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:158
msgid "// ...these two are the same:\n"
msgstr "// ...这二者相同：\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:168
msgid "r\\[lifetime-elision.const-static\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lifetime-elision.const-static\\]"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:169
msgid "`const` and `static` elision"
msgstr "`const` 和 `static` 省略"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:171
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.const-static.implicit-static\\] Both [constant](items/"
"constant-items.md) and [static](items/static-items.md) declarations of "
"reference types have _implicit_ `'static` lifetimes unless an explicit "
"lifetime is specified. As such, the constant declarations involving "
"`'static` above may be written without the lifetimes."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.const-static.implicit-static\\] 除非指定显式生命周期，否"
"则引用类型的[常量项](items/constant-items.md)声明和[静态项](items/static-"
"items.md)声明都具有*隐式*的 `'static` 生命周期。因此，上面涉及 `'static` 的常"
"量声明可以写成不带生命周期的形式。"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:175
msgid "// STRING: &'static str\n"
msgstr "// STRING: &'static str\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:182
msgid "// BITS_N_STRINGS: BitsNStrings<'static>\n"
msgstr "// BITS_N_STRINGS: BitsNStrings<'static>\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:190
msgid ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.const-static.fn-references\\] Note that if the `static` "
"or `const` items include function or closure references, which themselves "
"include references, the compiler will first try the standard elision rules. "
"If it is unable to resolve the lifetimes by its usual rules, then it will "
"error. By way of example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[lifetime-elision.const-static.fn-references\\] 注意，如果 `static` 或 "
"`const` 项包含函数引用或闭包引用，而这些函数或闭包引用自身又包含引用，则编译"
"器会先尝试标准省略规则。如果它无法按通常规则解析生命周期，则会报错。例如："

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:197
msgid "// Resolved as `for<'a> fn(&'a str) -> &'a str`.\n"
msgstr "// 解析为 `for<'a> fn(&'a str) -> &'a str`。\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:200
msgid ""
"// Resolved as `for<'a, 'b, 'c> Fn(&'a Foo, &'b Bar, &'c Baz) -> usize`.\n"
msgstr "// 解析为 `for<'a, 'b, 'c> Fn(&'a Foo, &'b Bar, &'c Baz) -> usize`。\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:209
msgid ""
"// There is insufficient information to bound the return reference lifetime\n"
"// relative to the argument lifetimes, so this is an error.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 信息不足，无法相对于实参生命周期来约束返回引用生命周期，\n"
"// 因此这是一个错误。\n"

#: src/lifetime-elision.md:212
msgid ""
"//                                            ^\n"
"// this function's return type contains a borrowed value, but the signature\n"
"// does not say whether it is borrowed from argument 1 or argument 2\n"
msgstr ""
"//                                            ^\n"
"// 此函数的返回类型包含一个借用值，但签名\n"
"// 没有说明它是从实参 1 还是实参 2 借用而来\n"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:1
msgid "r\\[lang-types\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.intro\\] Certain types and traits that exist in [the standard "
"library](std) are known to the Rust compiler. This chapter documents the "
"special features of these types and traits."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.intro\\] 存在于[标准库](std)中的某些类型和 trait 是 Rust 编译"
"器知晓的。本章记录这些类型和 trait 的特殊特性。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:7
msgid "r\\[lang-types.box\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.box\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.box.intro\\] \\[`Box<T>`\\] has a few special features that "
"Rust doesn't currently allow for user defined types."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.box.intro\\] \\[`Box<T>`\\] 具有一些 Rust 目前不允许用户定义类"
"型拥有的特殊特性。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:13
msgid "r\\[lang-types.box.deref\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.box.deref\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:14
msgid ""
"The [dereference operator](expressions/operator-expr.md#the-dereference-"
"operator) for `Box<T>` produces a place which can be [moved from]"
"(expr.move.movable-place). This means that the `*` operator and the "
"destructor of `Box<T>` are built-in to the language."
msgstr ""
"`Box<T>` 的[解引用运算符](expressions/operator-expr.md#the-dereference-"
"operator)会产生一个可以[从中移动](expr.move.movable-place)的位置。这意味着 "
"`*` 运算符和 `Box<T>` 的析构器是内建于语言中的。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:16
msgid "r\\[lang-types.box.receiver\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.box.receiver\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:17
msgid ""
"[Methods](items/associated-items.md#associated-functions-and-methods) can "
"take `Box<Self>` as a receiver."
msgstr ""
"[方法](items/associated-items.md#associated-functions-and-methods)可以接受 "
"`Box<Self>` 作为接收者。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:19
msgid "r\\[lang-types.box.fundamental\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.box.fundamental\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:20
msgid ""
"A trait may be implemented for `Box<T>` in the same crate as `T`, which the "
"[orphan rules](items/implementations.md#trait-implementation-coherence) "
"prevent for other generic types."
msgstr ""
"可以在与 `T` 相同的 crate 中为 `Box<T>` 实现 trait，而[孤儿规则](items/"
"implementations.md#trait-implementation-coherence)会禁止对其他泛型类型这样"
"做。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:24
msgid "r\\[lang-types.rc\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.rc\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:25
msgid "`Rc<T>`"
msgstr "`Rc<T>`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:27
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.rc.receiver\\] [Methods](items/associated-items.md#associated-"
"functions-and-methods) can take [`Rc<Self>`](std::rc::Rc) as a receiver."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.rc.receiver\\] [方法](items/associated-items.md#associated-"
"functions-and-methods)可以接受 [`Rc<Self>`](std::rc::Rc) 作为接收者。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:30
msgid "r\\[lang-types.arc\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.arc\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:31
msgid "`Arc<T>`"
msgstr "`Arc<T>`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:33
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.arc.receiver\\] [Methods](items/associated-"
"items.md#associated-functions-and-methods) can take [`Arc<Self>`]"
"(std::sync::Arc) as a receiver."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.arc.receiver\\] [方法](items/associated-items.md#associated-"
"functions-and-methods)可以接受 [`Arc<Self>`](std::sync::Arc) 作为接收者。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:36
msgid "r\\[lang-types.pin\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.pin\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:37
msgid "`Pin<P>`"
msgstr "`Pin<P>`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:39
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.pin.receiver\\] [Methods](items/associated-"
"items.md#associated-functions-and-methods) can take [`Pin<P>`]"
"(std::pin::Pin) as a receiver."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.pin.receiver\\] [方法](items/associated-items.md#associated-"
"functions-and-methods)可以接受 [`Pin<P>`](std::pin::Pin) 作为接收者。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:42
msgid "r\\[lang-types.unsafe-cell\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.unsafe-cell\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:43
msgid "`UnsafeCell<T>`"
msgstr "`UnsafeCell<T>`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:45
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.unsafe-cell.interior-mut\\] \\[`std::cell::UnsafeCell<T>`\\] "
"is used for [interior mutability](interior-mutability.md). It ensures that "
"the compiler doesn't perform optimisations that are incorrect for such types."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.unsafe-cell.interior-mut\\] \\[`std::cell::UnsafeCell<T>`\\] "
"用于[内部可变性](interior-mutability.md)。它确保编译器不会执行对这类类型而言"
"不正确的优化。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:48
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.unsafe-cell.read-only-alloc\\] It also ensures that [`static` "
"items](items/static-items.md) which have a type with interior mutability "
"aren't placed in memory marked as read only."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.unsafe-cell.read-only-alloc\\] 它还确保具有内部可变性类型的 "
"[`static` 项](items/static-items.md)不会被放置在标记为只读的内存中。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:51
msgid "r\\[lang-types.phantom-data\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.phantom-data\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:52
msgid "`PhantomData<T>`"
msgstr "`PhantomData<T>`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:54
msgid ""
"\\[`std::marker::PhantomData<T>`\\] is a [zero-sized](glossary.zst), minimum "
"alignment, type that is considered to own a `T` for the purposes of "
"[variance](subtyping.md#variance), [drop check](../nomicon/dropck.html), and "
"[auto traits](#auto-traits)."
msgstr ""
"\\[`std::marker::PhantomData<T>`\\] 是一种[零大小](glossary.zst)、最小对齐的"
"类型；出于[型变](subtyping.md#variance)、[drop 检查](../nomicon/dropck.html)"
"和[auto trait](#auto-traits)的目的，它被视为拥有一个 `T`。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:56
msgid "r\\[lang-types.ops\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.ops\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:57
msgid "Operator traits"
msgstr "运算符 trait"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:59
msgid ""
"The traits in \\[`std::ops`\\] and \\[`std::cmp`\\] are used to overload "
"[operators](expressions/operator-expr.md), [indexing expressions]"
"(expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-slice-indexing-expressions), and [call "
"expressions](expressions/call-expr.md)."
msgstr ""
"\\[`std::ops`\\] 和 \\[`std::cmp`\\] 中的 trait 用于重载[运算符](expressions/"
"operator-expr.md)、[索引表达式](expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-slice-"
"indexing-expressions)和[调用表达式](expressions/call-expr.md)。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:61
msgid "r\\[lang-types.deref\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.deref\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:62
msgid "`Deref` and `DerefMut`"
msgstr "`Deref` 和 `DerefMut`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:64
msgid ""
"As well as overloading the unary `*` operator, [`Deref`](std::ops::Deref) "
"and [`DerefMut`](std::ops::DerefMut) are also used in [method resolution]"
"(expressions/method-call-expr.md) and [deref coercions](type-"
"coercions.md#coercion-types)."
msgstr ""
"除了重载一元 `*` 运算符外，[`Deref`](std::ops::Deref) 和 [`DerefMut`]"
"(std::ops::DerefMut) 还用于[方法解析](expressions/method-call-expr.md)和"
"[deref 强制转换](type-coercions.md#coercion-types)。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:66
msgid "r\\[lang-types.drop\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.drop\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:67
msgid "`Drop`"
msgstr "`Drop`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:69
msgid ""
"The \\[`Drop`\\] trait provides a [destructor](destructors.md), to be run "
"whenever a value of this type is to be destroyed."
msgstr ""
"\\[`Drop`\\] trait 提供一个[析构器](destructors.md)，每当该类型的值即将被销毁"
"时运行。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:71
msgid "r\\[lang-types.copy\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.copy\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:72
msgid "`Copy`"
msgstr "`Copy`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:74
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.copy.intro\\] The \\[`Copy`\\] trait changes the semantics of "
"a type implementing it."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.copy.intro\\] \\[`Copy`\\] trait 会改变实现它的类型的语义。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:77
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.copy.behavior\\] Values whose type implements `Copy` are "
"copied rather than moved upon assignment."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.copy.behavior\\] 类型实现了 `Copy` 的值在赋值时会被复制，而不"
"是被移动。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:80
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.copy.constraint\\] `Copy` can only be implemented for types "
"which do not implement `Drop`, and whose fields are all `Copy`. For enums, "
"this means all fields of all variants have to be `Copy`. For unions, this "
"means all variants have to be `Copy`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.copy.constraint\\] `Copy` 只能为未实现 `Drop` 且其字段全都是 "
"`Copy` 的类型实现。对于枚举，这意味着所有变体的所有字段都必须是 `Copy`。对于"
"联合体，这意味着所有变体都必须是 `Copy`。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:83
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.copy.builtin-types\\] `Copy` is implemented by the compiler "
"for"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.copy.builtin-types\\] 编译器为以下类型实现了 `Copy`："

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:86
msgid "r\\[lang-types.copy.tuple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.copy.tuple\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:87
msgid "[Tuples](types/tuple.md) of `Copy` types"
msgstr "`Copy` 类型组成的[元组](types/tuple.md)"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:89
msgid "r\\[lang-types.copy.fn-pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.copy.fn-pointer\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:92
msgid "r\\[lang-types.copy.fn-item\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.copy.fn-item\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:93
msgid "[Function items](types/function-item.md)"
msgstr "[函数项](types/function-item.md)"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:95
msgid "r\\[lang-types.copy.closure\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.copy.closure\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:96
msgid ""
"[Closures](types/closure.md) that capture no values or that only capture "
"values of `Copy` types"
msgstr "不捕获任何值或只捕获 `Copy` 类型的值的[闭包](types/closure.md)"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:98
msgid "r\\[lang-types.clone\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.clone\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:99
msgid "`Clone`"
msgstr "`Clone`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:101
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.clone.intro\\] The \\[`Clone`\\] trait is a supertrait of "
"`Copy`, so it also needs compiler generated implementations."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.clone.intro\\] \\[`Clone`\\] trait 是 `Copy` 的 supertrait，因"
"此它也需要由编译器生成的实现。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:104
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.clone.builtin-types\\] It is implemented by the compiler for "
"the following types:"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.clone.builtin-types\\] 编译器会为以下类型实现它："

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:107
msgid "r\\[lang-types.clone.builtin-copy\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.clone.builtin-copy\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:108
msgid "Types with a built-in `Copy` implementation (see above)"
msgstr "具有内置 `Copy` 实现的类型（见上文）"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:110
msgid "r\\[lang-types.clone.tuple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.clone.tuple\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:111
msgid "[Tuples](types/tuple.md) of `Clone` types"
msgstr "`Clone` 类型组成的[元组](types/tuple.md)"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:113
msgid "r\\[lang-types.clone.closure\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.clone.closure\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:114
msgid ""
"[Closures](types/closure.md) that only capture values of `Clone` types or "
"capture no values from the environment"
msgstr ""
"只捕获 `Clone` 类型的值或不从环境中捕获任何值的[闭包](types/closure.md)"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:116
msgid "r\\[lang-types.send\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.send\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:117
msgid "`Send`"
msgstr "`Send`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:119
msgid ""
"The \\[`Send`\\] trait indicates that a value of this type is safe to send "
"from one thread to another."
msgstr ""
"\\[`Send`\\] trait 表示此类型的值可以安全地从一个线程发送到另一个线程。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:121
msgid "r\\[lang-types.sync\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.sync\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:122
msgid "`Sync`"
msgstr "`Sync`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:124
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.sync.intro\\] The \\[`Sync`\\] trait indicates that a value "
"of this type is safe to share between multiple threads."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.sync.intro\\] \\[`Sync`\\] trait 表示此类型的值可以安全地在多"
"个线程之间共享。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:127
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.sync.static-constraint\\] This trait must be implemented for "
"all types used in immutable [`static` items](items/static-items.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.sync.static-constraint\\] 所有用于不可变 [`static` 项](items/"
"static-items.md)的类型都必须实现此 trait。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:130
msgid "r\\[lang-types.termination\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.termination\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:131
msgid "`Termination`"
msgstr "`Termination`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:133
msgid ""
"The [`Termination`](std::process::Termination) trait indicates the "
"acceptable return types for the [main function](crates-and-source-"
"files.md#main-functions) and [test functions](attributes/testing.md#the-test-"
"attribute)."
msgstr ""
"[`Termination`](std::process::Termination) trait 表示[main 函数](crates-and-"
"source-files.md#main-functions)和[测试函数](attributes/testing.md#the-test-"
"attribute)可接受的返回类型。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:135
msgid "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:136
msgid "Auto traits"
msgstr "auto trait"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:138
msgid ""
"The \\[`Send`\\], \\[`Sync`\\], [`Unpin`](std::marker::Unpin), [`UnwindSafe`]"
"(std::panic::UnwindSafe), and [`RefUnwindSafe`](std::panic::RefUnwindSafe) "
"traits are _auto traits_. Auto traits have special properties."
msgstr ""
"\\[`Send`\\]、\\[`Sync`\\]、[`Unpin`](std::marker::Unpin)、[`UnwindSafe`]"
"(std::panic::UnwindSafe) 和 [`RefUnwindSafe`](std::panic::RefUnwindSafe) "
"trait 是 _auto trait_。auto trait 具有特殊属性。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:140
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.auto-impl\\] If no explicit implementation or "
"negative implementation is written out for an auto trait for a given type, "
"then the compiler implements it automatically according to the following "
"rules:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.auto-impl\\] 如果没有为给定类型写出某个 auto "
"trait 的显式实现或否定实现，那么编译器会根据以下规则自动实现它："

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:143
msgid "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.builtin-composite\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.builtin-composite\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:144
msgid ""
"`&T`, `&mut T`, `*const T`, `*mut T`, `[T; n]`, and `[T]` implement the "
"trait if `T` does."
msgstr ""
"如果 `T` 实现该 trait，则 `&T`、`&mut T`、`*const T`、`*mut T`、`[T; n]` 和 "
"`[T]` 也实现该 trait。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:146
msgid "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.fn-item-pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.fn-item-pointer\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:147
msgid ""
"Function item types and function pointers automatically implement the trait."
msgstr "函数项类型和函数指针会自动实现该 trait。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:149
msgid "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.aggregate\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.aggregate\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:150
msgid ""
"Structs, enums, unions, and tuples implement the trait if all of their "
"fields do."
msgstr ""
"如果结构体、枚举、联合体和元组的所有字段都实现该 trait，则它们也实现该 "
"trait。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:152
msgid "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.closure\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.closure\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:153
msgid ""
"Closures implement the trait if the types of all of their captures do. A "
"closure that captures a `T` by shared reference and a `U` by value "
"implements any auto traits that both `&T` and `U` do."
msgstr ""
"如果闭包所有捕获项的类型都实现该 trait，则闭包也实现该 trait。通过共享引用捕"
"获一个 `T` 并按值捕获一个 `U` 的闭包，会实现 `&T` 和 `U` 二者都实现的任何 "
"auto trait。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:155
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.generic-impl\\] For generic types (counting the "
"built-in types above as generic over `T`), if a generic implementation is "
"available, then the compiler does not automatically implement it for types "
"that could use the implementation except that they do not meet the requisite "
"trait bounds. For instance, the standard library implements `Send` for all "
"`&T` where `T` is `Sync`; this means that the compiler will not implement "
"`Send` for `&T` if `T` is `Send` but not `Sync`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.generic-impl\\] 对于泛型类型（将上述内置类型视为关"
"于 `T` 的泛型类型），如果存在可用的泛型实现，那么对于本可以使用该实现、只是未"
"满足所需 trait 约束的类型，编译器不会自动实现它。例如，标准库为所有满足 `T` "
"为 `Sync` 的 `&T` 实现 `Send`；这意味着如果 `T` 是 `Send` 但不是 `Sync`，编译"
"器不会为 `&T` 实现 `Send`。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:158
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.negative\\] Auto traits can also have negative "
"implementations, shown as `impl !AutoTrait for T` in the standard library "
"documentation, that override the automatic implementations. For example "
"`*mut T` has a negative implementation of `Send`, and so `*mut T` is not "
"`Send`, even if `T` is. There is currently no stable way to specify "
"additional negative implementations; they exist only in the standard library."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.negative\\] auto trait 也可以有否定实现，在标准库"
"文档中显示为 `impl !AutoTrait for T`，它们会覆盖自动实现。例如，`*mut T` 有一"
"个 `Send` 的否定实现，因此即使 `T` 是 `Send`，`*mut T` 也不是 `Send`。目前没"
"有稳定方式指定额外的否定实现；它们只存在于标准库中。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:161
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.trait-object-marker\\] Auto traits may be added "
"as an additional bound to any [trait object](types/trait-object.md), even "
"though normally only one trait is allowed. For instance, `Box<dyn Debug + "
"Send + UnwindSafe>` is a valid type."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.auto-traits.trait-object-marker\\] auto trait 可以作为附加约束"
"添加到任何 [trait 对象](types/trait-object.md) 上，即使通常只允许一个 trait。"
"例如，`Box<dyn Debug + Send + UnwindSafe>` 是一个有效类型。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:164
msgid "r\\[lang-types.sized\\]"
msgstr "r\\[lang-types.sized\\]"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:165
msgid "`Sized`"
msgstr "`Sized`"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:167
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.sized.intro\\] The \\[`Sized`\\] trait indicates that the "
"size of this type is known at compile-time; that is, it's not a [dynamically "
"sized type](dynamically-sized-types.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.sized.intro\\] \\[`Sized`\\] trait 表示此类型的大小在编译时已"
"知；也就是说，它不是[动态大小类型](dynamically-sized-types.md)。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:170
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.sized.implicit-sized\\] [Type parameters](types/"
"parameters.md) (except `Self` in traits) are `Sized` by default, as are "
"[associated types](items/associated-items.md#associated-types)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.sized.implicit-sized\\] [类型参数](types/parameters.md)"
"（trait 中的 `Self` 除外）默认是 `Sized`，[关联类型](items/associated-"
"items.md#associated-types)也是如此。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:173
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.sized.implicit-impl\\] `Sized` is always implemented "
"automatically by the compiler, not by [implementation items](items/"
"implementations.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.sized.implicit-impl\\] `Sized` 始终由编译器自动实现，而不是由"
"[实现项](items/implementations.md)实现。"

#: src/special-types-and-traits.md:176
msgid ""
"r\\[lang-types.sized.relaxation\\] These implicit `Sized` bounds may be "
"relaxed by using the special `?Sized` bound."
msgstr ""
"r\\[lang-types.sized.relaxation\\] 这些隐式 `Sized` 约束可以通过使用特殊的 `?"
"Sized` 约束来放宽。"

#: src/names.md:1
msgid "r\\[names\\]"
msgstr "r\\[names\\]"

#: src/names.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[names.intro\\] An _entity_ is a language construct that can be referred "
"to in some way within the source program, usually via a [path](paths.md). "
"Entities include [types](types.md), [items](items.md), [generic parameters]"
"(items/generics.md), [variable bindings](patterns.md), [loop labels]"
"(expressions/loop-expr.md#loop-labels), [lifetimes](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-"
"loop-labels), [fields](expressions/field-expr.md), [attributes]"
"(attributes.md), and [lints](attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-"
"attributes)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[names.intro\\] *实体*是一种语言构造，可以在源程序中以某种方式引用，通常经"
"由[路径](paths.md)引用。实体包括[类型](types.md)、[项](items.md)、[泛型参数]"
"(items/generics.md)、[变量绑定](patterns.md)、[循环标签](expressions/loop-"
"expr.md#loop-labels)、[生命周期](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-loop-labels)、[字段]"
"(expressions/field-expr.md)、[属性](attributes.md)和 [lint](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes)。"

#: src/names.md:7
msgid ""
"A _declaration_ is a syntactical construct that can introduce a _name_ to "
"refer to an entity. Entity names are valid within a [_scope_](names/"
"scopes.md) --- a region of source text where that name may be referenced."
msgstr ""
"*声明*是一种可以引入*名称*来指代实体的语法构造。实体名称在[*作用域*](names/"
"scopes.md)内有效 --- 作用域是源文本中可以引用该名称的一片区域。"

#: src/names.md:9
msgid ""
"Some entities are [explicitly declared](#explicitly-declared-entities) in "
"the source code, and some are [implicitly declared](#implicitly-declared-"
"entities) as part of the language or compiler extensions."
msgstr ""
"有些实体在源代码中[显式声明](#r-names.explicit)，有些实体则作为语言或编译器扩"
"展的一部分[隐式声明](#r-names.implicit)。"

#: src/names.md:11
msgid ""
"[_Paths_](paths.md) are used to refer to an entity, possibly in another "
"module or type."
msgstr "[*路径*](paths.md)用于引用实体，该实体可能位于另一个模块或类型中。"

#: src/names.md:13
msgid ""
"Lifetimes and loop labels use a [dedicated syntax](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-"
"loop-labels) using a leading quote."
msgstr ""
"生命周期和循环标签使用带有前导引号的[专用语法](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-loop-"
"labels)。"

#: src/names.md:15
msgid ""
"Names are segregated into different [_namespaces_](names/namespaces.md), "
"allowing entities in different namespaces to share the same name without "
"conflict."
msgstr ""
"名称被划分到不同的[*命名空间*](names/namespaces.md)中，从而允许不同命名空间中"
"的实体共享同一名称而不发生冲突。"

#: src/names.md:17
msgid ""
"[_Name resolution_](names/name-resolution.md) is the compile-time process of "
"tying paths, identifiers, and labels to entity declarations."
msgstr ""
"[*名称解析*](names/name-resolution.md)是在编译时将路径、标识符和标签关联到实"
"体声明的过程。"

#: src/names.md:19
msgid ""
"Access to certain names may be restricted based on their [_visibility_]"
"(visibility-and-privacy.md)."
msgstr ""
"对某些名称的访问可以根据其[*可见性*](visibility-and-privacy.md)而受到限制。"

