"有关详情，请参见 [Rust PR #62086](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/"
"62086) 和 [Rust PR #139493](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/139493)。"

#: src/names/preludes.md:220
msgid ""
"r\\[names.preludes.no_implicit_prelude.lang\\] The `no_implicit_prelude` "
"attribute does not affect the [language prelude](#language-prelude)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[names.preludes.no_implicit_prelude.lang\\] `no_implicit_prelude` 属性不会"
"影响[语言 prelude](#language-prelude)。"

#: src/names/preludes.md:223
msgid "r\\[names.preludes.no_implicit_prelude.edition2018\\]"
msgstr "r\\[names.preludes.no_implicit_prelude.edition2018\\]"

#: src/names/preludes.md:224
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] In the 2015 edition, the `no_implicit_prelude` attribute "
"does not affect the [`macro_use` prelude](#macro_use-prelude), and all "
"macros exported from the standard library are still included in the "
"`macro_use` prelude. Starting in the 2018 edition, the attribute does remove "
"the `macro_use` prelude."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] 在 2015 edition 中，`no_implicit_prelude` 属性不会影响 "
"[`macro_use` prelude](#macro_use-prelude)，并且标准库导出的所有宏仍会包含在 "
"`macro_use` prelude 中。从 2018 edition 开始，该属性确实会移除 `macro_use` "
"prelude。"

#: src/paths.md:1
msgid "r\\[paths\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths\\]"

#: src/paths.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.intro\\] A _path_ is a sequence of one or more path segments "
"separated by `::` tokens. Paths are used to refer to [items](items.md), "
"values, [types](types.md), [macros](macros.md), and [attributes]"
"(attributes.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.intro\\] *路径* 是由一个或多个路径段组成的序列，路径段之间由 `::` "
"token 分隔。路径用于引用[项](items.md)、值、[类型](types.md)、[宏](macros.md)"
"和[属性](attributes.md)。"

#: src/paths.md:7
msgid "Two examples of simple paths consisting of only identifier segments:"
msgstr "两个仅由标识符段组成的简单路径示例："

#: src/paths.md:15
msgid "Types of paths"
msgstr "路径的类型"

#: src/paths.md:17
msgid "r\\[paths.simple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.simple\\]"

#: src/paths.md:18
msgid "Simple paths"
msgstr "简单路径"

#: src/paths.md:20
msgid "r\\[paths.simple.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.simple.syntax\\]"

#: src/paths.md:29
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.simple.intro\\] Simple paths are used in [visibility](visibility-"
"and-privacy.md) markers, [attributes](attributes.md), [macros](macros-by-"
"example.md), and [`use`](items/use-declarations.md) items. For example:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.simple.intro\\] 简单路径用于[可见性](visibility-and-privacy.md)标"
"记、[属性](attributes.md)、[宏](macros-by-example.md)和 [`use`](items/use-"
"declarations.md) 项。例如："

#: src/paths.md:40
msgid "r\\[paths.expr\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.expr\\]"

#: src/paths.md:41
msgid "Paths in expressions"
msgstr "表达式中的路径"

#: src/paths.md:43
msgid "r\\[paths.expr.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.expr.syntax\\]"

#: src/paths.md:80
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.expr.intro\\] Paths in expressions allow for paths with generic "
"arguments to be specified. They are used in various places in [expressions]"
"(expressions.md) and [patterns](patterns.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.expr.intro\\] 表达式中的路径允许指定带有泛型实参的路径。它们用于[表"
"达式](expressions.md)和[模式](patterns.md)中的多种位置。"

#: src/paths.md:83
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.expr.turbofish\\] The `::` token is required before the opening "
"`<` for generic arguments to avoid ambiguity with the less-than operator. "
"This is colloquially known as \"turbofish\" syntax."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.expr.turbofish\\] 为避免与小于运算符产生歧义，泛型实参的开头 `<` 前"
"必须有 `::` token。这通常称为 “turbofish” 语法。"

#: src/paths.md:91
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.expr.argument-order\\] The order of generic arguments is "
"restricted to lifetime arguments, then type arguments, then const arguments, "
"then equality constraints."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.expr.argument-order\\] 泛型实参的顺序限定为：先是生命周期实参，然后"
"是类型实参，然后是 const 实参，最后是等式约束。"

#: src/paths.md:94
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.expr.complex-const-params\\] Const arguments must be surrounded by "
"braces unless they are a [literal](expressions/literal-expr.md), an "
"[inferred const](items.generics.const.inferred), or a single segment path. "
"An [inferred const](items.generics.const.inferred) may not be surrounded by "
"braces."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.expr.complex-const-params\\] const 实参必须用花括号括起来，除非它们"
"是[字面量](expressions/literal-expr.md)、[推断 const]"
"(items.generics.const.inferred)或单段路径。[推断 const]"
"(items.generics.const.inferred) 不能用花括号括起来。"

#: src/paths.md:108
msgid "// Multi-segment path must be braced.\n"
msgstr "// 多段路径必须用花括号括起。\n"

#: src/paths.md:120
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.expr.impl-trait-params\\] The synthetic type parameters "
"corresponding to `impl Trait` types are implicit, and these cannot be "
"explicitly specified."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.expr.impl-trait-params\\] 与 `impl Trait` 类型对应的合成类型参数是"
"隐式的，不能显式指定这些参数。"

#: src/paths.md:123
msgid "r\\[paths.qualified\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualified\\]"

#: src/paths.md:124
msgid "Qualified paths"
msgstr "限定路径"

#: src/paths.md:126
msgid "r\\[paths.qualified.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualified.syntax\\]"

#: src/paths.md:135
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualified.intro\\] Fully qualified paths allow for disambiguating "
"the path for [trait implementations](items/implementations.md#trait-"
"implementations) and for specifying [canonical paths](#canonical-paths). "
"When used in a type specification, it supports using the type syntax "
"specified below."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualified.intro\\] 完全限定路径可用于消除[trait 实现](items/"
"implementations.md#trait-implementations)中路径的歧义，并用于指定[规范路径]"
"(#canonical-paths)。当用于类型说明时，它支持使用下面指定的类型语法。"

#: src/paths.md:144
msgid "\"T1 f\""
msgstr "\"T1 f\""

#: src/paths.md:148
msgid "\"T2 f\""
msgstr "\"T2 f\""

#: src/paths.md:151
msgid "// Calls the inherent impl.\n"
msgstr "// 调用固有 impl。\n"

#: src/paths.md:152
msgid "// Calls the T1 trait function.\n"
msgstr "// 调用 T1 trait 函数。\n"

#: src/paths.md:153
msgid "// Calls the T2 trait function.\n"
msgstr "// 调用 T2 trait 函数。\n"

#: src/paths.md:156
msgid "r\\[paths.type\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.type\\]"

#: src/paths.md:157
msgid "Paths in types"
msgstr "类型中的路径"

#: src/paths.md:159
msgid "r\\[paths.type.syntax\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.type.syntax\\]"

#: src/paths.md:166
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.type.intro\\] Type paths are used within type definitions, trait "
"bounds, and qualified paths."
msgstr "r\\[paths.type.intro\\] 类型路径用于类型定义、trait 约束和限定路径。"

#: src/paths.md:169
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.type.turbofish\\] Although the `::` token is allowed before the "
"generics arguments, it is not required because there is no ambiguity like "
"there is in \\[PathInExpression\\]."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.type.turbofish\\] 虽然允许在泛型实参前使用 `::` token，但这不是必需"
"的，因为不存在像 \\[PathInExpression\\] 中那样的歧义。"

#: src/paths.md:179
msgid "/*...*/"
msgstr "/*...*/"

#: src/paths.md:188
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers\\]"

#: src/paths.md:189
msgid "Path qualifiers"
msgstr "路径限定符"

#: src/paths.md:191
msgid ""
"Paths can be denoted with various leading qualifiers to change the meaning "
"of how it is resolved."
msgstr "路径可以用各种前导限定符表示，以改变其被解析的含义。"

#: src/paths.md:193
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] [`use` declarations](items/use-declarations.md) have additional "
"behaviors and restrictions for `self`, `super`, `crate`, and `$crate`."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] [`use` 声明](items/use-declarations.md) 对 `self`、`super`、"
"`crate` 和 `$crate` 有额外的行为和限制。"

#: src/paths.md:196
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.global-root\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.global-root\\]"

#: src/paths.md:197 src/syntax-index.md:109
msgid "`::`"
msgstr "[路径分隔符](paths.md#r-paths)"

#: src/paths.md:199
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.global-root.intro\\] Paths starting with `::` are "
"considered to be _global paths_ where the segments of the path start being "
"resolved from a place which differs based on edition. Each identifier in the "
"path must resolve to an item."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.global-root.intro\\] 以 `::` 开头的路径被视为 *全局路径"
"*，其中路径段开始解析的位置会因 edition 而异。路径中的每个标识符都必须解析为"
"一个项。"

#: src/paths.md:202
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.global-root.edition2018\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.global-root.edition2018\\]"

#: src/paths.md:203
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] In the 2015 Edition, identifiers resolve from the "
"\"crate root\" (`crate::` in the 2018 edition), which contains a variety of "
"different items, including external crates, default crates such as `std` or "
"`core`, and items in the top level of the crate (including `use` imports)."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2018\\] 在 2015 edition 中，标识符从“crate 根”（2018 edition 中"
"为 `crate::`）解析；crate 根包含各种不同项，包括外部 crate、`std` 或 `core` "
"等默认 crate，以及 crate 顶层中的项（包括 `use` 导入）。"

#: src/paths.md:206
msgid ""
"Beginning with the 2018 Edition, paths starting with `::` resolve from "
"crates in the [extern prelude](names/preludes.md#extern-prelude). That is, "
"they must be followed by the name of a crate."
msgstr ""
"从 2018 edition 开始，以 `::` 开头的路径会从 [extern prelude](names/"
"preludes.md#extern-prelude) 中的 crate 解析。也就是说，它们后面必须跟随一个 "
"crate 的名称。"

#: src/paths.md:210
msgid ""
"// In the 2018 edition, this accesses `std` via the extern prelude.\n"
"    // In the 2015 edition, this accesses `std` via the crate root.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 在 2018 edition 中，这会通过 extern prelude 访问 `std`。\n"
"    // 在 2015 edition 中，这会通过 crate root 访问 `std`。\n"

#: src/paths.md:224
msgid ""
"// call `a`'s foo function\n"
"        // In Rust 2018, `::a` would be interpreted as the crate `a`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 调用 `a` 的 foo 函数\n"
"        // 在 Rust 2018 中，`::a` 会被解释为 crate `a`。\n"

#: src/paths.md:231
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.mod-self\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.mod-self\\]"

#: src/paths.md:234
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.mod-self.intro\\] `self` resolves the path relative to "
"the current module."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.mod-self.intro\\] `self` 会相对于当前模块解析路径。"

#: src/paths.md:237
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.mod-self.restriction\\] `self` may only be used as the "
"first segment of a path (without a preceding `::`) or as the last segment "
"(preceded by `::`)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.mod-self.restriction\\] `self` 只能作为路径的第一段（前"
"面没有 `::`）使用，或者作为最后一段（前面有 `::`）使用。"

#: src/paths.md:240
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.mod-self.trailing\\] When `self` appears as the last "
"segment of a path, it refers to the entity named by the preceding segment. "
"The preceding path must resolve to a [module](items/modules.md), "
"[enumeration](items/enumerations.md), or [trait](items/traits.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.mod-self.trailing\\] 当 `self` 作为路径的最后一段出现"
"时，它指代由前一段命名的实体。前面的路径必须解析为[模块](items/modules.md)、"
"[枚举](items/enumerations.md)或 [trait](items/traits.md)。"

#: src/paths.md:249
msgid "// OK: Enumerations can be parents of `self`.\n"
msgstr "// OK: Enumerations can be parents of `self`.\n"

#: src/paths.md:260
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] See \\[items.use.self\\] for additional rules about `self` in "
"`use` declarations."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 有关 `use` 声明中 `self` 的额外规则，参见 \\[items.use.self\\]。"

#: src/paths.md:263
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.self-pat\\] In a method body, a path which consists of "
"a single `self` segment resolves to the method's self parameter."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.self-pat\\] 在方法体中，由单个 `self` 段组成的路径会解析"
"为该方法的 self 参数。"

#: src/paths.md:280
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self\\]"

#: src/paths.md:283
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.intro\\] `Self`, with a capital \"S\", is "
"used to refer to the current type being implemented or defined. It may be "
"used in the following situations:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.intro\\] 首字母大写的 `Self` 用于指代当前正在"
"实现或定义的类型。它可以在以下情况下使用："

#: src/paths.md:286
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.trait\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.trait\\]"

#: src/paths.md:287
msgid ""
"In a [trait](items/traits.md) definition, it refers to the type implementing "
"the trait."
msgstr "在 [trait](items/traits.md) 定义中，它指代实现该 trait 的类型。"

#: src/paths.md:289
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.impl\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.impl\\]"

#: src/paths.md:290
msgid ""
"In an [implementation](items/implementations.md), it refers to the type "
"being implemented. When implementing a tuple or unit [struct](items/"
"structs.md), it also refers to the constructor in the [value namespace]"
"(names/namespaces.md)."
msgstr ""
"在[实现](items/implementations.md)中，它指代正在实现的类型。当实现元组[结构"
"体](items/structs.md)或单元[结构体](items/structs.md)时，它还指代[值命名空间]"
"(names/namespaces.md)中的构造器。"

#: src/paths.md:292
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.type\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.type\\]"

#: src/paths.md:293
msgid ""
"In the definition of a [struct](items/structs.md), [enumeration](items/"
"enumerations.md), or [union](items/unions.md), it refers to the type being "
"defined. The definition is not allowed to be infinitely recursive (there "
"must be an indirection)."
msgstr ""
"在[结构体](items/structs.md)、[枚举](items/enumerations.md)或[联合体](items/"
"unions.md)的定义中，它指代正在定义的类型。该定义不允许无限递归（必须有一层间"
"接性）。"

#: src/paths.md:295
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.scope\\] The scope of `Self` behaves "
"similarly to a generic parameter; see the [`Self` scope](names/"
"scopes.md#self-scope) section for more details."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.scope\\] `Self` 的作用域行为类似于泛型参数；更"
"多细节见 [`Self` 作用域](names/scopes.md#self-scope)章节。"

#: src/paths.md:298
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.allowed-positions\\] `Self` can only be used "
"as the first segment, without a preceding `::`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.allowed-positions\\] `Self` 只能作为第一段使"
"用，前面不能有 `::`。"

#: src/paths.md:301
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.no-generics\\] The `Self` path cannot include "
"generic arguments (as in `Self::<i32>`)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.type-self.no-generics\\] `Self` 路径不能包含泛型实参"
"（如 `Self::<i32>`）。"

#: src/paths.md:308
msgid "// `Self` will be whatever type that implements `T`.\n"
msgstr "// `Self` 将是实现 `T` 的任意类型。\n"

#: src/paths.md:310
msgid "// `Self::Item` will be the type alias in the implementation.\n"
msgstr "// `Self::Item` 将是实现中的类型别名。\n"

#: src/paths.md:317
msgid "// `Self` is the type `S`.\n"
msgstr "// `Self` 是类型 `S`。\n"

#: src/paths.md:320
msgid "// `Self::Item` is the type `i32`.\n"
msgstr "// `Self::Item` 是类型 `i32`。\n"

#: src/paths.md:321
msgid "// `Self::C` is the constant value `9`.\n"
msgstr "// `Self::C` 是常量值 `9`。\n"

#: src/paths.md:324
msgid ""
"// `Self` is in scope within the generics of a trait definition,\n"
"// to refer to the type being defined.\n"
msgstr ""
"// `Self` 在 trait 定义的泛型中处于作用域内，\n"
"// 用来指代正在定义的类型。\n"

#: src/paths.md:329
msgid ""
"// `Self` can also reference associated items of the\n"
"    // type being implemented.\n"
msgstr ""
"// `Self` 也可以引用正在实现的\n"
"    // 类型的关联项。\n"

#: src/paths.md:336
msgid ""
"// A struct can reference itself (as long as it is not\n"
"    // infinitely recursive).\n"
msgstr ""
"// struct 可以引用自身（只要它不是\n"
"    // 无限递归的）。\n"

#: src/paths.md:342
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.super\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.super\\]"

#: src/paths.md:345
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.super.intro\\] `super` in a path resolves to the parent "
"module."
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.super.intro\\] 路径中的 `super` 解析为父模块。"

#: src/paths.md:348
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.super.allowed-positions\\] It may only be used in "
"leading segments of the path, possibly after an initial `self` segment."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.super.allowed-positions\\] 它只能用于路径的前导段，可能"
"跟在初始的 `self` 段之后。"

#: src/paths.md:357 src/paths.md:373 src/paths.md:374
msgid "// call a's foo function\n"
msgstr "// 调用 a 的 foo 函数\n"

#: src/paths.md:363
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.super.repetition\\] `super` may be repeated several "
"times after the first `super` or `self` to refer to ancestor modules."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.super.repetition\\] 在第一个 `super` 或 `self` 之后，可"
"以重复使用 `super` 多次以指代祖先模块。"

#: src/paths.md:382
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.crate\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.crate\\]"

#: src/paths.md:385
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.crate.intro\\] `crate` resolves the path relative to "
"the current crate."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.crate.intro\\] `crate` 会相对于当前 crate 解析路径。"

#: src/paths.md:388
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.crate.allowed-positions\\] `crate` can only be used as "
"the first segment, without a preceding `::`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.crate.allowed-positions\\] `crate` 只能作为第一段使用，"
"前面不能有 `::`。"

#: src/paths.md:401
msgid "r\\[paths.qualifiers.macro-crate\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.qualifiers.macro-crate\\]"

#: src/paths.md:402
msgid "`$crate`"
msgstr "`$crate`"

#: src/paths.md:404
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.macro-crate.allowed-positions\\] [`$crate`]"
"(macro.decl.hygiene.crate) is only used within [macro transcribers](macros-"
"by-example.md), and can only be used as the first segment, without a "
"preceding `::`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.macro-crate.allowed-positions\\] [`$crate`]"
"(macro.decl.hygiene.crate) 只在[宏转录器](macros-by-example.md)中使用，并且只"
"能作为第一段使用，前面不能有 `::`。"

#: src/paths.md:407
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.macro-crate.hygiene\\] [`$crate`]"
"(macro.decl.hygiene.crate) will expand to a path to access items from the "
"top level of the crate where the macro is defined, regardless of which crate "
"the macro is invoked."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.qualifiers.macro-crate.hygiene\\] [`$crate`]"
"(macro.decl.hygiene.crate) 会展开为一条路径，用于访问定义该宏的 crate 顶层中"
"的项，而不管该宏是在哪个 crate 中被调用的。"

#: src/paths.md:422
msgid "r\\[paths.canonical\\]"
msgstr "r\\[paths.canonical\\]"

#: src/paths.md:423
msgid "Canonical paths"
msgstr "规范路径"

#: src/paths.md:425
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.intro\\] Each item defined in a module or implementation "
"has a _canonical path_ that corresponds to where within its crate it is "
"defined."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.intro\\] 模块或实现中定义的每个项都有一条 *规范路径*，对"
"应它在其 crate 内的定义位置。"

#: src/paths.md:428
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.alias\\] All other paths to these items are aliases."
msgstr "r\\[paths.canonical.alias\\] 指向这些项的所有其他路径都是别名。"

#: src/paths.md:431
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.def\\] The canonical path is defined as a _path prefix_ "
"appended by the path segment the item itself defines."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.def\\] 规范路径定义为：由 *路径前缀* 附加该项自身定义的路"
"径段组成。"

#: src/paths.md:434
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.non-canonical\\] [Implementations](items/"
"implementations.md) and [use declarations](items/use-declarations.md) do not "
"have canonical paths, although the items that implementations define do have "
"them. Items defined in block expressions do not have canonical paths. Items "
"defined in a module that does not have a canonical path do not have a "
"canonical path. Associated items defined in an implementation that refers to "
"an item without a canonical path, e.g. as the implementing type, the trait "
"being implemented, a type parameter or bound on a type parameter, do not "
"have canonical paths."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.non-canonical\\] [实现](items/implementations.md)和 [use "
"声明](items/use-declarations.md)没有规范路径，尽管实现所定义的项确实有规范路"
"径。在块表达式中定义的项没有规范路径。在没有规范路径的模块中定义的项也没有规"
"范路径。在实现中定义的关联项，如果该实现引用了一个没有规范路径的项，例如作为"
"被实现类型、被实现的 trait、类型参数或类型参数上的约束，则这些关联项没有规范"
"路径。"

#: src/paths.md:437
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.module-prefix\\] The path prefix for modules is the "
"canonical path to that module."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.module-prefix\\] 模块的路径前缀是指向该模块的规范路径。"

#: src/paths.md:440
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.bare-impl-prefix\\] For bare implementations, it is the "
"canonical path of the item being implemented surrounded by <span "
"class=\"parenthetical\">angle (`<>`)</span> brackets."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.bare-impl-prefix\\] 对于不带 trait 的实现，它是被实现项的"
"规范路径，并用 <span class=\"parenthetical\">尖括号（`<>`）</span> 括起来。"

#: src/paths.md:443
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.trait-impl-prefix\\] For [trait implementations](items/"
"implementations.md#trait-implementations), it is the canonical path of the "
"item being implemented followed by `as` followed by the canonical path to "
"the trait all surrounded in <span class=\"parenthetical\">angle (`<>`)</"
"span> brackets."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.trait-impl-prefix\\] 对于 [trait 实现](items/"
"implementations.md#trait-implementations)，它是被实现项的规范路径，后接 "
"`as`，再后接指向该 trait 的规范路径，整体用 <span class=\"parenthetical\">尖"
"括号（`<>`）</span> 括起来。"

#: src/paths.md:446
msgid ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.local-canonical-path\\] The canonical path is only "
"meaningful within a given crate. There is no global namespace across crates; "
"an item's canonical path merely identifies it within the crate."
msgstr ""
"r\\[paths.canonical.local-canonical-path\\] 规范路径只在给定 crate 内有意义。"
"跨 crate 不存在全局命名空间；项的规范路径仅在该 crate 内标识该项。"

#: src/paths.md:450
msgid "// Comments show the canonical path of the item.\n"
msgstr "// 注释显示该项的规范路径。\n"

#: src/paths.md:452
msgid "// crate::a\n"
msgstr "// crate::a\n"

#: src/paths.md:453
msgid "// crate::a::Struct\n"
msgstr "// crate::a::Struct\n"

#: src/paths.md:455
msgid "// crate::a::Trait\n"
msgstr "// crate::a::Trait\n"

#: src/paths.md:456
msgid "// crate::a::Trait::f\n"
msgstr "// crate::a::Trait::f\n"

#: src/paths.md:460
msgid "// <crate::a::Struct as crate::a::Trait>::f\n"
msgstr "// <crate::a::Struct as crate::a::Trait>::f\n"

#: src/paths.md:464
msgid "// <crate::a::Struct>::g\n"
msgstr "// <crate::a::Struct>::g\n"

#: src/paths.md:468
msgid "// crate::without\n"
msgstr "// crate::without\n"

#: src/paths.md:469
msgid "// crate::without::canonicals\n"
msgstr "// crate::without::canonicals\n"

