#: src/unsafety.md:1
msgid "r\\[safety\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[safety.intro\\] Unsafe operations are those that can potentially violate "
"the memory-safety guarantees of Rust's static semantics."
msgstr ""
"r\\[safety.intro\\] 不安全操作是那些可能违反 Rust 静态语义所提供的内存安全保"
"证的操作。"

#: src/unsafety.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[safety.unsafe-ops\\] The following language level features cannot be "
"used in the safe subset of Rust:"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-ops\\] 以下语言级特性不能在 Rust 的安全子集中使用："

#: src/unsafety.md:10
msgid "r\\[safety.unsafe-deref\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-deref\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:11
msgid "Dereferencing a [raw pointer](types/pointer.md)."
msgstr "解引用[裸指针](types/pointer.md)。"

#: src/unsafety.md:13
msgid "r\\[safety.unsafe-static\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-static\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:14
msgid ""
"Reading or writing a [mutable](items/static-items.md#mutable-statics) or "
"unsafe [external](items/external-blocks.md) static variable."
msgstr ""
"读取或写入[可变](items/static-items.md#mutable-statics)静态变量，或 unsafe "
"[外部](items/external-blocks.md)静态变量。"

#: src/unsafety.md:16
msgid "r\\[safety.unsafe-union-access\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-union-access\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:17
msgid ""
"Accessing a field of a [`union`](items/unions.md), other than to assign to "
"it."
msgstr "访问 [`union`](items/unions.md) 的字段，但为其赋值除外。"

#: src/unsafety.md:19
msgid "r\\[safety.unsafe-call\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-call\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:20
msgid "Calling an unsafe function."
msgstr "调用 unsafe 函数。"

#: src/unsafety.md:22
msgid "r\\[safety.unsafe-target-feature-call\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-target-feature-call\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:23
msgid ""
"Calling a safe function marked with a \\[`target_feature`\\]\\"
"[attributes.codegen.target_feature\\] from a function that does not have a "
"`target_feature` attribute enabling the same features (see \\"
"[attributes.codegen.target_feature.safety-restrictions\\])."
msgstr ""
"从一个没有启用相同特性的 `target_feature` 属性的函数中，调用标记了 \\"
"[`target_feature`\\]\\[attributes.codegen.target_feature\\] 的安全函数（参见 "
"\\[attributes.codegen.target_feature.safety-restrictions\\]）。"

#: src/unsafety.md:25
msgid "r\\[safety.unsafe-impl\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-impl\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:26
msgid "Implementing an [unsafe trait](items/traits.md#unsafe-traits)."
msgstr "实现 [unsafe trait](items/traits.md#unsafe-traits)。"

#: src/unsafety.md:28
msgid "r\\[safety.unsafe-extern\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-extern\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:29
msgid "Declaring an [`extern`](items/external-blocks.md) block[^extern-2024]."
msgstr "声明 [`extern`](items/external-blocks.md) 块[^extern-2024]。"

#: src/unsafety.md:31
msgid "r\\[safety.unsafe-attribute\\]"
msgstr "r\\[safety.unsafe-attribute\\]"

#: src/unsafety.md:32
msgid "Applying an [unsafe attribute](attributes.md) to an item."
msgstr "将 [unsafe 属性](attributes.md)应用于项。"

#: src/unsafety.md:34
msgid ""
"Prior to the 2024 edition, extern blocks were allowed to be declared without "
"`unsafe`."
msgstr "在 2024 edition 之前，允许在不使用 `unsafe` 的情况下声明 extern 块。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:1
msgid "r\\[unsafe\\]"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe\\]"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[unsafe.intro\\] The `unsafe` keyword is used to create or discharge the "
"obligation to prove something safe. Specifically:"
msgstr ""
"r\\[unsafe.intro\\] `unsafe` 关键字用于创建或履行证明某事物安全的义务。具体而"
"言："

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:7
msgid ""
"It is used to mark code that _defines_ extra safety conditions that must be "
"upheld elsewhere."
msgstr "它用于标记*定义*额外安全条件的代码，这些条件必须在别处得到维护。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:8
msgid "This includes `unsafe fn`, `unsafe static`, and `unsafe trait`."
msgstr "这包括 `unsafe fn`、`unsafe static` 和 `unsafe trait`。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:9
msgid ""
"It is used to mark code that the programmer _asserts_ satisfies safety "
"conditions defined elsewhere."
msgstr "它用于标记程序员*断言*满足别处所定义安全条件的代码。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:10
msgid ""
"This includes `unsafe {}`, `unsafe impl`, `unsafe fn` without "
"[`unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn`](../rustc/lints/listing/allowed-by-"
"default.html#unsafe-op-in-unsafe-fn), `unsafe extern`, and `#[unsafe(attr)]`."
msgstr ""
"这包括 `unsafe {}`、`unsafe impl`、没有 [`unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn`](../rustc/"
"lints/listing/allowed-by-default.html#unsafe-op-in-unsafe-fn) 的 `unsafe "
"fn`、`unsafe extern` 和 `#[unsafe(attr)]`。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:12
msgid ""
"The following discusses each of these cases. See the [keyword documentation]"
"(../std/keyword.unsafe.html) for some illustrative examples."
msgstr ""
"下文讨论这些情形中的每一种。若要查看一些说明性示例，请参见[关键字文档](../"
"std/keyword.unsafe.html)。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:14
msgid ""
"r\\[unsafe.positions\\] The `unsafe` keyword can occur in several different "
"contexts:"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe.positions\\] `unsafe` 关键字可以出现在几种不同的上下文中："

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:17
msgid "unsafe functions (`unsafe fn`)"
msgstr "unsafe 函数（`unsafe fn`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:18
msgid "unsafe blocks (`unsafe {}`)"
msgstr "unsafe 块（`unsafe {}`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:19
msgid "unsafe traits (`unsafe trait`)"
msgstr "unsafe trait（`unsafe trait`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:20
msgid "unsafe trait implementations (`unsafe impl`)"
msgstr "unsafe trait 实现（`unsafe impl`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:21
msgid "unsafe external blocks (`unsafe extern`)"
msgstr "unsafe 外部块（`unsafe extern`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:22
msgid "unsafe external statics (`unsafe static`)"
msgstr "unsafe 外部静态项（`unsafe static`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:23
msgid "unsafe attributes (`#[unsafe(attr)]`)"
msgstr "unsafe 属性（`#[unsafe(attr)]`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:25
msgid "r\\[unsafe.fn\\]"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe.fn\\]"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:26
msgid "Unsafe functions (`unsafe fn`)"
msgstr "Unsafe 函数（`unsafe fn`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:28
msgid ""
"r\\[unsafe.fn.intro\\] Unsafe functions are functions that are not safe in "
"all contexts and/or for all possible inputs. We say they have _extra safety "
"conditions_, which are requirements that must be upheld by all callers and "
"that the compiler does not check. For example, [`get_unchecked`]"
"(slice::get_unchecked) has the extra safety condition that the index must be "
"in-bounds. The unsafe function should come with documentation explaining "
"what those extra safety conditions are."
msgstr ""
"r\\[unsafe.fn.intro\\] unsafe 函数是在并非所有上下文和/或并非所有可能输入下都"
"安全的函数。我们说它们具有*额外安全条件*，这些条件是所有调用者都必须维护、且"
"编译器不会检查的要求。例如，[`get_unchecked`](slice::get_unchecked) 具有索引"
"必须在边界内这一额外安全条件。unsafe 函数应当附带说明这些额外安全条件是什么的"
"文档。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:31
msgid ""
"r\\[unsafe.fn.safety\\] Such a function must be prefixed with the keyword "
"`unsafe` and can only be called from inside an `unsafe` block, or inside "
"`unsafe fn` without the [`unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn`](../rustc/lints/listing/"
"allowed-by-default.html#unsafe-op-in-unsafe-fn) lint."
msgstr ""
"r\\[unsafe.fn.safety\\] 这样的函数必须以关键字 `unsafe` 作为前缀，并且只能从 "
"`unsafe` 块内部调用，或者在没有 [`unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn`](../rustc/lints/"
"listing/allowed-by-default.html#unsafe-op-in-unsafe-fn) lint 的 `unsafe fn` "
"内部调用。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:34
msgid "r\\[unsafe.block\\]"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe.block\\]"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:35
msgid "Unsafe blocks (`unsafe {}`)"
msgstr "Unsafe 块（`unsafe {}`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:37
msgid ""
"r\\[unsafe.block.intro\\] A block of code can be prefixed with the `unsafe` "
"keyword to permit using the unsafe actions as defined in the [Unsafety]"
"(unsafety.md) chapter, such as calling other unsafe functions or "
"dereferencing raw pointers."
msgstr ""
"r\\[unsafe.block.intro\\] 代码块可以带有 `unsafe` 关键字前缀，以允许使用 "
"[Unsafety](unsafety.md) 一章中定义的 unsafe 动作，例如调用其他 unsafe 函数或"
"解引用裸指针。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:40
msgid ""
"r\\[unsafe.block.fn-body\\] By default, the body of an unsafe function is "
"also considered to be an unsafe block; this can be changed by enabling the "
"[`unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn`](../rustc/lints/listing/allowed-by-"
"default.html#unsafe-op-in-unsafe-fn) lint."
msgstr ""
"r\\[unsafe.block.fn-body\\] 默认情况下，unsafe 函数的函数体也被视为一个 "
"unsafe 块；这可以通过启用 [`unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn`](../rustc/lints/listing/"
"allowed-by-default.html#unsafe-op-in-unsafe-fn) lint 来改变。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:43
msgid ""
"By putting operations into an unsafe block, the programmer states that they "
"have taken care of satisfying the extra safety conditions of all operations "
"inside that block."
msgstr ""
"通过将操作放入 unsafe 块，程序员声明自己已经负责满足该块中所有操作的额外安全"
"条件。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:45
msgid ""
"Unsafe blocks are the logical dual to unsafe functions: where unsafe "
"functions define a proof obligation that callers must uphold, unsafe blocks "
"state that all relevant proof obligations of functions or operations called "
"inside the block have been discharged. There are many ways to discharge "
"proof obligations; for example, there could be run-time checks or data "
"structure invariants that guarantee that certain properties are definitely "
"true, or the unsafe block could be inside an `unsafe fn`, in which case the "
"block can use the proof obligations of that function to discharge the proof "
"obligations arising inside the block."
msgstr ""
"unsafe 块在逻辑上与 unsafe 函数对偶：unsafe 函数定义调用者必须维护的证明义"
"务，而 unsafe 块声明块内所调用函数或操作的所有相关证明义务已经被履行。履行证"
"明义务有很多方式；例如，可以有运行时检查或数据结构不变式来保证某些性质一定为"
"真，或者 unsafe 块可以位于 `unsafe fn` 内部，此时该块可以使用该函数的证明义务"
"来履行块内部产生的证明义务。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:47
msgid ""
"Unsafe blocks are used to wrap foreign libraries, make direct use of "
"hardware or implement features not directly present in the language. For "
"example, Rust provides the language features necessary to implement memory-"
"safe concurrency in the language but the implementation of threads and "
"message passing in the standard library uses unsafe blocks."
msgstr ""
"unsafe 块用于包装外部库、直接使用硬件，或实现语言中并未直接提供的特性。例如，"
"Rust 提供了在语言中实现内存安全并发所需的语言特性，但标准库中线程和消息传递的"
"实现使用了 unsafe 块。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:49
msgid ""
"Rust's type system is a conservative approximation of the dynamic safety "
"requirements, so in some cases there is a performance cost to using safe "
"code. For example, a doubly-linked list is not a tree structure and can only "
"be represented with reference-counted pointers in safe code. By using "
"`unsafe` blocks to represent the reverse links as raw pointers, it can be "
"implemented without reference counting. (See [\"Learn Rust With Entirely Too "
"Many Linked Lists\"](https://rust-unofficial.github.io/too-many-lists/) for "
"a more in-depth exploration of this particular example.)"
msgstr ""
"Rust 的类型系统是对动态安全要求的保守近似，因此在某些情况下，使用安全代码会有"
"性能成本。例如，双向链表不是树结构，在安全代码中只能用引用计数指针表示。通过"
"使用 `unsafe` 块将反向链接表示为裸指针，可以在不使用引用计数的情况下实现它。"
"（关于这个特定示例的更深入探讨，请参见 [\"Learn Rust With Entirely Too Many "
"Linked Lists\"](https://rust-unofficial.github.io/too-many-lists/)。）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:53
msgid "r\\[unsafe.trait\\]"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe.trait\\]"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:54
msgid "Unsafe traits (`unsafe trait`)"
msgstr "Unsafe trait（`unsafe trait`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:56
msgid ""
"r\\[unsafe.trait.intro\\] An unsafe trait is a trait that comes with extra "
"safety conditions that must be upheld by _implementations_ of the trait. The "
"unsafe trait should come with documentation explaining what those extra "
"safety conditions are."
msgstr ""
"r\\[unsafe.trait.intro\\] unsafe trait 是带有额外安全条件的 trait，这些条件必"
"须由该 trait 的*实现*来维护。unsafe trait 应当附带说明这些额外安全条件是什么"
"的文档。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:59
msgid ""
"r\\[unsafe.trait.safety\\] Such a trait must be prefixed with the keyword "
"`unsafe` and can only be implemented by `unsafe impl` blocks."
msgstr ""
"r\\[unsafe.trait.safety\\] 这样的 trait 必须以关键字 `unsafe` 作为前缀，并且"
"只能由 `unsafe impl` 块实现。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:62
msgid "r\\[unsafe.impl\\]"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe.impl\\]"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:63
msgid "Unsafe trait implementations (`unsafe impl`)"
msgstr "Unsafe trait 实现（`unsafe impl`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:65
msgid ""
"When implementing an unsafe trait, the implementation needs to be prefixed "
"with the `unsafe` keyword. By writing `unsafe impl`, the programmer states "
"that they have taken care of satisfying the extra safety conditions required "
"by the trait."
msgstr ""
"实现 unsafe trait 时，该实现需要以 `unsafe` 关键字作为前缀。通过写下 `unsafe "
"impl`，程序员声明自己已经负责满足该 trait 所要求的额外安全条件。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:67
msgid ""
"Unsafe trait implementations are the logical dual to unsafe traits: where "
"unsafe traits define a proof obligation that implementations must uphold, "
"unsafe implementations state that all relevant proof obligations have been "
"discharged."
msgstr ""
"unsafe trait 实现在逻辑上与 unsafe trait 对偶：unsafe trait 定义实现必须维护"
"的证明义务，而 unsafe 实现声明所有相关证明义务已经被履行。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:73
msgid "r\\[unsafe.extern\\]"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe.extern\\]"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:74
msgid "Unsafe external blocks (`unsafe extern`)"
msgstr "Unsafe 外部块（`unsafe extern`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:76
msgid ""
"The programmer who declares an [external block](items/external-blocks.md) "
"must assure that the signatures of the items contained within are correct. "
"Failing to do so may lead to undefined behavior.  That this obligation has "
"been met is indicated by writing `unsafe extern`."
msgstr ""
"声明[外部块](items/external-blocks.md)的程序员必须确保其中所含项的签名是正确"
"的。未能做到这一点可能导致未定义行为。写下 `unsafe extern` 表示这一义务已经得"
"到履行。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:78
msgid "r\\[unsafe.extern.edition2024\\]"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe.extern.edition2024\\]"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:79
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] Prior to edition 2024, `extern` blocks were allowed "
"without being qualified as `unsafe`."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] 在 edition 2024 之前，允许 `extern` 块不被限定为 "
"`unsafe`。"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:84
msgid "r\\[unsafe.attribute\\]"
msgstr "r\\[unsafe.attribute\\]"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:85
msgid "Unsafe attributes (`#[unsafe(attr)]`)"
msgstr "Unsafe 属性（`#[unsafe(attr)]`）"

#: src/unsafe-keyword.md:87
msgid ""
"An [unsafe attribute](attributes.md) is one that has extra safety conditions "
"that must be upheld when using the attribute. The compiler cannot check "
"whether these conditions have been upheld.  To assert that they have been, "
"these attributes must be wrapped in `unsafe(..)`, e.g. "
"`#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`."
msgstr ""
"[unsafe 属性](attributes.md)是带有额外安全条件的属性，在使用该属性时必须维护"
"这些条件。编译器无法检查这些条件是否已经得到维护。要断言它们已经得到维护，这"
"些属性必须包裹在 `unsafe(..)` 中，例如 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:1
msgid "r\\[undefined\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.intro\\] Rust code is incorrect if it exhibits any of the "
"behaviors in the following list. This includes code within `unsafe` blocks "
"and `unsafe` functions. `unsafe` only means that avoiding undefined behavior "
"is on the programmer; it does not change anything about the fact that Rust "
"programs must never cause undefined behavior."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.intro\\] 如果 Rust 代码表现出以下列表中的任何行为，则它是不正确"
"的。这包括 `unsafe` 块和 `unsafe` 函数内的代码。`unsafe` 只意味着避免未定义行"
"为由程序员负责；它并不会改变 Rust 程序绝不能导致未定义行为这一事实。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:7
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.soundness\\] It is the programmer's responsibility when "
"writing `unsafe` code to ensure that any safe code interacting with the "
"`unsafe` code cannot trigger these behaviors. `unsafe` code that satisfies "
"this property for any safe client is called _sound_; if `unsafe` code can be "
"misused by safe code to exhibit undefined behavior, it is _unsound_."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.soundness\\] 编写 `unsafe` 代码时，程序员有责任确保任何与该 "
"`unsafe` 代码交互的安全代码都不能触发这些行为。对于任何安全客户端都满足此属性"
"的 `unsafe` 代码称为 *健全的*；如果 `unsafe` 代码能被安全代码误用而表现出未定"
"义行为，则它是 *不健全的*。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:10
msgid ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] The following list is not exhaustive; it may grow or shrink. "
"There is no formal model of Rust's semantics for what is and is not allowed "
"in unsafe code, so there may be more behavior considered unsafe. We also "
"reserve the right to make some of the behavior in that list defined in the "
"future. In other words, this list does not say that anything will "
"_definitely_ always be undefined in all future Rust versions (but we might "
"make such commitments for some list items in the future)."
msgstr ""
"\\[!WARNING\\] 以下列表并非详尽无遗；它可能增加或减少。对于 unsafe 代码中哪些"
"允许、哪些不允许，Rust 语义没有形式化模型，因此可能还有更多被视为 unsafe 的行"
"为。我们也保留将来把该列表中的某些行为定义为有定义的权利。换言之，该列表并不"
"是说在所有未来 Rust 版本中任何内容都 *一定* 会一直是未定义的（但我们将来可能"
"会对某些列表项作出这样的承诺）。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:13
msgid ""
"Please read the [Rustonomicon](../nomicon/index.html) before writing unsafe "
"code."
msgstr "编写 unsafe 代码之前，请阅读 [Rustonomicon](../nomicon/index.html)。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:15
msgid "r\\[undefined.race\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.race\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:16
msgid "Data races."
msgstr "数据竞争。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:18
msgid "r\\[undefined.pointer-access\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.pointer-access\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:19
msgid ""
"Accessing (loading from or storing to) a place that is [dangling](#dangling-"
"pointers) or [based on a misaligned pointer](#places-based-on-misaligned-"
"pointers)."
msgstr ""
"访问（从中加载或向其中存储）一个[悬垂](#dangling-pointers)或[基于未对齐指针]"
"(#places-based-on-misaligned-pointers)的位置。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:21
msgid "r\\[undefined.place-projection\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.place-projection\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:22
msgid ""
"Performing an offsetting place projection that violates the requirements of "
"[in-bounds pointer arithmetic](pointer#method.offset). An offsetting place "
"projection is a [field expression](expressions/field-expr.md), a [tuple "
"index expression](expressions/tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions), or "
"an [array/slice index expression](expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-slice-"
"indexing-expressions)."
msgstr ""
"执行违反[界内指针算术](pointer#method.offset)要求的偏移式位置投影。偏移式位置"
"投影是[字段表达式](expressions/field-expr.md)、[元组索引表达式](expressions/"
"tuple-expr.md#tuple-indexing-expressions)或[数组/切片索引表达式](expressions/"
"array-expr.md#array-and-slice-indexing-expressions)。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:24
msgid "r\\[undefined.alias\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.alias\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:25
msgid ""
"Breaking the pointer aliasing rules. The exact aliasing rules are not "
"determined yet, but here is an outline of the general principles:"
msgstr "破坏指针别名规则。确切的别名规则尚未确定，但以下是一般原则的概要："

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:27
msgid ""
"`&T` must point to memory that is not mutated while they are live (except "
"for data inside an [`UnsafeCell<U>`](std::cell::UnsafeCell)), and `&mut T` "
"must point to memory that is not read or written by any pointer not derived "
"from the reference and that no other reference points to while they are "
"live. `Box<T>` is treated similar to `&'static mut T` for the purpose of "
"these rules. The exact liveness duration is not specified, but some bounds "
"exist:"
msgstr ""
"`&T` 必须指向在它存活期间不会被修改的内存（[`UnsafeCell<U>`]"
"(std::cell::UnsafeCell) 内部的数据除外），而 `&mut T` 必须指向这样的内存：在"
"它存活期间，不会被任何并非派生自该引用的指针读取或写入，并且没有其他引用指向"
"它。就这些规则而言，`Box<T>` 的处理类似于 `&'static mut T`。确切的存活时长未"
"指定，但存在一些界限："

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:29
msgid ""
"For references, the liveness duration is upper-bounded by the syntactic "
"lifetime assigned by the borrow checker; it cannot be live any _longer_ than "
"that lifetime."
msgstr ""
"对于引用，存活时长以借用检查器分配的语法生命周期为上界；它不能比该生命周期存"
"活得 *更久*。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:30
msgid ""
"Each time a reference or box is dereferenced or reborrowed, it is considered "
"live."
msgstr "每当引用或 box 被解引用或重新借用时，它都被认为是存活的。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:31
msgid ""
"Each time a reference or box is passed to or returned from a function, it is "
"considered live."
msgstr "每当引用或 box 被传递给函数或从函数返回时，它都被认为是存活的。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:32
msgid ""
"When a reference (but not a `Box`!) is passed to a function, it is live at "
"least as long as that function call, again except if the `&T` contains an "
"[`UnsafeCell<U>`](std::cell::UnsafeCell)."
msgstr ""
"当引用（但不是 `Box`！）被传递给函数时，它至少在该函数调用期间是存活的；同"
"样，如果该 `&T` 包含 [`UnsafeCell<U>`](std::cell::UnsafeCell) 则除外。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:34
msgid ""
"All this also applies when values of these types are passed in a (nested) "
"field of a compound type, but not behind pointer indirections."
msgstr ""
"当这些类型的值通过复合类型的（嵌套）字段传递时，以上内容也适用，但通过指针间"
"接层传递则不适用。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:36
msgid "r\\[undefined.immutable\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.immutable\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:37
msgid ""
"Mutating immutable bytes. All bytes reachable through a [const-promoted]"
"(destructors.md#constant-promotion) expression are immutable, as well as "
"bytes reachable through borrows in `static` and `const` initializers that "
"have been [lifetime-extended](destructors.md#temporary-lifetime-extension) "
"to `'static`. The bytes owned by an immutable binding or immutable `static` "
"are immutable, unless those bytes are part of an [`UnsafeCell<U>`]"
"(std::cell::UnsafeCell)."
msgstr ""
"修改不可变字节。通过 [const 提升](destructors.md#constant-promotion)表达式可"
"到达的所有字节都是不可变的，在 `static` 和 `const` 初始化器中通过借用可到达且"
"已被[生命周期延长](destructors.md#temporary-lifetime-extension)到 `'static` "
"的字节也是如此。不可变绑定或不可变 `static` 所拥有的字节是不可变的，除非这些"
"字节是 [`UnsafeCell<U>`](std::cell::UnsafeCell) 的一部分。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:39
msgid ""
"Moreover, the bytes [pointed to](#pointed-to-bytes) by a shared reference, "
"including transitively through other references (both shared and mutable) "
"and `Box`es, are immutable; transitivity includes those references stored in "
"fields of compound types."
msgstr ""
"此外，共享引用所[指向](#pointed-to-bytes)的字节也是不可变的，包括通过其他引用"
"（共享引用和可变引用）以及 `Box` 传递可达的字节；这种传递性包括存储在复合类型"
"字段中的那些引用。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:41
msgid ""
"A mutation is any write of more than 0 bytes which overlaps with any of the "
"relevant bytes (even if that write does not change the memory contents)."
msgstr ""
"修改是指任何超过 0 字节、并与任何相关字节重叠的写入（即使该写入不会改变内存内"
"容）。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:43
msgid "r\\[undefined.intrinsic\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.intrinsic\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:44
msgid "Invoking undefined behavior via compiler intrinsics."
msgstr "通过编译器内部函数调用未定义行为。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:46
msgid "r\\[undefined.target-feature\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.target-feature\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:47
msgid ""
"Executing code compiled with platform features that the current platform "
"does not support (see [`target_feature`](attributes/codegen.md#the-"
"target_feature-attribute)), _except_ if the platform explicitly documents "
"this to be safe."
msgstr ""
"执行使用当前平台不支持的平台特性编译的代码（见 [`target_feature`](attributes/"
"codegen.md#the-target_feature-attribute)），*除非* 平台明确将此记录为安全。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:49
msgid "r\\[undefined.call\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.call\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:50
msgid ""
"Calling a function with the wrong [call ABI](items/external-blocks.md#abi), "
"or unwinding past a stack frame that does not allow unwinding (e.g. by "
"calling a `\"C-unwind\"` function imported or transmuted as a `\"C\"` "
"function or function pointer)."
msgstr ""
"使用错误的[调用 ABI](items/external-blocks.md#abi) 调用函数，或越过不允许展开"
"的栈帧进行展开（例如，调用一个被导入或 transmute 为 `\"C\"` 函数或函数指针的 "
"`\"C-unwind\"` 函数）。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:52
msgid "r\\[undefined.invalid\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.invalid\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:53
msgid ""
"Producing an [invalid value](#invalid-values). \"Producing\" a value happens "
"any time a value is assigned to or read from a place, passed to a function/"
"primitive operation or returned from a function/primitive operation."
msgstr ""
"产生[无效值](#invalid-values)。“产生”一个值发生在任何时候：将值赋给某个位置或"
"从某个位置读取、传递给函数/原语操作，或从函数/原语操作返回。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:55
msgid "r\\[undefined.asm\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.asm\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:56
msgid ""
"Incorrect use of inline assembly. For more details, refer to the [rules]"
"(inline-assembly.md#rules-for-inline-assembly) to follow when writing code "
"that uses inline assembly."
msgstr ""
"错误使用内联汇编。有关更多细节，请参阅编写使用内联汇编的代码时需要遵守的[规"
"则](inline-assembly.md#rules-for-inline-assembly)。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:58
msgid "r\\[undefined.runtime\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.runtime\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:59
msgid ""
"Violating assumptions of the Rust runtime. Most assumptions of the Rust "
"runtime are currently not explicitly documented."
msgstr "违反 Rust 运行时的假设。Rust 运行时的大多数假设目前没有显式文档化。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:60
msgid ""
"For assumptions specifically related to unwinding, see the [panic "
"documentation](panic.md#unwinding-across-ffi-boundaries)."
msgstr ""
"关于专门与展开相关的假设，见 [panic 文档](panic.md#unwinding-across-ffi-"
"boundaries)。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:61
msgid ""
"The runtime assumes that a Rust stack frame is not deallocated without "
"executing destructors for local variables owned by the stack frame. This "
"assumption can be violated by C functions like `longjmp`."
msgstr ""
"运行时假设 Rust 栈帧在未执行该栈帧所拥有局部变量的析构器之前不会被释放。像 "
"`longjmp` 这样的 C 函数可能违反这一假设。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:63
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] Undefined behavior affects the entire program. For example, "
"calling a function in C that exhibits undefined behavior of C means your "
"entire program contains undefined behaviour that can also affect the Rust "
"code. And vice versa, undefined behavior in Rust can cause adverse affects "
"on code executed by any FFI calls to other languages."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] 未定义行为会影响整个程序。例如，调用一个表现出 C 未定义行为的 C "
"函数，意味着你的整个程序包含未定义行为，而这也可能影响 Rust 代码。反之亦然，"
"Rust 中的未定义行为也可能对通过任何 FFI 调用执行的其他语言代码产生不利影响。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:66
msgid "r\\[undefined.pointed-to\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.pointed-to\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:67
msgid "Pointed-to bytes"
msgstr "所指向的字节"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:69
msgid ""
"The span of bytes a pointer or reference \"points to\" is determined by the "
"pointer value and the size of the pointee type (using `size_of_val`)."
msgstr ""
"指针或引用“指向”的字节范围由指针值和被指向类型的大小（使用 `size_of_val`）决"
"定。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:71
msgid "r\\[undefined.misaligned\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.misaligned\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:72
msgid "Places based on misaligned pointers"
msgstr "基于未对齐指针的位置"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:75
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.ptr\\] A place is said to be \"based on a "
"misaligned pointer\" if the last `*` projection during place computation was "
"performed on a pointer that was not aligned for its type. (If there is no "
"`*` projection in the place expression, then this is accessing the field of "
"a local or `static` and rustc will guarantee proper alignment. If there are "
"multiple `*` projections, then each of them incurs a load of the pointer-to-"
"be-dereferenced itself from memory, and each of these loads is subject to "
"the alignment constraint. Note that some `*` projections can be omitted in "
"surface Rust syntax due to automatic dereferencing; we are considering the "
"fully expanded place expression here.)"
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.ptr\\] 如果在位置计算期间最后一个 `*` 投影是在一个未"
"按其类型对齐的指针上执行的，则称该位置“基于未对齐指针”。（如果位置表达式中没"
"有 `*` 投影，那么这是在访问局部变量或 `static` 的字段，rustc 会保证正确对齐。"
"如果有多个 `*` 投影，那么每个投影都会导致从内存中加载待解引用指针本身，而这些"
"加载都受到对齐约束。注意，由于自动解引用，表层 Rust 语法中可以省略某些 `*` 投"
"影；这里考虑的是完全展开后的位置表达式。）"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:78
msgid ""
"For instance, if `ptr` has type `*const S` where `S` has an alignment of 8, "
"then `ptr` must be 8-aligned or else `(*ptr).f` is \"based on an misaligned "
"pointer\". This is true even if the type of the field `f` is `u8` (i.e., a "
"type with alignment 1). In other words, the alignment requirement derives "
"from the type of the pointer that was dereferenced, _not_ the type of the "
"field that is being accessed."
msgstr ""
"例如，如果 `ptr` 的类型是 `*const S`，而 `S` 的对齐为 8，那么 `ptr` 必须是 8 "
"字节对齐的，否则 `(*ptr).f` 就“基于未对齐指针”。即使字段 `f` 的类型是 `u8`"
"（即对齐为 1 的类型），这一点也成立。换言之，对齐要求来自被解引用指针的类型，"
"而 *不是* 正在访问的字段类型。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:80
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.load-store\\] Note that a place based on a "
"misaligned pointer only leads to undefined behavior when it is loaded from "
"or stored to."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.load-store\\] 注意，基于未对齐指针的位置只有在从中加"
"载或向其中存储时才会导致未定义行为。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:83
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.raw\\] `&raw const`/`&raw mut` on such a place is "
"allowed."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.raw\\] 在这样的位置上使用 `&raw const`/`&raw mut` 是"
"允许的。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:86
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.reference\\] `&`/`&mut` on a place requires the "
"alignment of the field type (or else the program would be \"producing an "
"invalid value\"), which generally is a less restrictive requirement than "
"being based on an aligned pointer."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.reference\\] 在某个位置上使用 `&`/`&mut` 要求满足字"
"段类型的对齐（否则程序会“产生无效值”），这通常比基于已对齐指针的要求更宽松。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:89
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.packed\\] Taking a reference will lead to a "
"compiler error in cases where the field type might be more aligned than the "
"type that contains it, i.e., `repr(packed)`. This means that being based on "
"an aligned pointer is always sufficient to ensure that the new reference is "
"aligned, but it is not always necessary."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.misaligned.packed\\] 在字段类型可能比包含它的类型具有更严格对齐"
"的情况下，即 `repr(packed)`，获取引用会导致编译器错误。这意味着，基于已对齐指"
"针始终足以确保新引用是对齐的，但并不总是必要条件。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:92
msgid "r\\[undefined.dangling\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.dangling\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:93
msgid "Dangling pointers"
msgstr "悬垂指针"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:96
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.dangling.def\\] A reference/pointer is \"dangling\" if not all "
"of the bytes it [points to](#pointed-to-bytes) are part of the same live "
"allocation (so in particular they all have to be part of _some_ allocation)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.dangling.def\\] 如果一个引用/指针[指向](#pointed-to-bytes)的字"
"节并非全部属于同一个活动分配（因此尤其必须全部属于 *某个* 分配），则该引用/指"
"针是“悬垂”的。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:99
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.dangling.zero-size\\] If the [size is 0](glossary.zst), then "
"the pointer is trivially never \"dangling\" (even if it is a null pointer)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.dangling.zero-size\\] 如果[大小为 0](glossary.zst)，那么该指针"
"显然绝不会是“悬垂”的（即使它是空指针）。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:102
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.dangling.dynamic-size\\] Note that dynamically sized types "
"(such as slices and strings) point to their entire range, so it is important "
"that the length metadata is never too large."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.dangling.dynamic-size\\] 注意，动态大小类型（如切片和字符串）指"
"向其整个范围，因此必须确保长度元数据绝不能过大。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:105
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.dangling.alloc-limit\\] In particular, the dynamic size of a "
"Rust value (as determined by `size_of_val`) must never exceed `isize::MAX`, "
"since it is impossible for a single allocation to be larger than "
"`isize::MAX`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.dangling.alloc-limit\\] 尤其是，Rust 值的动态大小（由 "
"`size_of_val` 确定）绝不能超过 `isize::MAX`，因为单个分配不可能大于 "
"`isize::MAX`。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:108
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:109
msgid "Invalid values"
msgstr "无效值"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:112
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.validity.def\\] The Rust compiler assumes that all values "
"produced during program execution are \"valid\", and producing an invalid "
"value is hence immediate UB."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.validity.def\\] Rust 编译器假定程序执行期间产生的所有值都是“有"
"效的”，因此产生无效值会立即导致 UB。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:115
msgid "Whether a value is valid depends on the type:"
msgstr "值是否有效取决于其类型："

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:117
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.bool\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.bool\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:118
msgid ""
"A [`bool`](types/boolean.md) value must be `false` (`0`) or `true` (`1`)."
msgstr "[`bool`](types/boolean.md) 值必须是 `false`（`0`）或 `true`（`1`）。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:120
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.fn-pointer\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.fn-pointer\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:121
msgid "A `fn` pointer value must be non-null."
msgstr "`fn` 指针值必须非空。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:123
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.char\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.char\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:124
msgid ""
"A `char` value must not be a surrogate (i.e., must not be in the range "
"`0xD800..=0xDFFF`) and must be equal to or less than `char::MAX`."
msgstr ""
"`char` 值不得是代理项（即不得位于 `0xD800..=0xDFFF` 范围内），并且必须等于或"
"小于 `char::MAX`。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:126
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.never\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.never\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:127
msgid "A `!` value must never exist."
msgstr "`!` 值绝不能存在。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:129
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.scalar\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.scalar\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:130
msgid ""
"An integer (`i*`/`u*`), floating point value (`f*`), or raw pointer must be "
"initialized, i.e., must not be obtained from uninitialized memory."
msgstr ""
"整数（`i*`/`u*`）、浮点值（`f*`）或裸指针必须已初始化，即不得从未初始化内存获"
"得。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:132
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.str\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.str\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:133
msgid "A `str` value is treated like `[u8]`, i.e. it must be initialized."
msgstr "`str` 值按 `[u8]` 处理，即它必须已初始化。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:135
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.enum\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.enum\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:136
msgid ""
"An `enum` must have a valid discriminant, and all fields of the variant "
"indicated by that discriminant must be valid at their respective type."
msgstr ""
"`enum` 必须具有有效判别值，并且由该判别值指示的变体的所有字段都必须在其各自类"
"型下有效。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:138
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.struct\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.struct\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:139
msgid ""
"A `struct`, tuple, and array requires all fields/elements to be valid at "
"their respective type."
msgstr "`struct`、元组和数组要求所有字段/元素都在其各自类型下有效。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:141
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.union\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.union\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:142
msgid ""
"For a `union`, the exact validity requirements are not decided yet. "
"Obviously, all values that can be created entirely in safe code are valid. "
"If the union has a [zero-sized](glossary.zst) field, then every possible "
"value is valid. Further details are [still being debated](https://github.com/"
"rust-lang/unsafe-code-guidelines/issues/438)."
msgstr ""
"对于 `union`，确切的有效性要求尚未决定。显然，所有完全可以在安全代码中创建的"
"值都是有效的。如果该 union 有一个[零大小](glossary.zst)字段，那么每个可能的值"
"都是有效的。更多细节[仍在讨论中](https://github.com/rust-lang/unsafe-code-"
"guidelines/issues/438)。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:144
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.reference-box\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.reference-box\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:145
msgid ""
"A reference or \\[`Box<T>`\\] must be aligned and non-null, it cannot be "
"[dangling](#dangling-pointers), and it must point to a valid value (in case "
"of dynamically sized types, using the actual dynamic type of the pointee as "
"determined by the metadata). Note that the last point (about pointing to a "
"valid value) remains a subject of some debate."
msgstr ""
"引用或 \\[`Box<T>`\\] 必须对齐且非空，不能[悬垂](#dangling-pointers)，并且必"
"须指向有效值（对于动态大小类型，使用由元数据确定的被指向对象的实际动态类"
"型）。注意，最后一点（关于指向有效值）仍存在一些争议。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:147
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.wide\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.wide\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:148
msgid ""
"The metadata of a wide reference, \\[`Box<T>`\\], or raw pointer must match "
"the type of the unsized tail:"
msgstr "宽引用、\\[`Box<T>`\\] 或裸指针的元数据必须与未定大小尾部的类型匹配："

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:149
msgid ""
"`dyn Trait` metadata must be a pointer to a compiler-generated vtable for "
"`Trait`. (For raw pointers, this requirement remains a subject of some "
"debate.)"
msgstr ""
"`dyn Trait` 元数据必须是指向编译器为 `Trait` 生成的 vtable 的指针。（对于裸指"
"针，这一要求仍存在一些争议。）"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:150
msgid ""
"Slice (`[T]`) metadata must be a valid `usize`. Furthermore, for wide "
"references and \\[`Box<T>`\\], slice metadata is invalid if it makes the "
"total size of the pointed-to value bigger than `isize::MAX`."
msgstr ""
"切片（`[T]`）元数据必须是有效的 `usize`。此外，对于宽引用和 \\[`Box<T>`\\]，"
"如果切片元数据使所指向值的总大小大于 `isize::MAX`，则该切片元数据无效。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:152
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.valid-range\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.valid-range\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:153
msgid ""
"If a type has a custom range of a valid values, then a valid value must be "
"in that range. In the standard library, this affects [`NonNull<T>`]"
"(core::ptr::NonNull) and [`NonZero<T>`](core::num::NonZero)."
msgstr ""
"如果某个类型具有自定义的有效值范围，那么有效值必须在该范围内。在标准库中，这"
"会影响 [`NonNull<T>`](core::ptr::NonNull) 和 [`NonZero<T>`]"
"(core::num::NonZero)。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:155
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` achieves this with the unstable "
"`rustc_layout_scalar_valid_range_*` attributes."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `rustc` 通过不稳定的 `rustc_layout_scalar_valid_range_*` 属性实现"
"这一点。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:158
msgid "r\\[undefined.validity.const-provenance\\]"
msgstr "r\\[undefined.validity.const-provenance\\]"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:159
msgid ""
"**In [const contexts](const-eval.const-context)**: In addition to what is "
"described above, further provenance-related requirements apply during const "
"evaluation. Any value that holds pure integer data (the `i*`/`u*`/`f*` types "
"as well as `bool` and `char`, enum discriminants, and slice metadata) must "
"not carry any provenance. Any value that holds pointer data (references, raw "
"pointers, function pointers, and `dyn Trait` metadata) must either carry no "
"provenance, or all bytes must be fragments of the same original pointer "
"value in the correct order."
msgstr ""
"**在 [const 上下文](const-eval.const-context)中**：除上文所述内容外，const 求"
"值期间还适用更多与 provenance（来源）相关的要求。任何保存纯整数数据的值"
"（`i*`/`u*`/`f*` 类型以及 `bool` 和 `char`、enum 判别值、切片元数据）都不得携"
"带任何 provenance（来源）。任何保存指针数据的值（引用、裸指针、函数指针和 "
"`dyn Trait` 元数据）必须要么不携带 provenance（来源），要么所有字节都必须是同"
"一个原始指针值的片段，并且顺序正确。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:161
msgid ""
"This implies that transmuting or otherwise reinterpreting a pointer "
"(reference, raw pointer, or function pointer) into a non-pointer type (such "
"as integers) is undefined behavior if the pointer had provenance."
msgstr ""
"这意味着，如果指针（引用、裸指针或函数指针）具有 provenance（来源），那么将"
"其 transmute 或以其他方式重新解释为非指针类型（如整数）是未定义行为。"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:163
msgid "\\[!EXAMPLE\\] All of the following are UB:"
msgstr "\\[!EXAMPLE\\] 以下所有情况都是 UB："

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:169
msgid "// We cannot reinterpret a pointer with provenance as an integer,\n"
msgstr "// 不能把带有 provenance（来源）的指针重新解释为整数，\n"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:170
msgid "// as then the bytes of the integer will have provenance.\n"
msgstr "// 因为这样整数的字节就会带有 provenance（来源）。\n"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:176
msgid "// We cannot rearrange the bytes of a pointer with provenance and\n"
msgstr "// 不能重新排列带有 provenance（来源）的指针的字节，\n"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:177
msgid "// then interpret them as a reference, as then a value holding\n"
msgstr "// 然后再把它们解释为引用，因为这样保存\n"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:178
msgid "// pointer data will have pointer fragments in the wrong order.\n"
msgstr "// 指针数据的值会以错误顺序包含指针片段。\n"

#: src/behavior-considered-undefined.md:187
msgid ""
"r\\[undefined.validity.undef\\] **Note:** Uninitialized memory is also "
"implicitly invalid for any type that has a restricted set of valid values. "
"In other words, the only cases in which reading uninitialized memory is "
"permitted are inside `union`s and in \"padding\" (the gaps between the "
"fields of a type)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[undefined.validity.undef\\] **注意：** 对于任何有效值集合受限的类型，未初"
"始化内存也隐式地无效。换言之，允许读取未初始化内存的唯一情况是在 `union` 内部"
"以及在“填充”（类型字段之间的间隙）中。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:1
msgid "Behavior not considered `unsafe`"
msgstr "不被认为是 `unsafe` 的行为"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:3
msgid ""
"The Rust compiler does not consider the following behaviors _unsafe_, though "
"a programmer may (should) find them undesirable, unexpected, or erroneous."
msgstr ""
"Rust 编译器不认为以下行为是 _unsafe_，尽管程序员可能（也应该）认为它们不合需"
"求、出乎意料或存在错误。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:5
msgid "Deadlocks"
msgstr "死锁"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:6
msgid "Leaks of memory and other resources"
msgstr "内存和其他资源泄漏"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:7
msgid "Exiting without calling destructors"
msgstr "未调用析构器即退出"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:8
msgid "Exposing randomized base addresses through pointer leaks"
msgstr "通过指针泄漏暴露随机化的基址"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:10
msgid "Integer overflow"
msgstr "整数溢出"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:12
msgid ""
"If a program contains arithmetic overflow, the programmer has made an error. "
"In the following discussion, we maintain a distinction between arithmetic "
"overflow and wrapping arithmetic. The first is erroneous, while the second "
"is intentional."
msgstr ""
"如果程序包含算术溢出，则程序员犯了错误。在下面的讨论中，我们会区分算术溢出和"
"回绕算术。前者是错误的，而后者是有意的。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:14
msgid ""
"When the programmer has enabled `debug_assert!` assertions (for example, by "
"enabling a non-optimized build), implementations must insert dynamic checks "
"that `panic` on overflow. Other kinds of builds may result in `panics` or "
"silently wrapped values on overflow, at the implementation's discretion."
msgstr ""
"当程序员启用了 `debug_assert!` 断言时（例如通过启用非优化构建），实现必须插入"
"动态检查，并在溢出时 `panic`。其他类型的构建在溢出时可能会导致 `panics`，也可"
"能静默地产生回绕后的值，这由实现自行决定。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:16
msgid ""
"In the case of implicitly-wrapped overflow, implementations must provide "
"well-defined (even if still considered erroneous) results by using two's "
"complement overflow conventions."
msgstr ""
"对于隐式回绕的溢出，实现必须使用二进制补码溢出约定来提供定义明确的结果，即使"
"该结果仍被认为是错误的。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:18
msgid ""
"The integral types provide inherent methods to allow programmers explicitly "
"to perform wrapping arithmetic. For example, `i32::wrapping_add` provides "
"two's complement, wrapping addition."
msgstr ""
"整数类型提供固有方法，允许程序员显式执行回绕算术。例如，`i32::wrapping_add` "
"提供二进制补码的回绕加法。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:20
msgid ""
"The standard library also provides a `Wrapping<T>` newtype which ensures all "
"standard arithmetic operations for `T` have wrapping semantics."
msgstr ""
"标准库还提供了一个 `Wrapping<T>` newtype，它会确保 `T` 的所有标准算术操作都具"
"有回绕语义。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:22
msgid ""
"See [RFC 560](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/0560-"
"integer-overflow.md) for error conditions, rationale, and more details about "
"integer overflow."
msgstr ""
"关于错误条件、设计理由以及整数溢出的更多细节，请参见 [RFC 560](https://"
"github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/0560-integer-overflow.md)。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:24
msgid "Logic errors"
msgstr "逻辑错误"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:26
msgid ""
"Safe code may impose extra logical constraints that can be checked at "
"neither compile-time nor runtime. If a program breaks such a constraint, the "
"behavior may be unspecified but will not result in undefined behavior. This "
"could include panics, incorrect results, aborts, and non-termination. The "
"behavior may also differ between runs, builds, or kinds of build."
msgstr ""
"安全代码可能会施加一些既不能在编译时也不能在运行时检查的额外逻辑约束。如果程"
"序破坏了这样的约束，其行为可能是未指定的，但不会导致未定义行为。这可能包括 "
"panic、错误结果、中止以及不终止。该行为还可能在不同运行、不同构建或不同构建种"
"类之间有所不同。"

#: src/behavior-not-considered-unsafe.md:28
msgid ""
"For example, implementing both `Hash` and `Eq` requires that values "
"considered equal have equal hashes. Another example are data structures like "
"`BinaryHeap`, `BTreeMap`, `BTreeSet`, `HashMap` and `HashSet` which describe "
"constraints on the modification of their keys while they are in the data "
"structure. Violating such constraints is not considered unsafe, yet the "
"program is considered erroneous and its behavior unpredictable."
msgstr ""
"例如，同时实现 `Hash` 和 `Eq` 要求被认为相等的值具有相等的哈希。另一个例子是 "
"`BinaryHeap`、`BTreeMap`、`BTreeSet`、`HashMap` 和 `HashSet` 这样的数据结构，"
"它们描述了键位于数据结构中时对这些键进行修改的约束。违反此类约束不被认为是不"
"安全的，但该程序会被认为是错误的，其行为不可预测。"

#: src/const_eval.md:1
msgid "r\\[const-eval\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[const-eval.intro\\] Constant evaluation is the process of computing the "
"result of [expressions](expressions.md) during compilation. Only a subset of "
"all expressions can be evaluated at compile-time."
msgstr ""
"r\\[const-eval.intro\\] 常量求值是在编译期间计算[表达式](expressions.md)结果"
"的过程。只有所有表达式中的一个子集可以在编译时求值。"

#: src/const_eval.md:7
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:8
msgid "Constant expressions"
msgstr "常量表达式"

#: src/const_eval.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.intro\\] Certain forms of expressions, called "
"constant expressions, can be evaluated at compile time."
msgstr ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.intro\\] 某些形式的表达式称为常量表达式，可以在编译"
"时求值。"

#: src/const_eval.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.const-context\\] Expressions in a [const context]"
"(#const-context) must be constant expressions."
msgstr ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.const-context\\] [const 上下文](#const-context)中的"
"表达式必须是常量表达式。"

#: src/const_eval.md:16
msgid ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.evaluation\\] Expressions in const contexts are "
"always evaluated at compile time."
msgstr ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.evaluation\\] const 上下文中的表达式总是在编译时求"
"值。"

#: src/const_eval.md:19
msgid ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.runtime-context\\] Outside of const contexts, "
"constant expressions _may_ be, but are not guaranteed to be, evaluated at "
"compile time."
msgstr ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.runtime-context\\] 在 const 上下文之外，常量表达式 "
"*可以* 在编译时求值，但不保证一定如此。"

#: src/const_eval.md:22
msgid ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.error\\] Behaviors such as out of bounds [array "
"indexing](expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-slice-indexing-expressions) or "
"[overflow](expressions/operator-expr.md#overflow) are compiler errors if the "
"value must be evaluated at compile time (i.e. in const contexts). Otherwise, "
"these behaviors are warnings, but will likely panic at run-time."
msgstr ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.error\\] 如果值必须在编译时求值（即处于 const 上下"
"文中），那么诸如越界[数组索引](expressions/array-expr.md#array-and-slice-"
"indexing-expressions)或[溢出](expressions/operator-expr.md#overflow)这样的行"
"为是编译器错误。否则，这些行为是警告，但很可能会在运行时 panic。"

#: src/const_eval.md:25
msgid ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.list\\] The following expressions are constant "
"expressions, so long as any operands are also constant expressions and do "
"not cause any [`Drop::drop`](destructors.md) calls to be run."
msgstr ""
"r\\[const-eval.const-expr.list\\] 只要所有操作数也是常量表达式，并且不会导致"
"运行任何 [`Drop::drop`](destructors.md) 调用，以下表达式就是常量表达式。"

#: src/const_eval.md:28
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.literal\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.literal\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:29
msgid "[Literals](expressions/literal-expr.md)."
msgstr "[字面量](expressions/literal-expr.md)。"

#: src/const_eval.md:31
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.parameter\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.parameter\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:32
msgid "[Const parameters](items/generics.md)."
msgstr "[const 参数](items/generics.md)。"

#: src/const_eval.md:34
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.path-item\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.path-item\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:35
msgid ""
"[Paths](expressions/path-expr.md) to [functions](items/functions.md) and "
"[constants](items/constant-items.md). Recursively defining constants is not "
"allowed."
msgstr ""
"指向[函数](items/functions.md)和[常量](items/constant-items.md)的[路径]"
"(expressions/path-expr.md)。不允许递归定义常量。"

#: src/const_eval.md:37
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.path-static\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.path-static\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:38
msgid "Paths to [statics](items/static-items.md) with these restrictions:"
msgstr "指向 [static](items/static-items.md) 的路径需满足以下限制："

#: src/const_eval.md:39
msgid ""
"Writes to `static` items are not allowed in any constant evaluation context."
msgstr "在任何常量求值上下文中，都不允许写入 `static` 条目。"

#: src/const_eval.md:40
msgid ""
"Reads from `extern` statics are not allowed in any constant evaluation "
"context."
msgstr "在任何常量求值上下文中，都不允许读取 `extern` static。"

#: src/const_eval.md:41
msgid ""
"If the evaluation is _not_ carried out in an initializer of a `static` item, "
"then reads from any mutable `static` are not allowed. A mutable `static` is "
"a `static mut` item, or a `static` item with an interior-mutable type."
msgstr ""
"如果求值*不是*在 `static` 条目的初始化器中进行的，则不允许读取任何可变 "
"`static`。可变 `static` 是 `static mut` 条目，或具有内部可变类型的 `static` "
"条目。"

#: src/const_eval.md:43
msgid ""
"These requirements are checked only when the constant is evaluated. In other "
"words, having such accesses syntactically occur in const contexts is allowed "
"as long as they never get executed."
msgstr ""
"这些要求仅在常量被求值时检查。换言之，只要这些访问永远不会被执行，就允许它们"
"在语法上出现在 const 上下文中。"

#: src/const_eval.md:45
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.tuple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.tuple\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:46
msgid "[Tuple expressions](expressions/tuple-expr.md)."
msgstr "[元组表达式](expressions/tuple-expr.md)。"

#: src/const_eval.md:48
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.array\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.array\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:49
msgid "[Array expressions](expressions/array-expr.md)."
msgstr "[数组表达式](expressions/array-expr.md)。"

#: src/const_eval.md:51
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.constructor\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.constructor\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:52
msgid "[Struct expressions](expressions/struct-expr.md)."
msgstr "[结构体表达式](expressions/struct-expr.md)。"

#: src/const_eval.md:54
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.block\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.block\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:55
msgid ""
"[Block expressions](expressions/block-expr.md), including `unsafe` and "
"`const` blocks."
msgstr "[块表达式](expressions/block-expr.md)，包括 `unsafe` 块和 `const` 块。"

#: src/const_eval.md:56
msgid ""
"[let statements](statements.md#let-statements) and thus irrefutable "
"[patterns](patterns.md), including mutable bindings"
msgstr ""
"[let 语句](statements.md#let-statements)，以及由此产生的不可反驳[模式]"
"(patterns.md)，包括可变绑定"

#: src/const_eval.md:57
msgid ""
"[assignment expressions](expressions/operator-expr.md#assignment-expressions)"
msgstr "[赋值表达式](expressions/operator-expr.md#assignment-expressions)"

#: src/const_eval.md:58
msgid ""
"[compound assignment expressions](expressions/operator-expr.md#compound-"
"assignment-expressions)"
msgstr ""
"[复合赋值表达式](expressions/operator-expr.md#compound-assignment-"
"expressions)"

#: src/const_eval.md:59
msgid "[expression statements](statements.md#expression-statements)"
msgstr "[表达式语句](statements.md#expression-statements)"

#: src/const_eval.md:61
msgid "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.field\\]"
msgstr "r\\[const-eval.const-expr.field\\]"

#: src/const_eval.md:62
msgid "[Field expressions](expressions/field-expr.md)."
