msgstr "应用二进制接口（ABI）"

#: src/abi.md:4
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.intro\\] This section documents features that affect the ABI of the "
"compiled output of a crate."
msgstr "r\\[abi.intro\\] 本节记录会影响 crate 编译输出 ABI 的特性。"

#: src/abi.md:7
msgid ""
"See _[extern functions](items/functions.md#extern-function-qualifier)_ for "
"information on specifying the ABI for exporting functions. See _[external "
"blocks](items/external-blocks.md)_ for information on specifying the ABI for "
"linking external libraries."
msgstr ""
"有关为导出函数指定 ABI 的信息，请参阅 _[extern functions](items/"
"functions.md#extern-function-qualifier)_。有关为链接外部库指定 ABI 的信息，请"
"参阅 _[external blocks](items/external-blocks.md)_。"

#: src/abi.md:10
msgid "r\\[abi.used\\]"
msgstr "r\\[abi.used\\]"

#: src/abi.md:11
msgid "The `used` attribute"
msgstr "`used` 属性"

#: src/abi.md:13
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.used.intro\\] The _`used` [attribute](attributes.md)_ forces a "
"[static](items/static-items.md) to be kept in the output object file "
"(.o, .rlib, etc., excluding final binaries) even if it's never used or "
"referenced by any other item in the crate. The linker, however, is still "
"free to remove it."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.used.intro\\] *`used` [属性](attributes.md)*强制将 [static](items/"
"static-items.md) 保留在输出目标文件（.o、.rlib 等，不包括最终二进制文件）中，"
"即使它从未被 crate 中的任何其他项使用或引用。不过，链接器仍然可以移除它。"

#: src/abi.md:18
msgid "// lib.rs\n"
msgstr "// lib.rs\n"

#: src/abi.md:20
msgid "// This is kept because of `#[used]`.\n"
msgstr "// 由于 `#[used]`，这会被保留。\n"

#: src/abi.md:24
msgid "// This is removable because it's unused.\n"
msgstr "// 由于它未被使用，这可以被移除。\n"

#: src/abi.md:28
msgid "// This is kept because it's publicly reachable.\n"
msgstr "// 由于它公开可达，这会被保留。\n"

#: src/abi.md:31
msgid "// This is kept because it's referenced by a publicly\n"
msgstr "// 由于它被一个公开可达的函数\n"

#: src/abi.md:32
msgid "// reachable function.\n"
msgstr "// 引用，这会被保留。\n"

#: src/abi.md:36
msgid "// This is removable because it's referenced only by a\n"
msgstr "// 由于它只被一个私有且未使用的\n"

#: src/abi.md:37
msgid "// private, unused (dead) function.\n"
msgstr "// （dead）函数引用，这可以被移除。\n"

#: src/abi.md:52
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.used.syntax\\] The `used` attribute uses the \\[MetaWord\\] syntax."
msgstr "r\\[abi.used.syntax\\] `used` 属性使用 \\[MetaWord\\] 语法。"

#: src/abi.md:55
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.used.allowed-positions\\] The `used` attribute may only be applied "
"to [`static` items](items.static)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.used.allowed-positions\\] `used` 属性只能应用于 [`static` 项]"
"(items.static)。"

#: src/abi.md:58
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.used.duplicates\\] Only the first use of `used` on an item has "
"effect."
msgstr "r\\[abi.used.duplicates\\] 在一个项上，只有第一次使用 `used` 会生效。"

#: src/abi.md:64
msgid "r\\[abi.no_mangle\\]"
msgstr "r\\[abi.no_mangle\\]"

#: src/abi.md:65
msgid "The `no_mangle` attribute"
msgstr "`no_mangle` 属性"

#: src/abi.md:67
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.no_mangle.intro\\] The _`no_mangle` attribute_ may be used on any "
"[item](items.md) to disable standard symbol name mangling. The symbol for "
"the item will be the identifier of the item's name."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.no_mangle.intro\\] *`no_mangle` 属性*可用于任何[项](items.md)，以禁用"
"标准符号名修饰。该项的符号将是项名称的标识符。"

#: src/abi.md:70
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.no_mangle.publicly-exported\\] Additionally, the item will be "
"publicly exported from the produced library or object file, similar to the "
"[`used` attribute](#the-used-attribute)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.no_mangle.publicly-exported\\] 此外，类似于 [`used` 属性](#r-"
"abi.used)，该项将从生成的库或目标文件中公开导出。"

#: src/abi.md:73
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.no_mangle.unsafe\\] This attribute is unsafe as an unmangled symbol "
"may collide with another symbol with the same name (or with a well-known "
"symbol), leading to undefined behavior."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.no_mangle.unsafe\\] 此属性是 unsafe 的，因为未修饰的符号可能会与同名"
"的另一个符号（或知名符号）发生冲突，从而导致未定义行为。"

#: src/abi.md:81
msgid "r\\[abi.no_mangle.edition2024\\]"
msgstr "r\\[abi.no_mangle.edition2024\\]"

#: src/abi.md:82
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] Before the 2024 edition it is allowed to use the "
"`no_mangle` attribute without the `unsafe` qualification."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] 在 2024 edition 之前，允许在不带 `unsafe` 限定的情况下使"
"用 `no_mangle` 属性。"

#: src/abi.md:85
msgid "r\\[abi.link_section\\]"
msgstr "r\\[abi.link_section\\]"

#: src/abi.md:86
msgid "The `link_section` attribute"
msgstr "`link_section` 属性"

#: src/abi.md:88
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.link_section.intro\\] The _`link_section` attribute_ specifies the "
"section of the object file that a [function](items/functions.md) or [static]"
"(items/static-items.md)'s content will be placed into."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.link_section.intro\\] *`link_section` 属性*指定[函数](items/"
"functions.md)或 [static](items/static-items.md) 的内容将被放入目标文件的哪个"
"节。"

#: src/abi.md:91
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.link_section.syntax\\] The `link_section` attribute uses the \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntax to specify the section name."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.link_section.syntax\\] `link_section` 属性使用 \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] 语法来指定节名称。"

#: src/abi.md:98
msgid "\".example_section\""
msgstr "\".example_section\""

#: src/abi.md:103
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.link_section.unsafe\\] This attribute is unsafe as it allows users "
"to place data and code into sections of memory not expecting them, such as "
"mutable data into read-only areas."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.link_section.unsafe\\] 此属性是 unsafe 的，因为它允许用户将数据和代码"
"放入并不预期它们的内存节中，例如将可变数据放入只读区域。"

#: src/abi.md:106
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.link_section.duplicates\\] Only the first use of `link_section` on "
"an item has effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.link_section.duplicates\\] 在一个项上，只有第一次使用 `link_section` "
"会生效。"

#: src/abi.md:112
msgid "r\\[abi.link_section.edition2024\\]"
msgstr "r\\[abi.link_section.edition2024\\]"

#: src/abi.md:113
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] Before the 2024 edition it is allowed to use the "
"`link_section` attribute without the `unsafe` qualification."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] 在 2024 edition 之前，允许在不带 `unsafe` 限定的情况下使"
"用 `link_section` 属性。"

#: src/abi.md:116
msgid "r\\[abi.export_name\\]"
msgstr "r\\[abi.export_name\\]"

#: src/abi.md:117
msgid "The `export_name` attribute"
msgstr "`export_name` 属性"

#: src/abi.md:119
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.export_name.intro\\] The _`export_name` attribute_ specifies the "
"name of the symbol that will be exported on a [function](items/functions.md) "
"or [static](items/static-items.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.export_name.intro\\] *`export_name` 属性*指定将在[函数](items/"
"functions.md)或 [static](items/static-items.md) 上导出的符号名称。"

#: src/abi.md:122
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.export_name.syntax\\] The `export_name `attribute uses the \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntax to specify the symbol name."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.export_name.syntax\\] `export_name` 属性使用 \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] "
"语法来指定符号名称。"

#: src/abi.md:126
msgid "\"exported_symbol_name\""
msgstr "\"exported_symbol_name\""

#: src/abi.md:130
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.export_name.unsafe\\] This attribute is unsafe as a symbol with a "
"custom name may collide with another symbol with the same name (or with a "
"well-known symbol), leading to undefined behavior."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.export_name.unsafe\\] 此属性是 unsafe 的，因为具有自定义名称的符号可"
"能会与同名的另一个符号（或知名符号）发生冲突，从而导致未定义行为。"

#: src/abi.md:133
msgid ""
"r\\[abi.export_name.duplicates\\] Only the first use of `export_name` on an "
"item has effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[abi.export_name.duplicates\\] 在一个项上，只有第一次使用 `export_name` 会"
"生效。"

#: src/abi.md:139
msgid "r\\[abi.export_name.edition2024\\]"
msgstr "r\\[abi.export_name.edition2024\\]"

#: src/abi.md:140
msgid ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] Before the 2024 edition it is allowed to use the "
"`export_name` attribute without the `unsafe` qualification."
msgstr ""
"\\[!EDITION-2024\\] 在 2024 edition 之前，允许在不带 `unsafe` 限定的情况下使"
"用 `export_name` 属性。"

#: src/runtime.md:1
msgid "r\\[runtime\\]"
msgstr "r\\[runtime\\]"

#: src/runtime.md:4
msgid ""
"This section documents features that define some aspects of the Rust runtime."
msgstr "本节记录定义 Rust 运行时某些方面的特性。"

#: src/runtime.md:7
msgid "r\\[runtime.global_allocator\\]"
msgstr "r\\[runtime.global_allocator\\]"

#: src/runtime.md:8
msgid "The `global_allocator` attribute"
msgstr "`global_allocator` 属性"

#: src/runtime.md:10
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.intro\\] The _`global_allocator` \\[attribute\\]"
"\\[attributes\\]_ selects a \\[memory allocator\\]\\[std::alloc\\]."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.intro\\] *`global_allocator` \\[属性\\]\\"
"[attributes\\]* 会选择一个\\[内存分配器\\]\\[std::alloc\\]。"

#: src/runtime.md:33
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.syntax\\] The `global_allocator` attribute uses "
"the \\[MetaWord\\] syntax."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.syntax\\] `global_allocator` 属性使用 \\"
"[MetaWord\\] 语法。"

#: src/runtime.md:36
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.allowed-positions\\] The `global_allocator` "
"attribute may only be applied to a [static item](items/static-items.md) "
"whose type implements the [`GlobalAlloc`](alloc::alloc::GlobalAlloc) trait."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.allowed-positions\\] `global_allocator` 属性只能"
"应用于类型实现 [`GlobalAlloc`](alloc::alloc::GlobalAlloc) trait 的[静态项]"
"(items/static-items.md)。"

#: src/runtime.md:39
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.duplicates\\] The `global_allocator` attribute "
"may only be used once on an item."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.duplicates\\] `global_allocator` 属性在一个项上"
"只能使用一次。"

#: src/runtime.md:42
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.single\\] The `global_allocator` attribute may "
"only be used once in the crate graph."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.single\\] `global_allocator` 属性在 crate 图中只"
"能使用一次。"

#: src/runtime.md:45
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.stdlib\\] The `global_allocator` attribute is "
"exported from the \\[standard library prelude\\]\\[core::prelude::v1\\]."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.global_allocator.stdlib\\] `global_allocator` 属性从\\[标准库 "
"prelude\\]\\[core::prelude::v1\\]中导出。"

#: src/runtime.md:49
msgid "r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem\\]"
msgstr "r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem\\]"

#: src/runtime.md:50
msgid "The `windows_subsystem` attribute"
msgstr "`windows_subsystem` 属性"

#: src/runtime.md:52
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.intro\\] The _`windows_subsystem` \\"
"[attribute\\]\\[attributes\\]_ sets the [subsystem](https://"
"msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/fcc1zstk.aspx) when linking on a Windows "
"target."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.intro\\] *`windows_subsystem` \\[属性\\]\\"
"[attributes\\]* 会在链接 Windows 目标时设置[子系统](https://"
"msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/fcc1zstk.aspx)。"

#: src/runtime.md:60
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.syntax\\] The `windows_subsystem` attribute "
"uses the \\[MetaNameValueStr\\] syntax. Accepted values are `\"console\"` "
"and `\"windows\"`."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.syntax\\] `windows_subsystem` 属性使用 \\"
"[MetaNameValueStr\\] 语法。接受的值为 `\"console\"` 和 `\"windows\"`。"

#: src/runtime.md:63
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.allowed-positions\\] The `windows_subsystem` "
"attribute may only be applied to the crate root."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.allowed-positions\\] `windows_subsystem` 属性只"
"能应用于 crate 根。"

#: src/runtime.md:66
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.duplicates\\] Only the first use of "
"`windows_subsystem` has effect."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.duplicates\\] 只有第一次使用 "
"`windows_subsystem` 会生效。"

#: src/runtime.md:72
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.ignored\\] The `windows_subsystem` attribute "
"is ignored on non-Windows targets and non-`bin` [crate types](linkage.md)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.ignored\\] `windows_subsystem` 属性在非 "
"Windows 目标和非 `bin` [crate 类型](linkage.md)上会被忽略。"

#: src/runtime.md:75
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.console\\] The `\"console\"` subsystem is the "
"default. If a console process is run from an existing console then it will "
"be attached to that console; otherwise a new console window will be created."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.console\\] `\"console\"` 子系统是默认值。如果控"
"制台进程从已有控制台运行，它会附加到该控制台；否则会创建一个新的控制台窗口。"

#: src/runtime.md:78
msgid ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.windows\\] The `\"windows\"` subsystem will "
"run detached from any existing console."
msgstr ""
"r\\[runtime.windows_subsystem.windows\\] `\"windows\"` 子系统会以脱离任何已有"
"控制台的方式运行。"

#: src/runtime.md:81
msgid ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] The `\"windows\"` subsystem is commonly used by GUI applications "
"that do not want to display a console window on startup."
msgstr ""
"\\[!NOTE\\] `\"windows\"` 子系统通常由不希望在启动时显示控制台窗口的 GUI 应用"
"程序使用。"

