#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:1
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:2
msgid "Appendix: Macro follow-set ambiguity formal specification"
msgstr "附录：宏 follow 集歧义形式化规约"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:4
msgid ""
"This page documents the formal specification of the follow rules for [Macros "
"By Example](macros-by-example.md). They were originally specified in [RFC "
"550](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/0550-macro-future-"
"proofing.md), from which the bulk of this text is copied, and expanded upon "
"in subsequent RFCs."
msgstr ""
"本页记录 [Macros By Example](macros-by-example.md) 的 follow 规则的形式化规"
"约。它们最初在 [RFC 550](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/"
"0550-macro-future-proofing.md) 中规定，本文大部分内容复制自该 RFC，并在后续 "
"RFC 中有所扩展。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:6
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:7
msgid "Definitions & conventions"
msgstr "定义与约定"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:9
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.defs\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.defs\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:10
msgid "`macro`: anything invocable as `foo!(...)` in source code."
msgstr "`macro`：源代码中任何可作为 `foo!(...)` 调用的东西。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:11
msgid "`MBE`: macro-by-example, a macro defined by `macro_rules`."
msgstr "`MBE`：macro-by-example，即由 `macro_rules` 定义的宏。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:12
msgid ""
"`matcher`: the left-hand-side of a rule in a `macro_rules` invocation, or a "
"subportion thereof."
msgstr "`matcher`：`macro_rules` 调用中某条规则的左侧，或其子部分。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:13
msgid ""
"`macro parser`: the bit of code in the Rust parser that will parse the input "
"using a grammar derived from all of the matchers."
msgstr ""
"`macro parser`：Rust 解析器中的一段代码，它会使用从所有 matcher 派生出的文法"
"来解析输入。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:14
msgid ""
"`fragment`: The class of Rust syntax that a given matcher will accept (or "
"\"match\")."
msgstr "`fragment`：给定 matcher 会接受（或“匹配”）的一类 Rust 语法。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:15
msgid "`repetition` : a fragment that follows a regular repeating pattern"
msgstr "`repetition`：遵循规则重复模式的 fragment"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:16
msgid ""
"`NT`: non-terminal, the various \"meta-variables\" or repetition matchers "
"that can appear in a matcher, specified in MBE syntax with a leading `$` "
"character."
msgstr ""
"`NT`：非终结符，即可以出现在 matcher 中的各种“元变量”或 repetition matcher，"
"在 MBE 语法中用前导 `$` 字符指定。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:17
msgid ""
"`simple NT`: a \"meta-variable\" non-terminal (further discussion below)."
msgstr "`simple NT`：“元变量”非终结符（下文会进一步讨论）。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:18
msgid ""
"`complex NT`: a repetition matching non-terminal, specified via repetition "
"operators (`*`, `+`, `?`)."
msgstr ""
"`complex NT`：进行重复匹配的非终结符，通过 repetition operator（`*`、`+`、`?"
"`）指定。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:19
msgid ""
"`token`: an atomic element of a matcher; i.e. identifiers, operators, open/"
"close delimiters, _and_ simple NT's."
msgstr ""
"`token`：matcher 的原子元素；即标识符、运算符、开/闭分隔符，*以及* simple "
"NT。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:20
msgid ""
"`token tree`: a tree structure formed from tokens (the leaves), complex "
"NT's, and finite sequences of token trees."
msgstr ""
"`token tree`：由 token（叶子）、complex NT 和 token tree 的有限序列形成的树结"
"构。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:21
msgid ""
"`delimiter token`: a token that is meant to divide the end of one fragment "
"and the start of the next fragment."
msgstr ""
"`delimiter token`：用于分隔一个 fragment 的结尾和下一个 fragment 的开头的 "
"token。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:22
msgid ""
"`separator token`: an optional delimiter token in an complex NT that "
"separates each pair of elements in the matched repetition."
msgstr ""
"`separator token`：complex NT 中可选的 delimiter token，用于分隔匹配到的 "
"repetition 中每一对元素。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:23
msgid "`separated complex NT`: a complex NT that has its own separator token."
msgstr "`separated complex NT`：拥有自身 separator token 的 complex NT。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:24
msgid ""
"`delimited sequence`: a sequence of token trees with appropriate open- and "
"close-delimiters at the start and end of the sequence."
msgstr ""
"`delimited sequence`：token tree 的序列，其序列开头和结尾带有适当的开分隔符和"
"闭分隔符。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:25
msgid ""
"`empty fragment`: The class of invisible Rust syntax that separates tokens, "
"i.e. whitespace, or (in some lexical contexts), the empty token sequence."
msgstr ""
"`empty fragment`：分隔 token 的不可见 Rust 语法类别，即空白，或（在某些词法上"
"下文中）空 token 序列。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:26
msgid ""
"`fragment specifier`: The identifier in a simple NT that specifies which "
"fragment the NT accepts."
msgstr ""
"`fragment specifier`：simple NT 中指定该 NT 接受哪种 fragment 的标识符。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:27
msgid "`language`: a context-free language."
msgstr "`language`：上下文无关语言。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:37
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.matcher\\] `(start $foo:expr $($i:ident),* "
"end)` is a matcher. The whole matcher is a delimited sequence (with open- "
"and close-delimiters `(` and `)`), and `$foo` and `$i` are simple NT's with "
"`expr` and `ident` as their respective fragment specifiers."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.matcher\\] `(start $foo:expr $($i:ident),* "
"end)` 是一个 matcher。整个 matcher 是一个 delimited sequence（带有开分隔符 "
"`(` 和闭分隔符 `)`），而 `$foo` 和 `$i` 是 simple NT，其各自的 fragment "
"specifier 分别为 `expr` 和 `ident`。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:40
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.complex-nt\\] `$(i:ident),*` is _also_ an NT; "
"it is a complex NT that matches a comma-separated repetition of identifiers. "
"The `,` is the separator token for the complex NT; it occurs in between each "
"pair of elements (if any) of the matched fragment."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.complex-nt\\] `$(i:ident),*` *也是* 一个 NT；"
"它是一个 complex NT，匹配由逗号分隔的标识符 repetition。`,` 是该 complex NT "
"的 separator token；它出现在匹配到的 fragment 中每一对元素（如果有）之间。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:43
msgid ""
"Another example of a complex NT is `$(hi $e:expr ;)+`, which matches any "
"fragment of the form `hi <expr>; hi <expr>; ...` where `hi <expr>;` occurs "
"at least once. Note that this complex NT does not have a dedicated separator "
"token."
msgstr ""
"complex NT 的另一个例子是 `$(hi $e:expr ;)+`，它匹配形式为 `hi <expr>; hi "
"<expr>; ...` 的任何 fragment，其中 `hi <expr>;` 至少出现一次。注意，这个 "
"complex NT 没有专用的 separator token。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:45
msgid ""
"(Note that Rust's parser ensures that delimited sequences always occur with "
"proper nesting of token tree structure and correct matching of open- and "
"close-delimiters.)"
msgstr ""
"（注意，Rust 的解析器会确保 delimited sequence 总是以 token tree 结构的正确嵌"
"套和开/闭分隔符的正确匹配出现。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:47
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.vars\\] We will tend to use the variable "
"\"M\" to stand for a matcher, variables \"t\" and \"u\" for arbitrary "
"individual tokens, and the variables \"tt\" and \"uu\" for arbitrary token "
"trees. (The use of \"tt\" does present potential ambiguity with its "
"additional role as a fragment specifier; but it will be clear from context "
"which interpretation is meant.)"
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.vars\\] 我们通常使用变量 \"M\" 表示 matcher，"
"变量 \"t\" 和 \"u\" 表示任意单个 token，变量 \"tt\" 和 \"uu\" 表示任意 token "
"tree。（\"tt\" 的使用确实会因其还作为 fragment specifier 而带来潜在歧义；但从"
"上下文可以清楚看出所指的是哪种解释。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:50
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.set\\] \"SEP\" will range over separator "
"tokens, \"OP\" over the repetition operators `*`, `+`, and `?`, \"OPEN\"/"
"\"CLOSE\" over matching token pairs surrounding a delimited sequence (e.g. "
"`[` and `]`)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.set\\] \"SEP\" 的取值范围是 separator token，"
"\"OP\" 的取值范围是 repetition operator `*`、`+` 和 `?`，\"OPEN\"/\"CLOSE\" "
"的取值范围是围绕 delimited sequence 的匹配 token 对（例如 `[` 和 `]`）。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:53
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.sequence-vars\\] Greek letters \"α\" \"β\" "
"\"γ\" \"δ\"  stand for potentially empty token-tree sequences. (However, the "
"Greek letter \"ε\" (epsilon) has a special role in the presentation and does "
"not stand for a token-tree sequence.)"
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.convention.sequence-vars\\] 希腊字母 \"α\" \"β\" \"γ\" "
"\"δ\" 表示可能为空的 token-tree 序列。（不过，希腊字母 \"ε\"（epsilon）在此表"
"述中具有特殊角色，并不表示 token-tree 序列。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:56
msgid ""
"This Greek letter convention is usually just employed when the presence of a "
"sequence is a technical detail; in particular, when we wish to _emphasize_ "
"that we are operating on a sequence of token-trees, we will use the notation "
"\"tt ...\" for the sequence, not a Greek letter."
msgstr ""
"这种希腊字母约定通常只在序列的存在属于技术细节时使用；特别是，当我们希望 *强"
"调* 正在操作 token-tree 序列时，会使用 \"tt ...\" 这一记号表示该序列，而不是"
"使用希腊字母。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:58
msgid ""
"Note that a matcher is merely a token tree. A \"simple NT\", as mentioned "
"above, is an meta-variable NT; thus it is a non-repetition. For example, "
"`$foo:ty` is a simple NT but `$($foo:ty)+` is a complex NT."
msgstr ""
"注意，matcher 只不过是一个 token tree。如上所述，\"simple NT\" 是元变量 NT；"
"因此它不是 repetition。例如，`$foo:ty` 是 simple NT，但 `$($foo:ty)+` 是 "
"complex NT。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:60
msgid ""
"Note also that in the context of this formalism, the term \"token\" "
"generally _includes_ simple NTs."
msgstr ""
"还要注意，在此形式化体系的上下文中，术语 \"token\" 通常 *包括* simple NT。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:62
msgid ""
"Finally, it is useful for the reader to keep in mind that according to the "
"definitions of this formalism, no simple NT matches the empty fragment, and "
"likewise no token matches the empty fragment of Rust syntax. (Thus, the "
"_only_ NT that can match the empty fragment is a complex NT.) This is not "
"actually true, because the `vis` matcher can match an empty fragment. Thus, "
"for the purposes of the formalism, we will treat `$v:vis` as actually being "
"`$($v:vis)?`, with a requirement that the matcher match an empty fragment."
msgstr ""
"最后，读者最好记住，按照此形式化体系的定义，没有 simple NT 会匹配空片段，同样"
"也没有 token 会匹配 Rust 语法中的空片段。（因此，*唯一* 能够匹配空片段的 NT "
"是 complex NT。）这实际上并不正确，因为 `vis` matcher 可以匹配空片段。因此，"
"出于形式化体系的目的，我们会把 `$v:vis` 视为实际上是 `$($v:vis)?`，并要求该 "
"matcher 匹配空片段。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:64
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:65
msgid "The matcher invariants"
msgstr "matcher 不变式"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:67
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant.list\\] To be valid, a matcher must meet the "
"following three invariants. The definitions of FIRST and FOLLOW are "
"described later."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant.list\\] 要成为有效 matcher，必须满足以下三个不"
"变式。FIRST 和 FOLLOW 的定义稍后描述。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:70
msgid ""
"For any two successive token tree sequences in a matcher `M` (i.e. `M = ... "
"tt uu ...`) with `uu ...` nonempty, we must have FOLLOW(`... tt`) ∪ {ε} ⊇ "
"FIRST(`uu ...`)."
msgstr ""
"对于 matcher `M` 中任意两个连续的 token tree 序列（即 `M = ... tt uu ...`）"
"且 `uu ...` 非空时，必须有 FOLLOW(`... tt`) ∪ {ε} ⊇ FIRST(`uu ...`)。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:71
msgid ""
"For any separated complex NT in a matcher, `M = ... $(tt ...) SEP OP ...`, "
"we must have `SEP` ∈ FOLLOW(`tt ...`)."
msgstr ""
"对于 matcher 中的任意 separated complex NT，`M = ... $(tt ...) SEP OP ...`，"
"必须有 `SEP` ∈ FOLLOW(`tt ...`)。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:72
msgid ""
"For an unseparated complex NT in a matcher, `M = ... $(tt ...) OP ...`, if "
"OP = `*` or `+`, we must have FOLLOW(`tt ...`) ⊇ FIRST(`tt ...`)."
msgstr ""
"对于 matcher 中的 unseparated complex NT，`M = ... $(tt ...) OP ...`，如果 "
"OP = `*` 或 `+`，则必须有 FOLLOW(`tt ...`) ⊇ FIRST(`tt ...`)。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:74
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant.follow-matcher\\] The first invariant says "
"that whatever actual token that comes after a matcher, if any, must be "
"somewhere in the predetermined follow set.  This ensures that a legal macro "
"definition will continue to assign the same determination as to where `... "
"tt` ends and `uu ...` begins, even as new syntactic forms are added to the "
"language."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant.follow-matcher\\] 第一个不变式说明，matcher 之"
"后出现的任何实际 token（如果有）都必须位于预先确定的 follow 集中。这确保合法"
"的宏定义即使在语言加入新的语法形式之后，也会继续对 `... tt` 在何处结束以及 "
"`uu ...` 在何处开始作出相同判断。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:77
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant.separated-complex-nt\\] The second invariant "
"says that a separated complex NT must use a separator token that is part of "
"the predetermined follow set for the internal contents of the NT. This "
"ensures that a legal macro definition will continue to parse an input "
"fragment into the same delimited sequence of `tt ...`'s, even as new "
"syntactic forms are added to the language."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant.separated-complex-nt\\] 第二个不变式说明，"
"separated complex NT 必须使用一个 separator token，且该 token 是该 NT 内部内"
"容的预定 follow 集的一部分。这确保合法的宏定义即使在语言加入新的语法形式之"
"后，也会继续把输入 fragment 解析为相同的 `tt ...` delimited sequence。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:80
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant.unseparated-complex-nt\\] The third invariant "
"says that when we have a complex NT that can match two or more copies of the "
"same thing with no separation in between, it must be permissible for them to "
"be placed next to each other as per the first invariant. This invariant also "
"requires they be nonempty, which eliminates a possible ambiguity."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.invariant.unseparated-complex-nt\\] 第三个不变式说明，当 "
"complex NT 可以匹配同一事物的两个或更多副本且它们之间没有分隔时，按照第一个不"
"变式，必须允许它们彼此相邻放置。这个不变式还要求它们为非空，从而消除一种可能"
"的歧义。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:83
msgid ""
"**NOTE: The third invariant is currently unenforced due to historical "
"oversight and significant reliance on the behaviour. It is currently "
"undecided what to do about this going forward. Macros that do not respect "
"the behaviour may become invalid in a future edition of Rust. See the "
"[tracking issue](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/56575).**"
msgstr ""
"**注意：由于历史疏忽以及对该行为存在大量依赖，第三个不变式目前尚未强制执行。"
"今后如何处理这一点目前尚未决定。不遵守该行为的宏可能会在 Rust 的未来 edition "
"中变为无效。参见 [tracking issue](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/"
"56575)。**"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:85
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:86
msgid "FIRST and FOLLOW, informally"
msgstr "FIRST 和 FOLLOW 的非正式说明"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:88
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.intro\\] A given matcher M maps to three sets: "
"FIRST(M), LAST(M) and FOLLOW(M)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.intro\\] 给定 matcher M 映射到三个集合：FIRST(M)、"
"LAST(M) 和 FOLLOW(M)。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:91
msgid ""
"Each of the three sets is made up of tokens. FIRST(M) and LAST(M) may also "
"contain a distinguished non-token element ε (\"epsilon\"), which indicates "
"that M can match the empty fragment. (But FOLLOW(M) is always just a set of "
"tokens.)"
msgstr ""
"这三个集合都由 token 组成。FIRST(M) 和 LAST(M) 还可以包含一个特殊的非 token "
"元素 ε（\"epsilon\"），表示 M 可以匹配空片段。（但 FOLLOW(M) 始终只是 token "
"集合。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:93
msgid "Informally:"
msgstr "非正式地说："

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:95
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.first\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.first\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:96
msgid ""
"FIRST(M): collects the tokens potentially used first when matching a "
"fragment to M."
msgstr "FIRST(M)：收集把 fragment 与 M 匹配时可能首先使用的 token。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:98
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.last\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.last\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:99
msgid ""
"LAST(M): collects the tokens potentially used last when matching a fragment "
"to M."
msgstr "LAST(M)：收集把 fragment 与 M 匹配时可能最后使用的 token。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:101
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.follow\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.follow\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:102
msgid ""
"FOLLOW(M): the set of tokens allowed to follow immediately after some "
"fragment matched by M."
msgstr "FOLLOW(M)：允许紧跟在某个由 M 匹配的 fragment 之后的 token 集合。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:104
msgid ""
"In other words: t ∈ FOLLOW(M) if and only if there exists (potentially "
"empty) token sequences α, β, γ, δ where:"
msgstr ""
"换言之：t ∈ FOLLOW(M) 当且仅当存在（可能为空的）token 序列 α、β、γ、δ，使得："

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:106
msgid "M matches β,"
msgstr "M 匹配 β，"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:108
msgid "t matches γ, and"
msgstr "t 匹配 γ，并且"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:110
msgid "The concatenation α β γ δ is a parseable Rust program."
msgstr "拼接结果 α β γ δ 是可解析的 Rust 程序。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:112
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.universe\\] We use the shorthand ANYTOKEN to denote "
"the set of all tokens (including simple NTs). For example, if any token is "
"legal after a matcher M, then FOLLOW(M) = ANYTOKEN."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.universe\\] 我们使用简写 ANYTOKEN 表示所有 token（包"
"括 simple NT）的集合。例如，如果在 matcher M 之后任何 token 都是合法的，则 "
"FOLLOW(M) = ANYTOKEN。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:115
msgid ""
"(To review one's understanding of the above informal descriptions, the "
"reader at this point may want to jump ahead to the [examples of FIRST/LAST]"
"(#examples-of-first-and-last) before reading their formal definitions.)"
msgstr ""
"（为了检验对上述非正式描述的理解，读者此时可以先跳到 [FIRST/LAST 的示例]"
"(#examples-of-first-and-last)，再阅读它们的形式化定义。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:117
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:118
msgid "FIRST, LAST"
msgstr "FIRST、LAST"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:120
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.intro\\] Below are formal inductive definitions "
"for FIRST and LAST."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.intro\\] 下面是 FIRST 和 LAST 的形式化归纳定义。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:123
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.notation\\] \"A ∪ B\" denotes set union, \"A ∩ "
"B\" denotes set intersection, and \"A \\ B\" denotes set difference (i.e. "
"all elements of A that are not present in B)."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.notation\\] \"A ∪ B\" 表示集合并集，\"A ∩ B\" 表"
"示集合交集，\"A \\ B\" 表示集合差集（即 A 中所有不在 B 中出现的元素）。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:126
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:127
msgid "FIRST"
msgstr "FIRST"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:129
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first.intro\\] FIRST(M) is defined by case "
"analysis on the sequence M and the structure of its first token-tree (if "
"any):"
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first.intro\\] FIRST(M) 通过对序列 M 及其第一个 "
"token-tree（如果有）的结构分类讨论来定义："

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:132
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first.epsilon\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first.epsilon\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:133
msgid "if M is the empty sequence, then FIRST(M) = { ε },"
msgstr "如果 M 是空序列，则 FIRST(M) = { ε }，"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:135
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first.token\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first.token\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:136
msgid "if M starts with a token t, then FIRST(M) = { t },"
msgstr "如果 M 以 token t 开头，则 FIRST(M) = { t }，"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:138
msgid ""
"(Note: this covers the case where M starts with a delimited token-tree "
"sequence, `M = OPEN tt ... CLOSE ...`, in which case `t = OPEN` and thus "
"FIRST(M) = { `OPEN` }.)"
msgstr ""
"（注意：这涵盖 M 以 delimited token-tree 序列开头的情况，`M = OPEN tt ... "
"CLOSE ...`，此时 `t = OPEN`，因此 FIRST(M) = { `OPEN` }。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:140
msgid ""
"(Note: this critically relies on the property that no simple NT matches the "
"empty fragment.)"
msgstr "（注意：这关键依赖于没有 simple NT 会匹配空片段这一性质。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:142
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first.complex\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.first.complex\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:143
msgid ""
"Otherwise, M is a token-tree sequence starting with a complex NT: `M = $"
"( tt ... ) OP α`, or `M = $( tt ... ) SEP OP α`, (where `α` is the "
"(potentially empty) sequence of token trees for the rest of the matcher)."
msgstr ""
"否则，M 是以 complex NT 开头的 token-tree 序列：`M = $( tt ... ) OP α`，或 "
"`M = $( tt ... ) SEP OP α`，（其中 `α` 是 matcher 其余部分的 token tree 序"
"列，可能为空）。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:145
msgid ""
"Let SEP\\_SET(M) = { SEP } if SEP is present and ε ∈ FIRST(`tt ...`); "
"otherwise SEP\\_SET(M) = {}."
msgstr ""
"令 SEP\\_SET(M) = { SEP }，如果 SEP 存在且 ε ∈ FIRST(`tt ...`)；否则 "
"SEP\\_SET(M) = {}。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:147
msgid ""
"Let ALPHA\\_SET(M) = FIRST(`α`) if OP = `*` or `?` and ALPHA\\_SET(M) = {} "
"if OP = `+`."
msgstr ""
"令 ALPHA\\_SET(M) = FIRST(`α`)，如果 OP = `*` 或 `?`；如果 OP = `+`，则 "
"ALPHA\\_SET(M) = {}。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:148
msgid "FIRST(M) = (FIRST(`tt ...`) \\\\ {ε}) ∪ SEP\\_SET(M) ∪ ALPHA\\_SET(M)."
msgstr ""
"FIRST(M) = (FIRST(`tt ...`) \\\\ {ε}) ∪ SEP\\_SET(M) ∪ ALPHA\\_SET(M)。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:150
msgid ""
"The definition for complex NTs deserves some justification. SEP\\_SET(M) "
"defines the possibility that the separator could be a valid first token for "
"M, which happens when there is a separator defined and the repeated fragment "
"could be empty. ALPHA\\_SET(M) defines the possibility that the complex NT "
"could be empty, meaning that M's valid first tokens are those of the "
"following token-tree sequences `α`. This occurs when either `*` or `?` is "
"used, in which case there could be zero repetitions. In theory, this could "
"also occur if `+` was used with a potentially-empty repeating fragment, but "
"this is forbidden by the third invariant."
msgstr ""
"complex NT 的定义值得作一些说明。SEP\\_SET(M) 定义了 separator 可能是 M 的有"
"效首 token 的可能性，这发生在定义了 separator 且重复 fragment 可能为空时。"
"ALPHA\\_SET(M) 定义了 complex NT 可能为空的可能性，意味着 M 的有效首 token 是"
"后续 token-tree 序列 `α` 的首 token。使用 `*` 或 `?` 时会出现这种情况，因为可"
"能存在零次重复。理论上，如果 `+` 与可能为空的 repeating fragment 一起使用，也"
"可能出现这种情况，但第三个不变式禁止这样做。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:152
msgid ""
"From there, clearly FIRST(M) can include any token from SEP\\_SET(M) or "
"ALPHA\\_SET(M), and if the complex NT match is nonempty, then any token "
"starting FIRST(`tt ...`) could work too. The last piece to consider is ε. "
"SEP\\_SET(M) and FIRST(`tt ...`) \\ {ε} cannot contain ε, but ALPHA\\_SET(M) "
"could. Hence, this definition allows M to accept ε if and only if ε ∈ "
"ALPHA\\_SET(M) does. This is correct because for M to accept ε in the "
"complex NT case, both the complex NT and α must accept it. If OP = `+`, "
"meaning that the complex NT cannot be empty, then by definition ε ∉ "
"ALPHA\\_SET(M). Otherwise, the complex NT can accept zero repetitions, and "
"then ALPHA\\_SET(M) = FOLLOW(`α`). So this definition is correct with "
"respect to \\varepsilon as well."
msgstr ""
"由此可见，FIRST(M) 显然可以包含 SEP\\_SET(M) 或 ALPHA\\_SET(M) 中的任何 "
"token；如果 complex NT 匹配结果非空，那么 FIRST(`tt ...`) 中作为起始的任何 "
"token 也可以起作用。最后要考虑的是 ε。SEP\\_SET(M) 和 FIRST(`tt ...`) \\ {ε} "
"不能包含 ε，但 ALPHA\\_SET(M) 可以。因此，当且仅当 ε ∈ ALPHA\\_SET(M) 时，此"
"定义才允许 M 接受 ε。这是正确的，因为在 complex NT 情况下，要让 M 接受 ε，"
"complex NT 和 α 都必须接受它。如果 OP = `+`，意味着 complex NT 不能为空，那么"
"根据定义 ε ∉ ALPHA\\_SET(M)。否则，complex NT 可以接受零次重复，于是 "
"ALPHA\\_SET(M) = FOLLOW(`α`)。所以这个定义对于 \\varepsilon 也是正确的。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:154
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:155
msgid "LAST"
msgstr "LAST"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:157
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.intro\\] LAST(M), defined by case analysis "
"on M itself (a sequence of token-trees):"
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.intro\\] LAST(M) 通过对 M 本身（一个 token-"
"tree 序列）分类讨论来定义："

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:160
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.empty\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.empty\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:161
msgid "if M is the empty sequence, then LAST(M) = { ε }"
msgstr "如果 M 是空序列，则 LAST(M) = { ε }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:163
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.token\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.token\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:164
msgid "if M is a singleton token t, then LAST(M) = { t }"
msgstr "如果 M 是单个 token t，则 LAST(M) = { t }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:166
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.rep-star\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.rep-star\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:167
msgid ""
"if M is the singleton complex NT repeating zero or more times, `M = $"
"( tt ... ) *`, or `M = $( tt ... ) SEP *`"
msgstr ""
"如果 M 是重复零次或多次的单个 complex NT，`M = $( tt ... ) *`，或 `M = $"
"( tt ... ) SEP *`"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:169 src/macro-ambiguity.md:178
msgid "Let sep_set = { SEP } if SEP present; otherwise sep_set = {}."
msgstr "如果 SEP 存在，则令 sep_set = { SEP }；否则 sep_set = {}。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:171 src/macro-ambiguity.md:180
msgid "if ε ∈ LAST(`tt ...`) then LAST(M) = LAST(`tt ...`) ∪ sep_set"
msgstr "如果 ε ∈ LAST(`tt ...`)，则 LAST(M) = LAST(`tt ...`) ∪ sep_set"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:173
msgid ""
"otherwise, the sequence `tt ...` must be non-empty; LAST(M) = LAST(`tt ...`) "
"∪ {ε}."
msgstr "否则，序列 `tt ...` 必须非空；LAST(M) = LAST(`tt ...`) ∪ {ε}。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:175
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.rep-plus\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.rep-plus\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:176
msgid ""
"if M is the singleton complex NT repeating one or more times, `M = $"
"( tt ... ) +`, or `M = $( tt ... ) SEP +`"
msgstr ""
"如果 M 是重复一次或多次的单个 complex NT，`M = $( tt ... ) +`，或 `M = $"
"( tt ... ) SEP +`"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:182
msgid ""
"otherwise, the sequence `tt ...` must be non-empty; LAST(M) = LAST(`tt ...`)"
msgstr "否则，序列 `tt ...` 必须非空；LAST(M) = LAST(`tt ...`)"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:184
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.rep-question\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.rep-question\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:185
msgid ""
"if M is the singleton complex NT repeating zero or one time, `M = $"
"( tt ...) ?`, then LAST(M) = LAST(`tt ...`) ∪ {ε}."
msgstr ""
"如果 M 是重复零次或一次的单个 complex NT，`M = $( tt ...) ?`，则 LAST(M) = "
"LAST(`tt ...`) ∪ {ε}。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:187
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.delim\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.delim\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:188
msgid ""
"if M is a delimited token-tree sequence `OPEN tt ... CLOSE`, then LAST(M) = "
"{ `CLOSE` }."
msgstr ""
"如果 M 是 delimited token-tree 序列 `OPEN tt ... CLOSE`，则 LAST(M) = "
"{ `CLOSE` }。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:190
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.sequence\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.last.sequence\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:191
msgid "if M is a non-empty sequence of token-trees `tt uu ...`,"
msgstr "如果 M 是非空 token-tree 序列 `tt uu ...`，"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:193
msgid ""
"If ε ∈ LAST(`uu ...`), then LAST(M) = LAST(`tt`) ∪ (LAST(`uu ...`) \\ { ε })."
msgstr ""
"如果 ε ∈ LAST(`uu ...`)，则 LAST(M) = LAST(`tt`) ∪ (LAST(`uu ...`) \\ "
"{ ε })。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:195
msgid ""
"Otherwise, the sequence `uu ...` must be non-empty; then LAST(M) = "
"LAST(`uu ...`)."
msgstr "否则，序列 `uu ...` 必须非空；此时 LAST(M) = LAST(`uu ...`)。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:197
msgid "Examples of FIRST and LAST"
msgstr "FIRST 和 LAST 的示例"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:199
msgid ""
"Below are some examples of FIRST and LAST. (Note in particular how the "
"special ε element is introduced and eliminated based on the interaction "
"between the pieces of the input.)"
msgstr ""
"下面是 FIRST 和 LAST 的一些示例。（请特别注意，特殊元素 ε 是如何基于输入各部"
"分之间的相互作用被引入和消除的。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:201
msgid ""
"Our first example is presented in a tree structure to elaborate on how the "
"analysis of the matcher composes. (Some of the simpler subtrees have been "
"elided.)"
msgstr ""
"第一个示例以树结构呈现，用来详细说明 matcher 的分析是如何组合起来的。（一些较"
"简单的子树已被省略。）"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:227
msgid "Thus:"
msgstr "因此："

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:229
msgid ""
"FIRST(`$($d:ident $e:expr );* $( $(h)* );* $( f ;)+ g`) = { `$d:ident`, `h`, "
"`;`, `f` }"
msgstr ""
"FIRST(`$($d:ident $e:expr );* $( $(h)* );* $( f ;)+ g`) = { `$d:ident`, `h`, "
"`;`, `f` }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:231
msgid "Note however that:"
msgstr "但请注意："

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:233
msgid ""
"FIRST(`$($d:ident $e:expr );* $( $(h)* );* $($( f ;)+ g)*`) = { `$d:ident`, "
"`h`, `;`, `f`, ε }"
msgstr ""
"FIRST(`$($d:ident $e:expr );* $( $(h)* );* $($( f ;)+ g)*`) = { `$d:ident`, "
"`h`, `;`, `f`, ε }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:235
msgid "Here are similar examples but now for LAST."
msgstr "下面是类似示例，不过这次针对 LAST。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:237
msgid "LAST(`$d:ident $e:expr`) = { `$e:expr` }"
msgstr "LAST(`$d:ident $e:expr`) = { `$e:expr` }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:238
msgid "LAST(`$( $d:ident $e:expr );*`) = { `$e:expr`, ε }"
msgstr "LAST(`$( $d:ident $e:expr );*`) = { `$e:expr`, ε }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:239
msgid "LAST(`$( $d:ident $e:expr );* $(h)*`) = { `$e:expr`, ε, `h` }"
msgstr "LAST(`$( $d:ident $e:expr );* $(h)*`) = { `$e:expr`, ε, `h` }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:240
msgid "LAST(`$( $d:ident $e:expr );* $(h)* $( f ;)+`) = { `;` }"
msgstr "LAST(`$( $d:ident $e:expr );* $(h)* $( f ;)+`) = { `;` }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:241
msgid "LAST(`$( $d:ident $e:expr );* $(h)* $( f ;)+ g`) = { `g` }"
msgstr "LAST(`$( $d:ident $e:expr );* $(h)* $( f ;)+ g`) = { `g` }"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:243
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:244
msgid "FOLLOW(M)"
msgstr "FOLLOW(M)"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:246
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.intro\\] Finally, the definition for "
"FOLLOW(M) is built up as follows. pat, expr, etc. represent simple "
"nonterminals with the given fragment specifier."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.intro\\] 最后，FOLLOW(M) 的定义按如下方式"
"构建。pat、expr 等表示带有给定 fragment specifier 的 simple nonterminal。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:249
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.pat\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.pat\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:250
msgid "FOLLOW(pat) = {`=>`, `,`, `=`, `|`, `if`, `in`}\\`."
msgstr "FOLLOW(pat) = {`=>`, `,`, `=`, `|`, `if`, `in`}\\`。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:252
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.expr-stmt\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.expr-stmt\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:253
msgid "FOLLOW(expr) = FOLLOW(expr_2021) = FOLLOW(stmt) =  {`=>`, `,`, `;`}\\`."
msgstr ""
"FOLLOW(expr) = FOLLOW(expr_2021) = FOLLOW(stmt) =  {`=>`, `,`, `;`}\\`。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:255
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.ty-path\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.ty-path\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:256
msgid ""
"FOLLOW(ty) = FOLLOW(path) = {`{`, `[`, `,`, `=>`, `:`, `=`, `>`, `>>`, `;`, "
"`|`, `as`, `where`, block nonterminals}."
msgstr ""
"FOLLOW(ty) = FOLLOW(path) = {`{`, `[`, `,`, `=>`, `:`, `=`, `>`, `>>`, `;`, "
"`|`, `as`, `where`, block nonterminal}。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:258
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.vis\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.vis\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:259
msgid ""
"FOLLOW(vis) = {`,`l any keyword or identifier except a non-raw `priv`; any "
"token that can begin a type; ident, ty, and path nonterminals}."
msgstr ""
"FOLLOW(vis) = {`,`l 除一个非 raw 的 `priv` 之外的任何关键字或标识符；任何可以"
"开始类型的 token；ident、ty 和 path nonterminal}。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:261
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.simple\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.simple\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:262
msgid ""
"FOLLOW(t) = ANYTOKEN for any other simple token, including block, ident, tt, "
"item, lifetime, literal and meta simple nonterminals, and all terminals."
msgstr ""
"对于任何其他 simple token，FOLLOW(t) = ANYTOKEN，包括 block、ident、tt、"
"item、lifetime、literal 和 meta simple nonterminal，以及所有 terminal。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:264
msgid "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.other-matcher\\]"
msgstr "r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.other-matcher\\]"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:265
msgid ""
"FOLLOW(M), for any other M, is defined as the intersection, as t ranges over "
"(LAST(M) \\ {ε}), of FOLLOW(t)."
msgstr ""
"对于任何其他 M，FOLLOW(M) 定义为当 t 遍历 (LAST(M) \\ {ε}) 时 FOLLOW(t) 的交"
"集。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:267
msgid ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.type-first\\] The tokens that can begin "
"a type are, as of this writing, {`(`, `[`, `!`, `*`, `&`, `&&`, `?`, "
"lifetimes, `>`, `>>`, `::`, any non-keyword identifier, `super`, `self`, "
"`Self`, `extern`, `crate`, `$crate`, `_`, `for`, `impl`, `fn`, `unsafe`, "
"`typeof`, `dyn`}, although this list may not be complete because people "
"won't always remember to update the appendix when new ones are added."
msgstr ""
"r\\[macro.ambiguity.sets.def.follow.type-first\\] 截至本文撰写时，可以开始一"
"个类型的 token 包括 {`(`, `[`, `!`, `*`, `&`, `&&`, `?`, lifetime, `>`, "
"`>>`, `::`, 任何非关键字标识符, `super`, `self`, `Self`, `extern`, `crate`, "
"`$crate`, `_`, `for`, `impl`, `fn`, `unsafe`, `typeof`, `dyn`}，不过这个列表"
"可能并不完整，因为新增此类 token 时人们并不总会记得更新本附录。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:270
msgid "Examples of FOLLOW for complex M:"
msgstr "complex M 的 FOLLOW 示例："

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:272
msgid "FOLLOW(`$( $d:ident $e:expr )*`) = FOLLOW(`$e:expr`)"
msgstr "FOLLOW(`$( $d:ident $e:expr )*`) = FOLLOW(`$e:expr`)"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:273
msgid ""
"FOLLOW(`$( $d:ident $e:expr )* $(;)*`) = FOLLOW(`$e:expr`) ∩ ANYTOKEN = "
"FOLLOW(`$e:expr`)"
msgstr ""
"FOLLOW(`$( $d:ident $e:expr )* $(;)*`) = FOLLOW(`$e:expr`) ∩ ANYTOKEN = "
"FOLLOW(`$e:expr`)"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:274
msgid "FOLLOW(`$( $d:ident $e:expr )* $(;)* $( f |)+`) = ANYTOKEN"
msgstr "FOLLOW(`$( $d:ident $e:expr )* $(;)* $( f |)+`) = ANYTOKEN"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:276
msgid "Examples of valid and invalid matchers"
msgstr "有效和无效 matcher 的示例"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:278
msgid ""
"With the above specification in hand, we can present arguments for why "
"particular matchers are legal and others are not."
msgstr ""
"有了上述规约，我们就可以说明为什么某些 matcher 是合法的，而另一些不是。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:280
msgid ""
"`($ty:ty < foo ,)` : illegal, because FIRST(`< foo ,`) = { `<` } ⊈ "
"FOLLOW(`ty`)"
msgstr ""
"`($ty:ty < foo ,)`：非法，因为 FIRST(`< foo ,`) = { `<` } ⊈ FOLLOW(`ty`)"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:282
msgid ""
"`($ty:ty , foo <)` : legal, because FIRST(`, foo <`) = { `,` }  is ⊆ "
"FOLLOW(`ty`)."
msgstr ""
"`($ty:ty , foo <)`：合法，因为 FIRST(`, foo <`) = { `,` } 是 ⊆ FOLLOW(`ty`)。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:284
msgid ""
"`($pa:pat $pb:pat $ty:ty ,)` : illegal, because FIRST(`$pb:pat $ty:ty ,`) = "
"{ `$pb:pat` } ⊈ FOLLOW(`pat`), and also FIRST(`$ty:ty ,`) = { `$ty:ty` } ⊈ "
"FOLLOW(`pat`)."
msgstr ""
"`($pa:pat $pb:pat $ty:ty ,)`：非法，因为 FIRST(`$pb:pat $ty:ty ,`) = "
"{ `$pb:pat` } ⊈ FOLLOW(`pat`)，并且 FIRST(`$ty:ty ,`) = { `$ty:ty` } 也 ⊈ "
"FOLLOW(`pat`)。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:286
msgid ""
"`( $($a:tt $b:tt)* ; )` : legal, because FIRST(`$b:tt`) = { `$b:tt` } is ⊆ "
"FOLLOW(`tt`) = ANYTOKEN, as is FIRST(`;`) = { `;` }."
msgstr ""
"`( $($a:tt $b:tt)* ; )`：合法，因为 FIRST(`$b:tt`) = { `$b:tt` } 是 ⊆ "
"FOLLOW(`tt`) = ANYTOKEN，FIRST(`;`) = { `;` } 也是如此。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:288
msgid ""
"`( $($t:tt),* , $(t:tt),* )` : legal,  (though any attempt to actually use "
"this macro will signal a local ambiguity error during expansion)."
msgstr ""
"`( $($t:tt),* , $(t:tt),* )`：合法，（但任何实际使用此宏的尝试都会在展开期间"
"报告局部歧义错误）。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:290
msgid ""
"`($ty:ty $(; not sep)* -)` : illegal, because FIRST(`$(; not sep)* -`) = "
"{ `;`, `-` } is not in FOLLOW(`ty`)."
msgstr ""
"`($ty:ty $(; not sep)* -)`：非法，因为 FIRST(`$(; not sep)* -`) = { `;`, `-"
"` } 不在 FOLLOW(`ty`) 中。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:292
msgid ""
"`($($ty:ty)-+)` : illegal, because separator `-` is not in FOLLOW(`ty`)."
msgstr "`($($ty:ty)-+)`：非法，因为 separator `-` 不在 FOLLOW(`ty`) 中。"

#: src/macro-ambiguity.md:294
msgid "`($($e:expr)*)` : illegal, because expr NTs are not in FOLLOW(expr NT)."
msgstr "`($($e:expr)*)`：非法，因为 expr NT 不在 FOLLOW(expr NT) 中。"

#: src/influences.md:3
msgid ""
"Rust is not a particularly original language, with design elements coming "
"from a wide range of sources. Some of these are listed below (including "
"elements that have since been removed):"
msgstr ""
"Rust 并不是一门特别原创的语言，其设计元素来自广泛的来源。下面列出了其中一些来"
"源（包括后来已经被移除的元素）："

#: src/influences.md:5
msgid ""
"SML, OCaml: algebraic data types, pattern matching, type inference, "
"semicolon statement separation"
msgstr "SML, OCaml：代数数据类型、模式匹配、类型推断、分号语句分隔"

#: src/influences.md:6
msgid ""
"C++: references, RAII, smart pointers, move semantics, monomorphization, "
"memory model"
msgstr "C++：引用、RAII、智能指针、移动语义、单态化、内存模型"

#: src/influences.md:7
msgid "ML Kit, Cyclone: region based memory management"
msgstr "ML Kit, Cyclone：基于区域的内存管理"

#: src/influences.md:8
msgid "Haskell (GHC): typeclasses, type families"
msgstr "Haskell (GHC)：类型类、类型族"

#: src/influences.md:9
msgid "Newsqueak, Alef, Limbo: channels, concurrency"
msgstr "Newsqueak, Alef, Limbo：通道、并发"

#: src/influences.md:10
msgid ""
"Erlang: message passing, thread failure, ~~linked thread failure~~, "
"~~lightweight concurrency~~"
msgstr "Erlang：消息传递、线程失败、~~链接线程失败~~、~~轻量级并发~~"

#: src/influences.md:11
msgid "Swift: optional bindings"
msgstr "Swift：可选绑定"

#: src/influences.md:12
msgid "Scheme: hygienic macros"
msgstr "Scheme：卫生宏"

#: src/influences.md:13
msgid "C#: attributes"
msgstr "C#：属性"

#: src/influences.md:14
msgid "Ruby: closure syntax, ~~block syntax~~"
msgstr "Ruby：闭包语法、~~块语法~~"

#: src/influences.md:15
msgid "NIL, Hermes: ~~typestate~~"
msgstr "NIL, Hermes：~~类型状态~~"

#: src/influences.md:16
msgid ""
"[Unicode Annex #31](http://www.unicode.org/reports/tr31/): identifier and "
"pattern syntax"
msgstr ""
"[Unicode Annex #31](http://www.unicode.org/reports/tr31/)：标识符和模式语法"

#: src/test-summary.md:3
msgid ""
"The following is a summary of the total tests that are linked to individual "
"rule identifiers within the reference."
msgstr "下面汇总了本参考中链接到各个规则标识符的测试总数。"

#: src/test-summary.md:5
