msgstr "{{summary-table}}"

#: src/glossary.md:3
msgid "r\\[glossary.ast\\]"
msgstr "r\\[glossary.ast\\]"

#: src/glossary.md:4
msgid "Abstract syntax tree"
msgstr "抽象语法树"

#: src/glossary.md:6
msgid ""
"An ‘abstract syntax tree’, or ‘AST’, is an intermediate representation of "
"the structure of the program when the compiler is compiling it."
msgstr "“抽象语法树”，或称 “AST”，是编译器编译程序时程序结构的一种中间表示。"

#: src/glossary.md:8
msgid "Alignment"
msgstr "对齐"

#: src/glossary.md:10
msgid ""
"The alignment of a value specifies what addresses values are preferred to "
"start at. Always a power of two. References to a value must be aligned. "
"[More](type-layout.md#size-and-alignment)."
msgstr ""
"值的对齐指定了值优先从哪些地址开始存放。它始终是 2 的幂。对值的引用必须是对齐"
"的。[更多信息](type-layout.md#size-and-alignment)。"

#: src/glossary.md:12
msgid "r\\[glossary.abi\\]"
msgstr "r\\[glossary.abi\\]"

#: src/glossary.md:15
msgid ""
"An _application binary interface_ (ABI) defines how compiled code interacts "
"with other compiled code. With [`extern` blocks](items.extern) and [`extern "
"fn`](items.fn.extern), _ABI strings_ affect:"
msgstr ""
"*应用程序二进制接口*（ABI）定义编译后的代码如何与其他编译后的代码交互。对于 "
"[`extern` 块](items.extern)和 [`extern fn`](items.fn.extern)，*ABI 字符串*会"
"影响："

#: src/glossary.md:17
msgid ""
"**Calling convention**: How function arguments are passed, values are "
"returned (e.g., in registers or on the stack), and who is responsible for "
"cleaning up the stack."
msgstr ""
"**调用约定**：函数实参如何传递、值如何返回（例如在寄存器中或在栈上），以及由"
"谁负责清理栈。"

#: src/glossary.md:18
msgid ""
"**Unwinding**: Whether stack unwinding is allowed. For example, the `\"C-"
"unwind\"` ABI allows unwinding across the FFI boundary, while the `\"C\"` "
"ABI does not."
msgstr ""
"**展开**：是否允许栈展开。例如，`\"C-unwind\"` ABI 允许跨 FFI 边界展开，而 "
"`\"C\"` ABI 不允许。"

#: src/glossary.md:20
msgid "Arity"
msgstr "元数"

#: src/glossary.md:22
msgid ""
"Arity refers to the number of arguments a function or operator takes. For "
"some examples, `f(2, 3)` and `g(4, 6)` have arity 2, while `h(8, 2, 6)` has "
"arity 3. The `!` operator has arity 1."
msgstr ""
"元数指函数或运算符接受的实参数量。例如，`f(2, 3)` 和 `g(4, 6)` 的元数为 2，"
"而 `h(8, 2, 6)` 的元数为 3。`!` 运算符的元数为 1。"

#: src/glossary.md:24
msgid "Array"
msgstr "数组"

#: src/glossary.md:26
msgid ""
"An array, sometimes also called a fixed-size array or an inline array, is a "
"value describing a collection of elements, each selected by an index that "
"can be computed at run time by the program. It occupies a contiguous region "
"of memory."
msgstr ""
"数组有时也称为固定大小数组或内联数组，是一个表示元素集合的值；每个元素由索引"
"选择，而该索引可由程序在运行时计算。数组占据一段连续的内存区域。"

#: src/glossary.md:28
msgid "Associated item"
msgstr "关联项"

#: src/glossary.md:30
msgid ""
"An associated item is an item that is associated with another item. "
"Associated items are defined in [implementations](items/implementations.md) "
"and declared in [traits](items/traits.md). Only functions, constants, and "
"type aliases can be associated. Contrast to a [free item](#free-item)."
msgstr ""
"关联项是与另一个项相关联的项。关联项定义在[实现](items/implementations.md)"
"中，并声明在 [trait](items/traits.md) 中。只有函数、常量和类型别名可以成为关"
"联项。对比[自由项](#free-item)。"

#: src/glossary.md:32
msgid "Blanket implementation"
msgstr "毯式实现"

#: src/glossary.md:34
msgid ""
"Any implementation where a type appears [uncovered](#uncovered-type). "
"`impl<T> Foo for T`, `impl<T> Bar<T> for T`, `impl<T> Bar<Vec<T>> for T`, "
"and `impl<T> Bar<T> for Vec<T>` are considered blanket impls. However, "
"`impl<T> Bar<Vec<T>> for Vec<T>` is not a blanket impl, as all instances of "
"`T` which appear in this `impl` are covered by `Vec`."
msgstr ""
"任何有某个类型以[未覆盖](#uncovered-type)形式出现的实现。`impl<T> Foo for "
"T`、`impl<T> Bar<T> for T`、`impl<T> Bar<Vec<T>> for T` 和 `impl<T> Bar<T> "
"for Vec<T>` 都被视为毯式 impl。不过，`impl<T> Bar<Vec<T>> for Vec<T>` 不是毯"
"式 impl，因为此 `impl` 中出现的所有 `T` 都由 `Vec` 覆盖。"

#: src/glossary.md:36
msgid "Bound"
msgstr "约束"

#: src/glossary.md:38
msgid ""
"Bounds are constraints on a type or trait. For example, if a bound is placed "
"on the argument a function takes, types passed to that function must abide "
"by that constraint."
msgstr ""
"约束是施加在类型或 trait 上的限制。例如，如果对函数接受的参数施加约束，则传递"
"给该函数的类型必须遵守该约束。"

#: src/glossary.md:40
msgid "Combinator"
msgstr "组合子"

#: src/glossary.md:42
msgid ""
"Combinators are higher-order functions that apply only functions and earlier "
"defined combinators to provide a result from its arguments. They can be used "
"to manage control flow in a modular fashion."
msgstr ""
"组合子是高阶函数，它们只应用函数和先前定义的组合子，根据它们的参数产生结果。"
"它们可用于以模块化方式管理控制流。"

#: src/glossary.md:44
msgid "Crate"
msgstr "crate"

#: src/glossary.md:46
msgid ""
"A crate is the unit of compilation and linking. There are different [types "
"of crates](linkage.md), such as libraries or executables. Crates may link "
"and refer to other library crates, called external crates. A crate has a "
"self-contained tree of [modules](items/modules.md), starting from an unnamed "
"root module called the crate root. [Items](items.md) may be made visible to "
"other crates by marking them as public in the crate root, including through "
"[paths](paths.md) of public modules. [More](crates-and-source-files.md)."
msgstr ""
"crate 是编译和链接的单位。crate 有不同的 [crate 类型](linkage.md)，例如库或可"
"执行文件。crate 可以链接并引用其他库 crate，这些库 crate 称为外部 crate。"
"crate 拥有一个自包含的[模块](items/modules.md)树，从一个未命名的根模块开始，"
"该根模块称为 crate 根。可以通过在 crate 根中将[项](items.md)标记为公开，使其"
"对其他 crate 可见；这也包括通过公开模块的[路径](paths.md)使其可见。[更多信息]"
"(crates-and-source-files.md)。"

#: src/glossary.md:48
msgid "Dispatch"
msgstr "分派"

#: src/glossary.md:50
msgid ""
"Dispatch is the mechanism to determine which specific version of code is "
"actually run when it involves polymorphism. Two major forms of dispatch are "
"static dispatch and dynamic dispatch. Rust supports dynamic dispatch through "
"the use of \\[trait objects\\]\\[type.trait-object\\]."
msgstr ""
"分派是在涉及多态时，确定实际运行代码的哪个具体版本的机制。分派的两种主要形式"
"是静态分派和动态分派。Rust 通过使用\\[trait 对象\\]\\[type.trait-object\\]支"
"持动态分派。"

#: src/glossary.md:52
msgid "Dynamically sized type"
msgstr "动态大小类型"

#: src/glossary.md:54
msgid ""
"A dynamically sized type (DST) is a type without a statically known size or "
"alignment."
msgstr "动态大小类型（DST）是没有静态已知大小或对齐的类型。"

#: src/glossary.md:56
msgid "Entity"
msgstr "实体"

#: src/glossary.md:58
msgid ""
"An [_entity_](names.md) is a language construct that can be referred to in "
"some way within the source program, usually via a [path](paths.md). Entities "
"include [types](types.md), [items](items.md), [generic parameters](items/"
"generics.md), [variable bindings](patterns.md), [loop labels]"
"(tokens.md#lifetimes-and-loop-labels), [lifetimes](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-"
"loop-labels), [fields](expressions/field-expr.md), [attributes]"
"(attributes.md), and [lints](attributes/diagnostics.md#lint-check-"
"attributes)."
msgstr ""
"[*实体*](names.md)是一种语言构造，可在源程序中以某种方式引用，通常是通过[路"
"径](paths.md)引用。实体包括[类型](types.md)、[项](items.md)、[泛型参数]"
"(items/generics.md)、[变量绑定](patterns.md)、[循环标签](tokens.md#lifetimes-"
"and-loop-labels)、[生命周期](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-loop-labels)、[字段]"
"(expressions/field-expr.md)、[属性](attributes.md)和 [lint](attributes/"
"diagnostics.md#lint-check-attributes)。"

#: src/glossary.md:62
msgid ""
"An expression is a combination of values, constants, variables, operators "
"and functions that evaluate to a single value, with or without side-effects."
msgstr ""
"表达式是值、常量、变量、运算符和函数的组合，会求值为单个值，可以带有或不带有"
"副作用。"

#: src/glossary.md:64
msgid "For example, `2 + (3 * 4)` is an expression that returns the value 14."
msgstr "例如，`2 + (3 * 4)` 是一个返回值 14 的表达式。"

#: src/glossary.md:66
msgid "Free item"
msgstr "自由项"

#: src/glossary.md:68
msgid ""
"An [item](items.md) that is not a member of an [implementation](items/"
"implementations.md), such as a _free function_ or a _free const_. Contrast "
"to an [associated item](#associated-item)."
msgstr ""
"不属于[实现](items/implementations.md)成员的[项](items.md)，例如*自由函数*或*"
"自由 const*。对比[关联项](#associated-item)。"

#: src/glossary.md:70
msgid "Fundamental traits"
msgstr "基本 trait"

#: src/glossary.md:72
msgid ""
"A fundamental trait is one where adding an impl of it for an existing type "
"is a breaking change. The `Fn` traits and `Sized` are fundamental."
msgstr ""
"基本 trait 指这样一种 trait：如果为某个既有类型添加它的 impl，就会造成破坏性"
"变更。`Fn` trait 和 `Sized` 都是基本 trait。"

#: src/glossary.md:74
msgid "Fundamental type constructors"
msgstr "基本类型构造器"

#: src/glossary.md:76
msgid ""
"A fundamental type constructor is a type where implementing a [blanket "
"implementation](#blanket-implementation) over it is a breaking change. `&`, "
"`&mut`, `Box`, and `Pin`  are fundamental."
msgstr ""
"基本类型构造器指这样一种类型：如果在它之上实现[毯式实现](#blanket-"
"implementation)，就会造成破坏性变更。`&`、`&mut`、`Box` 和 `Pin` 都是基本类型"
"构造器。"

#: src/glossary.md:78
msgid ""
"Any time a type `T` is considered [local](#local-type), `&T`, `&mut T`, "
"`Box<T>`, and `Pin<T>` are also considered local. Fundamental type "
"constructors cannot [cover](#uncovered-type) other types. Any time the term "
"\"covered type\" is used, the `T` in `&T`, `&mut T`, `Box<T>`, and `Pin<T>` "
"is not considered covered."
msgstr ""
"每当类型 `T` 被认为是[本地](#local-type)类型时，`&T`、`&mut T`、`Box<T>` 和 "
"`Pin<T>` 也被认为是本地的。基本类型构造器不能[覆盖](#uncovered-type)其他类"
"型。每当使用术语“已覆盖类型”时，`&T`、`&mut T`、`Box<T>` 和 `Pin<T>` 中的 "
"`T` 都不被视为已覆盖。"

#: src/glossary.md:80
msgid "Inhabited"
msgstr "有值类型"

#: src/glossary.md:82
msgid ""
"A type is inhabited if it has constructors and therefore can be "
"instantiated. An inhabited type is not \"empty\" in the sense that there can "
"be values of the type. Opposite of [Uninhabited](#uninhabited)."
msgstr ""
"如果一个类型具有构造器，因而可以被实例化，则它是有值类型。有值类型在可以存在"
"该类型的值这一意义上不是“空”的。与[无值类型](#uninhabited)相对。"

#: src/glossary.md:84
msgid "Inherent implementation"
msgstr "固有实现"

#: src/glossary.md:86
msgid ""
"An [implementation](items/implementations.md) that applies to a nominal "
"type, not to a trait-type pair. [More](items/implementations.md#inherent-"
"implementations)."
msgstr ""
"适用于名义类型而不是 trait-类型对的[实现](items/implementations.md)。[更多信"
"息](items/implementations.md#inherent-implementations)。"

#: src/glossary.md:88
msgid "Inherent method"
msgstr "固有方法"

#: src/glossary.md:90
msgid ""
"A [method](items/associated-items.md#methods) defined in an [inherent "
"implementation](items/implementations.md#inherent-implementations), not in a "
"trait implementation."
msgstr ""
"定义在[固有实现](items/implementations.md#inherent-implementations)中，而不是"
"定义在 trait 实现中的[方法](items/associated-items.md#methods)。"

#: src/glossary.md:92
msgid "Initialized"
msgstr "已初始化"

#: src/glossary.md:94
msgid ""
"A variable is initialized if it has been assigned a value and hasn't since "
"been moved from. All other memory locations are assumed to be uninitialized. "
"Only unsafe Rust can create a memory location without initializing it."
msgstr ""
"如果变量已被赋值，并且此后未被移出，则它是已初始化的。所有其他内存位置都假定"
"为未初始化。只有 unsafe Rust 能创建未初始化的内存位置。"

#: src/glossary.md:96
msgid "Local trait"
msgstr "本地 trait"

#: src/glossary.md:98
msgid ""
"A `trait` which was defined in the current crate. A trait definition is "
"local or not independent of applied type arguments. Given `trait Foo<T, U>`, "
"`Foo` is always local, regardless of the types substituted for `T` and `U`."
msgstr ""
"在当前 crate 中定义的 `trait`。一个 trait 定义是否本地，不取决于所应用的类型"
"实参。给定 `trait Foo<T, U>`，无论替换 `T` 和 `U` 的类型是什么，`Foo` 始终是"
"本地的。"

#: src/glossary.md:100
msgid "Local type"
msgstr "本地类型"

#: src/glossary.md:102
msgid ""
"A `struct`, `enum`, or `union` which was defined in the current crate. This "
"is not affected by applied type arguments. `struct Foo` is considered local, "
"but `Vec<Foo>` is not. `LocalType<ForeignType>` is local. Type aliases do "
"not affect locality."
msgstr ""
"在当前 crate 中定义的 `struct`、`enum` 或 `union`。这不受所应用的类型实参影"
"响。`struct Foo` 被认为是本地的，但 `Vec<Foo>` 不是。"
"`LocalType<ForeignType>` 是本地的。类型别名不影响本地性。"

#: src/glossary.md:104
msgid "Module"
msgstr "模块"

#: src/glossary.md:106
msgid ""
"A module is a container for zero or more [items](items.md). Modules are "
"organized in a tree, starting from an unnamed module at the root called the "
"crate root or the root module. [Paths](paths.md) may be used to refer to "
"items from other modules, which may be restricted by [visibility rules]"
"(visibility-and-privacy.md). [More](items/modules.md)"
msgstr ""
"模块是包含零个或多个[项](items.md)的容器。模块组织成一棵树，从根部一个未命名"
"模块开始，该模块称为 crate 根或根模块。[路径](paths.md)可用于引用其他模块中的"
"项，这种引用可能受到[可见性规则](visibility-and-privacy.md)限制。[更多信息]"
"(items/modules.md)"

#: src/glossary.md:110
msgid ""
"A [_name_](names.md) is an [identifier](identifiers.md) or [lifetime or loop "
"label](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-loop-labels) that refers to an [entity]"
"(#entity). A _name binding_ is when an entity declaration introduces an "
"identifier or label associated with that entity. [Paths](paths.md), "
"identifiers, and labels are used to refer to an entity."
msgstr ""
"[*名称*](names.md)是指称某个[实体](#entity)的[标识符](identifiers.md)或[生命"
"周期或循环标签](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-loop-labels)。当实体声明引入一个与该"
"实体关联的标识符或标签时，就形成了*名称绑定*。[路径](paths.md)、标识符和标签"
"用于指称实体。"

#: src/glossary.md:114
msgid ""
"[_Name resolution_](names/name-resolution.md) is the compile-time process of "
"tying [paths](paths.md), [identifiers](identifiers.md), and [labels]"
"(tokens.md#lifetimes-and-loop-labels) to [entity](#entity) declarations."
msgstr ""
"[*名称解析*](names/name-resolution.md)是在编译时将[路径](paths.md)、[标识符]"
"(identifiers.md)和[标签](tokens.md#lifetimes-and-loop-labels)关联到[实体]"
"(#entity)声明的过程。"

#: src/glossary.md:116
msgid "Namespace"
msgstr "命名空间"

#: src/glossary.md:118
msgid ""
"A _namespace_ is a logical grouping of declared [names](#name) based on the "
"kind of [entity](#entity) the name refers to. Namespaces allow the "
"occurrence of a name in one namespace to not conflict with the same name in "
"another namespace."
msgstr ""
"*命名空间*是根据名称所指称的[实体](#entity)种类，对已声明[名称](#name)进行的"
"逻辑分组。命名空间允许一个命名空间中出现的名称不与另一个命名空间中的同名名称"
"冲突。"

#: src/glossary.md:120
msgid ""
"Within a namespace, names are organized in a hierarchy, where each level of "
"the hierarchy has its own collection of named entities."
msgstr ""
"在一个命名空间内，名称按层次结构组织，该层次结构的每一级都有自己的具名实体集"
"合。"

#: src/glossary.md:122
msgid "Nominal types"
msgstr "名义类型"

#: src/glossary.md:124
msgid ""
"Types that can be referred to by a path directly. Specifically [enums](items/"
"enumerations.md), [structs](items/structs.md), [unions](items/unions.md), "
"and [trait object types](types/trait-object.md)."
msgstr ""
"可以由路径直接引用的类型。具体而言，包括[枚举](items/enumerations.md)、[结构"
"体](items/structs.md)、[联合体](items/unions.md)和 [trait 对象类型](types/"
"trait-object.md)。"

#: src/glossary.md:126
msgid "Dyn-compatible traits"
msgstr "dyn 兼容 trait"

#: src/glossary.md:128
msgid ""
"[Traits](items/traits.md) that can be used in [trait object types](types/"
"trait-object.md) (`dyn Trait`). Only traits that follow specific [rules]"
"(items/traits.md#dyn-compatibility) are _dyn compatible_."
msgstr ""
"可用于 [trait 对象类型](types/trait-object.md)（`dyn Trait`）的 [trait]"
"(items/traits.md)。只有遵循特定[规则](items/traits.md#dyn-compatibility)的 "
"trait 才是 *dyn 兼容* 的。"

#: src/glossary.md:130
msgid "These were formerly known as _object safe_ traits."
msgstr "这些过去称为 _object safe_ trait（对象安全 trait）。"

#: src/glossary.md:132
msgid "Path"
msgstr "路径"

#: src/glossary.md:134
msgid ""
"A [_path_](paths.md) is a sequence of one or more path segments used to "
"refer to an [entity](#entity) in the current scope or other levels of a "
"[namespace](#namespace) hierarchy."
msgstr ""
"[*路径*](paths.md)是由一个或多个路径段组成的序列，用于指称当前作用域或[命名空"
"间](#namespace)层次结构其他层级中的[实体](#entity)。"

#: src/glossary.md:136
msgid "Prelude"
msgstr "Prelude"

#: src/glossary.md:138
msgid ""
"Prelude, or The Rust Prelude, is a small collection of items - mostly traits "
"- that are imported into every module of every crate. The traits in the "
"prelude are pervasive."
msgstr ""
"Prelude，或称 The Rust Prelude，是一小组项（主要是 trait），会导入到每个 "
"crate 的每个模块中。prelude 中的 trait 是普遍可用的。"

#: src/glossary.md:142
msgid ""
"A [_scope_](names/scopes.md) is the region of source text where a named "
"[entity](#entity) may be referenced with that name."
msgstr ""
"[*作用域*](names/scopes.md)是源文本中的区域，在该区域内，可以用某个名称引用具"
"名[实体](#entity)。"

#: src/glossary.md:144
msgid "Scrutinee"
msgstr "被匹配值"

#: src/glossary.md:146
msgid ""
"A scrutinee is the expression that is matched on in `match` expressions and "
"similar pattern matching constructs. For example, in `match x { A => 1, B => "
"2 }`, the expression `x` is the scrutinee."
msgstr ""
"被匹配值是在 `match` 表达式和类似模式匹配构造中被匹配的表达式。例如，在 "
"`match x { A => 1, B => 2 }` 中，表达式 `x` 就是被匹配值。"

#: src/glossary.md:148
msgid "Size"
msgstr "大小"

#: src/glossary.md:150
msgid "The size of a value has two definitions."
msgstr "值的大小有两个定义。"

#: src/glossary.md:152
msgid ""
"The first is that it is how much memory must be allocated to store that "
"value."
msgstr "第一个定义是：存储该值必须分配多少内存。"

#: src/glossary.md:154
msgid ""
"The second is that it is the offset in bytes between successive elements in "
"an array with that item type."
msgstr ""
"第二个定义是：在以该值的类型作为元素类型的数组中，相邻元素之间的字节偏移量。"

#: src/glossary.md:156
msgid ""
"It is a multiple of the alignment, including zero. The size can change "
"depending on compiler version (as new optimizations are made) and target "
"platform (similar to how `usize` varies per-platform)."
msgstr ""
"它是对齐的倍数，零也包括在内。大小可能随编译器版本（随着新的优化实现）和目标"
"平台而改变（类似于 `usize` 随平台而异）。"

#: src/glossary.md:158
msgid "[More](type-layout.md#size-and-alignment)."
msgstr "[更多信息](type-layout.md#size-and-alignment)。"

#: src/glossary.md:160
msgid "Slice"
msgstr "切片"

#: src/glossary.md:162
msgid ""
"A slice is dynamically-sized view into a contiguous sequence, written as "
"`[T]`."
msgstr "切片是对一个连续序列的动态大小视图，写作 `[T]`。"

#: src/glossary.md:164
msgid ""
"It is often seen in its borrowed forms, either mutable or shared. The shared "
"slice type is `&[T]`, while the mutable slice type is `&mut [T]`, where `T` "
"represents the element type."
msgstr ""
"它通常以借用形式出现，可以是可变借用或共享借用。共享切片类型是 `&[T]`，而可变"
"切片类型是 `&mut [T]`，其中 `T` 表示元素类型。"

#: src/glossary.md:166
msgid "Statement"
msgstr "语句"

#: src/glossary.md:168
msgid ""
"A statement is the smallest standalone element of a programming language "
"that commands a computer to perform an action."
msgstr "语句是编程语言中最小的独立元素，用于命令计算机执行一个动作。"

#: src/glossary.md:170
msgid "String literal"
msgstr "字符串字面量"

#: src/glossary.md:172
msgid ""
"A string literal is a string stored directly in the final binary, and so "
"will be valid for the `'static` duration."
msgstr ""
"字符串字面量是直接存储在最终二进制文件中的字符串，因此会在 `'static` 生命周期"
"内有效。"

#: src/glossary.md:174
msgid "Its type is `'static` duration borrowed string slice, `&'static str`."
msgstr "它的类型是具有 `'static` 生命周期的借用字符串切片，`&'static str`。"

#: src/glossary.md:176
msgid "String slice"
msgstr "字符串切片"

#: src/glossary.md:178
msgid ""
"A string slice is the most primitive string type in Rust, written as `str`. "
"It is often seen in its borrowed forms, either mutable or shared. The shared "
"string slice type is `&str`, while the mutable string slice type is `&mut "
"str`."
msgstr ""
"字符串切片是 Rust 中最原始的字符串类型，写作 `str`。它通常以借用形式出现，可"
"以是可变借用或共享借用。共享字符串切片类型是 `&str`，而可变字符串切片类型是 "
"`&mut str`。"

#: src/glossary.md:180
msgid "Strings slices are always valid UTF-8."
msgstr "字符串切片始终是有效的 UTF-8。"

#: src/glossary.md:182
msgid "Trait"
msgstr "Trait"

#: src/glossary.md:184
msgid ""
"A trait is a language item that is used for describing the functionalities a "
"type must provide. It allows a type to make certain promises about its "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"trait 是一种语言项，用于描述类型必须提供的功能。它允许类型对其行为作出某些承"
"诺。"

#: src/glossary.md:186
msgid ""
"Generic functions and generic structs can use traits to constrain, or bound, "
"the types they accept."
msgstr "泛型函数和泛型结构体可以使用 trait 来约束，或者说限定，其接受的类型。"

#: src/glossary.md:188
msgid "Turbofish"
msgstr "Turbofish"

#: src/glossary.md:190
msgid ""
"Paths with generic parameters in expressions must prefix the opening "
"brackets with a `::`. Combined with the angular brackets for generics, this "
"looks like a fish `::<>`. As such, this syntax is colloquially referred to "
"as turbofish syntax."
msgstr ""
"表达式中带有泛型参数的路径必须在起始尖括号前加上 `::`。与泛型的尖括号结合后，"
"这看起来像一条鱼 `::<>`。因此，这种语法俗称 turbofish 语法。"

#: src/glossary.md:199
msgid ""
"This `::` prefix is required to disambiguate generic paths with multiple "
"comparisons in a comma-separate list. See [the bastion of the turbofish]"
"(https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/1.58.0/src/test/ui/parser/bastion-of-"
"the-turbofish.rs) for an example where not having the prefix would be "
"ambiguous."
msgstr ""
"此 `::` 前缀是必需的，用于消除泛型路径与逗号分隔列表中的多个比较之间的歧义。"
"请参见 [the bastion of the turbofish](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/"
"1.58.0/src/test/ui/parser/bastion-of-the-turbofish.rs)，其中给出了没有该前缀"
"时会产生歧义的示例。"

#: src/glossary.md:201
msgid "Uncovered type"
msgstr "未覆盖类型"

#: src/glossary.md:203
msgid ""
"A type which does not appear as an argument to another type. For example, "
"`T` is uncovered, but the `T` in `Vec<T>` is covered. This is only relevant "
"for type arguments."
msgstr ""
"未作为另一种类型的实参出现的类型。例如，`T` 是未覆盖的，但 `Vec<T>` 中的 `T` "
"是已覆盖的。这只与类型实参有关。"

#: src/glossary.md:205
msgid "Undefined behavior"
msgstr "未定义行为"

#: src/glossary.md:207
msgid ""
"Compile-time or run-time behavior that is not specified. This may result in, "
"but is not limited to: process termination or corruption; improper, "
"incorrect, or unintended computation; or platform-specific results. [More]"
"(behavior-considered-undefined.md)."
msgstr ""
"编译时或运行时未指定的行为。这可能导致但不限于：进程终止或损坏；不当、错误或"
"非预期的计算；或平台特定的结果。[更多信息](behavior-considered-"
"undefined.md)。"

#: src/glossary.md:209
msgid "r\\[glossary.uninhabited\\]"
msgstr "r\\[glossary.uninhabited\\]"

#: src/glossary.md:210
msgid "Uninhabited"
msgstr "无值类型"

#: src/glossary.md:212
msgid ""
"A type is uninhabited if it has no constructors and therefore can never be "
"instantiated. An uninhabited type is \"empty\" in the sense that there are "
"no values of the type. The canonical example of an uninhabited type is the "
"[never type](types/never.md) `!`, or an enum with no variants `enum Never { }"
"`. Opposite of [Inhabited](#inhabited)."
msgstr ""
"如果一个类型没有构造器，因而永远不能被实例化，则它是无值类型。无值类型在不存"
"在该类型的任何值这一意义上是“空”的。无值类型的标准示例是 [never 类型](types/"
"never.md) `!`，或没有变体的 enum `enum Never { }`。与[有值类型](#inhabited)相"
"对。"

#: src/glossary.md:214
msgid "r\\[glossary.zst\\]"
msgstr "r\\[glossary.zst\\]"

#: src/glossary.md:215
msgid "Zero-sized type (ZST)"
msgstr "零大小类型 (ZST)"

#: src/glossary.md:217
msgid ""
"A type is zero sized (a ZST) if its size is 0. Such types have at most one "
"possible value. Examples include:"
msgstr ""
"如果某个类型的大小为 0，则它是零大小类型（ZST）。这类类型最多只有一个可能的"
"值。例子包括："

#: src/glossary.md:219
msgid "The [unit type](type.tuple.unit) (see \\[layout.tuple.unit\\])."
msgstr "[单元类型](type.tuple.unit)（见 \\[layout.tuple.unit\\]）。"

#: src/glossary.md:220
msgid "[Function items](type.fn-item) (see \\[type.fn-item.intro\\])."
msgstr "[函数项](type.fn-item)（见 \\[type.fn-item.intro\\]）。"

#: src/glossary.md:221
msgid ""
"The constructors of [tuple-like structs](items.struct.tuple) (see \\[type.fn-"
"item.intro\\])."
msgstr ""
"[类元组结构体](items.struct.tuple)的构造器（见 \\[type.fn-item.intro\\]）。"

#: src/glossary.md:222
msgid ""
"The constructors of [tuple-like enum variants](items.enum.constructor-"
"namespace) (see \\[type.fn-item.intro\\])."
msgstr ""
"[类元组 enum 变体](items.enum.constructor-namespace)的构造器（见 \\[type.fn-"
"item.intro\\]）。"

#: src/glossary.md:223
msgid ""
"`repr(C)` [structs](items/structs.md) with no fields or where all fields are "
"zero-sized (see \\[layout.repr.c.struct.size-field-offset\\])."
msgstr ""
"无字段或所有字段均为零大小的 `repr(C)` [结构体](items/structs.md)（见 \\"
"[layout.repr.c.struct.size-field-offset\\]）。"

#: src/glossary.md:224
msgid ""
"`repr(transparent)` [structs](items/structs.md) with no fields or where all "
"fields are zero-sized (see \\[layout.repr.transparent.layout-abi\\])."
msgstr ""
"无字段或所有字段均为零大小的 `repr(transparent)` [结构体](items/structs.md)"
"（见 \\[layout.repr.transparent.layout-abi\\]）。"

#: src/glossary.md:225
msgid "[Arrays](type.array) of zero-sized types (see \\[layout.array\\])."
msgstr "零大小类型的[数组](type.array)（见 \\[layout.array\\]）。"

#: src/glossary.md:226
msgid "[Arrays](type.array) of length zero (see \\[layout.array\\])."
msgstr "长度为零的[数组](type.array)（见 \\[layout.array\\]）。"

#: src/glossary.md:227
msgid ""
"[Unions](items/unions.md) of zero-sized types (see \\[items.union.common-"
"storage\\])."
msgstr ""
